		}
		p {
			a href="#serializable-objects" id=serializable-objects:serializable-objects "Serializable objects"
			- " support being serialized, and later deserialized, in a way that is independent of any given "
			a data-x-internal=realm href="https://tc39.es/ecma262/#sec-code-realms" id=serializable-objects:realm realm
			- ". This allows them to be stored on disk and later restored, or cloned across "
			a data-x-internal=agent href="https://tc39.es/ecma262/#sec-agents" id=serializable-objects:agent agent
			- " and even "
			a data-x-internal=agent-cluster href="https://tc39.es/ecma262/#sec-agent-clusters" id=serializable-objects:agent-cluster "agent cluster"
			- " boundaries."
		}
		p {
			- "Not all objects are "
			a href="#serializable-objects" id=serializable-objects:serializable-objects-2 "serializable objects"
			- ", and not all aspects of objects that are "
			a href="#serializable-objects" id=serializable-objects:serializable-objects-3 "serializable objects"
			- " are necessarily preserved when they are serialized."
		}
		p {
			a data-x-internal=platform-object href="https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#dfn-platform-object" id=serializable-objects:platform-object "Platform objects"
			- " can be "
			a href="#serializable-objects" id=serializable-objects:serializable-objects-4 "serializable objects"
			- " if their "
			a data-x-internal=primary-interface href="https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#dfn-primary-interface" id=serializable-objects:primary-interface "primary interface"
			- " is decorated with the "
			dfn data-dfn-type=extended-attribute data-lt=Serializable id=serializable {
				code "[Serializable]"
			}
			- " IDL "
			a data-x-internal=extended-attribute href="https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#dfn-extended-attribute" id=serializable-objects:extended-attribute "extended attribute"
			- ". Such interfaces must also define the following algorithms:"
		}
		dl {
			dt {
				dfn data-export="" id=serialization-steps "serialization steps"
				- ", taking a "
				a data-x-internal=platform-object href="https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#dfn-platform-object" id=serializable-objects:platform-object-2 "platform object"
				var value
				- ", a "
				a data-x-internal=record href="https://tc39.es/ecma262/#sec-list-and-record-specification-type" id=serializable-objects:record Record
				var serialized
				- ", and a boolean "
				var forStorage
			}
			dd {
				p {
					- "A set of steps that serializes the data in "
					var value
					- " into fields of "
					var serialized
					- ". The resulting data serialized into "
					var serialized
					- " must be independent of any "
					a data-x-internal=realm href="https://tc39.es/ecma262/#sec-code-realms" id=serializable-objects:realm-2 realm
					- .
				}
				p "These steps may throw an exception if serialization is not possible."
				p {
					- "These steps may perform a "
					a href="#sub-serialization" id=serializable-objects:sub-serialization sub-serialization
					- " to serialize nested data structures. They should not call "
					a href="#structuredserialize" id=serializable-objects:structuredserialize StructuredSerialize
					- " directly, as doing so will omit the important "
					var memory
					- " argument."
				}
				p {
					- "The introduction of these steps should omit mention of the "
					var forStorage
					- " argument if it is not relevant to the algorithm."
				}
			}
			dt {
				dfn data-export="" id=deserialization-steps "deserialization steps"
				- ", taking a "
				a data-x-internal=record href="https://tc39.es/ecma262/#sec-list-and-record-specification-type" id=serializable-objects:record-2 Record
				var serialized
				- ", a "
				a data-x-internal=platform-object href="https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#dfn-platform-object" id=serializable-objects:platform-object-3 "platform object"
				var value
				- ", and a "
				a data-x-internal=realm href="https://tc39.es/ecma262/#sec-code-realms" id=serializable-objects:realm-3 realm
				var targetRealm
			}
			dd {
				p {
					- "A set of steps that deserializes the data in "
					var serialized
					- ", using it to set up "
					var value
					- " as appropriate. "
					var value
					- " will be a newly-created instance of the "
					a data-x-internal=platform-object href="https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#dfn-platform-object" id=serializable-objects:platform-object-4 "platform object"
					- " type in question, with none of its internal data set up; setting that up is the job of these steps."
				}
				p "These steps may throw an exception if deserialization is not possible."
				p {
					- "These steps may perform a "
					a href="#sub-deserialization" id=serializable-objects:sub-deserialization sub-deserialization
					- " to deserialize nested data structures. They should not call "
					a href="#structureddeserialize" id=serializable-objects:structureddeserialize StructuredDeserialize
					- " directly, as doing so will omit the important "
					var targetRealm
					- " and "
					var memory
					- " arguments."
				}
			}
		}
		p "It is up to the definition of individual platform objects to determine what data is serialized and deserialized by these steps. Typically the steps are very symmetric."
		p {
			- "The "
			code id=serializable-objects:serializable {
				a href="#serializable" "[Serializable]"
			}
			- " extended attribute must take no arguments, and must only appear on an interface. It must not appear more than once on an interface."
		}
		p {
			- "For a given "
			a data-x-internal=platform-object href="https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#dfn-platform-object" id=serializable-objects:platform-object-5 "platform object"
			- ", only the object's "
