				}
			}
		}
		p {
			- "Objects defined in the JavaScript specification are handled by the "
			a href="#structuredserialize" id=serializable-objects:structuredserialize-2 StructuredSerialize
			- " abstract operation directly."
		}
		p class=note id=cloneable-objects {
			- "Originally, this specification defined the concept of \"cloneable objects\", which could be cloned from one "
			a data-x-internal=realm href="https://tc39.es/ecma262/#sec-code-realms" id=serializable-objects:realm-4 realm
			- " to another. However, to better specify the behavior of certain more complex situations, the model was updated to make the serialization and deserialization explicit."
		}
		h4 data-export="" data-lt="transferable object" id=transferable-objects {
			span class=secno "2.7.2"
			dfn "Transferable objects"
			a class=self-link href="#transferable-objects"
		}
		p {
			a href="#transferable-objects" id=transferable-objects:transferable-objects "Transferable objects"
			- " support being transferred across "
			a data-x-internal=agent href="https://tc39.es/ecma262/#sec-agents" id=transferable-objects:agent agents
			- ". Transferring is effectively recreating the object while sharing a reference to the underlying data and then detaching the object being transferred. This is useful to transfer ownership of expensive resources. Not all objects are "
			a href="#transferable-objects" id=transferable-objects:transferable-objects-2 "transferable objects"
			- " and not all aspects of objects that are "
			a href="#transferable-objects" id=transferable-objects:transferable-objects-3 "transferable objects"
			- " are necessarily preserved when transferred."
		}
		p class=note "Transferring is an irreversible and non-idempotent operation. Once an object has been transferred, it cannot be transferred, or indeed used, again."
		p {
			a data-x-internal=platform-object href="https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#dfn-platform-object" id=transferable-objects:platform-object "Platform objects"
			- " can be "
			a href="#transferable-objects" id=transferable-objects:transferable-objects-4 "transferable objects"
			- " if their "
			a data-x-internal=primary-interface href="https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#dfn-primary-interface" id=transferable-objects:primary-interface "primary interface"
			- " is decorated with the "
			dfn data-dfn-type=extended-attribute data-lt=Transferable id=transferable {
				code "[Transferable]"
			}
			- " IDL "
			a data-x-internal=extended-attribute href="https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#dfn-extended-attribute" id=transferable-objects:extended-attribute "extended attribute"
			- ". Such interfaces must also define the following algorithms:"
		}
		dl {
			dt {
				dfn data-export="" id=transfer-steps "transfer steps"
				- ", taking a "
				a data-x-internal=platform-object href="https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#dfn-platform-object" id=transferable-objects:platform-object-2 "platform object"
				var value
				- " and a "
				a data-x-internal=record href="https://tc39.es/ecma262/#sec-list-and-record-specification-type" id=transferable-objects:record Record
				var dataHolder
			}
			dd {
				p {
					- "A set of steps that transfers the data in "
					var value
					- " into fields of "
					var dataHolder
					- ". The resulting data held in "
					var dataHolder
					- " must be independent of any "
					a data-x-internal=realm href="https://tc39.es/ecma262/#sec-code-realms" id=transferable-objects:realm realm
					- .
				}
				p "These steps may throw an exception if transferral is not possible."
			}
			dt {
				dfn data-export="" id=transfer-receiving-steps "transfer-receiving steps"
				- ", taking a "
				a data-x-internal=record href="https://tc39.es/ecma262/#sec-list-and-record-specification-type" id=transferable-objects:record-2 Record
				var dataHolder
				- " and a "
				a data-x-internal=platform-object href="https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#dfn-platform-object" id=transferable-objects:platform-object-3 "platform object"
				var value
			}
			dd {
				p {
					- "A set of steps that receives the data in "
					var dataHolder
					- ", using it to set up "
					var value
					- " as appropriate. "
					var value
					- " will be a newly-created instance of the "
					a data-x-internal=platform-object href="https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#dfn-platform-object" id=transferable-objects:platform-object-4 "platform object"
					- " type in question, with none of its internal data set up; setting that up is the job of these steps."
				}
				p "These steps may throw an exception if it is not possible to receive the transfer."
			}
		}
		p "It is up to the definition of individual platform objects to determine what data is transferred by these steps. Typically the steps are very symmetric."
		p {
			- "The "
			code id=transferable-objects:transferable {
				a href="#transferable" "[Transferable]"
			}
			- " extended attribute must take no arguments, and must only appear on an interface. It must not appear more than once on an interface."
		}
		p {
			- "For a given "
			a data-x-internal=platform-object href="https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#dfn-platform-object" id=transferable-objects:platform-object-5 "platform object"
			- ", only the object's "
			a data-x-internal=primary-interface href="https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#dfn-primary-interface" id=transferable-objects:primary-interface-2 "primary interface"
			- " is considered during the transferring process. Thus, if inheritance is involved in defining the interface, each "
			code id=transferable-objects:transferable-2 {
				a href="#transferable" "[Transferable]"
			}
			- "-annotated interface in the inheritance chain needs to define standalone "
			a href="#transfer-steps" id=transferable-objects:transfer-steps "transfer steps"
			- " and "
			a href="#transfer-receiving-steps" id=transferable-objects:transfer-receiving-steps "transfer-receiving steps"
			- ", including taking into account any important data that might come from inherited interfaces."
		}
		p {
			a data-x-internal=platform-object href="https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#dfn-platform-object" id=transferable-objects:platform-object-6 "Platform objects"
			- " that are "
			a href="#transferable-objects" id=transferable-objects:transferable-objects-5 "transferable objects"
			- " have a "
			dfn data-dfn-for="platform object" data-dfn-type=attribute id=detached "[[Detached]]"
			- " internal slot. This is used to ensure that once a platform object has been transferred, it cannot be transferred again."
		}
		p {
			- "Objects defined in the JavaScript specification are handled by the "
			a href="#structuredserializewithtransfer" id=transferable-objects:structuredserializewithtransfer StructuredSerializeWithTransfer
			- " abstract operation directly."
		}
		h4 data-dfn-type=abstract-op data-lt=StructuredSerializeInternal data-noexport="" id=structuredserializeinternal {
