			}
			li {
				code id=interactive-content:the-textarea-element {
					a href="#the-textarea-element" textarea
				}
			}
			li {
				code id=interactive-content:the-video-element {
					a href="#the-video-element" video
				}
				- " (if the "
				code id=interactive-content:attr-media-controls-2 {
					a href="#attr-media-controls" controls
				}
				- " attribute is present)"
			}
		}
		h6 id=palpable-content {
			span class=secno "3.2.5.2.8"
			- " Palpable content"
			a class=self-link href="#palpable-content"
		}
		p {
			- "As a general rule, elements whose content model allows any "
			a href="#flow-content-2" id=palpable-content:flow-content-2 "flow content"
			- " or "
			a href="#phrasing-content-2" id=palpable-content:phrasing-content-2 "phrasing content"
			- " should have at least one node in its "
			a href="#concept-html-contents" id=palpable-content:concept-html-contents contents
			- " that is "
			dfn data-export="" id=palpable-content-2 "palpable content"
			- " and that does not have the "
			code id=palpable-content:attr-hidden {
				a href="#attr-hidden" hidden
			}
			- " attribute specified."
		}
		p class=note {
			a href="#palpable-content-2" id=palpable-content:palpable-content-2 "Palpable content"
			- " makes an element non-empty by providing either some descendant non-empty "
			a href="#text-content" id=palpable-content:text-content text
			- ", or else something users can hear ("
			code id=palpable-content:the-audio-element {
				a href="#the-audio-element" audio
			}
			- " elements) or view ("
			code id=palpable-content:the-video-element {
				a href="#the-video-element" video
			}
			- ", "
			code id=palpable-content:the-img-element {
				a href="#the-img-element" img
			}
			- ", or "
			code id=palpable-content:the-canvas-element {
				a href="#the-canvas-element" canvas
			}
			- " elements) or otherwise interact with (for example, interactive form controls)."
		}
		p "This requirement is not a hard requirement, however, as there are many cases where an element can be empty legitimately, for example when it is used as a placeholder which will later be filled in by a script, or when the element is part of a template and would on most pages be filled in but on some pages is not relevant."
		p "Conformance checkers are encouraged to provide a mechanism for authors to find elements that fail to fulfill this requirement, as an authoring aid."
		p "The following elements are palpable content:"
		ul class="brief category-list" {
			li {
				code id=palpable-content:the-a-element {
					a href="#the-a-element" a
				}
			}
			li {
				code id=palpable-content:the-abbr-element {
					a href="#the-abbr-element" abbr
				}
			}
			li {
				code id=palpable-content:the-address-element {
					a href="#the-address-element" address
				}
			}
			li {
				code id=palpable-content:the-article-element {
					a href="#the-article-element" article
				}
			}
			li {
				code id=palpable-content:the-aside-element {
					a href="#the-aside-element" aside
				}
			}
			li {
				code id=palpable-content:the-audio-element-2 {
					a href="#the-audio-element" audio
				}
				- " (if the "
				code id=palpable-content:attr-media-controls {
					a href="#attr-media-controls" controls
				}
				- " attribute is present)"
			}
			li {
				code id=palpable-content:the-b-element {
					a href="#the-b-element" b
				}
			}
			li {
				code id=palpable-content:the-bdi-element {
					a href="#the-bdi-element" bdi
				}
			}
			li {
				code id=palpable-content:the-bdo-element {
					a href="#the-bdo-element" bdo
				}
			}
			li {
				code id=palpable-content:the-blockquote-element {
					a href="#the-blockquote-element" blockquote
				}
			}
			li {
				code id=palpable-content:the-button-element {
					a href="#the-button-element" button
				}
			}
			li {
				code id=palpable-content:the-canvas-element-2 {
					a href="#the-canvas-element" canvas
				}
			}
