		p {
			- "Let "
			var view
			- " be a view of the DOM that replaces all "
			code id=paragraphs:the-a-element-2 {
				a href="#the-a-element" a
			}
			- ", "
			code id=paragraphs:the-ins-element-5 {
				a href="#the-ins-element" ins
			}
			- ", "
			code id=paragraphs:the-del-element-5 {
				a href="#the-del-element" del
			}
			- ", and "
			code id=paragraphs:the-map-element-2 {
				a href="#the-map-element" map
			}
			- " elements in the document with their "
			a href="#concept-html-contents" id=paragraphs:concept-html-contents contents
			- ". Then, in "
			var view
			- ", for each run of sibling "
			a href="#phrasing-content-2" id=paragraphs:phrasing-content-2-2 "phrasing content"
			- " nodes uninterrupted by other types of content, in an element that accepts content other than "
			a href="#phrasing-content-2" id=paragraphs:phrasing-content-2-3 "phrasing content"
			- " as well as "
			a href="#phrasing-content-2" id=paragraphs:phrasing-content-2-4 "phrasing content"
			- ", let "
			var first
			- " be the first node of the run, and let "
			var last
			- " be the last node of the run. For each such run that consists of at least one node that is neither "
			a href="#embedded-content-category" id=paragraphs:embedded-content-category "embedded content"
			- " nor "
			a href="#inter-element-whitespace" id=paragraphs:inter-element-whitespace-2 "inter-element whitespace"
			- ", a paragraph exists in the original DOM from immediately before "
			var first
			- " to immediately after "
			var last
			- ". (Paragraphs can thus span across "
			code id=paragraphs:the-a-element-3 {
				a href="#the-a-element" a
