		}
		p {
			- "The "
			dfn data-dfn-for=html-global data-dfn-type=element-attr id=attr-lang {
				code lang
			}
			- " attribute (in no namespace) specifies the primary language for the element's contents and for any of the element's attributes that contain text. Its value must be a valid BCP 47 language tag, or the empty string. Setting the attribute to the empty string indicates that the primary language is unknown. "
			a href="#refsBCP47" "[BCP47]"
		}
		p {
			- "The "
			dfn id=attr-xml-lang {
				a href="https://www.w3.org/TR/xml/#sec-lang-tag" {
					code lang
				}
			}
			- " attribute in the "
			a data-x-internal=xml-namespace href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#xml-namespace" id=the-lang-and-xml:lang-attributes:xml-namespace "XML namespace"
			- " is defined in XML. "
			a href="#refsXML" "[XML]"
		}
		p {
			- "If these attributes are omitted from an element, then the language of this element is the same as the language of its parent element, if any (except for "
			code id=the-lang-and-xml:lang-attributes:the-slot-element {
				a href="#the-slot-element" slot
			}
			- " elements in a "
			a data-x-internal=shadow-tree href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-shadow-tree" id=the-lang-and-xml:lang-attributes:shadow-tree "shadow tree"
			- ")."
		}
		p {
			- "The "
			code id=the-lang-and-xml:lang-attributes:attr-lang-2 {
				a href="#attr-lang" lang
			}
			- " attribute in no namespace may be used on any "
			a href="#html-elements" id=the-lang-and-xml:lang-attributes:html-elements "HTML element"
			- .
		}
		p {
			- "The "
			a data-x-internal=attr-xml-lang href="https://www.w3.org/TR/xml/#sec-lang-tag" id=the-lang-and-xml:lang-attributes:attr-xml-lang-2 {
				code lang
				- " attribute in the "
				span "XML namespace"
			}
			- " may be used on "
			a href="#html-elements" id=the-lang-and-xml:lang-attributes:html-elements-2 "HTML elements"
			- " in "
			a data-x-internal=xml-documents href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#xml-document" id=the-lang-and-xml:lang-attributes:xml-documents "XML documents"
			- ", as well as elements in other namespaces if the relevant specifications allow it (in particular, MathML and SVG allow "
			a data-x-internal=attr-xml-lang href="https://www.w3.org/TR/xml/#sec-lang-tag" id=the-lang-and-xml:lang-attributes:attr-xml-lang-3 {
				code lang
				- " attributes in the "
				span "XML namespace"
			}
			- " to be specified on their elements). If both the "
			code id=the-lang-and-xml:lang-attributes:attr-lang-3 {
				a href="#attr-lang" lang
			}
			- " attribute in no namespace and the "
			a data-x-internal=attr-xml-lang href="https://www.w3.org/TR/xml/#sec-lang-tag" id=the-lang-and-xml:lang-attributes:attr-xml-lang-4 {
				code lang
				- " attribute in the "
				span "XML namespace"
			}
			- " are specified on the same element, they must have exactly the same value when compared in an "
			a data-x-internal=ascii-case-insensitive href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ascii-case-insensitive" id=the-lang-and-xml:lang-attributes:ascii-case-insensitive "ASCII case-insensitive"
			- " manner."
		}
		p {
			- "Authors must not use the "
			a data-x-internal=attr-xml-lang href="https://www.w3.org/TR/xml/#sec-lang-tag" id=the-lang-and-xml:lang-attributes:attr-xml-lang-5 {
				code lang
				- " attribute in the "
				span "XML namespace"
			}
			- " on "
			a href="#html-elements" id=the-lang-and-xml:lang-attributes:html-elements-3 "HTML elements"
			- " in "
			a data-x-internal=html-documents href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#html-document" id=the-lang-and-xml:lang-attributes:html-documents "HTML documents"
			- ". To ease migration to and from XML, authors may specify an attribute in no namespace with no prefix and with the literal localname \""
			code xml:lang
			- "\" on "
			a href="#html-elements" id=the-lang-and-xml:lang-attributes:html-elements-4 "HTML elements"
			- " in "
			a data-x-internal=html-documents href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#html-document" id=the-lang-and-xml:lang-attributes:html-documents-2 "HTML documents"
			- ", but such attributes must only be specified if a "
			code id=the-lang-and-xml:lang-attributes:attr-lang-4 {
				a href="#attr-lang" lang
			}
			- " attribute in no namespace is also specified, and both attributes must have the same value when compared in an "
			a data-x-internal=ascii-case-insensitive href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ascii-case-insensitive" id=the-lang-and-xml:lang-attributes:ascii-case-insensitive-2 "ASCII case-insensitive"
			- " manner."
		}
		p class=note {
			- "The attribute in no namespace with no prefix and with the literal localname \""
			code xml:lang
			- "\" has no effect on language processing."
		}
		hr
		p {
			- "To determine the "
			dfn data-dfn-for=Node data-export="" id=language language
			- " of a node, user agents must use the first appropriate step in the following list:"
		}
		dl class=switch {
			dt {
				- "If the node is an element that has a "
				a data-x-internal=attr-xml-lang href="https://www.w3.org/TR/xml/#sec-lang-tag" id=the-lang-and-xml:lang-attributes:attr-xml-lang-6 {
					code lang
					- " attribute in the "
					span "XML namespace"
				}
				- " set"
			}
			dd {
				p "Use the value of that attribute."
			}
			dt {
				- "If the node is an "
				a href="#html-elements" id=the-lang-and-xml:lang-attributes:html-elements-5 "HTML element"
				- " or an element in the "
				a data-x-internal=svg-namespace href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#svg-namespace" id=the-lang-and-xml:lang-attributes:svg-namespace "SVG namespace"
				- ", and it has a "
				code id=the-lang-and-xml:lang-attributes:attr-lang-5 {
					a href="#attr-lang" lang
				}
				- " in no namespace attribute set"
			}
			dd {
				p "Use the value of that attribute."
			}
			dt {
				- "If the node's parent is a "
				a data-x-internal=shadow-root href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-shadow-root" id=the-lang-and-xml:lang-attributes:shadow-root "shadow root"
			}
			dd {
				p {
					- "Use the "
					a href="#language" id=the-lang-and-xml:lang-attributes:language language
					- " of that "
					a data-x-internal=shadow-root href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-shadow-root" id=the-lang-and-xml:lang-attributes:shadow-root-2 "shadow root"
					- "'s "
					a data-x-internal=concept-documentfragment-host href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-documentfragment-host" id=the-lang-and-xml:lang-attributes:concept-documentfragment-host host
					- .
				}
			}
			dt {
				- "If the node's "
				a data-x-internal=parent-element href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#parent-element" id=the-lang-and-xml:lang-attributes:parent-element "parent element"
				- " is not null"
			}
			dd {
				p {
					- "Use the "
					a href="#language" id=the-lang-and-xml:lang-attributes:language-2 language
					- " of that "
					a data-x-internal=parent-element href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#parent-element" id=the-lang-and-xml:lang-attributes:parent-element-2 "parent element"
					- .
				}
			}
			dt Otherwise
			dd {
				p {
					- "If there is a "
					a href="#pragma-set-default-language" id=the-lang-and-xml:lang-attributes:pragma-set-default-language "pragma-set default language"
					- " set, then that is the language of the node. If there is no "
					a href="#pragma-set-default-language" id=the-lang-and-xml:lang-attributes:pragma-set-default-language-2 "pragma-set default language"
					- " set, then language information from a higher-level protocol (such as HTTP), if any, must be used as the final fallback language instead. In the absence of any such language information, and in cases where the higher-level protocol reports multiple languages, the language of the node is unknown, and the corresponding language tag is the empty string."
				}
			}
		}
		p {
			- "If the resulting value is not a recognized language tag, then it must be treated as an unknown language having the given language tag, distinct from all other languages. For the purposes of round-tripping or communicating with other services that expect language tags, user agents should pass unknown language tags through unmodified, and tagged as being BCP 47 language tags, so that subsequent services do not interpret the data as another type of language description. "
			a href="#refsBCP47" "[BCP47]"
		}
		p class=example {
			- "Thus, for instance, an element with "
			code "lang=\"xyzzy\""
			- " would be matched by the selector "
			code ":lang(xyzzy)"
			- " (e.g. in CSS), but it would not be matched by "
			code ":lang(abcde)"
			- ", even though both are equally invalid. Similarly, if a web browser and screen reader working in unison communicated about the language of the element, the browser would tell the screen reader that the language was \"xyzzy\", even if it knew it was invalid, just in case the screen reader actually supported a language with that tag after all. Even if the screen reader supported both BCP 47 and another syntax for encoding language names, and in that other syntax the string \"xyzzy\" was a way to denote the Belarusian language, it would be "
			em incorrect
			- " for the screen reader to then start treating text as Belarusian, because \"xyzzy\" is not how Belarusian is described in BCP 47 codes (BCP 47 uses the code \"be\" for Belarusian)."
		}
		p "If the resulting value is the empty string, then it must be interpreted as meaning that the language of the node is explicitly unknown."
		hr
		p "User agents may use the element's language to determine proper processing or rendering (e.g. in the selection of appropriate fonts or pronunciations, for dictionary selection, or for the user interfaces of form controls such as date pickers). "
		hr
