		h4 id=requirements-relating-to-the-bidirectional-algorithm {
			span class=secno "3.2.8"
			- " Requirements relating to the bidirectional algorithm"
			a class=self-link href="#requirements-relating-to-the-bidirectional-algorithm"
		}
		h5 id=authoring-conformance-criteria-for-bidirectional-algorithm-formatting-characters {
			span class=secno "3.2.8.1"
			- " Authoring conformance criteria for bidirectional-algorithm formatting characters"
			a class=self-link href="#authoring-conformance-criteria-for-bidirectional-algorithm-formatting-characters"
		}
		p {
			a href="#text-content" id=authoring-conformance-criteria-for-bidirectional-algorithm-formatting-characters:text-content "Text content"
			- " in "
			a href="#html-elements" id=authoring-conformance-criteria-for-bidirectional-algorithm-formatting-characters:html-elements "HTML elements"
			- " with "
			code id=authoring-conformance-criteria-for-bidirectional-algorithm-formatting-characters:text {
				a data-x-internal=text href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#interface-text" Text
			}
			- " nodes in their "
			a href="#concept-html-contents" id=authoring-conformance-criteria-for-bidirectional-algorithm-formatting-characters:concept-html-contents contents
			- ", and text in attributes of "
			a href="#html-elements" id=authoring-conformance-criteria-for-bidirectional-algorithm-formatting-characters:html-elements-2 "HTML elements"
			- " that allow free-form text, may contain characters in the ranges U+202A to U+202E and U+2066 to U+2069 (the bidirectional-algorithm formatting characters). "
			a href="#refsBIDI" "[BIDI]"
		}
		p class=note {
			- "Authors are encouraged to use the "
			code id=authoring-conformance-criteria-for-bidirectional-algorithm-formatting-characters:attr-dir {
				a href="#attr-dir" dir
			}
			- " attribute, the "
			code id=authoring-conformance-criteria-for-bidirectional-algorithm-formatting-characters:the-bdo-element {
				a href="#the-bdo-element" bdo
			}
			- " element, and the "
			code id=authoring-conformance-criteria-for-bidirectional-algorithm-formatting-characters:the-bdi-element {
				a href="#the-bdi-element" bdi
			}
			- " element, rather than maintaining the bidirectional-algorithm formatting characters manually. The bidirectional-algorithm formatting characters interact poorly with CSS."
		}
		h5 id=user-agent-conformance-criteria {
			span class=secno "3.2.8.2"
			- " User agent conformance criteria"
			a class=self-link href="#user-agent-conformance-criteria"
		}
		p {
			- "User agents must implement the Unicode bidirectional algorithm to determine the proper ordering of characters when rendering documents and parts of documents. "
			a href="#refsBIDI" "[BIDI]"
		}
		p {
			- "The mapping of HTML to the Unicode bidirectional algorithm must be done in one of three ways. Either the user agent must implement CSS, including in particular the CSS "
			a data-x-internal='unicode-bidi' href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-writing-modes/#unicode-bidi" id=user-agent-conformance-criteria:'unicode-bidi' 'unicode-bidi'
			- ", "
			a data-x-internal='direction' href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-writing-modes/#direction" id=user-agent-conformance-criteria:'direction' 'direction'
			- ", and "
			a data-x-internal='content' href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css2/#content%E2%91%A0" id=user-agent-conformance-criteria:'content' 'content'
			- " properties, and must have, in its user agent style sheet, the rules using those properties given in this specification's "
			a href="#rendering" rendering
			- " section, or, alternatively, the user agent must act as if it implemented just the aforementioned properties and had a user agent style sheet that included all the aforementioned rules, but without letting style sheets specified in documents override them, or, alternatively, the user agent must implement another styling language with equivalent semantics. "
			a href="#refsCSSGC" "[CSSGC]"
		}
		p id=bidireq {
			- "The following elements and attributes have requirements defined by the "
			a href="#rendering" rendering
			- " section that, due to the requirements in this section, are requirements on all user agents (not just those that "
			a href="#renderingUA" "support the suggested default rendering"
