				div class=example {
					p {
						- "This page about typefaces on British motorways uses a "
						code id=standard-metadata-names:the-meta-element-7 {
							a href="#the-meta-element" meta
						}
						- " element to specify some keywords that users might use to look for the page:"
					}
					pre {
						code class=html {
							c- cp="" "<!DOCTYPE HTML>"
							c- p="" <
							c- f="" html
							c- e="" lang
							c- o="" "="
							c- s="" "\"en-GB\""
							c- p="" >
							c- p="" <
							c- f="" head
							c- p="" >
							c- p="" <
							c- f="" title
							c- p="" >
							- "Typefaces on UK motorways"
							c- p="" "</"
							c- f="" title
							c- p="" >
							c- p="" <
							c- f="" meta
							c- e="" name
							c- o="" "="
							c- s="" "\"keywords\""
							c- e="" content
							c- o="" "="
							c- s="" "\"british,type face,font,fonts,highway,highways\""
							c- p="" >
							c- p="" "</"
							c- f="" head
							c- p="" >
							c- p="" <
							c- f="" body
							c- p="" >
							- " ..."
						}
					}
				}
				p class=note "Many search engines do not consider such keywords, because this feature has historically been used unreliably and even misleadingly as a way to spam search engine results in a way that is not helpful for users."
				p "To obtain the list of keywords that the author has specified as applicable to the page, the user agent must run the following steps:"
				ol {
					li {
						p {
							- "Let "
							var keywords
							- " be an empty list."
						}
					}
					li {
						p {
							- "For each "
							code id=standard-metadata-names:the-meta-element-8 {
								a href="#the-meta-element" meta
							}
							- " element with a "
							code id=standard-metadata-names:attr-meta-name-6 {
								a href="#attr-meta-name" name
							}
							- " attribute and a "
							code id=standard-metadata-names:attr-meta-content-2 {
								a href="#attr-meta-content" content
							}
							- " attribute and where the "
							code id=standard-metadata-names:attr-meta-name-7 {
								a href="#attr-meta-name" name
							}
							- " attribute value is an "
							a data-x-internal=ascii-case-insensitive href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ascii-case-insensitive" id=standard-metadata-names:ascii-case-insensitive-6 "ASCII case-insensitive"
							- " match for "
							code id=standard-metadata-names:meta-keywords {
								a href="#meta-keywords" keywords
							}
							- :
						}
						ol {
							li {
								p {
									a data-x-internal=split-a-string-on-commas href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#split-on-commas" id=standard-metadata-names:split-a-string-on-commas {
										- "Split the value of the element's "
										code content
										- " attribute on commas"
									}
									- .
								}
							}
							li {
								p {
									- "Add the resulting tokens, if any, to "
									var keywords
									- .
								}
							}
						}
					}
					li {
						p {
							- "Remove any duplicates from "
							var keywords
							- .
						}
					}
					li {
						p {
							- "Return "
							var keywords
							- ". This is the list of keywords that the author has specified as applicable to the page."
						}
					}
				}
				p "User agents should not use this information when there is insufficient confidence in the reliability of the value."
				p class=example "For instance, it would be reasonable for a content management system to use the keyword information of pages within the system to populate the index of a site-specific search engine, but a large-scale content aggregator that used this information would likely find that certain users would try to game its ranking mechanism through the use of inappropriate keywords."
			}
