					}
					- ", "
					code id=standard-metadata-names:attr-meta-content-8 {
						a href="#attr-meta-content" content
					}
					- ", or "
					code id=standard-metadata-names:attr-link-media-2 {
						a href="#attr-link-media" media
					}
					- " attributes changed, or if the environment changes such that any "
					code id=standard-metadata-names:the-meta-element-15 {
						a href="#the-meta-element" meta
					}
					- " element's "
					code id=standard-metadata-names:attr-link-media-3 {
						a href="#attr-link-media" media
					}
					- " attribute's value may now or may no longer "
					a href="#matches-the-environment" id=standard-metadata-names:matches-the-environment-2 "match the environment"
					- ", user agents must re-run the above algorithm and apply the result to any affected UI."
				}
				p "When using the theme color in UI, user agents may adjust it in implementation-specific ways to make it more suitable for the UI in question. For example, if a user agent intends to use the theme color as a background and display white text over it, it might use a darker variant of the theme color in that part of the UI, to ensure adequate contrast."
			}
			dt {
				dfn data-dfn-for="meta/name" data-dfn-type=attr-value id=meta-color-scheme {
					code color-scheme
				}
			}
			dd {
				p {
					- "To aid user agents in rendering the page background with the desired color scheme immediately (rather than waiting for all CSS in the page to load), a "
					a data-x-internal='color-scheme' href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-color-adjust/#color-scheme-prop" id=standard-metadata-names:'color-scheme' 'color-scheme'
					- " value can be provided in a "
					code id=standard-metadata-names:the-meta-element-16 {
						a href="#the-meta-element" meta
					}
					- " element."
				}
				p {
					- "The value must be a string that matches the syntax for the CSS "
					a data-x-internal='color-scheme' href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-color-adjust/#color-scheme-prop" id=standard-metadata-names:'color-scheme'-2 'color-scheme'
					- " property value. It determines the "
					a data-x-internal=page's-supported-color-schemes href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-color-adjust/#pages-supported-color-schemes" id=standard-metadata-names:page's-supported-color-schemes "page's supported color-schemes"
					- .
				}
				p {
					- "There must not be more than one "
					code id=standard-metadata-names:the-meta-element-17 {
						a href="#the-meta-element" meta
					}
					- " element with its "
					code id=standard-metadata-names:attr-meta-name-13 {
						a href="#attr-meta-name" name
					}
					- " attribute value set to an "
					a data-x-internal=ascii-case-insensitive href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ascii-case-insensitive" id=standard-metadata-names:ascii-case-insensitive-10 "ASCII case-insensitive"
					- " match for "
					code id=standard-metadata-names:meta-color-scheme {
						a href="#meta-color-scheme" color-scheme
					}
					- " per document."
				}
				div class=example {
					p "The following declaration indicates that the page is aware of and can handle a color scheme with dark background colors and light foreground colors:"
					pre {
						code class=html {
							c- p="" <
							c- f="" meta
							c- e="" name
							c- o="" "="
							c- s="" "\"color-scheme\""
							c- e="" content
							c- o="" "="
							c- s="" "\"dark\""
							c- p="" >
						}
					}
				}
				p {
					- "To obtain a "
					a data-x-internal=page's-supported-color-schemes href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-color-adjust/#pages-supported-color-schemes" id=standard-metadata-names:page's-supported-color-schemes-2 "page's supported color-schemes"
					- ", user agents must run the following steps:"
				}
				ol {
					li {
						p {
							- "Let "
							var "candidate elements"
							- " be the list of all "
							code id=standard-metadata-names:the-meta-element-18 {
								a href="#the-meta-element" meta
							}
							- " elements that meet the following criteria, in "
							a data-x-internal=tree-order href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-tree-order" id=standard-metadata-names:tree-order-4 "tree order"
							- :
						}
						ul {
							li {
								p {
									- "the element is "
									a data-x-internal=in-a-document-tree href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#in-a-document-tree" id=standard-metadata-names:in-a-document-tree-3 "in a document tree"
									- ";"
								}
							}
							li {
								p {
									- "the element has a "
									code id=standard-metadata-names:attr-meta-name-14 {
										a href="#attr-meta-name" name
									}
									- " attribute, whose value is an "
									a data-x-internal=ascii-case-insensitive href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ascii-case-insensitive" id=standard-metadata-names:ascii-case-insensitive-11 "ASCII case-insensitive"
									- " match for "
									code id=standard-metadata-names:meta-color-scheme-2 {
										a href="#meta-color-scheme" color-scheme
									}
									- "; and"
								}
							}
							li {
								p {
									- "the element has a "
									code id=standard-metadata-names:attr-meta-content-9 {
										a href="#attr-meta-content" content
									}
									- " attribute."
								}
							}
						}
					}
					li {
						p {
							- "For each "
							var element
							- " in "
							var "candidate elements"
							- :
						}
						ol {
							li {
								- "Let "
								var parsed
								- " be the result of "
								a data-x-internal=parse-a-list-of-component-values href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-syntax/#parse-a-list-of-component-values" id=standard-metadata-names:parse-a-list-of-component-values "parsing a list of component values"
								- " given the value of "
								var element
								- "'s "
								code id=standard-metadata-names:attr-meta-content-10 {
									a href="#attr-meta-content" content
								}
								- " attribute."
							}
							li {
								- "If "
								var parsed
								- " is a valid CSS "
								a data-x-internal='color-scheme' href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-color-adjust/#color-scheme-prop" id=standard-metadata-names:'color-scheme'-3 'color-scheme'
								- " property value, then return "
								var parsed
								- .
							}
						}
					}
					li {
						p "Return null."
					}
				}
				p {
					- "If any "
					code id=standard-metadata-names:the-meta-element-19 {
						a href="#the-meta-element" meta
					}
					- " elements are "
					a href="#insert-an-element-into-a-document" id=standard-metadata-names:insert-an-element-into-a-document-3 "inserted into the document"
					- " or "
					a href="#remove-an-element-from-a-document" id=standard-metadata-names:remove-an-element-from-a-document-2 "removed from the document"
					- ", or existing "
					code id=standard-metadata-names:the-meta-element-20 {
						a href="#the-meta-element" meta
					}
					- " elements have their "
					code id=standard-metadata-names:attr-meta-name-15 {
						a href="#attr-meta-name" name
					}
					- " or "
					code id=standard-metadata-names:attr-meta-content-11 {
						a href="#attr-meta-content" content
					}
					- " attributes changed, user agents must re-run the above algorithm."
				}
				p class=note "Because these rules check successive elements until they find a match, an author can provide multiple such values to handle fallback for legacy user agents. Opposite to how CSS fallback works for properties, the multiple meta elements needs to be arranged with the legacy values after the newer values."
			}
		}
		h5 id=other-metadata-names {
			span class=secno "4.2.5.2"
			- " Other metadata names"
			a class=self-link href="#other-metadata-names"
		}
		p {
			- "Anyone can create and use their own "
			dfn id=concept-meta-extensions "extensions to the predefined set of metadata names"
			- ". There is no requirement to register such extensions."
		}
		p "However, a new metadata name should not be created in any of the following cases:"
		ul {
			li {
				p {
					- "If either the name is a "
					a data-x-internal=url href="https://url.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-url" id=other-metadata-names:url URL
					- ", or the value of its accompanying "
					code id=other-metadata-names:attr-meta-content {
						a href="#attr-meta-content" content
					}
					- " attribute is a "
					a data-x-internal=url href="https://url.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-url" id=other-metadata-names:url-2 URL
					- "; in those cases, registering it as an "
					a href="#concept-rel-extensions" id=other-metadata-names:concept-rel-extensions "extension to the predefined set of link types"
					- " is encouraged (rather than creating a new metadata name)."
				}
			}
			li {
				p "If the name is for something expected to have processing requirements in user agents; in that case it ought to be standardized."
			}
		}
		p {
			- "Also, before creating and using a new metadata name, consulting the "
			a href="https://wiki.whatwg.org/wiki/MetaExtensions" "WHATWG Wiki MetaExtensions page"
			- " is encouraged — to avoid choosing a metadata name that's already in use, and to avoid duplicating the purpose of any metadata names that are already in use, and to avoid new standardized names clashing with your chosen name. "
			a href="#refsWHATWGWIKI" "[WHATWGWIKI]"
		}
		p "Anyone is free to edit the WHATWG Wiki MetaExtensions page at any time to add a metadata name. New metadata names can be specified with the following information:"
		dl {
			dt Keyword
			dd {
				p "The actual name being defined. The name should not be confusingly similar to any other defined name (e.g. differing only in case)."
			}
			dt "Brief description"
			dd {
				p "A short non-normative description of what the metadata name's meaning is, including the format the value is required to be in."
			}
			dt Specification
			dd "A link to a more detailed description of the metadata name's semantics and requirements. It could be another page on the wiki, or a link to an external page."
			dt Synonyms
			dd {
				p "A list of other names that have exactly the same processing requirements. Authors should not use the names defined to be synonyms (they are only intended to allow user agents to support legacy content). Anyone may remove synonyms that are not used in practice; only names that need to be processed as synonyms for compatibility with legacy content are to be registered in this way."
			}
			dt Status
			dd {
				p "One of the following:"
				dl {
					dt Proposed
					dd "The name has not received wide peer review and approval. Someone has proposed it and is, or soon will be, using it."
					dt Ratified
					dd "The name has received wide peer review and approval. It has a specification that unambiguously defines how to handle pages that use the name, including when they use it in incorrect ways."
					dt Discontinued
					dd "The metadata name has received wide peer review and it has been found wanting. Existing pages are using this metadata name, but new pages should avoid it. The \"brief description\" and \"specification\" entries will give details of what authors should use instead, if anything."
				}
				p "If a metadata name is found to be redundant with existing values, it should be removed and listed as a synonym for the existing value."
				p "If a metadata name is added in the \"proposed\" state for a period of a month or more without being used or specified, then it may be removed from the WHATWG Wiki MetaExtensions page."
				p "If a metadata name is added with the \"proposed\" status and found to be redundant with existing values, it should be removed and listed as a synonym for the existing value. If a metadata name is added with the \"proposed\" status and found to be harmful, then it should be changed to \"discontinued\" status."
				p "Anyone can change the status at any time, but should only do so in accordance with the definitions above."
			}
		}
		h5 id=pragma-directives {
			span class=secno "4.2.5.3"
			- " Pragma directives"
			a class=self-link href="#pragma-directives"
		}
		p {
			- "When the "
			dfn data-dfn-for=meta data-dfn-type=element-attr id=attr-meta-http-equiv {
				code http-equiv
			}
			- " attribute is specified on a "
			code id=pragma-directives:the-meta-element {
				a href="#the-meta-element" meta
			}
			- " element, the element is a pragma directive."
		}
		p {
			- "The "
			code id=pragma-directives:attr-meta-http-equiv {
				a href="#attr-meta-http-equiv" http-equiv
			}
			- " attribute is an "
			a href="#enumerated-attribute" id=pragma-directives:enumerated-attribute "enumerated attribute"
			- " with the following keywords and states:"
		}
		table class=yesno id=table-http-equiv {
			thead {
				tr {
					th "Keyword "
					th "Conforming "
					th "State "
					th "Brief description "
				}
			}
			tbody {
				tr {
					td {
						dfn data-dfn-for="meta/http-equiv" data-dfn-type=attr-value id=attr-meta-http-equiv-keyword-content-language {
							code content-language
						}
					}
					td class=no "No "
					td {
						a href="#attr-meta-http-equiv-content-language" id=pragma-directives:attr-meta-http-equiv-content-language "Content language"
					}
					td {
						- "Sets the "
						a href="#pragma-set-default-language" id=pragma-directives:pragma-set-default-language "pragma-set default language"
						- ". "
					}
				}
				tr {
					td {
						dfn data-dfn-for="meta/http-equiv" data-dfn-type=attr-value id=attr-meta-http-equiv-keyword-content-type {
							code content-type
						}
					}
					td {					}
					td {
						a href="#attr-meta-http-equiv-content-type" id=pragma-directives:attr-meta-http-equiv-content-type "Encoding declaration"
					}
					td {
						- "An alternative form of setting the "
						code id=pragma-directives:attr-meta-charset {
							a href="#attr-meta-charset" charset
						}
						- ". "
					}
				}
				tr {
					td {
						dfn data-dfn-for="meta/http-equiv" data-dfn-type=attr-value id=attr-meta-http-equiv-keyword-default-style {
							code default-style
						}
					}
					td {					}
					td {
						a href="#attr-meta-http-equiv-default-style" id=pragma-directives:attr-meta-http-equiv-default-style "Default style"
					}
					td {
						- "Sets the "
						a data-x-internal=css-style-sheet-set-name href="https://drafts.csswg.org/cssom/#css-style-sheet-set-name" id=pragma-directives:css-style-sheet-set-name name
						- " of the default "
						a data-x-internal=css-style-sheet-set href="https://drafts.csswg.org/cssom/#css-style-sheet-set" id=pragma-directives:css-style-sheet-set "CSS style sheet set"
						- ". "
					}
				}
				tr {
					td {
						dfn data-dfn-for="meta/http-equiv" data-dfn-type=attr-value id=attr-meta-http-equiv-keyword-refresh {
							code refresh
						}
					}
					td {					}
					td {
						a href="#attr-meta-http-equiv-refresh" id=pragma-directives:attr-meta-http-equiv-refresh Refresh
					}
					td "Acts as a timed redirect. "
				}
				tr {
					td {
						dfn data-dfn-for="meta/http-equiv" data-dfn-type=attr-value id=attr-meta-http-equiv-keyword-set-cookie {
							code set-cookie
						}
					}
					td class=no "No "
					td {
						a href="#attr-meta-http-equiv-set-cookie" id=pragma-directives:attr-meta-http-equiv-set-cookie Set-Cookie
					}
					td "Has no effect. "
				}
				tr {
					td {
						dfn data-dfn-for="meta/http-equiv" data-dfn-type=attr-value id=attr-meta-http-equiv-keyword-x-ua-compatible {
							code x-ua-compatible
						}
					}
					td {					}
					td {
						a href="#attr-meta-http-equiv-x-ua-compatible" id=pragma-directives:attr-meta-http-equiv-x-ua-compatible X-UA-Compatible
					}
					td "In practice, encourages Internet Explorer to more closely follow the specifications. "
				}
				tr {
					td {
						dfn data-dfn-for="meta/http-equiv" data-dfn-type=attr-value id=attr-meta-http-equiv-keyword-content-security-policy {
							code content-security-policy
						}
					}
					td {					}
					td {
						a href="#attr-meta-http-equiv-content-security-policy" id=pragma-directives:attr-meta-http-equiv-content-security-policy "Content security policy"
					}
					td {
						a data-x-internal=enforce-the-policy href="https://w3c.github.io/webappsec-csp/#enforced" id=pragma-directives:enforce-the-policy Enforces
						- " a "
						a data-x-internal=content-security-policy href="https://w3c.github.io/webappsec-csp/#content-security-policy-object" id=pragma-directives:content-security-policy "Content Security Policy"
						- " on a "
						code id=pragma-directives:document {
							a href="#document" Document
						}
						- ". "
					}
				}
			}
		}
		p {
			- "When a "
			code id=pragma-directives:the-meta-element-2 {
				a href="#the-meta-element" meta
			}
			- " element is "
			a href="#insert-an-element-into-a-document" id=pragma-directives:insert-an-element-into-a-document "inserted into the document"
			- ", if its "
			code id=pragma-directives:attr-meta-http-equiv-2 {
				a href="#attr-meta-http-equiv" http-equiv
			}
			- " attribute is present and represents one of the above states, then the user agent must run the algorithm appropriate for that state, as described in the following list:"
		}
		dl {
			dt {
				dfn id=attr-meta-http-equiv-content-language "Content language state"
				- " ("
				code {
					- "http-equiv=\""
					code id=pragma-directives:attr-meta-http-equiv-keyword-content-language {
						a href="#attr-meta-http-equiv-keyword-content-language" content-language
					}
					- "\""
				}
				- ") "
			}
			dd {
				p class=note {
					- "This feature is non-conforming. Authors are encouraged to use the "
					code id=pragma-directives:attr-lang {
						a href="#attr-lang" lang
					}
					- " attribute instead."
				}
				p {
					- "This pragma sets the "
					dfn id=pragma-set-default-language "pragma-set default language"
					- ". Until such a pragma is successfully processed, there is no "
					a href="#pragma-set-default-language" id=pragma-directives:pragma-set-default-language-2 "pragma-set default language"
					- .
				}
				ol {
					li {
						p {
							- "If the "
							code id=pragma-directives:the-meta-element-3 {
								a href="#the-meta-element" meta
							}
							- " element has no "
							code id=pragma-directives:attr-meta-content {
								a href="#attr-meta-content" content
							}
							- " attribute, then return."
						}
					}
					li {
						p {
							- "If the element's "
							code id=pragma-directives:attr-meta-content-2 {
								a href="#attr-meta-content" content
							}
							- " attribute contains a U+002C COMMA character (,) then return."
						}
					}
					li {
						p {
							- "Let "
							var input
							- " be the value of the element's "
							code id=pragma-directives:attr-meta-content-3 {
								a href="#attr-meta-content" content
							}
							- " attribute."
						}
					}
					li {
						p {
							- "Let "
							var position
							- " point at the first character of "
							var input
							- .
						}
					}
					li {
						p {
							a data-x-internal=skip-ascii-whitespace href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#skip-ascii-whitespace" id=pragma-directives:skip-ascii-whitespace "Skip ASCII whitespace"
							- " within "
							var input
							- " given "
							var position
							- .
						}
					}
					li {
						p {
							a data-x-internal=collect-a-sequence-of-code-points href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#collect-a-sequence-of-code-points" id=pragma-directives:collect-a-sequence-of-code-points "Collect a sequence of code points"
							- " that are not "
							a data-x-internal=space-characters href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ascii-whitespace" id=pragma-directives:space-characters "ASCII whitespace"
							- " from "
							var input
							- " given "
							var position
							- .
						}
					}
					li {
						p {
							- "Let "
							var candidate
							- " be the string that resulted from the previous step."
						}
					}
					li {
						p {
							- "If "
							var candidate
							- " is the empty string, return."
						}
					}
					li {
						p {
							- "Set the "
							a href="#pragma-set-default-language" id=pragma-directives:pragma-set-default-language-3 "pragma-set default language"
							- " to "
							var candidate
							- .
						}
						p class=note "If the value consists of multiple space-separated tokens, tokens after the first are ignored."
					}
				}
				p class=note {
					- "This pragma is almost, but not quite, entirely unlike the HTTP `"
					code id=pragma-directives:http-content-language {
						a data-x-internal=http-content-language href="https://httpwg.org/specs/rfc7231.html#header.content-language" Content-Language
					}
					- "` header of the same name. "
					a href="#refsHTTP" "[HTTP]"
				}
			}
			dt {
				dfn id=attr-meta-http-equiv-content-type "Encoding declaration state"
				- " ("
				code {
					- "http-equiv=\""
					code id=pragma-directives:attr-meta-http-equiv-keyword-content-type {
						a href="#attr-meta-http-equiv-keyword-content-type" content-type
					}
					- "\""
				}
				- ") "
			}
			dd {
				p {
					- "The "
					a href="#attr-meta-http-equiv-content-type" id=pragma-directives:attr-meta-http-equiv-content-type-2 "Encoding declaration state"
					- " is just an alternative form of setting the "
					code id=pragma-directives:attr-meta-charset-2 {
						a href="#attr-meta-charset" charset
					}
					- " attribute: it is a "
					a href="#character-encoding-declaration" id=pragma-directives:character-encoding-declaration "character encoding declaration"
					- ". This state's user agent requirements are all handled by the parsing section of the specification."
				}
				p {
					- "For "
					code id=pragma-directives:the-meta-element-4 {
						a href="#the-meta-element" meta
					}
					- " elements with an "
					code id=pragma-directives:attr-meta-http-equiv-3 {
						a href="#attr-meta-http-equiv" http-equiv
					}
					- " attribute in the "
					a href="#attr-meta-http-equiv-content-type" id=pragma-directives:attr-meta-http-equiv-content-type-3 "Encoding declaration state"
					- ", the "
					code id=pragma-directives:attr-meta-content-4 {
						a href="#attr-meta-content" content
					}
					- " attribute must have a value that is an "
					a data-x-internal=ascii-case-insensitive href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ascii-case-insensitive" id=pragma-directives:ascii-case-insensitive "ASCII case-insensitive"
					- " match for a string that consists of: \""
					code "text/html;"
					- "\", optionally followed by any number of "
					a data-x-internal=space-characters href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ascii-whitespace" id=pragma-directives:space-characters-2 "ASCII whitespace"
					- ", followed by \""
