		p {
			- "The "
			code id=the-nav-element:the-nav-element {
				a href="#the-nav-element" nav
			}
			- " element "
			a href="#represents" id=the-nav-element:represents represents
			- " a section of a page that links to other pages or to parts within the page: a section with navigation links."
		}
		p class=note {
			- "Not all groups of links on a page need to be in a "
			code id=the-nav-element:the-nav-element-2 {
				a href="#the-nav-element" nav
			}
			- " element — the element is primarily intended for sections that consist of major navigation blocks. In particular, it is common for footers to have a short list of links to various pages of a site, such as the terms of service, the home page, and a copyright page. The "
			code id=the-nav-element:the-footer-element {
				a href="#the-footer-element" footer
			}
			- " element alone is sufficient for such cases; while a "
			code id=the-nav-element:the-nav-element-3 {
				a href="#the-nav-element" nav
			}
			- " element can be used in such cases, it is usually unnecessary."
		}
		p class=note "User agents (such as screen readers) that are targeted at users who can benefit from navigation information being omitted in the initial rendering, or who can benefit from navigation information being immediately available, can use this element as a way to determine what content on the page to initially skip or provide on request (or both)."
