		div class=example {
			p {
				- "A "
				code id=the-nav-element:the-nav-element-5 {
					a href="#the-nav-element" nav
				}
				- " element doesn't have to contain a list, it can contain other kinds of content as well. In this navigation block, links are provided in prose:"
			}
			pre {
				code class=html {
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" nav
					c- p="" >
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" h1
					c- p="" >
					- Navigation
					c- p="" "</"
					c- f="" h1
					c- p="" >
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" p
					c- p="" >
					- "You are on my home page. To the north lies "
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" a
					c- e="" href
					c- o="" "="
					c- s="" "\"/blog\""
					c- p="" >
					- "my blog"
					c- p="" "</"
					c- f="" a
					c- p="" >
					- ", from whence the sounds of battle can be heard. To the east you can see a large mountain, upon which many "
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" a
					c- e="" href
					c- o="" "="
					c- s="" "\"/school\""
					c- p="" >
					- "school papers"
					c- p="" "</"
					c- f="" a
					c- p="" >
					- " are littered. Far up thus mountain you can spy a little figure who appears to be me, desperately scribbling a "
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" a
					c- e="" href
					c- o="" "="
					c- s="" "\"/school/thesis\""
					c- p="" >
					- thesis
					c- p="" "</"
					c- f="" a
					c- p="" >
					- .
					c- p="" "</"
					c- f="" p
					c- p="" >
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" p
					c- p="" >
					- "To the west are several exits. One fun-looking exit is labeled "
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" a
					c- e="" href
					c- o="" "="
					c- s="" "\"https://games.example.com/\""
					c- p="" >
					- "\"games\""
					c- p="" "</"
					c- f="" a
					c- p="" >
					- ". Another more boring-looking exit is labeled "
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" a
					c- e="" href
					c- o="" "="
					c- s="" "\"https://isp.example.net/\""
					c- p="" >
					- ISP™
					c- p="" "</"
					c- f="" a
					c- p="" >
					- .
					c- p="" "</"
					c- f="" p
					c- p="" >
					c- p="" <
