		p class=note "While paragraphs are usually represented in visual media by blocks of text that are physically separated from adjacent blocks through blank lines, a style sheet or user agent would be equally justified in presenting paragraph breaks in a different manner, for instance using inline pilcrows (¶)."
		div class=example {
			p "The following examples are conforming HTML fragments:"
			pre {
				code class=html {
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" p
