					c- p="" ><
					c- f="" mark
					c- p="" >
					- "A wormhole in normal conditions can be held open for a maximum of just under 39 minutes."
					c- p="" "</"
					c- f="" mark
					c- p="" >
					- " Conditions that can increase the time include a powerful energy source coupled to one or both of the gates connecting the wormhole, and a large gravity well (such as a black hole)."
					c- p="" "</"
					c- f="" p
					c- p="" >
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" p
					c- p="" ><
					c- f="" mark
					c- p="" >
					- "Momentum is preserved across the wormhole. Electromagnetic radiation can travel in both directions through a wormhole, but matter cannot."
					c- p="" "</"
					c- f="" mark
					c- p="" "></"
					c- f="" p
					c- p="" >
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" p
					c- p="" >
					- "When a wormhole is created, a vortex normally forms. "
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" strong
					c- p="" >
					- "Warning: The vortex caused by the wormhole opening will annihilate anything in its path."
					c- p="" "</"
					c- f="" strong
					c- p="" >
					- " Vortexes can be avoided when using sufficiently advanced dialing technology."
					c- p="" "</"
					c- f="" p
					c- p="" >
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" p
					c- p="" ><
					c- f="" mark
					c- p="" >
					- "An obstruction in a gate will prevent it from accepting a wormhole connection."
					c- p="" "</"
					c- f="" mark
					c- p="" "></"
					c- f="" p
					c- p="" >
				}
			}
		}
