		p "The specified resource is an icon representing the page or site, and should be used by the user agent when representing the page in the user interface."
		p {
			- "Icons could be auditory icons, visual icons, or other kinds of icons. If multiple icons are provided, the user agent must select the most appropriate icon according to the "
			code id=rel-icon:attr-link-type {
				a href="#attr-link-type" type
			}
			- ", "
			code id=rel-icon:attr-link-media {
				a href="#attr-link-media" media
			}
			- ", and "
			code id=rel-icon:attr-link-sizes {
				a href="#attr-link-sizes" sizes
			}
			- " attributes. If there are multiple equally appropriate icons, user agents must use the last one declared in "
			a data-x-internal=tree-order href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-tree-order" id=rel-icon:tree-order "tree order"
			- " at the time that the user agent collected the list of icons. If the user agent tries to use an icon but that icon is determined, upon closer examination, to in fact be inappropriate (e.g. because it uses an unsupported format), then the user agent must try the next-most-appropriate icon as determined by the attributes."
		}
		p class=note "User agents are not required to update icons when the list of icons changes, but are encouraged to do so."
		p {
			- "There is no default type for resources given by the "
			code id=rel-icon:rel-icon-2 {
				a href="#rel-icon" icon
			}
			- " keyword. However, for the purposes of "
			a href="#concept-link-type-sniffing" "determining the type of the resource"
			- ", user agents must expect the resource to be an image."
		}
		p {
			- "The "
			code id=rel-icon:attr-link-sizes-2 {
				a href="#attr-link-sizes" sizes
			}
			- " keywords represent icon sizes in raw pixels (as opposed to "
			a data-x-internal='px' href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-values/#px" id=rel-icon:'px' "CSS pixels"
			- ")."
		}
		p class=note {
			- "An icon that is 50 "
			a data-x-internal='px' href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-values/#px" id=rel-icon:'px'-2 "CSS pixels"
			- " wide intended for displays with a device pixel density of two device pixels per "
			a data-x-internal='px' href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-values/#px" id=rel-icon:'px'-3 "CSS pixel"
			- " (2x, 192dpi) would have a width of 100 raw pixels. This feature does not support indicating that a different resource is to be used for small high-resolution icons vs large low-resolution icons (e.g. 50×50 2x vs 100×100 1x)."
		}
		p {
			- "To parse and process the attribute's value, the user agent must first "
			a data-x-internal=split-a-string-on-spaces href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#split-on-ascii-whitespace" id=rel-icon:split-a-string-on-spaces "split the attribute's value on ASCII whitespace"
			- ", and must then parse each resulting keyword to determine what it represents."
		}
		p {
			- "The "
			dfn id=attr-link-sizes-any {
				code any
			}
			- " keyword represents that the resource contains a scalable icon, e.g. as provided by an SVG image."
