						code id=other-link-types:the-area-element-5 {
							a href="#the-area-element" area
						}
						- " elements; it "
						a href="#hyperlink-annotation" id=other-link-types:hyperlink-annotation annotates
						- " other "
						a href="#hyperlink" id=other-link-types:hyperlink-3 hyperlinks
						- " created by the element."
					}
				}
			}
			dt {
				- "Effect on... "
				code id=other-link-types:the-form-element {
					a href="#the-form-element" form
				}
			}
			dd {
				p "One of the following:"
				dl {
					dt "Not allowed"
					dd {
						- "The keyword must not be specified on "
						code id=other-link-types:the-form-element-2 {
							a href="#the-form-element" form
						}
						- " elements."
					}
					dt Hyperlink
					dd {
						- "The keyword may be specified on "
						code id=other-link-types:the-form-element-3 {
							a href="#the-form-element" form
						}
						- " elements; it creates a "
						a href="#hyperlink" id=other-link-types:hyperlink-4 hyperlink
						- .
					}
					dt "External Resource"
					dd {
						- "The keyword may be specified on "
						code id=other-link-types:the-form-element-4 {
							a href="#the-form-element" form
						}
						- " elements; it creates an "
						a href="#external-resource-link" id=other-link-types:external-resource-link-3 "external resource link"
						- .
					}
					dt "Hyperlink Annotation"
					dd {
						- "The keyword may be specified on "
						code id=other-link-types:the-form-element-5 {
							a href="#the-form-element" form
						}
						- " elements; it "
						a href="#hyperlink-annotation" id=other-link-types:hyperlink-annotation-2 annotates
						- " other "
						a href="#hyperlink" id=other-link-types:hyperlink-5 hyperlinks
						- " created by the element."
					}
				}
			}
			dt "Brief description"
			dd {
				p "A short non-normative description of what the keyword's meaning is."
			}
			dt Specification
			dd {
				p "A link to a more detailed description of the keyword's semantics and requirements. It could be another page on the wiki, or a link to an external page."
			}
			dt Synonyms
			dd {
				p "A list of other keyword values that have exactly the same processing requirements. Authors should not use the values defined to be synonyms, they are only intended to allow user agents to support legacy content. Anyone may remove synonyms that are not used in practice; only names that need to be processed as synonyms for compatibility with legacy content are to be registered in this way."
			}
			dt Status
			dd {
				p "One of the following:"
				dl {
					dt Proposed
					dd "The keyword has not received wide peer review and approval. Someone has proposed it and is, or soon will be, using it."
					dt Ratified
					dd "The keyword has received wide peer review and approval. It has a specification that unambiguously defines how to handle pages that use the keyword, including when they use it in incorrect ways."
					dt Discontinued
					dd "The keyword has received wide peer review and it has been found wanting. Existing pages are using this keyword, but new pages should avoid it. The \"brief description\" and \"specification\" entries will give details of what authors should use instead, if anything."
				}
				p "If a keyword is found to be redundant with existing values, it should be removed and listed as a synonym for the existing value."
				p "If a keyword is registered in the \"proposed\" state for a period of a month or more without being used or specified, then it may be removed from the registry."
				p "If a keyword is added with the \"proposed\" status and found to be redundant with existing values, it should be removed and listed as a synonym for the existing value. If a keyword is added with the \"proposed\" status and found to be harmful, then it should be changed to \"discontinued\" status."
				p "Anyone can change the status at any time, but should only do so in accordance with the definitions above."
			}
		}
		p {
			- "Conformance checkers must use the information given on the "
			span "microformats page for existing rel values"
			- " to establish if a value is allowed or not: values defined in this specification or marked as \"proposed\" or \"ratified\" must be accepted when used on the elements for which they apply as described in the \"Effect on...\" field, whereas values marked as \"discontinued\" or not listed in either this specification or on the aforementioned page must be rejected as invalid. Conformance checkers may cache this information (e.g. for performance reasons or to avoid the use of unreliable network connectivity)."
		}
		p "When an author uses a new type not defined by either this specification or the wiki page, conformance checkers should offer to add the value to the wiki, with the details described above, with the \"proposed\" status."
		p {
			- "Types defined as extensions in the "
			a href="https://microformats.org/wiki/existing-rel-values#HTML5_link_type_extensions" "microformats page for existing rel values"
			- " with the status \"proposed\" or \"ratified\" may be used with the "
			code rel
			- " attribute on "
			code id=other-link-types:the-link-element-5 {
				a href="#the-link-element" link
			}
			- ", "
			code id=other-link-types:the-a-element-6 {
				a href="#the-a-element" a
			}
			- ", and "
			code id=other-link-types:the-area-element-6 {
				a href="#the-area-element" area
			}
			- " elements in accordance to the \"Effect on...\" field. "
			a href="#refsMFREL" "[MFREL]"
		}
