		}
		hr
		p {
			- "The "
			code id=adaptive-images:the-img-element-2 {
				a href="#the-img-element" img
			}
			- " element is used with the "
			code id=adaptive-images:attr-img-src {
				a href="#attr-img-src" src
			}
			- " attribute, which gives the URL of the image to use for legacy user agents that do not support the "
			code id=adaptive-images:the-picture-element-3 {
				a href="#the-picture-element" picture
			}
			- " element. This leads to a question of which image to provide in the "
			code id=adaptive-images:attr-img-src-2 {
				a href="#attr-img-src" src
			}
			- " attribute."
		}
		p "If the author wants the biggest image in legacy user agents, the markup could be as follows:"
		pre {
			code class=html {
				c- p="" <
				c- f="" picture
				c- p="" >
				c- p="" <
				c- f="" source
				c- e="" srcset
				c- o="" "="
				c- s="" "\"pear-mobile.jpeg\""
				c- e="" media
				c- o="" "="
				c- s="" "\"(max-width: 720px)\""
				c- p="" >
				c- p="" <
				c- f="" source
				c- e="" srcset
				c- o="" "="
				c- s="" "\"pear-tablet.jpeg\""
				c- e="" media
				c- o="" "="
				c- s="" "\"(max-width: 1280px)\""
				c- p="" >
				c- p="" <
				c- f="" img
				c- e="" src
				c- o="" "="
				c- s="" "\"pear-desktop.jpeg\""
				c- e="" alt
				c- o="" "="
				c- s="" "\"The pear is juicy.\""
				c- p="" >
				c- p="" "</"
				c- f="" picture
				c- p="" >
			}
		}
		p {
			- "However, if legacy mobile user agents are more important, one can list all three images in the "
			code id=adaptive-images:the-source-element {
				a href="#the-source-element" source
			}
			- " elements, overriding the "
			code id=adaptive-images:attr-img-src-3 {
				a href="#attr-img-src" src
			}
			- " attribute entirely."
		}
		pre {
			code class=html {
				c- p="" <
				c- f="" picture
				c- p="" >
				c- p="" <
				c- f="" source
				c- e="" srcset
				c- o="" "="
				c- s="" "\"pear-mobile.jpeg\""
				c- e="" media
				c- o="" "="
				c- s="" "\"(max-width: 720px)\""
				c- p="" >
				c- p="" <
				c- f="" source
				c- e="" srcset
				c- o="" "="
				c- s="" "\"pear-tablet.jpeg\""
				c- e="" media
				c- o="" "="
				c- s="" "\"(max-width: 1280px)\""
				c- p="" >
				c- p="" <
				c- f="" source
				c- e="" srcset
				c- o="" "="
				c- s="" "\"pear-desktop.jpeg\""
				c- p="" >
				c- p="" <
				c- f="" img
				c- e="" src
				c- o="" "="
				c- s="" "\"pear-mobile.jpeg\""
				c- e="" alt
				c- o="" "="
				c- s="" "\"The pear is juicy.\""
				c- p="" >
				c- p="" "</"
				c- f="" picture
				c- p="" >
			}
		}
		p {
			- "Since at this point the "
			code id=adaptive-images:attr-img-src-4 {
				a href="#attr-img-src" src
			}
			- " attribute is actually being ignored entirely by "
			code id=adaptive-images:the-picture-element-4 {
				a href="#the-picture-element" picture
			}
			- "-supporting user agents, the "
			code id=adaptive-images:attr-img-src-5 {
				a href="#attr-img-src" src
			}
			- " attribute can default to any image, including one that is neither the smallest nor biggest:"
		}
		pre {
			code class=html {
				c- p="" <
				c- f="" picture
				c- p="" >
				c- p="" <
				c- f="" source
				c- e="" srcset
				c- o="" "="
				c- s="" "\"pear-mobile.jpeg\""
				c- e="" media
