		p class=note "This allows servers to return images with error responses, and have them displayed."
		p id=img-determine-type {
			- "The user agent should apply the "
			a data-x-internal=content-type-sniffing:-image href="https://mimesniff.spec.whatwg.org/#rules-for-sniffing-images-specifically" id=images-processing-model:content-type-sniffing:-image "image sniffing rules"
			- " to determine the type of the image, with the image's "
			a href="#content-type" id=images-processing-model:content-type "associated Content-Type headers"
			- " giving the "
			var "official type"
			- ". If these rules are not applied, then the type of the image must be the type given by the image's "
			a href="#content-type" id=images-processing-model:content-type-2 "associated Content-Type headers"
			- .
		}
		p {
			- "User agents must not support non-image resources with the "
			code id=images-processing-model:the-img-element-11 {
				a href="#the-img-element" img
			}
			- " element (e.g. XML files whose "
			a data-x-internal=document-element href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#document-element" id=images-processing-model:document-element "document element"
			- " is an HTML element). User agents must not run executable code (e.g. scripts) embedded in the image resource. User agents must only display the first page of a multipage resource (e.g. a PDF file). User agents must not allow the resource to act in an interactive fashion, but should honour any animation in the resource."
		}
		p "This specification does not specify which image types are to be supported."
		h6 id=when-to-obtain-images {
			span class=secno "4.8.4.3.1"
			- " When to obtain images"
			a class=self-link href="#when-to-obtain-images"
		}
		p "By default, images are obtained immediately. User agents may provide users with the option to instead obtain them on-demand. (The on-demand option might be used by bandwidth-constrained users, for example.)"
		p {
			- "When obtaining images immediately, the user agent must synchronously "
			a href="#update-the-image-data" id=when-to-obtain-images:update-the-image-data "update the image data"
			- " of the "
			code id=when-to-obtain-images:the-img-element {
				a href="#the-img-element" img
			}
			- " element, with the "
			i "restart animation"
			- " flag set if so stated, whenever that element is created or has experienced "
			a href="#relevant-mutations" id=when-to-obtain-images:relevant-mutations "relevant mutations"
			- .
		}
		p {
			- "When obtaining images on demand, the user agent must "
			a href="#update-the-image-data" id=when-to-obtain-images:update-the-image-data-2 "update the image data"
			- " of an "
			code id=when-to-obtain-images:the-img-element-2 {
				a href="#the-img-element" img
			}
			- " element whenever it needs the image data (i.e., on demand), but only if the "
			code id=when-to-obtain-images:the-img-element-3 {
				a href="#the-img-element" img
			}
			- " element's "
			a href="#current-request" id=when-to-obtain-images:current-request "current request"
			- "'s "
			a href="#img-req-state" id=when-to-obtain-images:img-req-state state
			- " is "
			a href="#img-none" id=when-to-obtain-images:img-none unavailable
			- ". When an "
			code id=when-to-obtain-images:the-img-element-4 {
				a href="#the-img-element" img
			}
			- " element has experienced "
			a href="#relevant-mutations" id=when-to-obtain-images:relevant-mutations-2 "relevant mutations"
			- ", if the user agent only obtains images on demand, the "
			code id=when-to-obtain-images:the-img-element-5 {
				a href="#the-img-element" img
			}
			- " element's "
			a href="#current-request" id=when-to-obtain-images:current-request-2 "current request"
			- "'s "
			a href="#img-req-state" id=when-to-obtain-images:img-req-state-2 state
			- " must return to "
			a href="#img-none" id=when-to-obtain-images:img-none-2 unavailable
			- .
		}
		h6 id=reacting-to-dom-mutations {
			span class=secno "4.8.4.3.2"
			- " Reacting to DOM mutations"
			a class=self-link href="#reacting-to-dom-mutations"
		}
		p {
			- "The "
			dfn id=relevant-mutations "relevant mutations"
			- " for an "
			code id=reacting-to-dom-mutations:the-img-element {
				a href="#the-img-element" img
			}
			- " element are as follows:"
		}
		ul {
			li {
				p {
					- "The element's "
					code id=reacting-to-dom-mutations:attr-img-src {
						a href="#attr-img-src" src
					}
					- ", "
					code id=reacting-to-dom-mutations:attr-img-srcset {
						a href="#attr-img-srcset" srcset
					}
					- ", "
					code id=reacting-to-dom-mutations:attr-dim-width {
						a href="#attr-dim-width" width
					}
					- ", or "
					code id=reacting-to-dom-mutations:attr-img-sizes {
						a href="#attr-img-sizes" sizes
					}
					- " attributes are set, changed, or removed."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "The element's "
					code id=reacting-to-dom-mutations:attr-img-src-2 {
						a href="#attr-img-src" src
					}
					- " attribute is set to the same value as the previous value. This must set the "
					i "restart animation"
					- " flag for the "
					a href="#update-the-image-data" id=reacting-to-dom-mutations:update-the-image-data "update the image data"
					- " algorithm."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "The element's "
					code id=reacting-to-dom-mutations:attr-img-crossorigin {
						a href="#attr-img-crossorigin" crossorigin
					}
					- " attribute's state is changed."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "The element's "
					code id=reacting-to-dom-mutations:attr-img-referrerpolicy {
						a href="#attr-img-referrerpolicy" referrerpolicy
					}
					- " attribute's state is changed."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "The "
					code id=reacting-to-dom-mutations:the-img-element-2 {
						a href="#the-img-element" img
					}
					- " or "
					code id=reacting-to-dom-mutations:the-source-element {
						a href="#the-source-element" source
					}
					a href="#html-element-insertion-steps" id=reacting-to-dom-mutations:html-element-insertion-steps "HTML element insertion steps"
					- " or "
					a href="#html-element-removing-steps" id=reacting-to-dom-mutations:html-element-removing-steps "HTML element removing steps"
					- " count the mutation as a "
					a href="#relevant-mutations" id=reacting-to-dom-mutations:relevant-mutations "relevant mutation"
					- .
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "The element's parent is a "
					code id=reacting-to-dom-mutations:the-picture-element {
						a href="#the-picture-element" picture
					}
					- " element and a "
					code id=reacting-to-dom-mutations:the-source-element-2 {
						a href="#the-source-element" source
					}
					- " element that is a previous sibling has its "
					code id=reacting-to-dom-mutations:attr-source-srcset {
						a href="#attr-source-srcset" srcset
					}
					- ", "
					code id=reacting-to-dom-mutations:attr-source-sizes {
						a href="#attr-source-sizes" sizes
					}
					- ", "
					code id=reacting-to-dom-mutations:attr-source-media {
						a href="#attr-source-media" media
					}
					- ", "
					code id=reacting-to-dom-mutations:attr-source-type {
						a href="#attr-source-type" type
					}
					- ", "
					code id=reacting-to-dom-mutations:attr-dim-width-2 {
						a href="#attr-dim-width" width
					}
					- " or "
					code id=reacting-to-dom-mutations:attr-dim-height {
						a href="#attr-dim-height" height
					}
					- " attributes set, changed, or removed."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "The element's "
					a data-x-internal=concept-node-adopt-ext href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-node-adopt-ext" id=reacting-to-dom-mutations:concept-node-adopt-ext "adopting steps"
					- " are run."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "If the element "
					a href="#allows-auto-sizes" id=reacting-to-dom-mutations:allows-auto-sizes "allows auto-sizes"
					- ": the element starts or stops "
					a href="#being-rendered" id=reacting-to-dom-mutations:being-rendered "being rendered"
					- ", or its "
					a data-x-internal=concrete-object-size href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-images/#concrete-object-size" id=reacting-to-dom-mutations:concrete-object-size "concrete object size"
					- " width changes. This must set the "
					i "maybe omit events"
					- " flag for the "
					a href="#update-the-image-data" id=reacting-to-dom-mutations:update-the-image-data-2 "update the image data"
					- " algorithm."
				}
			}
		}
		h6 id=the-list-of-available-images {
			span class=secno "4.8.4.3.3"
			- " The list of available images"
			a class=self-link href="#the-list-of-available-images"
		}
		p {
			- "Each "
			code id=the-list-of-available-images:document {
				a href="#document" Document
			}
			- " object must have a "
			dfn id=list-of-available-images "list of available images"
			- ". Each image in this list is identified by a tuple consisting of an "
			a data-x-internal=absolute-url href="https://url.spec.whatwg.org/#syntax-url-absolute" id=the-list-of-available-images:absolute-url "absolute URL"
			- ", a "
			a href="#cors-settings-attribute" id=the-list-of-available-images:cors-settings-attribute "CORS settings attribute"
			- " mode, and, if the mode is not "
			a href="#attr-crossorigin-none" id=the-list-of-available-images:attr-crossorigin-none "No CORS"
			- ", an "
			a href="#concept-origin" id=the-list-of-available-images:concept-origin origin
			- ". Each image furthermore has an "
			dfn id=ignore-higher-layer-caching "ignore higher-layer caching"
			- " flag. User agents may copy entries from one "
			code id=the-list-of-available-images:document-2 {
				a href="#document" Document
			}
			- " object's "
			a href="#list-of-available-images" id=the-list-of-available-images:list-of-available-images "list of available images"
			- " to another at any time (e.g. when the "
			code id=the-list-of-available-images:document-3 {
				a href="#document" Document
			}
			- " is created, user agents can add to it all the images that are loaded in other "
			code id=the-list-of-available-images:document-4 {
				a href="#document" Document
			}
			- "s), but must not change the keys of entries copied in this way when doing so, and must unset the "
			a href="#ignore-higher-layer-caching" id=the-list-of-available-images:ignore-higher-layer-caching "ignore higher-layer caching"
			- " flag for the copied entry. User agents may also remove images from such lists at any time (e.g. to save memory). User agents must remove entries in the "
			a href="#list-of-available-images" id=the-list-of-available-images:list-of-available-images-2 "list of available images"
			- " as appropriate given higher-layer caching semantics for the resource (e.g. the HTTP `"
			code id=the-list-of-available-images:http-cache-control {
				a data-x-internal=http-cache-control href="https://httpwg.org/specs/rfc7234.html#header.cache-control" Cache-Control
			}
			- "` response header) when the "
			a href="#ignore-higher-layer-caching" id=the-list-of-available-images:ignore-higher-layer-caching-2 "ignore higher-layer caching"
			- " flag is unset."
		}
		p class=note {
			- "The "
			a href="#list-of-available-images" id=the-list-of-available-images:list-of-available-images-3 "list of available images"
			- " is intended to enable synchronous switching when changing the "
			code id=the-list-of-available-images:attr-img-src {
				a href="#attr-img-src" src
			}
			- " attribute to a URL that has previously been loaded, and to avoid re-downloading images in the same document even when they don't allow caching per HTTP. It is not used to avoid re-downloading the same image while the previous image is still loading."
		}
		p class=note {
			- "The user agent can also store the image data separately from the "
			a href="#list-of-available-images" id=the-list-of-available-images:list-of-available-images-4 "list of available images"
			- .
		}
		p class=example {
			- "For example, if a resource has the HTTP response header `"
			code "Cache-Control: must-revalidate"
			- "`, and its "
			a href="#ignore-higher-layer-caching" id=the-list-of-available-images:ignore-higher-layer-caching-3 "ignore higher-layer caching"
			- " flag is unset, the user agent would remove it from the "
			a href="#list-of-available-images" id=the-list-of-available-images:list-of-available-images-5 "list of available images"
			- " but could keep the image data separately, and use that if the server responds with a "
			code "304 Not Modified"
			- " status."
		}
		h6 id=decoding-images {
			span class=secno "4.8.4.3.4"
			- " Decoding images"
			a class=self-link href="#decoding-images"
		}
		p {
			- "Image data is usually encoded in order to reduce file size. This means that in order for the user agent to present the image to the screen, the data needs to be decoded. "
			dfn id=img-decoding-process Decoding
			- " is the process which converts an image's media data into a bitmap form, suitable for presentation to the screen. Note that this process can be slow relative to other processes involved in presenting content. Thus, the user agent can choose when to perform decoding, in order to create the best user experience."
		}
		p "Image decoding is said to be synchronous if it prevents presentation of other content until it is finished. Typically, this has an effect of atomically presenting the image and any other content at the same time. However, this presentation is delayed by the amount of time it takes to perform the decode."
		p "Image decoding is said to be asynchronous if it does not prevent presentation of other content. This has an effect of presenting non-image content faster. However, the image content is missing on screen until the decode finishes. Once the decode is finished, the screen is updated with the image."
		p "In both synchronous and asynchronous decoding modes, the final content is presented to screen after the same amount of time has elapsed. The main difference is whether the user agent presents non-image content ahead of presenting the final content."
		p {
			- "In order to aid the user agent in deciding whether to perform synchronous or asynchronous decode, the "
			code id=decoding-images:attr-img-decoding {
				a href="#attr-img-decoding" decoding
			}
			- " attribute can be set on "
			code id=decoding-images:the-img-element {
				a href="#the-img-element" img
			}
			- " elements. The possible values of the "
			code id=decoding-images:attr-img-decoding-2 {
				a href="#attr-img-decoding" decoding
			}
			- " attribute are the following "
			dfn id=image-decoding-hint "image decoding hint"
			- " keywords:"
		}
		table {
			thead {
				tr {
					th "Keyword "
					th "State "
					th "Description "
				}
			}
			tbody {
				tr {
					td {
						dfn data-dfn-for="img/decoding" data-dfn-type=attr-value id=attr-img-decoding-sync {
							code sync
						}
					}
					td {
						dfn id=attr-img-decoding-sync-state Sync
					}
					td {
						- "Indicates a preference to "
						a href="#img-decoding-process" id=decoding-images:img-decoding-process decode
						- " this image synchronously for atomic presentation with other content. "
					}
				}
				tr {
					td {
						dfn data-dfn-for="img/decoding" data-dfn-type=attr-value id=attr-img-decoding-async {
							code async
						}
					}
					td {
						dfn id=attr-img-decoding-async-state Async
					}
					td {
						- "Indicates a preference to "
						a href="#img-decoding-process" id=decoding-images:img-decoding-process-2 decode
						- " this image asynchronously to avoid delaying presentation of other content. "
					}
				}
				tr {
					td {
						dfn data-dfn-for="img/decoding" data-dfn-type=attr-value id=attr-img-decoding-auto {
							code auto
						}
					}
					td {
						dfn id=attr-img-decoding-auto-state Auto
					}
					td "Indicates no preference in decoding mode (the default). "
				}
			}
		}
		p {
			- "When "
			a href="#img-decoding-process" id=decoding-images:img-decoding-process-3 decoding
			- " an image, the user agent should respect the preference indicated by the "
			code id=decoding-images:attr-img-decoding-3 {
				a href="#attr-img-decoding" decoding
			}
			- " attribute's state. If the state indicated is "
			a href="#attr-img-decoding-auto-state" id=decoding-images:attr-img-decoding-auto-state auto
			- ", then the user agent is free to choose any decoding behavior."
		}
		p class=note {
			- "It is also possible to control the decoding behavior using the "
			code id=decoding-images:dom-img-decode {
				a href="#dom-img-decode" "decode()"
			}
			- " method. Since the "
			code id=decoding-images:dom-img-decode-2 {
				a href="#dom-img-decode" "decode()"
			}
			- " method performs "
			a href="#img-decoding-process" id=decoding-images:img-decoding-process-4 decoding
			- " independently from the process responsible for presenting content to screen, it is unaffected by the "
			code id=decoding-images:attr-img-decoding-4 {
				a href="#attr-img-decoding" decoding
			}
			- " attribute."
		}
		h6 id=updating-the-image-data {
			span class=secno "4.8.4.3.5"
			- " Updating the image data"
			a class=self-link href="#updating-the-image-data"
		}
		p class=note {
			- "This algorithm cannot be called from steps running "
			a href="#in-parallel" id=updating-the-image-data:in-parallel "in parallel"
			- ". If a user agent needs to call this algorithm from steps running "
			a href="#in-parallel" id=updating-the-image-data:in-parallel-2 "in parallel"
			- ", it needs to "
			a href="#queue-a-task" id=updating-the-image-data:queue-a-task queue
			- " a task to do so."
		}
		p {
			- "When the user agent is to "
			dfn id=update-the-image-data "update the image data"
			- " of an "
			code id=updating-the-image-data:the-img-element {
				a href="#the-img-element" img
			}
			- " element, optionally with the "
			i "restart animations"
			- " flag set, optionally with the "
			i "maybe omit events"
			- " flag set, it must run the following steps:"
		}
		ol {
			li {
				p {
					- "If the element's "
					a data-x-internal=node-document href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-node-document" id=updating-the-image-data:node-document "node document"
					- " is not "
					a href="#fully-active" id=updating-the-image-data:fully-active "fully active"
					- ", then:"
				}
				ol {
					li {
						p {
							- "Continue running this algorithm "
							a href="#in-parallel" id=updating-the-image-data:in-parallel-3 "in parallel"
							- .
						}
					}
					li {
						p {
							- "Wait until the element's "
							a data-x-internal=node-document href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-node-document" id=updating-the-image-data:node-document-2 "node document"
							- " is "
							a href="#fully-active" id=updating-the-image-data:fully-active-2 "fully active"
							- .
						}
					}
					li {
						p {
							- "If another instance of this algorithm for this "
							code id=updating-the-image-data:the-img-element-2 {
								a href="#the-img-element" img
							}
							- " element was started after this instance (even if it aborted and is no longer running), then return."
						}
					}
					li {
						p {
							a href="#queue-a-microtask" id=updating-the-image-data:queue-a-microtask "Queue a microtask"
							- " to continue this algorithm."
						}
					}
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "If the user agent cannot support images, or its support for images has been disabled, then "
					a href="#abort-the-image-request" id=updating-the-image-data:abort-the-image-request "abort the image request"
					- " for the "
					a href="#current-request" id=updating-the-image-data:current-request "current request"
					- " and the "
					a href="#pending-request" id=updating-the-image-data:pending-request "pending request"
					- ", set "
					a href="#current-request" id=updating-the-image-data:current-request-2 "current request"
					- "'s "
					a href="#img-req-state" id=updating-the-image-data:img-req-state state
					- " to "
					a href="#img-none" id=updating-the-image-data:img-none unavailable
					- ", set "
					a href="#pending-request" id=updating-the-image-data:pending-request-2 "pending request"
					- " to null, and return."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "Let "
					var "previous URL"
					- " be the "
					a href="#current-request" id=updating-the-image-data:current-request-3 "current request"
					- "'s "
					a href="#img-req-url" id=updating-the-image-data:img-req-url "current URL"
					- .
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "Let "
					var "selected source"
					- " be null and "
					var "selected pixel density"
					- " be undefined. "
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "If the element does not "
					a href="#use-srcset-or-picture" id=updating-the-image-data:use-srcset-or-picture {
						- "use "
						code srcset
						- " or "
						code picture
					}
					- " and it has a "
					code id=updating-the-image-data:attr-img-src {
						a href="#attr-img-src" src
					}
					- " attribute specified whose value is not the empty string, then set "
					var "selected source"
					- " to the value of the element's "
					code id=updating-the-image-data:attr-img-src-2 {
						a href="#attr-img-src" src
					}
					- " attribute and set "
					var "selected pixel density"
					- " to 1.0."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "Set the element's "
					a href="#last-selected-source" id=updating-the-image-data:last-selected-source "last selected source"
					- " to "
					var "selected source"
					- .
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "If "
					var "selected source"
					- " is not null, then:"
				}
				ol {
					li {
						p {
							- "Let "
							var urlString
							- " be the result of "
							a href="#encoding-parsing-and-serializing-a-url" id=updating-the-image-data:encoding-parsing-and-serializing-a-url "encoding-parsing-and-serializing a URL"
							- " given "
							var "selected source"
							- ", relative to the element's "
							a data-x-internal=node-document href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-node-document" id=updating-the-image-data:node-document-3 "node document"
							- .
						}
					}
					li {
						p {
							- "If "
							var urlString
							- " is failure, then abort this inner set of steps."
						}
					}
					li {
						p {
							- "Let "
							var key
							- " be a tuple consisting of "
							var urlString
							- ", the "
							code id=updating-the-image-data:the-img-element-3 {
								a href="#the-img-element" img
							}
							- " element's "
							code id=updating-the-image-data:attr-img-crossorigin {
								a href="#attr-img-crossorigin" crossorigin
							}
							- " attribute's mode, and, if that mode is not "
							a href="#attr-crossorigin-none" id=updating-the-image-data:attr-crossorigin-none "No CORS"
							- ", the "
							a data-x-internal=node-document href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-node-document" id=updating-the-image-data:node-document-4 "node document"
							- "'s "
							a data-x-internal=concept-document-origin href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-document-origin" id=updating-the-image-data:concept-document-origin origin
							- .
						}
					}
					li {
						p {
							- "If the "
							a href="#list-of-available-images" id=updating-the-image-data:list-of-available-images "list of available images"
							- " contains an entry for "
							var key
							- ", then:"
						}
						ol {
							li {
								p {
									- "Set the "
									a href="#ignore-higher-layer-caching" id=updating-the-image-data:ignore-higher-layer-caching "ignore higher-layer caching"
									- " flag for that entry."
								}
							}
							li {
								p {
									a href="#abort-the-image-request" id=updating-the-image-data:abort-the-image-request-2 "Abort the image request"
									- " for the "
									a href="#current-request" id=updating-the-image-data:current-request-4 "current request"
									- " and the "
									a href="#pending-request" id=updating-the-image-data:pending-request-3 "pending request"
									- .
								}
							}
							li {
								p {
									- "Set "
									a href="#pending-request" id=updating-the-image-data:pending-request-4 "pending request"
									- " to null."
								}
							}
							li {
								p {
									- "Let "
									a href="#current-request" id=updating-the-image-data:current-request-5 "current request"
									- " be a new "
									a href="#image-request" id=updating-the-image-data:image-request "image request"
									- " whose "
									a href="#img-req-data" id=updating-the-image-data:img-req-data "image data"
									- " is that of the entry and whose "
									a href="#img-req-state" id=updating-the-image-data:img-req-state-2 state
									- " is "
									a href="#img-all" id=updating-the-image-data:img-all "completely available"
									- .
								}
							}
							li {
								p {
									a href="#prepare-an-image-for-presentation" id=updating-the-image-data:prepare-an-image-for-presentation {
										- "Prepare "
										var "current request"
										- " for presentation"
									}
									- " given "
									var img
									- .
								}
							}
							li {
								p {
									- "Set "
									a href="#current-request" id=updating-the-image-data:current-request-6 "current request"
									- "'s "
									a href="#current-pixel-density" id=updating-the-image-data:current-pixel-density "current pixel density"
									- " to "
									var "selected pixel density"
									- .
								}
							}
