					- "\", and whose "
					a data-x-internal=use-url-credentials-flag href="https://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-request-use-url-credentials-flag" id=the-video-element:use-url-credentials-flag "use-URL-credentials flag"
					- " is set. "
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					a data-x-internal=concept-fetch href="https://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-fetch" id=the-video-element:concept-fetch Fetch
					var request
					- ". This must "
					a href="#delay-the-load-event" id=the-video-element:delay-the-load-event "delay the load event"
					- " of the element's "
					a data-x-internal=node-document href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-node-document" id=the-video-element:node-document-3 "node document"
					- .
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "If an image is thus obtained, the "
					a href="#poster-frame" id=the-video-element:poster-frame-4 "poster frame"
					- " is that image. Otherwise, there is no "
					a href="#poster-frame" id=the-video-element:poster-frame-5 "poster frame"
					- .
				}
			}
		}
		p class=note {
			- "The image given by the "
			code id=the-video-element:attr-video-poster-5 {
				a href="#attr-video-poster" poster
			}
			- " attribute, the "
			i id=the-video-element:poster-frame-6 {
				a href="#poster-frame" "poster frame"
			}
			- ", is intended to be a representative frame of the video (typically one of the first non-blank frames) that gives the user an idea of what the video is like."
		}
		p {
			- "The "
			dfn data-dfn-for=video data-dfn-type=element-attr id=attr-video-playsinline {
				code playsinline
			}
			- " attribute is a "
			a href="#boolean-attribute" id=the-video-element:boolean-attribute "boolean attribute"
			- ". If present, it serves as a hint to the user agent that the video ought to be displayed \"inline\" in the document by default, constrained to the element's playback area, instead of being displayed fullscreen or in an independent resizable window."
		}
		p class=note {
			- "The absence of the "
			code id=the-video-element:attr-video-playsinline-2 {
				a href="#attr-video-playsinline" playsinline
			}
			- " attribute does not imply that the video will display fullscreen by default. Indeed, most user agents have chosen to play all videos inline by default, and in such user agents the "
			code id=the-video-element:attr-video-playsinline-3 {
				a href="#attr-video-playsinline" playsinline
			}
			- " attribute has no effect."
		}
