			- .
		}
		p {
			- "Any audio associated with the "
			a href="#media-resource" id=the-video-element:media-resource-7 "media resource"
			- " must, if played, be played synchronized with the "
			a href="#current-playback-position" id=the-video-element:current-playback-position-8 "current playback position"
			- ", at the element's "
			a href="#effective-media-volume" id=the-video-element:effective-media-volume "effective media volume"
			- ". The user agent must play the audio from audio tracks that were "
			a href="#dom-audiotrack-enabled" id=the-video-element:dom-audiotrack-enabled enabled
			- " when the "
			a href="#event-loop" id=the-video-element:event-loop-2 "event loop"
			- " last reached step 1."
		}
		p "In addition to the above, the user agent may provide messages to the user (such as \"buffering\", \"no video loaded\", \"error\", or more detailed information) by overlaying text or icons on the video or other areas of the element's playback area, or in another appropriate manner."
		p {
			- "User agents that cannot render the video may instead make the element "
			a href="#represents" id=the-video-element:represents-7 represent
			- " a link to an external video playback utility or to the video data itself."
		}
		p {
			- "When a "
			code id=the-video-element:the-video-element-19 {
				a href="#the-video-element" video
			}
			- " element's "
			a href="#media-resource" id=the-video-element:media-resource-8 "media resource"
			- " has a video channel, the element provides a "
			a data-x-internal=paint-source href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-images-4/#paint-source" id=the-video-element:paint-source "paint source"
			- " whose width is the "
			a href="#media-resource" id=the-video-element:media-resource-9 "media resource"
			- "'s "
			a href="#concept-video-intrinsic-width" id=the-video-element:concept-video-intrinsic-width "natural width"
			- ", whose height is the "
			a href="#media-resource" id=the-video-element:media-resource-10 "media resource"
			- "'s "
			a href="#concept-video-intrinsic-height" id=the-video-element:concept-video-intrinsic-height "natural height"
			- ", and whose appearance is the frame of video corresponding to the "
			a href="#current-playback-position" id=the-video-element:current-playback-position-9 "current playback position"
			- ", if that is available, or else (e.g. when the video is seeking or buffering) its previous appearance, if any, or else (e.g. because the video is still loading the first frame) blackness."
		}
