								p {
									- "User agents may allow users to selectively block or slow "
									a href="#media-data" id=loading-the-media-resource:media-data-5 "media data"
									- " downloads. When a "
									a href="#media-element" id=loading-the-media-resource:media-element-46 "media element"
									- "'s download has been blocked altogether, the user agent must act as if it was stalled (as opposed to acting as if the connection was closed). The rate of the download may also be throttled automatically by the user agent, e.g. to balance the download with other connections sharing the same bandwidth."
								}
								p id=resourceSuspend {
									- "User agents may decide to not download more content at any time, e.g. after buffering five minutes of a one hour media resource, while waiting for the user to decide whether to play the resource or not, while waiting for user input in an interactive resource, or when the user navigates away from the page. When a "
									a href="#media-element" id=loading-the-media-resource:media-element-47 "media element"
									- "'s download has been suspended, the user agent must "
									a href="#queue-a-media-element-task" id=loading-the-media-resource:queue-a-media-element-task-13 "queue a media element task"
									- " given the "
