		h5 id=ready-states {
			span class=secno "4.8.11.7"
			- " Ready states"
			a class=self-link href="#ready-states"
		}
		dl class=domintro {
			dt {
				code {
					var media
					- .
					a href="#dom-media-readystate" id=dom-media-readystate-dev readyState
				}
				div class="mdn-anno wrapped before" {
					button class=mdn-anno-btn onclick="toggleStatus(this)" {
						b class=all-engines-flag title="Support in all current engines." ✔
						span MDN
					}
					div class=feature {
						p {
							a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/HTMLMediaElement/readyState" title="The HTMLMediaElement.readyState property indicates the readiness state of the media." "HTMLMediaElement/readyState"
						}
						p class=all-engines-text "Support in all current engines."
						div class=support {
							span class="firefox yes" {
								span Firefox
								span "3.5+"
							}
							span class="safari yes" {
								span Safari
								span "3.1+"
							}
							span class="chrome yes" {
								span Chrome
								span "3+"
							}
							hr
							span class="opera yes" {
								span Opera
								span "12.1+"
							}
							span class="edge_blink yes" {
								span Edge
								span "79+"
							}
							hr
							span class="edge yes" {
								span "Edge (Legacy)"
								span "12+"
							}
							span class="ie yes" {
								span "Internet Explorer"
								span "5.5+"
							}
							hr
							span class="firefox_android unknown" {
								span "Firefox Android"
								span ?
							}
							span class="safari_ios yes" {
								span "Safari iOS"
								span "3+"
							}
							span class="chrome_android unknown" {
								span "Chrome Android"
								span ?
							}
							span class="webview_android yes" {
								span "WebView Android"
								span "37+"
							}
							span class="samsunginternet_android unknown" {
								span "Samsung Internet"
								span ?
							}
							span class="opera_android yes" {
								span "Opera Android"
								span "12.1+"
							}
						}
					}
				}
			}
			dd {
				p {
					- "Returns a value that expresses the current state of the element with respect to rendering the "
					a href="#current-playback-position" id=ready-states:current-playback-position "current playback position"
					- ", from the codes in the list below."
				}
			}
		}
		p {
			a href="#media-element" id=ready-states:media-element "Media elements"
			- " have a "
			i "ready state"
			- ", which describes to what degree they are ready to be rendered at the "
			a href="#current-playback-position" id=ready-states:current-playback-position-2 "current playback position"
			- ". The possible values are as follows; the ready state of a media element at any particular time is the greatest value describing the state of the element:"
		}
		dl {
			dt {
				dfn data-dfn-for=HTMLMediaElement data-dfn-type=const id=dom-media-have_nothing {
					code HAVE_NOTHING
				}
				- " (numeric value 0)"
			}
			dd {
				p {
					- "No information regarding the "
					a href="#media-resource" id=ready-states:media-resource "media resource"
					- " is available. No data for the "
					a href="#current-playback-position" id=ready-states:current-playback-position-3 "current playback position"
					- " is available. "
					a href="#media-element" id=ready-states:media-element-2 "Media elements"
					- " whose "
					code id=ready-states:dom-media-networkstate {
						a href="#dom-media-networkstate" networkState
					}
					- " attribute are set to "
					code id=ready-states:dom-media-network_empty {
						a href="#dom-media-network_empty" NETWORK_EMPTY
					}
					- " are always in the "
					code id=ready-states:dom-media-have_nothing {
						a href="#dom-media-have_nothing" HAVE_NOTHING
					}
					- " state."
				}
			}
			dt {
				dfn data-dfn-for=HTMLMediaElement data-dfn-type=const id=dom-media-have_metadata {
					code HAVE_METADATA
				}
				- " (numeric value 1)"
			}
			dd {
				p {
					- "Enough of the resource has been obtained that the duration of the resource is available. In the case of a "
					code id=ready-states:the-video-element {
						a href="#the-video-element" video
					}
					- " element, the dimensions of the video are also available. No "
					a href="#media-data" id=ready-states:media-data "media data"
					- " is available for the immediate "
					a href="#current-playback-position" id=ready-states:current-playback-position-4 "current playback position"
					- .
				}
			}
			dt {
				dfn data-dfn-for=HTMLMediaElement data-dfn-type=const id=dom-media-have_current_data {
					code HAVE_CURRENT_DATA
				}
				- " (numeric value 2)"
			}
			dd {
				p {
					- "Data for the immediate "
					a href="#current-playback-position" id=ready-states:current-playback-position-5 "current playback position"
					- " is available, but either not enough data is available that the user agent could successfully advance the "
					a href="#current-playback-position" id=ready-states:current-playback-position-6 "current playback position"
					- " in the "
					a href="#direction-of-playback" id=ready-states:direction-of-playback "direction of playback"
					- " at all without immediately reverting to the "
					code id=ready-states:dom-media-have_metadata {
						a href="#dom-media-have_metadata" HAVE_METADATA
					}
					- " state, or there is no more data to obtain in the "
					a href="#direction-of-playback" id=ready-states:direction-of-playback-2 "direction of playback"
					- ". For example, in video this corresponds to the user agent having data from the current frame, but not the next frame, when the "
					a href="#current-playback-position" id=ready-states:current-playback-position-7 "current playback position"
					- " is at the end of the current frame; and to when "
					a href="#ended-playback" id=ready-states:ended-playback "playback has ended"
					- .
				}
			}
			dt {
				dfn data-dfn-for=HTMLMediaElement data-dfn-type=const id=dom-media-have_future_data {
					code HAVE_FUTURE_DATA
				}
				- " (numeric value 3)"
			}
			dd {
				p {
					- "Data for the immediate "
					a href="#current-playback-position" id=ready-states:current-playback-position-8 "current playback position"
					- " is available, as well as enough data for the user agent to advance the "
					a href="#current-playback-position" id=ready-states:current-playback-position-9 "current playback position"
					- " in the "
					a href="#direction-of-playback" id=ready-states:direction-of-playback-3 "direction of playback"
					- " at least a little without immediately reverting to the "
					code id=ready-states:dom-media-have_metadata-2 {
						a href="#dom-media-have_metadata" HAVE_METADATA
					}
					- " state, and "
					a href="#the-text-tracks-are-ready" id=ready-states:the-text-tracks-are-ready "the text tracks are ready"
					- ". For example, in video this corresponds to the user agent having data for at least the current frame and the next frame when the "
					a href="#current-playback-position" id=ready-states:current-playback-position-10 "current playback position"
					- " is at the instant in time between the two frames, or to the user agent having the video data for the current frame and audio data to keep playing at least a little when the "
					a href="#current-playback-position" id=ready-states:current-playback-position-11 "current playback position"
					- " is in the middle of a frame. The user agent cannot be in this state if "
					a href="#ended-playback" id=ready-states:ended-playback-2 "playback has ended"
					- ", as the "
					a href="#current-playback-position" id=ready-states:current-playback-position-12 "current playback position"
					- " can never advance in this case."
				}
			}
			dt {
				dfn data-dfn-for=HTMLMediaElement data-dfn-type=const id=dom-media-have_enough_data {
					code HAVE_ENOUGH_DATA
				}
				- " (numeric value 4)"
			}
			dd {
				p {
					- "All the conditions described for the "
					code id=ready-states:dom-media-have_future_data {
						a href="#dom-media-have_future_data" HAVE_FUTURE_DATA
					}
					- " state are met, and, in addition, either of the following conditions is also true:"
				}
				ul {
					li {
						- "The user agent estimates that data is being fetched at a rate where the "
						a href="#current-playback-position" id=ready-states:current-playback-position-13 "current playback position"
						- ", if it were to advance at the element's "
						code id=ready-states:dom-media-playbackrate {
							a href="#dom-media-playbackrate" playbackRate
						}
						- ", would not overtake the available data before playback reaches the end of the "
						a href="#media-resource" id=ready-states:media-resource-2 "media resource"
						- .
					}
					li "The user agent has entered a state where waiting longer will not result in further data being obtained, and therefore nothing would be gained by delaying playback any further. (For example, the buffer might be full.)"
				}
			}
		}
		p class=note {
			- "In practice, the difference between "
			code id=ready-states:dom-media-have_metadata-3 {
				a href="#dom-media-have_metadata" HAVE_METADATA
			}
			- " and "
			code id=ready-states:dom-media-have_current_data {
				a href="#dom-media-have_current_data" HAVE_CURRENT_DATA
			}
			- " is negligible. Really the only time the difference is relevant is when painting a "
			code id=ready-states:the-video-element-2 {
				a href="#the-video-element" video
			}
			- " element onto a "
			code id=ready-states:the-canvas-element {
				a href="#the-canvas-element" canvas
			}
			- ", where it distinguishes the case where something will be drawn ("
			code id=ready-states:dom-media-have_current_data-2 {
				a href="#dom-media-have_current_data" HAVE_CURRENT_DATA
			}
			- " or greater) from the case where nothing is drawn ("
			code id=ready-states:dom-media-have_metadata-4 {
				a href="#dom-media-have_metadata" HAVE_METADATA
			}
			- " or less). Similarly, the difference between "
			code id=ready-states:dom-media-have_current_data-3 {
				a href="#dom-media-have_current_data" HAVE_CURRENT_DATA
			}
			- " (only the current frame) and "
			code id=ready-states:dom-media-have_future_data-2 {
				a href="#dom-media-have_future_data" HAVE_FUTURE_DATA
			}
			- " (at least this frame and the next) can be negligible (in the extreme, only one frame). The only time that distinction really matters is when a page provides an interface for \"frame-by-frame\" navigation."
		}
		p {
			- "When the ready state of a "
			a href="#media-element" id=ready-states:media-element-3 "media element"
			- " whose "
			code id=ready-states:dom-media-networkstate-2 {
				a href="#dom-media-networkstate" networkState
			}
			- " is not "
			code id=ready-states:dom-media-network_empty-2 {
				a href="#dom-media-network_empty" NETWORK_EMPTY
			}
			- " changes, the user agent must follow the steps given below:"
		}
		ol {
			li {
				p "Apply the first applicable set of substeps from the following list:"
				dl class=switch {
					dt {
						- "If the previous ready state was "
						code id=ready-states:dom-media-have_nothing-2 {
							a href="#dom-media-have_nothing" HAVE_NOTHING
						}
						- ", and the new ready state is "
						code id=ready-states:dom-media-have_metadata-5 {
							a href="#dom-media-have_metadata" HAVE_METADATA
						}
					}
					dd id=fire-loadedmetadata {
						p {
							a href="#queue-a-media-element-task" id=ready-states:queue-a-media-element-task "Queue a media element task"
							- " given the "
							a href="#media-element" id=ready-states:media-element-4 "media element"
							- " to "
							a data-x-internal=concept-event-fire href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-event-fire" id=ready-states:concept-event-fire "fire an event"
							- " named "
