		p {
			- "A "
			a href="#media-element" id=user-interface:media-element-5 "media element"
			- " has a "
			dfn id=concept-media-volume "playback volume"
			- ", which is a fraction in the range 0.0 (silent) to 1.0 (loudest). Initially, the volume should be 1.0, but user agents may remember the last set value across sessions, on a per-site basis or otherwise, so the volume may start at other values."
		}
		p {
			- "The "
			dfn data-dfn-for=HTMLMediaElement data-dfn-type=attribute id=dom-media-volume {
				code volume
			}
			- " IDL attribute must return the "
			a href="#concept-media-volume" id=user-interface:concept-media-volume "playback volume"
			- " of any audio portions of the "
			a href="#media-element" id=user-interface:media-element-6 "media element"
			- ". On setting, if the new value is in the range 0.0 to 1.0 inclusive, the "
			a href="#media-element" id=user-interface:media-element-7 "media element"
			- "'s "
			a href="#concept-media-volume" id=user-interface:concept-media-volume-2 "playback volume"
			- " must be set to the new value. If the new value is outside the range 0.0 to 1.0 inclusive, then, on setting, an "
			a data-x-internal=indexsizeerror href="https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#indexsizeerror" id=user-interface:indexsizeerror-2 {
				- "\""
				code IndexSizeError
				- "\""
			}
			code id=user-interface:domexception-2 {
				a data-x-internal=domexception href="https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#dfn-DOMException" DOMException
			}
			- " must be thrown instead."
		}
		p {
			- "A "
			a href="#media-element" id=user-interface:media-element-8 "media element"
			- " can also be "
			dfn data-dfn-for="media element" data-export="" id=concept-media-muted muted
			- ". If anything is muting the element, then it is muted. (For example, when the "
			a href="#direction-of-playback" id=user-interface:direction-of-playback "direction of playback"
			- " is backwards, the element is muted.)"
		}
		p {
			- "The "
			dfn data-dfn-for=HTMLMediaElement data-dfn-type=attribute id=dom-media-muted {
				code muted
			}
			- " IDL attribute must return the value to which it was last set. When a "
			a href="#media-element" id=user-interface:media-element-9 "media element"
			- " is created, if the element has a "
			code id=user-interface:attr-media-muted {
				a href="#attr-media-muted" muted
			}
			- " content attribute specified, then the "
			code id=user-interface:dom-media-muted {
				a href="#dom-media-muted" muted
			}
			- " IDL attribute should be set to true; otherwise, the user agents may set the value to the user's preferred value (e.g. remembering the last set value across sessions, on a per-site basis or otherwise). While the "
			code id=user-interface:dom-media-muted-2 {
				a href="#dom-media-muted" muted
			}
			- " IDL attribute is set to true, the "
			a href="#media-element" id=user-interface:media-element-10 "media element"
			- " must be "
			a href="#concept-media-muted" id=user-interface:concept-media-muted muted
			- .
		}
		p {
			- "Whenever either of the values that would be returned by the "
			code id=user-interface:dom-media-volume-3 {
				a href="#dom-media-volume" volume
			}
			- " and "
			code id=user-interface:dom-media-muted-3 {
				a href="#dom-media-muted" muted
			}
			- " IDL attributes change, the user agent must "
			a href="#queue-a-media-element-task" id=user-interface:queue-a-media-element-task "queue a media element task"
			- " given the "
			a href="#media-element" id=user-interface:media-element-11 "media element"
			- " to "
			a data-x-internal=concept-event-fire href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-event-fire" id=user-interface:concept-event-fire "fire an event"
			- " named "
