		}
		p {
			- "The "
			dfn data-dfn-for=TimeRanges data-dfn-type=attribute id=dom-timeranges-length {
				code length
			}
			- " IDL attribute must return the number of ranges represented by the object."
		}
		p {
			- "The "
			dfn data-dfn-for=TimeRanges data-dfn-type=method id=dom-timeranges-start {
				code {
					- "start("
					var index
					- ")"
				}
			}
			- " method must return the position of the start of the "
			var index
			- "th range represented by the object, in seconds measured from the start of the timeline that the object covers."
		}
		p {
			- "The "
			dfn data-dfn-for=TimeRanges data-dfn-type=method id=dom-timeranges-end {
				code {
					- "end("
					var index
					- ")"
				}
			}
			- " method must return the position of the end of the "
			var index
			- "th range represented by the object, in seconds measured from the start of the timeline that the object covers."
		}
		p {
			- "These methods must throw "
			a data-x-internal=indexsizeerror href="https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#indexsizeerror" id=time-ranges:indexsizeerror-3 {
				- "\""
				code IndexSizeError
				- "\""
			}
			code id=time-ranges:domexception-3 {
				a data-x-internal=domexception href="https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#dfn-DOMException" DOMException
			}
			- "s if called with an "
			var index
			- " argument greater than or equal to the number of ranges represented by the object."
		}
		p {
			- "When a "
			code id=time-ranges:timeranges-2 {
				a href="#timeranges" TimeRanges
			}
			- " object is said to be a "
			dfn data-export="" id=normalised-timeranges-object {
				- "normalized "
				code TimeRanges
				- " object"
			}
			- ", the ranges it represents must obey the following criteria:"
		}
		ul {
			li "The start of a range must be greater than the end of all earlier ranges."
			li "The start of a range must be less than or equal to the end of that same range."
		}
		p {
			- "In other words, the ranges in such an object are ordered, don't overlap, and don't touch (adjacent ranges are folded into one bigger range). A range can be empty (referencing just a single moment in time), e.g. to indicate that only one frame is currently buffered in the case that the user agent has discarded the entire "
			a href="#media-resource" id=time-ranges:media-resource "media resource"
			- " except for the current frame, when a "
			a href="#media-element" id=time-ranges:media-element "media element"
			- " is paused."
		}
		p {
			- "Ranges in a "
			code id=time-ranges:timeranges-3 {
				a href="#timeranges" TimeRanges
			}
			- " object must be inclusive."
		}
		p class=example "Thus, the end of a range would be equal to the start of a following adjacent (touching but not overlapping) range. Similarly, a range covering a whole timeline anchored at zero would have a start equal to zero and an end equal to the duration of the timeline."
		p {
			- "The timelines used by the objects returned by the "
			code id=time-ranges:dom-media-buffered {
				a href="#dom-media-buffered" buffered
			}
			- ", "
			code id=time-ranges:dom-media-seekable {
				a href="#dom-media-seekable" seekable
			}
			- ", and "
			code id=time-ranges:dom-media-played {
				a href="#dom-media-played" played
			}
			- " IDL attributes of "
			a href="#media-element" id=time-ranges:media-element-2 "media elements"
			- " must be that element's "
			a href="#media-timeline" id=time-ranges:media-timeline "media timeline"
			- .
		}
