		p {
			- "We can use an "
			code id=writing-a-form's-user-interface:the-input-element-6 {
				a href="#the-input-element" input
			}
			- " element with its "
			code id=writing-a-form's-user-interface:attr-input-type-5 {
				a href="#attr-input-type" type
			}
			- " attribute set to "
			code id="writing-a-form's-user-interface:time-state-(type=time)" {
				a href="#time-state-(type=time)" time
			}
			- " to ask for a delivery time. Many of these form controls have attributes to control exactly what values can be specified; in this case, three attributes of particular interest are "
			code id=writing-a-form's-user-interface:attr-input-min {
				a href="#attr-input-min" min
			}
			- ", "
			code id=writing-a-form's-user-interface:attr-input-max {
				a href="#attr-input-max" max
			}
			- ", and "
			code id=writing-a-form's-user-interface:attr-input-step {
				a href="#attr-input-step" step
			}
			- ". These set the minimum time, the maximum time, and the interval between allowed values (in seconds). This pizzeria only delivers between 11am and 9pm, and doesn't promise anything better than 15 minute increments, which we can mark up as follows:"
		}
