		h5 id=implementing-the-server-side-processing-for-a-form {
			span class=secno "4.10.1.2"
			- " Implementing the server-side processing for a form"
			a class=self-link href="#implementing-the-server-side-processing-for-a-form"
		}
		p {
			i "This section is non-normative."
		}
		p {
			- "The exact details for writing a server-side processor are out of scope for this specification. For the purposes of this introduction, we will assume that the script at "
			code "https://pizza.example.com/order.cgi"
			- " is configured to accept submissions using the "
			code id=implementing-the-server-side-processing-for-a-form:attr-fs-enctype-urlencoded {
				a href="#attr-fs-enctype-urlencoded" "application/x-www-form-urlencoded"
			}
			- " format, expecting the following parameters sent in an HTTP POST body:"
		}
		dl {
			dt {
				code custname
			}
			dd "Customer's name"
			dt {
				code custtel
			}
			dd "Customer's telephone number"
			dt {
				code custemail
			}
			dd "Customer's email address"
			dt {
				code size
			}
			dd {
				- "The pizza size, either "
				code small
				- ", "
				code medium
				- ", or "
				code large
			}
			dt {
				code topping
			}
			dd {
				- "A topping, specified once for each selected topping, with the allowed values being "
				code bacon
				- ", "
				code cheese
				- ", "
				code onion
				- ", and "
				code mushroom
			}
			dt {
				code delivery
			}
			dd "The requested delivery time"
			dt {
				code comments
			}
			dd "The delivery instructions"
		}
		h5 id=configuring-a-form-to-communicate-with-a-server {
			span class=secno "4.10.1.3"
			- " Configuring a form to communicate with a server"
			a class=self-link href="#configuring-a-form-to-communicate-with-a-server"
		}
		p {
			i "This section is non-normative."
		}
		p {
			- "Form submissions are exposed to servers in a variety of ways, most commonly as HTTP GET or POST requests. To specify the exact method used, the "
			code id=configuring-a-form-to-communicate-with-a-server:attr-fs-method {
				a href="#attr-fs-method" method
			}
			- " attribute is specified on the "
			code id=configuring-a-form-to-communicate-with-a-server:the-form-element {
				a href="#the-form-element" form
			}
			- " element. This doesn't specify how the form data is encoded, though; to specify that, you use the "
			code id=configuring-a-form-to-communicate-with-a-server:attr-fs-enctype {
				a href="#attr-fs-enctype" enctype
			}
			- " attribute. You also have to specify the "
			a data-x-internal=url href="https://url.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-url" id=configuring-a-form-to-communicate-with-a-server:url URL
			- " of the service that will handle the submitted data, using the "
			code id=configuring-a-form-to-communicate-with-a-server:attr-fs-action {
				a href="#attr-fs-action" action
			}
			- " attribute."
		}
		p {
			- "For each form control you want submitted, you then have to give a name that will be used to refer to the data in the submission. We already specified the name for the group of radio buttons; the same attribute ("
			code id=configuring-a-form-to-communicate-with-a-server:attr-fe-name {
				a href="#attr-fe-name" name
			}
			- ") also specifies the submission name. Radio buttons can be distinguished from each other in the submission by giving them different values, using the "
			code id=configuring-a-form-to-communicate-with-a-server:attr-input-value {
				a href="#attr-input-value" value
			}
			- " attribute."
		}
		p {
			- "Multiple controls can have the same name; for example, here we give all the checkboxes the same name, and the server distinguishes which checkbox was checked by seeing which values are submitted with that name — like the radio buttons, they are also given unique values with the "
			code id=configuring-a-form-to-communicate-with-a-server:attr-input-value-2 {
				a href="#attr-input-value" value
			}
			- " attribute."
		}
		p "Given the settings in the previous section, this all becomes:"
		pre {
			code class=html {
				c- p="" <
				c- f="" form
				strong {
					c- e="" method
					c- o="" "="
					c- s="" "\"post\""
					c- e="" enctype
					c- o="" "="
					c- s="" "\"application/x-www-form-urlencoded\""
					c- e="" action
					c- o="" "="
					c- s="" "\"https://pizza.example.com/order.cgi\""
				}
				c- p="" >
				c- p="" <
				c- f="" p
				c- p="" ><
				c- f="" label
				c- p="" >
				- "Customer name: "
				c- p="" <
				c- f="" input
