					- ", then "
					a data-x-internal=strip-leading-and-trailing-ascii-whitespace href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#strip-leading-and-trailing-ascii-whitespace" id="email-state-(type=email):strip-leading-and-trailing-ascii-whitespace" "strip leading and trailing ASCII whitespace"
					- " from the "
					a href="#concept-fe-value" id="email-state-(type=email):concept-fe-value-9" value
					- .
				}
				p {
					strong "Constraint validation"
					- ": While the "
					a href="#concept-fe-value" id="email-state-(type=email):concept-fe-value-10" value
					- " of the element is neither the empty string nor a single "
					a href="#valid-e-mail-address" id="email-state-(type=email):valid-e-mail-address-3" "valid email address"
					- ", the element is "
					a href="#suffering-from-a-type-mismatch" id="email-state-(type=email):suffering-from-a-type-mismatch" "suffering from a type mismatch"
					- .
				}
			}
			dt {
				- "When the "
				code id="email-state-(type=email):attr-input-multiple-3" {
					a href="#attr-input-multiple" multiple
				}
				- " attribute "
				em is
				- " specified on the element"
			}
			dd {
				p {
					- "The "
					code id="email-state-(type=email):the-input-element-3" {
						a href="#the-input-element" input
					}
					- " element "
					a href="#represents" id="email-state-(type=email):represents-2" represents
					- " a control for adding, removing, and editing the email addresses given in the element's "
					a href="#concept-fe-values" id="email-state-(type=email):concept-fe-values" {
						- value
						em s
					}
					- .
				}
				p {
					- "If the element is "
					i id="email-state-(type=email):concept-fe-mutable-2" {
						a href="#concept-fe-mutable" mutable
					}
					- ", the user agent should allow the user to add, remove, and edit the email addresses represented by its "
					a href="#concept-fe-values" id="email-state-(type=email):concept-fe-values-2" values
					- ". User agents may allow the user to set any individual value in the list of "
					a href="#concept-fe-value" id="email-state-(type=email):concept-fe-value-11" {
						- value
						em s
					}
					- " to a string that is not a "
					a href="#valid-e-mail-address" id="email-state-(type=email):valid-e-mail-address-4" "valid email address"
					- ", but must not allow users to set any individual value to a string containing U+002C COMMA (,), U+000A LINE FEED (LF), or U+000D CARRIAGE RETURN (CR) characters. User agents should allow the user to remove all the addresses in the element's "
					a href="#concept-fe-values" id="email-state-(type=email):concept-fe-values-3" values
					- ". User agents may transform the "
					a href="#concept-fe-values" id="email-state-(type=email):concept-fe-values-4" values
					- " for display and editing; in particular, user agents should convert punycode in the domain labels of the "
					a href="#concept-fe-value" id="email-state-(type=email):concept-fe-value-12" value
					- " to IDN in the display and vice versa."
				}
				p {
					strong "Constraint validation"
					- ": While the user interface describes a situation where an individual value contains a U+002C COMMA (,) or is representing input that the user agent cannot convert to punycode, the control is "
					a href="#suffering-from-bad-input" id="email-state-(type=email):suffering-from-bad-input-2" "suffering from bad input"
					- .
				}
				p {
					- "Whenever the user changes the element's "
					a href="#concept-fe-value" id="email-state-(type=email):concept-fe-value-13" {
						- value
						em s
					}
					- ", the user agent must run the following steps:"
				}
				ol {
					li {
						p {
							- "Let "
							var "latest values"
							- " be a copy of the element's "
							a href="#concept-fe-value" id="email-state-(type=email):concept-fe-value-14" {
								- value
								em s
							}
							- .
						}
					}
					li {
						p {
							a data-x-internal=strip-leading-and-trailing-ascii-whitespace href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#strip-leading-and-trailing-ascii-whitespace" id="email-state-(type=email):strip-leading-and-trailing-ascii-whitespace-2" "Strip leading and trailing ASCII whitespace"
							- " from each value in "
							var "latest values"
							- .
						}
					}
					li {
						p {
							- "Let the element's "
							a href="#concept-fe-value" id="email-state-(type=email):concept-fe-value-15" value
							- " be the result of concatenating all the values in "
