		}
		p {
			- "When an "
			code id="number-state-(type=number):the-input-element" {
				a href="#the-input-element" input
			}
			- " element's "
			code id="number-state-(type=number):attr-input-type" {
				a href="#attr-input-type" type
			}
			- " attribute is in the "
			a href="#number-state-(type=number)" id="number-state-(type=number):number-state-(type=number)" Number
			- " state, the rules in this section apply."
		}
		p {
			- "The "
			code id="number-state-(type=number):the-input-element-2" {
				a href="#the-input-element" input
			}
			- " element "
			a href="#represents" id="number-state-(type=number):represents" represents
			- " a control for setting the element's "
			a href="#concept-fe-value" id="number-state-(type=number):concept-fe-value" value
			- " to a string representing a number."
		}
		p {
			- "If the element is "
			i id="number-state-(type=number):concept-fe-mutable" {
				a href="#concept-fe-mutable" mutable
			}
			- ", the user agent should allow the user to change the number represented by its "
			a href="#concept-fe-value" id="number-state-(type=number):concept-fe-value-2" value
			- ", as obtained from applying the "
			a href="#rules-for-parsing-floating-point-number-values" id="number-state-(type=number):rules-for-parsing-floating-point-number-values" "rules for parsing floating-point number values"
			- " to it. User agents must not allow the user to set the "
			a href="#concept-fe-value" id="number-state-(type=number):concept-fe-value-3" value
			- " to a non-empty string that is not a "
			a href="#valid-floating-point-number" id="number-state-(type=number):valid-floating-point-number" "valid floating-point number"
			- ". If the user agent provides a user interface for selecting a number, then the "
			a href="#concept-fe-value" id="number-state-(type=number):concept-fe-value-4" value
			- " must be set to the "
			a href="#best-representation-of-the-number-as-a-floating-point-number" id="number-state-(type=number):best-representation-of-the-number-as-a-floating-point-number" "best representation of the number representing the user's selection as a floating-point number"
			- ". User agents should allow the user to set the "
			a href="#concept-fe-value" id="number-state-(type=number):concept-fe-value-5" value
			- " to the empty string."
		}
		p {
			strong "Constraint validation"
			- ": While the user interface describes input that the user agent cannot convert to a "
			a href="#valid-floating-point-number" id="number-state-(type=number):valid-floating-point-number-2" "valid floating-point number"
			- ", the control is "
			a href="#suffering-from-bad-input" id="number-state-(type=number):suffering-from-bad-input" "suffering from bad input"
			- .
		}
		p class=note "This specification does not define what user interface user agents are to use; user agent vendors are encouraged to consider what would best serve their users' needs. For example, a user agent in Persian or Arabic markets might support Persian and Arabic numeric input (converting it to the format required for submission as described above). Similarly, a user agent designed for Romans might display the value in Roman numerals rather than in decimal; or (more realistically) a user agent designed for the French market might display the value with apostrophes between thousands and commas before the decimals, and allow the user to enter a value in that manner, internally converting it to the submission format described above."
		p {
			- "The "
			code id="number-state-(type=number):attr-input-value" {
				a href="#attr-input-value" value
			}
			- " attribute, if specified and not empty, must have a value that is a "
			a href="#valid-floating-point-number" id="number-state-(type=number):valid-floating-point-number-3" "valid floating-point number"
			- .
		}
		p {
			strong {
				- "The "
				a href="#value-sanitization-algorithm" id="number-state-(type=number):value-sanitization-algorithm" "value sanitization algorithm"
				- " is as follows"
			}
			- ": If the "
			a href="#concept-fe-value" id="number-state-(type=number):concept-fe-value-6" value
			- " of the element is not a "
			a href="#valid-floating-point-number" id="number-state-(type=number):valid-floating-point-number-4" "valid floating-point number"
			- ", then set it to the empty string instead."
		}
		p {
			- "The "
			code id="number-state-(type=number):attr-input-min" {
				a href="#attr-input-min" min
			}
			- " attribute, if specified, must have a value that is a "
			a href="#valid-floating-point-number" id="number-state-(type=number):valid-floating-point-number-5" "valid floating-point number"
			- ". The "
			code id="number-state-(type=number):attr-input-max" {
				a href="#attr-input-max" max
			}
			- " attribute, if specified, must have a value that is a "
			a href="#valid-floating-point-number" id="number-state-(type=number):valid-floating-point-number-6" "valid floating-point number"
			- .
		}
		p {
			- "The "
			a href="#concept-input-step-scale" id="number-state-(type=number):concept-input-step-scale" "step scale factor"
			- " is 1. The "
			a href="#concept-input-step-default" id="number-state-(type=number):concept-input-step-default" "default step"
			- " is 1 (allowing only integers to be selected by the user, unless the "
			a href="#concept-input-min-zero" id="number-state-(type=number):concept-input-min-zero" "step base"
			- " has a non-integer value)."
		}
		p {
			- "When the element is "
			a href="#suffering-from-a-step-mismatch" id="number-state-(type=number):suffering-from-a-step-mismatch" "suffering from a step mismatch"
			- ", the user agent may round the element's "
			a href="#concept-fe-value" id="number-state-(type=number):concept-fe-value-7" value
			- " to the nearest number for which the element would not "
			a href="#suffering-from-a-step-mismatch" id="number-state-(type=number):suffering-from-a-step-mismatch-2" "suffer from a step mismatch"
			- ". If there are two such numbers, user agents are encouraged to pick the one nearest positive infinity."
		}
		p {
			strong {
				- "The "
				a href="#concept-input-value-string-number" id="number-state-(type=number):concept-input-value-string-number" "algorithm to convert a string to a number"
				- ", given a string "
				var input
