		p {
			- "When an "
			code id="range-state-(type=range):the-input-element" {
				a href="#the-input-element" input
			}
			- " element's "
			code id="range-state-(type=range):attr-input-type" {
				a href="#attr-input-type" type
			}
			- " attribute is in the "
			a href="#range-state-(type=range)" id="range-state-(type=range):range-state-(type=range)" Range
			- " state, the rules in this section apply."
		}
		p {
			- "The "
			code id="range-state-(type=range):the-input-element-2" {
				a href="#the-input-element" input
			}
			- " element "
			a href="#represents" id="range-state-(type=range):represents" represents
			- " a control for setting the element's "
			a href="#concept-fe-value" id="range-state-(type=range):concept-fe-value" value
			- " to a string representing a number, but with the caveat that the exact value is not important, letting UAs provide a simpler interface than they do for the "
			a href="#number-state-(type=number)" id="range-state-(type=range):number-state-(type=number)" Number
			- " state."
		}
		p {
			- "If the element is "
			i id="range-state-(type=range):concept-fe-mutable" {
				a href="#concept-fe-mutable" mutable
			}
			- ", the user agent should allow the user to change the number represented by its "
			a href="#concept-fe-value" id="range-state-(type=range):concept-fe-value-2" value
			- ", as obtained from applying the "
			a href="#rules-for-parsing-floating-point-number-values" id="range-state-(type=range):rules-for-parsing-floating-point-number-values" "rules for parsing floating-point number values"
			- " to it. User agents must not allow the user to set the "
			a href="#concept-fe-value" id="range-state-(type=range):concept-fe-value-3" value
			- " to a string that is not a "
			a href="#valid-floating-point-number" id="range-state-(type=range):valid-floating-point-number" "valid floating-point number"
			- ". If the user agent provides a user interface for selecting a number, then the "
			a href="#concept-fe-value" id="range-state-(type=range):concept-fe-value-4" value
			- " must be set to a "
			a href="#best-representation-of-the-number-as-a-floating-point-number" id="range-state-(type=range):best-representation-of-the-number-as-a-floating-point-number" "best representation of the number representing the user's selection as a floating-point number"
			- ". User agents must not allow the user to set the "
			a href="#concept-fe-value" id="range-state-(type=range):concept-fe-value-5" value
			- " to the empty string."
		}
		p {
			strong "Constraint validation"
			- ": While the user interface describes input that the user agent cannot convert to a "
			a href="#valid-floating-point-number" id="range-state-(type=range):valid-floating-point-number-2" "valid floating-point number"
			- ", the control is "
			a href="#suffering-from-bad-input" id="range-state-(type=range):suffering-from-bad-input" "suffering from bad input"
			- .
		}
		p {
			- "The "
			code id="range-state-(type=range):attr-input-value" {
				a href="#attr-input-value" value
			}
			- " attribute, if specified, must have a value that is a "
			a href="#valid-floating-point-number" id="range-state-(type=range):valid-floating-point-number-3" "valid floating-point number"
			- .
		}
		p {
			strong {
				- "The "
				a href="#value-sanitization-algorithm" id="range-state-(type=range):value-sanitization-algorithm" "value sanitization algorithm"
				- " is as follows"
			}
			- ": If the "
			a href="#concept-fe-value" id="range-state-(type=range):concept-fe-value-6" value
			- " of the element is not a "
			a href="#valid-floating-point-number" id="range-state-(type=range):valid-floating-point-number-4" "valid floating-point number"
			- ", then set it to the "
			a href="#best-representation-of-the-number-as-a-floating-point-number" id="range-state-(type=range):best-representation-of-the-number-as-a-floating-point-number-2" "best representation, as a floating-point number"
			- ", of the "
			a href="#concept-input-value-default-range" id="range-state-(type=range):concept-input-value-default-range" "default value"
			- .
		}
		p {
			- "The "
			dfn id=concept-input-value-default-range "default value"
			- " is the "
			a href="#concept-input-min" id="range-state-(type=range):concept-input-min" minimum
			- " plus half the difference between the "
			a href="#concept-input-min" id="range-state-(type=range):concept-input-min-2" minimum
			- " and the "
			a href="#concept-input-max" id="range-state-(type=range):concept-input-max" maximum
			- ", unless the "
			a href="#concept-input-max" id="range-state-(type=range):concept-input-max-2" maximum
			- " is less than the "
			a href="#concept-input-min" id="range-state-(type=range):concept-input-min-3" minimum
			- ", in which case the "
			a href="#concept-input-value-default-range" id="range-state-(type=range):concept-input-value-default-range-2" "default value"
			- " is the "
			a href="#concept-input-min" id="range-state-(type=range):concept-input-min-4" minimum
			- .
		}
		p {
			- "When the element is "
			a href="#suffering-from-an-underflow" id="range-state-(type=range):suffering-from-an-underflow" "suffering from an underflow"
			- ", the user agent must set the element's "
			a href="#concept-fe-value" id="range-state-(type=range):concept-fe-value-7" value
			- " to the "
			a href="#best-representation-of-the-number-as-a-floating-point-number" id="range-state-(type=range):best-representation-of-the-number-as-a-floating-point-number-3" "best representation, as a floating-point number"
			- ", of the "
			a href="#concept-input-min" id="range-state-(type=range):concept-input-min-5" minimum
			- .
		}
		p {
			- "When the element is "
			a href="#suffering-from-an-overflow" id="range-state-(type=range):suffering-from-an-overflow" "suffering from an overflow"
			- ", if the "
			a href="#concept-input-max" id="range-state-(type=range):concept-input-max-3" maximum
			- " is not less than the "
			a href="#concept-input-min" id="range-state-(type=range):concept-input-min-6" minimum
			- ", the user agent must set the element's "
			a href="#concept-fe-value" id="range-state-(type=range):concept-fe-value-8" value
			- " to a "
			a href="#valid-floating-point-number" id="range-state-(type=range):valid-floating-point-number-5" "valid floating-point number"
			- " that represents the "
			a href="#concept-input-max" id="range-state-(type=range):concept-input-max-4" maximum
			- .
		}
		p {
			- "When the element is "
			a href="#suffering-from-a-step-mismatch" id="range-state-(type=range):suffering-from-a-step-mismatch" "suffering from a step mismatch"
			- ", the user agent must round the element's "
			a href="#concept-fe-value" id="range-state-(type=range):concept-fe-value-9" value
			- " to the nearest number for which the element would not "
			a href="#suffering-from-a-step-mismatch" id="range-state-(type=range):suffering-from-a-step-mismatch-2" "suffer from a step mismatch"
			- ", and which is greater than or equal to the "
			a href="#concept-input-min" id="range-state-(type=range):concept-input-min-7" minimum
			- ", and, if the "
			a href="#concept-input-max" id="range-state-(type=range):concept-input-max-5" maximum
			- " is not less than the "
			a href="#concept-input-min" id="range-state-(type=range):concept-input-min-8" minimum
			- ", which is less than or equal to the "
			a href="#concept-input-max" id="range-state-(type=range):concept-input-max-6" maximum
			- ", if there is a number that matches these constraints. If two numbers match these constraints, then user agents must use the one nearest to positive infinity."
		}
		p class=example {
			- "For example, the markup "
			code "<input type=\"range\" min=0 max=100 step=20 value=50>"
			- " results in a range control whose initial value is 60."
		}
		div class=example {
			p {
				- "Here is an example of a range control using an autocomplete list with the "
				code id="range-state-(type=range):attr-input-list" {
					a href="#attr-input-list" list
				}
				- " attribute. This could be useful if there are values along the full range of the control that are especially important, such as preconfigured light levels or typical speed limits in a range control used as a speed control. The following markup fragment:"
			}
			pre {
				code class=html {
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" input
					c- e="" type
					c- o="" "="
					c- s="" "\"range\""
					c- e="" min
					c- o="" "="
					c- s="" "\"-100\""
					c- e="" max
					c- o="" "="
					c- s="" "\"100\""
					c- e="" value
					c- o="" "="
					c- s="" "\"0\""
					c- e="" step
					c- o="" "="
					c- s="" "\"10\""
					c- e="" name
					c- o="" "="
					c- s="" "\"power\""
					c- e="" list
					c- o="" "="
					c- s="" "\"powers\""
					c- p="" >
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" datalist
					c- e="" id
					c- o="" "="
					c- s="" "\"powers\""
					c- p="" >
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" option
					c- e="" value
					c- o="" "="
					c- s="" "\"0\""
					c- p="" >
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" option
					c- e="" value
					c- o="" "="
					c- s="" "\"-30\""
					c- p="" >
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" option
					c- e="" value
					c- o="" "="
					c- s="" "\"30\""
					c- p="" >
					span class=bad {
						c- p="" <
						c- f="" option
						c- e="" value
						c- o="" "="
						c- s="" "\"++50\""
						c- p="" >
					}
					c- p="" "</"
					c- f="" datalist
					c- p="" >
				}
			}
			p "...with the following style sheet applied:"
			pre {
				code class=css {
					c- f="" "input "
					c- p="" "{"
					c- k="" writing-mode
					c- p="" :
					- " vertical-lr"
					c- p="" ";"
					c- k="" height
					c- p="" :
					c- m="" "75"
					c- l="" px
					c- p="" ";"
					c- k="" width
					c- p="" :
					c- m="" "49"
					c- l="" px
					c- p="" ";"
					c- k="" background
					c- p="" :
					- " #D5CCBB"
					c- p="" ";"
					c- k="" color
					c- p="" :
					- " black"
					c- p="" ";"
					c- p="" "}"
				}
			}
			p "...might render as:"
			p {
				img alt="A vertical slider control whose primary color is black and whose background color is beige, with the slider having five tick marks, one long one at each extremity, and three short ones clustered around the midpoint." height="75" src="/images/sample-range.png" width="49"
			}
			p {
				- "Note how the UA determined the orientation of the control from the ratio of the style-sheet-specified height and width properties. The colors were similarly derived from the style sheet. The tick marks, however, were derived from the markup. In particular, the "
				code id="range-state-(type=range):attr-input-step" {
					a href="#attr-input-step" step
				}
				- " attribute has not affected the placement of tick marks, the UA deciding to only use the author-specified completion values and then adding longer tick marks at the extremes."
			}
			p {
				- "Note also how the invalid value "
				code ++50
				- " was ignored."
			}
		}
		div class=example {
			p "For another example, consider the following markup fragment:"
			pre {
				code class=html {
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" input
					c- e="" name
					c- o="" "="
					c- s="" x
					c- e="" type
					c- o="" "="
					c- s="" range
					c- e="" min
					c- o="" "="
					c- s="" "100"
					c- e="" max
					c- o="" "="
					c- s="" "700"
					c- e="" step
					c- o="" "="
					c- s="" "9.09090909"
					c- e="" value
					c- o="" "="
					c- s="" "509.090909"
					c- p="" >
				}
			}
			p "A user agent could display in a variety of ways, for instance:"
			p {
				img alt="As a dial." height="57" src="/images/sample-range-2a.png" width="231"
			}
			p "Or, alternatively, for instance:"
			p {
				img alt="As a long horizontal slider with tick marks." height="56" src="/images/sample-range-2b.png" width="445"
			}
			p "The user agent could pick which one to display based on the dimensions given in the style sheet. This would allow it to maintain the same resolution for the tick marks, despite the differences in width."
		}
		div class=example {
			p "Finally, here is an example of a range control with two labeled values:"
			pre {
				code class=html {
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" input
					c- e="" type
					c- o="" "="
					c- s="" "\"range\""
					c- e="" name
					c- o="" "="
					c- s="" "\"a\""
					c- e="" list
					c- o="" "="
					c- s="" "\"a-values\""
					c- p="" >
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" datalist
					c- e="" id
					c- o="" "="
					c- s="" "\"a-values\""
					c- p="" >
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" option
					c- e="" value
					c- o="" "="
					c- s="" "\"10\""
					c- e="" label
					c- o="" "="
					c- s="" "\"Low\""
					c- p="" >
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" option
					c- e="" value
					c- o="" "="
					c- s="" "\"90\""
					c- e="" label
					c- o="" "="
					c- s="" "\"High\""
					c- p="" >
					c- p="" "</"
					c- f="" datalist
					c- p="" >
				}
			}
			p "With styles that make the control draw vertically, it might look as follows:"
			p {
				img alt="A vertical slider control with two tick marks, one near the top labeled 'High', and one near the bottom labeled 'Low'." height="164" src="/images/sample-range-labels.png" width="103"
			}
		}
		p class=note "In this state, the range and step constraints are enforced even during user input, and there is no way to set the value to the empty string."
		p {
			- "The "
			code id="range-state-(type=range):attr-input-min" {
				a href="#attr-input-min" min
			}
			- " attribute, if specified, must have a value that is a "
			a href="#valid-floating-point-number" id="range-state-(type=range):valid-floating-point-number-6" "valid floating-point number"
			- ". The "
			a href="#concept-input-min-default" id="range-state-(type=range):concept-input-min-default" "default minimum"
			- " is 0. The "
			code id="range-state-(type=range):attr-input-max" {
				a href="#attr-input-max" max
			}
			- " attribute, if specified, must have a value that is a "
			a href="#valid-floating-point-number" id="range-state-(type=range):valid-floating-point-number-7" "valid floating-point number"
			- ". The "
			a href="#concept-input-max-default" id="range-state-(type=range):concept-input-max-default" "default maximum"
			- " is 100."
		}
		p {
			- "The "
			a href="#concept-input-step-scale" id="range-state-(type=range):concept-input-step-scale" "step scale factor"
			- " is 1. The "
			a href="#concept-input-step-default" id="range-state-(type=range):concept-input-step-default" "default step"
			- " is 1 (allowing only integers, unless the "
			code id="range-state-(type=range):attr-input-min-2" {
				a href="#attr-input-min" min
			}
			- " attribute has a non-integer value)."
		}
		p {
			strong {
				- "The "
				a href="#concept-input-value-string-number" id="range-state-(type=range):concept-input-value-string-number" "algorithm to convert a string to a number"
				- ", given a string "
				var input
				- ", is as follows"
			}
			- ": If applying the "
			a href="#rules-for-parsing-floating-point-number-values" id="range-state-(type=range):rules-for-parsing-floating-point-number-values-2" "rules for parsing floating-point number values"
			- " to "
			var input
			- " results in an error, then return an error; otherwise, return the resulting number."
		}
		p {
			strong {
				- "The "
				a href="#concept-input-value-number-string" id="range-state-(type=range):concept-input-value-number-string" "algorithm to convert a number to a string"
				- ", given a number "
				var input
				- ", is as follows"
			}
			- ": Return the "
			a href="#best-representation-of-the-number-as-a-floating-point-number" id="range-state-(type=range):best-representation-of-the-number-as-a-floating-point-number-4" "best representation, as a floating-point number"
			- ", of "
			var input
			- .
		}
