		h6 id="color-state-(type=color)" {
			span class=secno "4.10.5.1.14"
			dfn data-dfn-for=input data-dfn-type=element-state Color
			- " state ("
			code "type=color"
			- ")"
			a class=self-link href="#color-state-(type=color)"
		}
		div class="mdn-anno wrapped" {
			button class=mdn-anno-btn onclick="toggleStatus(this)" {
				b class=all-engines-flag title="Support in all current engines." ✔
				span MDN
			}
			div class=feature {
				p {
					a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTML/Element/input/color" title="<input> elements of type color provide a user interface element that lets a user specify a color, either by using a visual color picker interface or by entering the color into a text field in #rrggbb hexadecimal format." "Element/input/color"
				}
				p class=all-engines-text "Support in all current engines."
				div class=support {
					span class="firefox yes" {
						span Firefox
						span "29+"
					}
					span class="safari yes" {
						span Safari
						span "12.1+"
					}
					span class="chrome yes" {
						span Chrome
						span "20+"
					}
					hr
					span class="opera yes" {
						span Opera
						span "12+"
					}
					span class="edge_blink yes" {
						span Edge
						span "79+"
					}
					hr
					span class="edge yes" {
						span "Edge (Legacy)"
						span "14+"
					}
					span class="ie no" {
						span "Internet Explorer"
						span No
					}
					hr
					span class="firefox_android yes" {
						span "Firefox Android"
						span title="Partial implementation." "🔰 27+"
					}
					span class="safari_ios unknown" {
						span "Safari iOS"
						span ?
					}
					span class="chrome_android unknown" {
						span "Chrome Android"
						span ?
					}
					span class="webview_android unknown" {
						span "WebView Android"
						span ?
					}
					span class="samsunginternet_android unknown" {
						span "Samsung Internet"
						span ?
					}
					span class="opera_android yes" {
						span "Opera Android"
						span "12+"
					}
				}
			}
		}
		p {
			- "When an "
			code id="color-state-(type=color):the-input-element" {
				a href="#the-input-element" input
			}
			- " element's "
			code id="color-state-(type=color):attr-input-type" {
				a href="#attr-input-type" type
			}
			- " attribute is in the "
			a href="#color-state-(type=color)" id="color-state-(type=color):color-state-(type=color)" Color
			- " state, the rules in this section apply."
		}
		p {
			- "The "
			code id="color-state-(type=color):the-input-element-2" {
				a href="#the-input-element" input
			}
			- " element "
			a href="#represents" id="color-state-(type=color):represents" represents
			- " a color well control, for setting the element's "
			a href="#concept-fe-value" id="color-state-(type=color):concept-fe-value" value
			- " to a string representing the serialization of a CSS color."
		}
		p class=note "In this state, there is always a CSS color picked, and there is no way for the end user to set the value to the empty string."
		p {
			- "The "
			dfn data-dfn-for=input data-dfn-type=element-attr id=attr-input-alpha {
				code alpha
			}
			- " attribute is a "
			a href="#boolean-attribute" id="color-state-(type=color):boolean-attribute" "boolean attribute"
			- ". If present, it indicates the CSS color's alpha component can be manipulated by the end user and does not have to be fully opaque."
		}
		p {
			- "The "
			dfn data-dfn-for=input data-dfn-type=element-attr id=attr-input-colorspace {
				code colorspace
			}
			- " attribute indicates the color space of the serialized CSS color. It also hints at the desired user interface for selecting a CSS color. It is an "
			a href="#enumerated-attribute" id="color-state-(type=color):enumerated-attribute" "enumerated attribute"
			- " with the following keywords and states:"
		}
		table {
			thead {
				tr {
					th " Keyword "
					th " State "
					th " Brief description "
				}
			}
			tbody {
				tr {
					td {
						dfn data-dfn-for="input/colorspace" data-dfn-type=attr-value id=attr-input-colorspace-limited-srgb {
							code limited-srgb
						}
					}
					td {
						dfn id=attr-input-colorspace-limited-srgb-state "Limited sRGB"
					}
					td {
						- "The CSS color is converted to the "
						a data-x-internal='srgb' href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-color/#valdef-color-srgb" id="color-state-(type=color):'srgb'" 'srgb'
						- " color space and limited to 8-bits per component, e.g., \""
						code "#123456"
						- "\" or \""
						code "color(srgb 0 1 0 / 0.5)"
						- "\". "
					}
				}
				tr {
					td {
						dfn data-dfn-for="input/colorspace" data-dfn-type=attr-value id=attr-input-colorspace-display-p3 {
							code display-p3
						}
					}
					td {
						dfn id=attr-input-colorspace-display-p3-state "Display P3"
					}
					td {
						- "The CSS color is converted to the "
						a data-x-internal='display-p3' href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-color/#valdef-color-display-p3" id="color-state-(type=color):'display-p3'" 'display-p3'
						- " color space, e.g., \""
						code "color(display-p3 1.84 -0.19 0.72 / 0.6)"
						- "\". "
					}
				}
			}
		}
		p {
			- "The attribute's "
			i id="color-state-(type=color):missing-value-default" {
				a href="#missing-value-default" "missing value default"
			}
			- " and "
			i id="color-state-(type=color):invalid-value-default" {
				a href="#invalid-value-default" "invalid value default"
			}
			- " are both the "
			a href="#attr-input-colorspace-limited-srgb-state" id="color-state-(type=color):attr-input-colorspace-limited-srgb-state" "Limited sRGB"
			- " state."
		}
		p {
			- "Whenever the element's "
			code id="color-state-(type=color):attr-input-alpha" {
				a href="#attr-input-alpha" alpha
			}
			- " or "
			code id="color-state-(type=color):attr-input-colorspace" {
				a href="#attr-input-colorspace" colorspace
			}
			- " attributes are changed, the user agent must run "
			a href="#update-a-color-well-control-color" id="color-state-(type=color):update-a-color-well-control-color" "update a color well control color"
			- " given the element."
		}
		p {
			- "If the element is "
			i id="color-state-(type=color):concept-fe-mutable" {
				a href="#concept-fe-mutable" mutable
			}
			- ", the user agent should allow the user to change the color represented by its "
			a href="#concept-fe-value" id="color-state-(type=color):concept-fe-value-2" value
			- ", as obtained from "
			a data-x-internal=parsed-as-a-css-color-value href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-color/#parse-a-css-color-value" id="color-state-(type=color):parsed-as-a-css-color-value" parsing
			- " it. User agents must not allow the user to set the "
			a href="#concept-fe-value" id="color-state-(type=color):concept-fe-value-3" value
			- " to a string that running "
			a href="#update-a-color-well-control-color" id="color-state-(type=color):update-a-color-well-control-color-2" "update a color well control color"
			- " for the element would not set it to. If the user agent provides a user interface for selecting a CSS color, then the "
