			div class=feature {
				p {
					a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTML/Element/input/checkbox" title="<input> elements of type checkbox are rendered by default as boxes that are checked (ticked) when activated, like you might see in an official government paper form. The exact appearance depends upon the operating system configuration under which the browser is running. Generally this is a square but it may have rounded corners. A checkbox allows you to select single values for submission in a form (or not)." "Element/input/checkbox"
				}
				p class=all-engines-text "Support in all current engines."
				div class=support {
					span class="firefox yes" {
						span Firefox
						span "1+"
					}
					span class="safari yes" {
						span Safari
						span "1+"
					}
					span class="chrome yes" {
						span Chrome
						span "1+"
					}
					hr
					span class="opera unknown" {
						span Opera
						span ?
					}
					span class="edge_blink yes" {
						span Edge
						span "79+"
					}
					hr
