		p {
			- "The "
			dfn data-dfn-for=input data-dfn-type=element-attr id=attr-input-list {
				code list
			}
			- " attribute is used to identify an element that lists predefined options suggested to the user."
		}
		p {
			- "If present, its value must be the "
			a data-x-internal=concept-id href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-id" id=the-list-attribute:concept-id ID
			- " of a "
			code id=the-list-attribute:the-datalist-element {
				a href="#the-datalist-element" datalist
			}
			- " element in the same "
			a data-x-internal=tree href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-tree" id=the-list-attribute:tree tree
			- .
		}
		p {
			- "The "
			dfn id=concept-input-list "suggestions source element"
			- " is the first element in the "
			a data-x-internal=tree href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-tree" id=the-list-attribute:tree-2 tree
			- " in "
			a data-x-internal=tree-order href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-tree-order" id=the-list-attribute:tree-order "tree order"
			- " to have an "
			a data-x-internal=concept-id href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-id" id=the-list-attribute:concept-id-2 ID
			- " equal to the value of the "
			code id=the-list-attribute:attr-input-list-2 {
				a href="#attr-input-list" list
			}
			- " attribute, if that element is a "
			code id=the-list-attribute:the-datalist-element-2 {
				a href="#the-datalist-element" datalist
			}
			- " element. If there is no "
			code id=the-list-attribute:attr-input-list-3 {
				a href="#attr-input-list" list
			}
			- " attribute, or if there is no element with that "
			a data-x-internal=concept-id href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-id" id=the-list-attribute:concept-id-3 ID
			- ", or if the first element with that "
			a data-x-internal=concept-id href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-id" id=the-list-attribute:concept-id-4 ID
			- " is not a "
			code id=the-list-attribute:the-datalist-element-3 {
				a href="#the-datalist-element" datalist
			}
			- " element, then there is no "
			a href="#concept-input-list" id=the-list-attribute:concept-input-list "suggestions source element"
			- .
		}
		p {
			- "If there is a "
			a href="#concept-input-list" id=the-list-attribute:concept-input-list-2 "suggestions source element"
			- ", then, when the user agent is allowing the user to edit the "
			code id=the-list-attribute:the-input-element {
				a href="#the-input-element" input
			}
			- " element's "
			a href="#concept-fe-value" id=the-list-attribute:concept-fe-value value
			- ", the user agent should offer the suggestions represented by the "
			a href="#concept-input-list" id=the-list-attribute:concept-input-list-3 "suggestions source element"
			- " to the user in a manner suitable for the type of control used. If appropriate, the user agent should use the suggestion's "
			a href="#concept-option-label" id=the-list-attribute:concept-option-label label
			- " and "
			a href="#concept-option-value" id=the-list-attribute:concept-option-value value
			- " to identify the suggestion to the user."
		}
		p {
			- "User agents are encouraged to filter the suggestions represented by the "
			a href="#concept-input-list" id=the-list-attribute:concept-input-list-4 "suggestions source element"
			- " when the number of suggestions is large, including only the most relevant ones (e.g. based on the user's input so far). No precise threshold is defined, but capping the list at four to seven values is reasonable. If filtering based on the user's input, user agents should search within both the "
			a href="#concept-option-label" id=the-list-attribute:concept-option-label-2 label
			- " and "
			a href="#concept-option-value" id=the-list-attribute:concept-option-value-2 value
			- " of the suggestions for matches. User agents should consider how input variations affect the matching process. Unicode normalization should be applied so that different underlying Unicode code point sequences, caused by different keyboard- or input-specific mechanisms, do not interfere with the matching process. Case variations should be ignored, which may require language-specific case mapping. For examples of these, see "
			cite "Character Model for the World Wide Web: String Matching"
			- ". User agents may also provide other matching features: for illustration, a few examples include matching different forms of kana to each other (or to kanji), ignoring accents, or applying spelling correction. "
			a href="#refsCHARMODNORM" "[CHARMODNORM]"
		}
		div class=example {
			p "This text field allows you to choose a type of JavaScript function."
			pre {
				code class=html {
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" input
					c- e="" type
					c- o="" "="
					c- s="" "\"text\""
					c- e="" list
					c- o="" "="
					c- s="" "\"function-types\""
					c- p="" >
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" datalist
					c- e="" id
					c- o="" "="
					c- s="" "\"function-types\""
					c- p="" >
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" option
					c- e="" value
					c- o="" "="
					c- s="" "\"function\""
					c- p="" >
					- function
					c- p="" "</"
					c- f="" option
					c- p="" >
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" option
					c- e="" value
					c- o="" "="
					c- s="" "\"async function\""
					c- p="" >
					- "async function"
					c- p="" "</"
					c- f="" option
					c- p="" >
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" option
					c- e="" value
					c- o="" "="
					c- s="" "\"function*\""
					c- p="" >
					- "generator function"
					c- p="" "</"
					c- f="" option
					c- p="" >
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" option
					c- e="" value
					c- o="" "="
					c- s="" "\"=>\""
					c- p="" >
					- "arrow function"
					c- p="" "</"
					c- f="" option
					c- p="" >
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" option
					c- e="" value
					c- o="" "="
					c- s="" "\"async =>\""
					c- p="" >
					- "async arrow function"
					c- p="" "</"
					c- f="" option
					c- p="" >
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" option
					c- e="" value
					c- o="" "="
					c- s="" "\"async function*\""
					c- p="" >
					- "async generator function"
					c- p="" "</"
					c- f="" option
					c- p="" >
					c- p="" "</"
					c- f="" datalist
					c- p="" >
				}
			}
			p {
				- "For user agents that follow the above suggestions, both the "
				a href="#concept-option-label" id=the-list-attribute:concept-option-label-3 label
				- " and "
				a href="#concept-option-value" id=the-list-attribute:concept-option-value-3 value
				- " would be shown:"
			}
			p {
				img alt="A text box with a drop down button on the right hand side; with, below, a drop down box containing a list of the six values the left and the six labels on the right." class=darkmode-aware height="150" src="/images/sample-datalist.svg" width="280"
			}
			p {
				- "Then, typing \""
				kbd arrow
				- "\" or \""
				kbd "=>"
				- "\" would filter the list to the entries with labels \"arrow function\" and \"async arrow function\". Typing \""
				kbd generator
				- "\" or \""
				kbd *
				- "\" would filter the list to the entries with labels \"generator function\" and \"async generator function\"."
			}
		}
		p class=note "As always, user agents are free to make user interface decisions which are appropriate for their particular requirements and for the user's particular circumstances. However, this has historically been an area of confusion for implementers, web developers, and users alike, so we've given some \"should\" suggestions above."
		p "How user selections of suggestions are handled depends on whether the element is a control accepting a single value only, or whether it accepts multiple values:"
		dl class=switch {
			dt {
				- "If the element does not have a "
				code id=the-list-attribute:attr-input-multiple {
					a href="#attr-input-multiple" multiple
				}
				- " attribute specified or if the "
				code id=the-list-attribute:attr-input-multiple-2 {
					a href="#attr-input-multiple" multiple
				}
				- " attribute "
				a href="#do-not-apply" id=the-list-attribute:do-not-apply "does not apply"
			}
			dd {
				p {
					- "When the user selects a suggestion, the "
					code id=the-list-attribute:the-input-element-2 {
						a href="#the-input-element" input
					}
					- " element's "
					a href="#concept-fe-value" id=the-list-attribute:concept-fe-value-2 value
					- " must be set to the selected suggestion's "
					a href="#concept-option-value" id=the-list-attribute:concept-option-value-4 value
					- ", as if the user had written that value themself."
				}
			}
			dt {
				- "If the element's "
				code id=the-list-attribute:attr-input-type {
					a href="#attr-input-type" type
				}
				- " attribute is in the "
				a href="#email-state-(type=email)" id="the-list-attribute:email-state-(type=email)" Email
				- " state and the element has a "
				code id=the-list-attribute:attr-input-multiple-3 {
					a href="#attr-input-multiple" multiple
				}
				- " attribute specified"
			}
			dd {
				p {
					- "When the user selects a suggestion, the user agent must either add a new entry to the "
					code id=the-list-attribute:the-input-element-3 {
						a href="#the-input-element" input
					}
					- " element's "
					a href="#concept-fe-values" id=the-list-attribute:concept-fe-values values
					- ", whose value is the selected suggestion's "
					a href="#concept-option-value" id=the-list-attribute:concept-option-value-5 value
					- ", or change an existing entry in the "
					code id=the-list-attribute:the-input-element-4 {
						a href="#the-input-element" input
					}
					- " element's "
					a href="#concept-fe-values" id=the-list-attribute:concept-fe-values-2 values
					- " to have the value given by the selected suggestion's "
					a href="#concept-option-value" id=the-list-attribute:concept-option-value-6 value
					- ", as if the user had themself added an entry with that value, or edited an existing entry to be that value. Which behavior is to be applied depends on the user interface in an "
					a data-x-internal=implementation-defined href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#implementation-defined" id=the-list-attribute:implementation-defined implementation-defined
					- " manner."
				}
			}
		}
		hr
		p {
			- "If the "
			code id=the-list-attribute:attr-input-list-4 {
				a href="#attr-input-list" list
			}
			- " attribute "
			a href="#do-not-apply" id=the-list-attribute:do-not-apply-2 "does not apply"
			- ", there is no "
			a href="#concept-input-list" id=the-list-attribute:concept-input-list-5 "suggestions source element"
			- .
		}
		div class=example {
			p "This URL field offers some suggestions."
			pre {
				code class=html {
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" label
					c- p="" >
					- "Homepage: "
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" input
					c- e="" name
					c- o="" "="
					c- s="" hp
					c- e="" type
					c- o="" "="
					c- s="" url
					c- e="" list
					c- o="" "="
					c- s="" hpurls
					c- p="" "></"
					c- f="" label
					c- p="" >
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" datalist
					c- e="" id
					c- o="" "="
					c- s="" hpurls
					c- p="" >
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" option
					c- e="" value
					c- o="" "="
					c- s="" "\"https://www.google.com/\""
					c- e="" label
					c- o="" "="
					c- s="" "\"Google\""
					c- p="" >
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" option
					c- e="" value
					c- o="" "="
					c- s="" "\"https://www.reddit.com/\""
					c- e="" label
					c- o="" "="
					c- s="" "\"Reddit\""
					c- p="" >
					c- p="" "</"
					c- f="" datalist
					c- p="" >
				}
