			p "Other URLs from the user's history might show also; this is up to the user agent."
		}
		div class=example {
			p "This example demonstrates how to design a form that uses the autocompletion list feature while still degrading usefully in legacy user agents."
			p {
				- "If the autocompletion list is merely an aid, and is not important to the content, then simply using a "
				code id=the-list-attribute:the-datalist-element-4 {
					a href="#the-datalist-element" datalist
				}
				- " element with children "
				code id=the-list-attribute:the-option-element {
					a href="#the-option-element" option
				}
				- " elements is enough. To prevent the values from being rendered in legacy user agents, they need to be placed inside the "
				code id=the-list-attribute:attr-option-value {
					a href="#attr-option-value" value
				}
				- " attribute instead of inline."
			}
			pre {
				code class=html {
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" p
					c- p="" >
					c- p="" <
