		p {
			- "The "
			dfn data-dfn-for=input data-dfn-type=element-attr id=attr-input-placeholder {
				code placeholder
			}
			- " attribute represents a "
			em short
			- " hint (a word or short phrase) intended to aid the user with data entry when the control has no value. A hint could be a sample value or a brief description of the expected format. The attribute, if specified, must have a value that contains no U+000A LINE FEED (LF) or U+000D CARRIAGE RETURN (CR) characters."
		}
		p {
			- "The "
			code id=the-placeholder-attribute:attr-input-placeholder-2 {
				a href="#attr-input-placeholder" placeholder
			}
			- " attribute should not be used as an alternative to a "
			code id=the-placeholder-attribute:the-label-element {
				a href="#the-label-element" label
			}
			- ". For a longer hint or other advisory text, the "
			code id=the-placeholder-attribute:attr-title {
				a href="#attr-title" title
			}
			- " attribute is more appropriate."
		}
		p class=note {
			- "These mechanisms are very similar but subtly different: the hint given by the control's "
			code id=the-placeholder-attribute:the-label-element-2 {
				a href="#the-label-element" label
			}
			- " is shown at all times; the short hint given in the "
			code id=the-placeholder-attribute:attr-input-placeholder-3 {
				a href="#attr-input-placeholder" placeholder
			}
			- " attribute is shown before the user enters a value; and the hint in the "
			code id=the-placeholder-attribute:attr-title-2 {
				a href="#attr-title" title
			}
			- " attribute is shown when the user requests further help."
		}
		p {
			- "User agents should present this hint to the user, after having "
			a data-x-internal=strip-newlines href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#strip-newlines" id=the-placeholder-attribute:strip-newlines "stripped newlines"
			- " from it, when the element's "
			a href="#concept-fe-value" id=the-placeholder-attribute:concept-fe-value value
			- " is the empty string, especially if the control is not "
			a href="#focused" id=the-placeholder-attribute:focused focused
			- .
		}
		p {
			- "If a user agent normally doesn't show this hint to the user when the control is "
			a href="#focused" id=the-placeholder-attribute:focused-2 focused
			- ", then the user agent should nonetheless show the hint for the control if it was focused as a result of the "
			code id=the-placeholder-attribute:attr-fe-autofocus {
				a href="#attr-fe-autofocus" autofocus
			}
			- " attribute, since in that case the user will not have had an opportunity to examine the control before focusing it."
		}
