				}
				p class=all-engines-text "Support in all current engines."
				div class=support {
					span class="firefox yes" {
						span Firefox
						span "16+"
					}
					span class="safari yes" {
						span Safari
						span "6+"
					}
					span class="chrome yes" {
						span Chrome
						span "6+"
					}
					hr
					span class="opera yes" {
						span Opera
						span "11+"
					}
					span class="edge_blink yes" {
						span Edge
						span "79+"
					}
					hr
					span class="edge yes" {
						span "Edge (Legacy)"
						span "18"
					}
					span class="ie no" {
						span "Internet Explorer"
						span No
					}
					hr
					span class="firefox_android unknown" {
						span "Firefox Android"
						span ?
					}
					span class="safari_ios yes" {
						span "Safari iOS"
						span "10.3+"
					}
					span class="chrome_android unknown" {
						span "Chrome Android"
						span ?
					}
					span class="webview_android no" {
						span "WebView Android"
						span No
					}
					span class="samsunginternet_android unknown" {
						span "Samsung Internet"
						span ?
					}
					span class="opera_android yes" {
						span "Opera Android"
						span "11+"
					}
				}
			}
		}
		p {
			- "The "
			dfn data-dfn-for=meter data-dfn-type=element-attr id=attr-meter-min {
				code min
			}
			- " attribute specifies the lower bound of the range, and the "
			dfn data-dfn-for=meter data-dfn-type=element-attr id=attr-meter-max {
				code max
			}
			- " attribute specifies the upper bound. The "
			dfn data-dfn-for=meter data-dfn-type=element-attr id=attr-meter-value {
				code value
			}
			- " attribute specifies the value to have the gauge indicate as the \"measured\" value."
		}
		p {
			- "The other three attributes can be used to segment the gauge's range into \"low\", \"medium\", and \"high\" parts, and to indicate which part of the gauge is the \"optimum\" part. The "
			dfn data-dfn-for=meter data-dfn-type=element-attr id=attr-meter-low {
				code low
			}
			- " attribute specifies the range that is considered to be the \"low\" part, and the "
			dfn data-dfn-for=meter data-dfn-type=element-attr id=attr-meter-high {
				code high
			}
			- " attribute specifies the range that is considered to be the \"high\" part. The "
			dfn data-dfn-for=meter data-dfn-type=element-attr id=attr-meter-optimum {
				code optimum
			}
			- " attribute gives the position that is \"optimum\"; if that is higher than the \"high\" value then this indicates that the higher the value, the better; if it's lower than the \"low\" mark then it indicates that lower values are better, and naturally if it is in between then it indicates that neither high nor low values are good."
		}
		p {
			strong "Authoring requirements"
			- ": The "
			code id=the-meter-element:attr-meter-value-2 {
				a href="#attr-meter-value" value
			}
			- " attribute must be specified. The "
			code id=the-meter-element:attr-meter-value-3 {
				a href="#attr-meter-value" value
			}
			- ", "
			code id=the-meter-element:attr-meter-min-2 {
				a href="#attr-meter-min" min
			}
			- ", "
			code id=the-meter-element:attr-meter-low-2 {
				a href="#attr-meter-low" low
			}
			- ", "
			code id=the-meter-element:attr-meter-high-2 {
				a href="#attr-meter-high" high
			}
			- ", "
			code id=the-meter-element:attr-meter-max-2 {
				a href="#attr-meter-max" max
			}
			- ", and "
			code id=the-meter-element:attr-meter-optimum-2 {
				a href="#attr-meter-optimum" optimum
			}
			- " attributes, when present, must have values that are "
			a href="#valid-floating-point-number" id=the-meter-element:valid-floating-point-number "valid floating-point numbers"
			- .
		}
		p "In addition, the attributes' values are further constrained:"
		p {
			- "Let "
			var value
			- " be the "
			code id=the-meter-element:attr-meter-value-4 {
				a href="#attr-meter-value" value
			}
			- " attribute's number."
		}
		p {
			- "If the "
			code id=the-meter-element:attr-meter-min-3 {
				a href="#attr-meter-min" min
			}
			- " attribute is specified, then let "
			var minimum
			- " be that attribute's value; otherwise, let it be zero."
		}
		p {
			- "If the "
			code id=the-meter-element:attr-meter-max-3 {
				a href="#attr-meter-max" max
			}
			- " attribute is specified, then let "
			var maximum
			- " be that attribute's value; otherwise, let it be 1.0."
		}
		p "The following inequalities must hold, as applicable:"
		ul {
			li {
				p {
					var minimum
					- " ≤ "
					var value
					- " ≤ "
					var maximum
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					var minimum
					- " ≤ "
					code id=the-meter-element:attr-meter-low-3 {
						a href="#attr-meter-low" low
					}
					- " ≤ "
					var maximum
					- " (if "
					code id=the-meter-element:attr-meter-low-4 {
						a href="#attr-meter-low" low
					}
					- " is specified)"
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					var minimum
					- " ≤ "
					code id=the-meter-element:attr-meter-high-3 {
						a href="#attr-meter-high" high
					}
					- " ≤ "
					var maximum
					- " (if "
					code id=the-meter-element:attr-meter-high-4 {
						a href="#attr-meter-high" high
					}
					- " is specified)"
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					var minimum
					- " ≤ "
					code id=the-meter-element:attr-meter-optimum-3 {
						a href="#attr-meter-optimum" optimum
					}
					- " ≤ "
					var maximum
					- " (if "
					code id=the-meter-element:attr-meter-optimum-4 {
						a href="#attr-meter-optimum" optimum
					}
					- " is specified)"
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					code id=the-meter-element:attr-meter-low-5 {
						a href="#attr-meter-low" low
					}
					- " ≤ "
					code id=the-meter-element:attr-meter-high-5 {
						a href="#attr-meter-high" high
					}
					- " (if both "
					code id=the-meter-element:attr-meter-low-6 {
						a href="#attr-meter-low" low
					}
					- " and "
					code id=the-meter-element:attr-meter-high-6 {
						a href="#attr-meter-high" high
					}
					- " are specified)"
				}
			}
		}
		p class=note "If no minimum or maximum is specified, then the range is assumed to be 0..1, and the value thus has to be within that range."
		p {
			- "Authors are encouraged to include a textual representation of the gauge's state in the element's contents, for users of user agents that do not support the "
			code id=the-meter-element:the-meter-element-5 {
				a href="#the-meter-element" meter
			}
			- " element."
		}
		p {
			- "When used with "
			a href="#microdata" id=the-meter-element:microdata microdata
			- ", the "
			code id=the-meter-element:the-meter-element-6 {
				a href="#the-meter-element" meter
			}
			- " element's "
			code id=the-meter-element:attr-meter-value-5 {
				a href="#attr-meter-value" value
			}
			- " attribute provides the element's machine-readable value."
		}
		div class=example {
			p "The following examples show three gauges that would all be three-quarters full:"
			pre {
				code class=html {
					- "Storage space usage: "
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" meter
					c- e="" value
					c- o="" "="
					c- s="" "6"
					c- e="" max
					c- o="" "="
					c- s="" "8"
					c- p="" >
					- "6 blocks used (out of 8 total)"
					c- p="" "</"
					c- f="" meter
					c- p="" >
				}
			}
			pre {
				code class=html {
					- "Voter turnout: "
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" meter
					c- e="" value
					c- o="" "="
					c- s="" "0.75"
					c- p="" ><
					c- f="" img
					c- e="" alt
					c- o="" "="
					c- s="" "\"75%\""
					c- e="" src
					c- o="" "="
					c- s="" "\"graph75.png\""
					c- p="" "></"
					c- f="" meter
					c- p="" >
				}
			}
			pre {
				code class=html {
					- "Tickets sold: "
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" meter
					c- e="" min
					c- o="" "="
					c- s="" "\"0\""
					c- e="" max
					c- o="" "="
					c- s="" "\"100\""
					c- e="" value
					c- o="" "="
					c- s="" "\"75\""
					c- p="" "></"
					c- f="" meter
					c- p="" >
				}
			}
			p "The following example is incorrect use of the element, because it doesn't give a range (and since the default maximum is 1, both of the gauges would end up looking maxed out):"
			pre class=bad {
				code class=html {
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" p
					c- p="" >
					- "The grapefruit pie had a radius of "
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" meter
					c- e="" value
					c- o="" "="
					c- s="" "12"
					c- p="" >
					- "12cm"
					c- p="" "</"
					c- f="" meter
					c- p="" >
					- " and a height of "
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" meter
					c- e="" value
					c- o="" "="
					c- s="" "2"
					c- p="" >
					- "2cm"
					c- p="" "</"
					c- f="" meter
					c- p="" >
					- .
					c- p="" "</"
					c- f="" p
					c- p="" >
					c- c="" "<!-- "
					strong {
						c- c="" BAD!
					}
					c- c="" " -->"
				}
			}
			p "Instead, one would either not include the meter element, or use the meter element with a defined range to give the dimensions in context compared to other pies:"
			pre {
				code class=html {
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" p
					c- p="" >
					- "The grapefruit pie had a radius of 12cm and a height of 2cm."
					c- p="" "</"
					c- f="" p
					c- p="" >
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" dl
					c- p="" >
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" dt
					c- p="" >
					- "Radius: "
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" dd
					c- p="" >
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" meter
					c- e="" min
					c- o="" "="
					c- s="" "0"
					c- e="" max
					c- o="" "="
					c- s="" "20"
					c- e="" value
					c- o="" "="
					c- s="" "12"
					c- p="" >
					- "12cm"
					c- p="" "</"
					c- f="" meter
					c- p="" >
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" dt
					c- p="" >
					- "Height: "
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" dd
					c- p="" >
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" meter
					c- e="" min
					c- o="" "="
					c- s="" "0"
					c- e="" max
					c- o="" "="
					c- s="" "10"
					c- e="" value
					c- o="" "="
					c- s="" "2"
					c- p="" >
					- "2cm"
					c- p="" "</"
					c- f="" meter
					c- p="" >
					c- p="" "</"
					c- f="" dl
					c- p="" >
				}
			}
		}
		p {
			- "There is no explicit way to specify units in the "
			code id=the-meter-element:the-meter-element-7 {
				a href="#the-meter-element" meter
			}
			- " element, but the units may be specified in the "
			code id=the-meter-element:attr-title {
				a href="#attr-title" title
			}
			- " attribute in free-form text."
		}
		div class=example {
			p "The example above could be extended to mention the units:"
			pre {
				code class=html {
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" dl
					c- p="" >
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" dt
					c- p="" >
					- "Radius: "
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" dd
					c- p="" >
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" meter
					c- e="" min
					c- o="" "="
					c- s="" "0"
					c- e="" max
					c- o="" "="
					c- s="" "20"
					c- e="" value
					c- o="" "="
					c- s="" "12"
					c- e="" title
					c- o="" "="
					c- s="" "\"centimeters\""
					c- p="" >
					- "12cm"
					c- p="" "</"
					c- f="" meter
					c- p="" >
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" dt
					c- p="" >
					- "Height: "
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" dd
					c- p="" >
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" meter
					c- e="" min
					c- o="" "="
					c- s="" "0"
					c- e="" max
					c- o="" "="
					c- s="" "10"
					c- e="" value
					c- o="" "="
					c- s="" "2"
					c- e="" title
					c- o="" "="
					c- s="" "\"centimeters\""
					c- p="" >
					- "2cm"
					c- p="" "</"
					c- f="" meter
					c- p="" >
					c- p="" "</"
					c- f="" dl
					c- p="" >
				}
			}
		}
		p {
			strong "User agent requirements"
			- ": User agents must parse the "
			code id=the-meter-element:attr-meter-min-4 {
				a href="#attr-meter-min" min
			}
			- ", "
			code id=the-meter-element:attr-meter-max-4 {
				a href="#attr-meter-max" max
			}
			- ", "
			code id=the-meter-element:attr-meter-value-6 {
				a href="#attr-meter-value" value
			}
			- ", "
			code id=the-meter-element:attr-meter-low-7 {
				a href="#attr-meter-low" low
			}
			- ", "
			code id=the-meter-element:attr-meter-high-7 {
				a href="#attr-meter-high" high
			}
			- ", and "
			code id=the-meter-element:attr-meter-optimum-5 {
				a href="#attr-meter-optimum" optimum
			}
			- " attributes using the "
			a href="#rules-for-parsing-floating-point-number-values" id=the-meter-element:rules-for-parsing-floating-point-number-values "rules for parsing floating-point number values"
			- .
		}
		p "User agents must then use all these numbers to obtain values for six points on the gauge, as follows. (The order in which these are evaluated is important, as some of the values refer to earlier ones.)"
		dl {
			dt {
				- "The "
				dfn id=concept-meter-minimum "minimum value"
			}
			dd {
				p {
					- "If the "
					code id=the-meter-element:attr-meter-min-5 {
						a href="#attr-meter-min" min
					}
					- " attribute is specified and a value could be parsed out of it, then the minimum value is that value. Otherwise, the minimum value is zero."
				}
			}
			dt {
				- "The "
				dfn id=concept-meter-maximum "maximum value"
			}
			dd {
				p {
					- "If the "
					code id=the-meter-element:attr-meter-max-5 {
						a href="#attr-meter-max" max
					}
					- " attribute is specified and a value could be parsed out of it, then the candidate maximum value is that value. Otherwise, the candidate maximum value is 1.0."
				}
				p "If the candidate maximum value is greater than or equal to the minimum value, then the maximum value is the candidate maximum value. Otherwise, the maximum value is the same as the minimum value."
			}
			dt {
				- "The "
				dfn id=concept-meter-actual "actual value"
			}
			dd {
				p {
					- "If the "
					code id=the-meter-element:attr-meter-value-7 {
						a href="#attr-meter-value" value
					}
					- " attribute is specified and a value could be parsed out of it, then that value is the candidate actual value. Otherwise, the candidate actual value is zero."
				}
				p "If the candidate actual value is less than the minimum value, then the actual value is the minimum value."
				p "Otherwise, if the candidate actual value is greater than the maximum value, then the actual value is the maximum value."
				p "Otherwise, the actual value is the candidate actual value."
			}
			dt {
				- "The "
				dfn id=concept-meter-low "low boundary"
			}
			dd {
				p {
					- "If the "
					code id=the-meter-element:attr-meter-low-8 {
						a href="#attr-meter-low" low
					}
					- " attribute is specified and a value could be parsed out of it, then the candidate low boundary is that value. Otherwise, the candidate low boundary is the same as the minimum value."
				}
				p "If the candidate low boundary is less than the minimum value, then the low boundary is the minimum value."
				p "Otherwise, if the candidate low boundary is greater than the maximum value, then the low boundary is the maximum value."
				p "Otherwise, the low boundary is the candidate low boundary."
			}
			dt {
				- "The "
				dfn id=concept-meter-high "high boundary"
			}
			dd {
				p {
					- "If the "
					code id=the-meter-element:attr-meter-high-8 {
						a href="#attr-meter-high" high
					}
					- " attribute is specified and a value could be parsed out of it, then the candidate high boundary is that value. Otherwise, the candidate high boundary is the same as the maximum value."
				}
				p "If the candidate high boundary is less than the low boundary, then the high boundary is the low boundary."
				p "Otherwise, if the candidate high boundary is greater than the maximum value, then the high boundary is the maximum value."
				p "Otherwise, the high boundary is the candidate high boundary."
			}
			dt {
				- "The "
				dfn id=concept-meter-optimum "optimum point"
			}
			dd {
				p {
					- "If the "
					code id=the-meter-element:attr-meter-optimum-6 {
						a href="#attr-meter-optimum" optimum
					}
					- " attribute is specified and a value could be parsed out of it, then the candidate optimum point is that value. Otherwise, the candidate optimum point is the midpoint between the minimum value and the maximum value."
				}
				p "If the candidate optimum point is less than the minimum value, then the optimum point is the minimum value."
				p "Otherwise, if the candidate optimum point is greater than the maximum value, then the optimum point is the maximum value."
				p "Otherwise, the optimum point is the candidate optimum point."
			}
		}
		p "All of which will result in the following inequalities all being true:"
		ul {
			li {
				p "minimum value ≤ actual value ≤ maximum value"
			}
			li {
				p "minimum value ≤ low boundary ≤ high boundary ≤ maximum value"
			}
			li {
				p "minimum value ≤ optimum point ≤ maximum value"
			}
		}
		p {
			strong "UA requirements for regions of the gauge"
			- ": If the optimum point is equal to the low boundary or the high boundary, or anywhere in between them, then the region between the low and high boundaries of the gauge must be treated as the optimum region, and the low and high parts, if any, must be treated as suboptimal. Otherwise, if the optimum point is less than the low boundary, then the region between the minimum value and the low boundary must be treated as the optimum region, the region from the low boundary up to the high boundary must be treated as a suboptimal region, and the remaining region must be treated as an even less good region. Finally, if the optimum point is higher than the high boundary, then the situation is reversed; the region between the high boundary and the maximum value must be treated as the optimum region, the region from the high boundary down to the low boundary must be treated as a suboptimal region, and the remaining region must be treated as an even less good region."
		}
		p {
			strong "UA requirements for showing the gauge"
			- ": When representing a "
			code id=the-meter-element:the-meter-element-8 {
				a href="#the-meter-element" meter
			}
			- " element to the user, the UA should indicate the relative position of the actual value to the minimum and maximum values, and the relationship between the actual value and the three regions of the gauge."
		}
		div class=example {
			p "The following markup:"
			pre {
				code class=html {
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" h3
					c- p="" >
					- "Suggested groups"
					c- p="" "</"
					c- f="" h3
					c- p="" >
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" menu
					c- p="" >
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" li
					c- p="" ><
					c- f="" a
					c- e="" href
					c- o="" "="
					c- s="" "\"?cmd=hsg\""
					c- e="" onclick
					c- o="" "="
					c- s="" "\"hideSuggestedGroups()\""
					c- p="" >
					- "Hide suggested groups"
					c- p="" "</"
					c- f="" a
					c- p="" "></"
					c- f="" li
					c- p="" >
					c- p="" "</"
					c- f="" menu
					c- p="" >
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" ul
					c- p="" >
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" li
					c- p="" >
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" p
					c- p="" ><
					c- f="" a
					c- e="" href
					c- o="" "="
					c- s="" "\"/group/comp.infosystems.www.authoring.stylesheets/view\""
					c- p="" >
					- comp.infosystems.www.authoring.stylesheets
					c- p="" "</"
					c- f="" a
					c- p="" >
					- " - "
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" a
					c- e="" href
					c- o="" "="
					c- s="" "\"/group/comp.infosystems.www.authoring.stylesheets/subscribe\""
					c- p="" >
					- join
					c- p="" "</"
					c- f="" a
					c- p="" "></"
					c- f="" p
					c- p="" >
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" p
					c- p="" >
					- "Group description: "
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" strong
					c- p="" >
					- "Layout/presentation on the WWW."
					c- p="" "</"
					c- f="" strong
					c- p="" "></"
					c- f="" p
					c- p="" >
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" p
					c- p="" >
					strong {
						c- p="" <
						c- f="" meter
						c- e="" value
						c- o="" "="
						c- s="" "\"0.5\""
						c- p="" >
						- "Moderate activity,"
						c- p="" "</"
						c- f="" meter
