		}
		h5 id=a-form-control's-value {
			span class=secno "4.10.17.1"
			- " A form control's value"
			a class=self-link href="#a-form-control's-value"
		}
		p {
			- "Most form controls have a "
			dfn id=concept-fe-value value
			- " and a "
			dfn id=concept-fe-checked checkedness
			- ". (The latter is only used by "
			code id=a-form-control's-value:the-input-element {
				a href="#the-input-element" input
			}
			- " elements.) These are used to describe how the user interacts with the control."
		}
		p {
			- "A control's "
			a href="#concept-fe-value" id=a-form-control's-value:concept-fe-value value
			- " is its internal state. As such, it might not match the user's current input."
		}
		p class=example {
			- "For instance, if a user enters the word \""
			kbd three
			- "\" into "
			a href="#number-state-(type=number)" id="a-form-control's-value:number-state-(type=number)" "a numeric field"
			- " that expects digits, the user's input would be the string \"three\" but the control's "
			a href="#concept-fe-value" id=a-form-control's-value:concept-fe-value-2 value
			- " would remain unchanged. Or, if a user enters the email address \""
			kbd " awesome@example.com"
			- "\" (with leading whitespace) into "
			a href="#email-state-(type=email)" id="a-form-control's-value:email-state-(type=email)" "an email field"
			- ", the user's input would be the string \" awesome@example.com\" but the browser's UI for email fields might translate that into a "
			a href="#concept-fe-value" id=a-form-control's-value:concept-fe-value-3 value
			- " of \""
			code awesome@example.com
			- "\" (without the leading whitespace)."
		}
		p id=concept-input-value-dirty-flag {
			span id=concept-textarea-dirty
			code id=a-form-control's-value:the-input-element-2 {
				a href="#the-input-element" input
			}
			- " and "
			code id=a-form-control's-value:the-textarea-element {
				a href="#the-textarea-element" textarea
			}
			- " elements have a "
			dfn id=concept-fe-dirty "dirty value flag"
			- ". This is used to track the interaction between the "
			a href="#concept-fe-value" id=a-form-control's-value:concept-fe-value-4 value
			- " and default value. If it is false, "
			a href="#concept-fe-value" id=a-form-control's-value:concept-fe-value-5 value
			- " mirrors the default value. If it is true, the default value is ignored."
		}
		p {
			code id=a-form-control's-value:the-input-element-3 {
