			- "Other than "
			code isindex
			- ", any non-empty value for "
			code id=naming-form-controls:-the-name-attribute:attr-form-name {
				a href="#attr-form-name" name
			}
			- " is allowed. An "
			a data-x-internal=ascii-case-insensitive href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ascii-case-insensitive" id=naming-form-controls:-the-name-attribute:ascii-case-insensitive "ASCII case-insensitive"
			- " match for the name "
			dfn id=attr-fe-name-charset {
				code _charset_
			}
			- " is special: if used as the name of a "
			a href="#hidden-state-(type=hidden)" id="naming-form-controls:-the-name-attribute:hidden-state-(type=hidden)" Hidden
			- " control with no "
			code id=naming-form-controls:-the-name-attribute:attr-input-value {
				a href="#attr-input-value" value
			}
			- " attribute, then during submission the "
			code id=naming-form-controls:-the-name-attribute:attr-input-value-2 {
				a href="#attr-input-value" value
			}
			- " attribute is automatically given a value consisting of the submission character encoding."
		}
		p {
			- "The "
			dfn data-dfn-for=HTMLInputElement,HTMLButtonElement,HTMLSelectElement,HTMLTextAreaElement,HTMLOutputElement,HTMLFieldSetElement data-dfn-type=attribute id=dom-fe-name {
				code name
			}
			- " IDL attribute must "
			a href="#reflect" id=naming-form-controls:-the-name-attribute:reflect reflect
			- " the "
			code id=naming-form-controls:-the-name-attribute:attr-fe-name-2 {
				a href="#attr-fe-name" name
			}
			- " content attribute."
		}
		div class=note {
			p {
				- "DOM clobbering is a common cause of security issues. Avoid using the names of built-in form properties with the "
				code id=naming-form-controls:-the-name-attribute:attr-fe-name-3 {
					a href="#attr-fe-name" name
				}
				- " content attribute."
			}
			p {
				- "In this example, the "
				code id=naming-form-controls:-the-name-attribute:the-input-element {
					a href="#the-input-element" input
				}
				- " element overrides the built-in "
				code id=naming-form-controls:-the-name-attribute:attr-fs-method {
					a href="#attr-fs-method" method
				}
				- " property:"
			}
			pre {
				code class=js {
					c- a="" let
					- " form "
					c- o="" "="
					- " document"
					c- p="" .
					- createElement
					c- p="" "("
					c- u="" "\"form\""
					c- p="" ");"
					c- a="" let
					- " input "
					c- o="" "="
					- " document"
					c- p="" .
					- createElement
					c- p="" "("
					c- u="" "\"input\""
					c- p="" ");"
					- " form"
					c- p="" .
					- appendChild
					c- p="" "("
					- input
					c- p="" ");"
					- " form"
					c- p="" .
					- method
					c- p="" ";"
					c- c1="" "// => \"get\""
					- " input"
					c- p="" .
					- "name "
					c- o="" "="
					c- u="" "\"method\""
					c- p="" ";"
					c- c1="" "// DOM clobbering occurs here"
					- " form"
					c- p="" .
					- "method "
					c- o="" "==="
					- " input"
					c- p="" ";"
					c- c1="" "// => true"
				}
			}
			p {
				- "Since the input name takes precedence over built-in form properties, the JavaScript reference "
				code form.method
				- " will point to the "
				code id=naming-form-controls:-the-name-attribute:the-input-element-2 {
					a href="#the-input-element" input
				}
				- " element named \"method\" instead of the built-in "
				code id=naming-form-controls:-the-name-attribute:attr-fs-method-2 {
					a href="#attr-fs-method" method
				}
				- " property."
			}
		}
		h5 id=submitting-element-directionality:-the-dirname-attribute {
			span class=secno "4.10.18.2"
			- " Submitting element directionality: the "
			code id=submitting-element-directionality:-the-dirname-attribute:attr-fe-dirname {
				a href="#attr-fe-dirname" dirname
			}
			- " attribute"
			a class=self-link href="#submitting-element-directionality:-the-dirname-attribute"
		}
		div class="mdn-anno wrapped before" {
			button class=mdn-anno-btn onclick="toggleStatus(this)" {
				b class=all-engines-flag title="Support in all current engines." ✔
				span MDN
			}
			div class=feature {
				p {
					a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTML/Element/input#dirname" title="The <input> HTML element is used to create interactive controls for web-based forms in order to accept data from the user; a wide variety of types of input data and control widgets are available, depending on the device and user agent. The <input> element is one of the most powerful and complex in all of HTML due to the sheer number of combinations of input types and attributes." "Element/input#dirname"
				}
				p class=all-engines-text "Support in all current engines."
				div class=support {
					span class="firefox yes" {
						span Firefox
						span "116+"
					}
					span class="safari yes" {
						span Safari
						span "6+"
					}
					span class="chrome yes" {
						span Chrome
						span "17+"
					}
					hr
					span class="opera yes" {
						span Opera
						span "12.1+"
					}
					span class="edge_blink yes" {
						span Edge
						span "79+"
					}
					hr
					span class="edge unknown" {
						span "Edge (Legacy)"
						span ?
					}
					span class="ie no" {
						span "Internet Explorer"
						span No
					}
					hr
					span class="firefox_android unknown" {
						span "Firefox Android"
						span ?
					}
					span class="safari_ios unknown" {
						span "Safari iOS"
						span ?
					}
					span class="chrome_android unknown" {
						span "Chrome Android"
						span ?
					}
					span class="webview_android unknown" {
						span "WebView Android"
						span ?
					}
					span class="samsunginternet_android unknown" {
						span "Samsung Internet"
						span ?
					}
					span class="opera_android yes" {
						span "Opera Android"
						span "12.1+"
					}
				}
			}
		}
		p {
			- "The "
			dfn data-dfn-for=input,textarea data-dfn-type=element-attr id=attr-fe-dirname {
				code dirname
			}
			- " attribute on a form control element enables the submission of "
			a href="#the-directionality" id=submitting-element-directionality:-the-dirname-attribute:the-directionality "the directionality"
			- " of the element, and gives the name of the control that contains this value during "
			a href="#form-submission-2" id=submitting-element-directionality:-the-dirname-attribute:form-submission-2 "form submission"
			- ". If such an attribute is specified, its value must not be the empty string."
		}
		div class=example {
			p "In this example, a form contains a text control and a submission button:"
			pre {
				code class=html {
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" form
					c- e="" action
					c- o="" "="
					c- s="" "\"addcomment.cgi\""
					c- e="" method
					c- o="" "="
					c- s="" post
					c- p="" >
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" p
					c- p="" ><
					c- f="" label
					c- p="" >
					- "Comment: "
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" input
					c- e="" type
					c- o="" "="
					c- s="" text
					c- e="" name
					c- o="" "="
					c- s="" "\"comment\""
					c- e="" dirname
					c- o="" "="
					c- s="" "\"comment.dir\""
					c- e="" required
					c- p="" "></"
					c- f="" label
					c- p="" "></"
					c- f="" p
					c- p="" >
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" p
					c- p="" ><
					c- f="" button
					c- e="" name
					c- o="" "="
					c- s="" "\"mode\""
					c- e="" type
					c- o="" "="
					c- s="" submit
					c- e="" value
					c- o="" "="
					c- s="" "\"add\""
					c- p="" >
					- "Post Comment"
					c- p="" "</"
					c- f="" button
					c- p="" "></"
					c- f="" p
					c- p="" >
					c- p="" "</"
					c- f="" form
					c- p="" >
				}
			}
			p "When the user submits the form, the user agent includes three fields, one called \"comment\", one called \"comment.dir\", and one called \"mode\"; so if the user types \"Hello\", the submission body might be something like:"
			pre {
				- "comment=Hello&"
				strong "comment.dir=ltr"
				- "&mode=add"
			}
			p {
				- "If the user manually switches to a right-to-left writing direction and enters \""
				span dir=rtl lang=ar مرحبا
				- "\", the submission body might be something like:"
			}
			pre {
				- "comment=%D9%85%D8%B1%D8%AD%D8%A8%D8%A7&"
				strong "comment.dir=rtl"
				- "&mode=add"
			}
		}
		h5 id=limiting-user-input-length:-the-maxlength-attribute {
			span class=secno "4.10.18.3"
			- " Limiting user input length: the "
			code id=limiting-user-input-length:-the-maxlength-attribute:attr-fe-maxlength {
				a href="#attr-fe-maxlength" maxlength
			}
			- " attribute"
			a class=self-link href="#limiting-user-input-length:-the-maxlength-attribute"
		}
		p {
			- "A "
			dfn data-dfn-for=input,textarea data-dfn-type=element-attr data-lt=maxlength id=attr-fe-maxlength {
				- "form control "
				code maxlength
				- " attribute"
			}
			- ", controlled by the "
			a href="#concept-fe-dirty" id=limiting-user-input-length:-the-maxlength-attribute:concept-fe-dirty "dirty value flag"
			- ", declares a limit on the number of characters a user can input. The number of characters is measured using "
			a data-x-internal=length href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#string-length" id=limiting-user-input-length:-the-maxlength-attribute:length length
			- " and, in the case of "
			code id=limiting-user-input-length:-the-maxlength-attribute:the-textarea-element {
				a href="#the-textarea-element" textarea
			}
			- " elements, with all newlines normalized to a single character (as opposed to CRLF pairs)."
		}
		p {
			- "If an element has its "
			a href="#attr-fe-maxlength" id=limiting-user-input-length:-the-maxlength-attribute:attr-fe-maxlength-2 {
				- "form control "
				code maxlength
				- " attribute"
			}
			- " specified, the attribute's value must be a "
			a href="#valid-non-negative-integer" id=limiting-user-input-length:-the-maxlength-attribute:valid-non-negative-integer "valid non-negative integer"
			- ". If the attribute is specified and applying the "
			a href="#rules-for-parsing-non-negative-integers" id=limiting-user-input-length:-the-maxlength-attribute:rules-for-parsing-non-negative-integers "rules for parsing non-negative integers"
			- " to its value results in a number, then that number is the element's "
			dfn id=maximum-allowed-value-length "maximum allowed value length"
			- ". If the attribute is omitted or parsing its value results in an error, then there is no "
			a href="#maximum-allowed-value-length" id=limiting-user-input-length:-the-maxlength-attribute:maximum-allowed-value-length "maximum allowed value length"
			- .
		}
		p {
			strong "Constraint validation"
			- ": If an element has a "
			a href="#maximum-allowed-value-length" id=limiting-user-input-length:-the-maxlength-attribute:maximum-allowed-value-length-2 "maximum allowed value length"
			- ", its "
			a href="#concept-fe-dirty" id=limiting-user-input-length:-the-maxlength-attribute:concept-fe-dirty-2 "dirty value flag"
			- " is true, its "
			a href="#concept-fe-value" id=limiting-user-input-length:-the-maxlength-attribute:concept-fe-value value
			- " was last changed by a user edit (as opposed to a change made by a script), and the "
			a data-x-internal=length href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#string-length" id=limiting-user-input-length:-the-maxlength-attribute:length-2 length
			- " of the element's "
			a href="#concept-fe-api-value" id=limiting-user-input-length:-the-maxlength-attribute:concept-fe-api-value "API value"
			- " is greater than the element's "
			a href="#maximum-allowed-value-length" id=limiting-user-input-length:-the-maxlength-attribute:maximum-allowed-value-length-3 "maximum allowed value length"
			- ", then the element is "
			a href="#suffering-from-being-too-long" id=limiting-user-input-length:-the-maxlength-attribute:suffering-from-being-too-long "suffering from being too long"
			- .
		}
		p {
			- "User agents may prevent the user from causing the element's "
			a href="#concept-fe-api-value" id=limiting-user-input-length:-the-maxlength-attribute:concept-fe-api-value-2 "API value"
			- " to be set to a value whose "
			a data-x-internal=length href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#string-length" id=limiting-user-input-length:-the-maxlength-attribute:length-3 length
			- " is greater than the element's "
			a href="#maximum-allowed-value-length" id=limiting-user-input-length:-the-maxlength-attribute:maximum-allowed-value-length-4 "maximum allowed value length"
			- .
		}
		p class=note {
			- "In the case of "
			code id=limiting-user-input-length:-the-maxlength-attribute:the-textarea-element-2 {
				a href="#the-textarea-element" textarea
			}
			- " elements, the "
			a href="#concept-fe-api-value" id=limiting-user-input-length:-the-maxlength-attribute:concept-fe-api-value-3 "API value"
			- " and "
			a href="#concept-fe-value" id=limiting-user-input-length:-the-maxlength-attribute:concept-fe-value-2 value
			- " differ. In particular, "
			a data-x-internal=normalize-newlines href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#normalize-newlines" id=limiting-user-input-length:-the-maxlength-attribute:normalize-newlines "newline normalization"
			- " is applied before the "
			a href="#maximum-allowed-value-length" id=limiting-user-input-length:-the-maxlength-attribute:maximum-allowed-value-length-5 "maximum allowed value length"
			- " is checked (whereas the "
			a href="#textarea-wrapping-transformation" id=limiting-user-input-length:-the-maxlength-attribute:textarea-wrapping-transformation "textarea wrapping transformation"
			- " is not applied)."
		}
		h5 id=setting-minimum-input-length-requirements:-the-minlength-attribute {
			span class=secno "4.10.18.4"
			- " Setting minimum input length requirements: the "
			code id=setting-minimum-input-length-requirements:-the-minlength-attribute:attr-fe-minlength {
