			- " is not the empty string, and the "
			a data-x-internal=length href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#string-length" id=setting-minimum-input-length-requirements:-the-minlength-attribute:length-2 length
			- " of the element's "
			a href="#concept-fe-api-value" id=setting-minimum-input-length-requirements:-the-minlength-attribute:concept-fe-api-value "API value"
			- " is less than the element's "
			a href="#minimum-allowed-value-length" id=setting-minimum-input-length-requirements:-the-minlength-attribute:minimum-allowed-value-length-5 "minimum allowed value length"
			- ", then the element is "
			a href="#suffering-from-being-too-short" id=setting-minimum-input-length-requirements:-the-minlength-attribute:suffering-from-being-too-short "suffering from being too short"
			- .
		}
		div class=example {
			p "In this example, there are four text controls. The first is required, and has to be at least 5 characters long. The other three are optional, but if the user fills one in, the user has to enter at least 10 characters."
			pre {
