		p id=more-on-address-levels {
			strong "Address levels"
			- ": The \""
			code id=autofilling-form-controls:-the-autocomplete-attribute:attr-fe-autocomplete-address-level1-2 {
				a href="#attr-fe-autocomplete-address-level1" address-level1
			}
			- "\" – \""
			code id=autofilling-form-controls:-the-autocomplete-attribute:attr-fe-autocomplete-address-level4-2 {
				a href="#attr-fe-autocomplete-address-level4" address-level4
			}
			- "\" fields are used to describe the locality of the street address. Different locales have different numbers of levels. For example, the US uses two levels (state and town), the UK uses one or two depending on the address (the post town, and in some cases the locality), and China can use three (province, city, district). The \""
			code id=autofilling-form-controls:-the-autocomplete-attribute:attr-fe-autocomplete-address-level1-3 {
				a href="#attr-fe-autocomplete-address-level1" address-level1
			}
			- "\" field represents the widest administrative division. Different locales order the fields in different ways; for example, in the US the town (level 2) precedes the state (level 1); while in Japan the prefecture (level 1) precedes the city (level 2) which precedes the district (level 3). Authors are encouraged to provide forms that are presented in a way that matches the country's conventions (hiding, showing, and rearranging fields accordingly as the user changes the country)."
		}
		h6 id=autofill-processing-model {
			span class=secno "4.10.18.7.2"
			span id=processing-model-3
			- "Processing model"
			a class=self-link href="#autofill-processing-model"
		}
		p {
			- "Each "
			code id=autofill-processing-model:the-input-element {
				a href="#the-input-element" input
			}
			- " element to which the "
			code id=autofill-processing-model:attr-fe-autocomplete {
				a href="#attr-fe-autocomplete" autocomplete
			}
			- " attribute "
			a href="#concept-input-apply" id=autofill-processing-model:concept-input-apply applies
			- ", each "
			code id=autofill-processing-model:the-select-element {
				a href="#the-select-element" select
			}
			- " element, and each "
			code id=autofill-processing-model:the-textarea-element {
				a href="#the-textarea-element" textarea
			}
			- " element, has an "
			dfn id=autofill-hint-set "autofill hint set"
			- ", an "
			dfn id=autofill-scope "autofill scope"
			- ", an "
			dfn id=autofill-field-name "autofill field name"
			- ", a "
			dfn id=non-autofill-credential-type "non-autofill credential type"
			- ", and an "
			dfn id=idl-exposed-autofill-value "IDL-exposed autofill value"
			- .
		}
		p {
			- "The "
			a href="#autofill-field-name" id=autofill-processing-model:autofill-field-name "autofill field name"
			- " specifies the specific kind of data expected in the field, e.g. \""
			code id=autofill-processing-model:attr-fe-autocomplete-street-address {
				a href="#attr-fe-autocomplete-street-address" street-address
			}
			- "\" or \""
			code id=autofill-processing-model:attr-fe-autocomplete-cc-exp {
				a href="#attr-fe-autocomplete-cc-exp" cc-exp
			}
			- "\"."
		}
		p {
			- "The "
			a href="#autofill-hint-set" id=autofill-processing-model:autofill-hint-set "autofill hint set"
			- " identifies what address or contact information type the user agent is to look at, e.g. \""
			code id=autofill-processing-model:attr-fe-autocomplete-shipping {
				a href="#attr-fe-autocomplete-shipping" shipping
			}
			code id=autofill-processing-model:attr-fe-autocomplete-fax {
				a href="#attr-fe-autocomplete-fax" fax
			}
			- "\" or \""
			code id=autofill-processing-model:attr-fe-autocomplete-billing {
				a href="#attr-fe-autocomplete-billing" billing
			}
			- "\"."
		}
		p {
			- "The "
			a href="#non-autofill-credential-type" id=autofill-processing-model:non-autofill-credential-type "non-autofill credential type"
			- " identifies a type of "
			a data-x-internal=credman-credential href="https://w3c.github.io/webappsec-credential-management/#credential" id=autofill-processing-model:credman-credential credential
			- " that may be offered by the user agent when the user interacts with the field alongside other "
			a href="#autofill-field" id=autofill-processing-model:autofill-field "autofill field"
			- " values. If this value is \""
			code webauthn
			- "\" instead of null, selecting a credential of that type will resolve a pending "
			code id=autofill-processing-model:conditional-mediation {
				a data-x-internal=conditional-mediation href="https://w3c.github.io/webappsec-credential-management/#dom-credentialmediationrequirement-conditional" conditional
			}
			- " mediation "
			code id="autofill-processing-model:navigator.credentials.get()" {
				a data-x-internal="navigator.credentials.get()" href="https://w3c.github.io/webappsec-credential-management/#dom-credentialscontainer-get" "navigator.credentials.get()"
			}
			- " request, instead of autofilling the field."
		}
		div class=example {
			p {
				- "For example, a sign-in page could instruct the user agent to either autofill a saved password, or show a "
				a data-x-internal=public-key-credential href="https://w3c.github.io/webauthn/#public-key-credential" id=autofill-processing-model:public-key-credential "public key credential"
				- " that will resolve a pending "
				code id="autofill-processing-model:navigator.credentials.get()-2" {
					a data-x-internal="navigator.credentials.get()" href="https://w3c.github.io/webappsec-credential-management/#dom-credentialscontainer-get" "navigator.credentials.get()"
				}
				- " request. A user can select either to sign-in."
			}
			pre {
				code class=html {
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" input
					c- e="" name
					c- o="" "="
					c- s="" password
					c- e="" type
					c- o="" "="
					c- s="" password
					c- e="" autocomplete
					c- o="" "="
					c- s="" "\"current-password webauthn\""
					c- p="" >
				}
			}
		}
		p {
			- "The "
			a href="#autofill-scope" id=autofill-processing-model:autofill-scope "autofill scope"
			- " identifies the group of fields whose information concerns the same subject, and consists of the "
			a href="#autofill-hint-set" id=autofill-processing-model:autofill-hint-set-2 "autofill hint set"
			- " with, if applicable, the \""
			code section-*
			- "\" prefix, e.g. \""
			code billing
			- "\", \""
			code "section-parent shipping"
			- "\", or \""
			code "section-child shipping home"
			- "\"."
		}
		p "These values are defined as the result of running the following algorithm:"
		ol {
			li {
				p {
					- "If the element has no "
					code id=autofill-processing-model:attr-fe-autocomplete-2 {
						a href="#attr-fe-autocomplete" autocomplete
					}
					- " attribute, then jump to the step labeled "
					i default
					- .
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "Let "
					var tokens
					- " be the result of "
					a data-x-internal=split-a-string-on-spaces href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#split-on-ascii-whitespace" id=autofill-processing-model:split-a-string-on-spaces "splitting the attribute's value on ASCII whitespace"
					- .
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "If "
					var tokens
					- " is empty, then jump to the step labeled "
					i default
					- .
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "Let "
					var index
					- " be the index of the last token in "
					var tokens
					- .
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "Let "
					var field
					- " be the "
					var index
					- "th token in "
					var tokens
					- .
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "Set the "
					var category
					- ", "
					var "maximum tokens"
					- " pair to the result of "
					a href="#determine-a-field's-category" id=autofill-processing-model:determine-a-field's-category "determining a field's category"
					- " given "
					var field
					- .
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "If "
					var category
					- " is null, then jump to the step labeled "
					i default
					- .
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "If the number of tokens in "
					var tokens
					- " is greater than "
					var "maximum tokens"
					- ", then jump to the step labeled "
					i default
					- .
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "If "
					var category
					- " is Off or Automatic but the element's "
					code id=autofill-processing-model:attr-fe-autocomplete-3 {
						a href="#attr-fe-autocomplete" autocomplete
					}
					- " attribute is wearing the "
					a href="#autofill-anchor-mantle" id=autofill-processing-model:autofill-anchor-mantle "autofill anchor mantle"
					- ", then jump to the step labeled "
					i default
					- .
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "If "
					var category
					- " is Off, let the element's "
					a href="#autofill-field-name" id=autofill-processing-model:autofill-field-name-2 "autofill field name"
					- " be the string \""
					code off
					- "\", let its "
					a href="#autofill-hint-set" id=autofill-processing-model:autofill-hint-set-3 "autofill hint set"
					- " be empty, and let its "
					a href="#idl-exposed-autofill-value" id=autofill-processing-model:idl-exposed-autofill-value "IDL-exposed autofill value"
					- " be the string \""
					code off
					- "\". Then, return."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "If "
					var category
					- " is Automatic, let the element's "
					a href="#autofill-field-name" id=autofill-processing-model:autofill-field-name-3 "autofill field name"
					- " be the string \""
					code on
					- "\", let its "
					a href="#autofill-hint-set" id=autofill-processing-model:autofill-hint-set-4 "autofill hint set"
					- " be empty, and let its "
					a href="#idl-exposed-autofill-value" id=autofill-processing-model:idl-exposed-autofill-value-2 "IDL-exposed autofill value"
					- " be the string \""
					code on
					- "\". Then, return."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "Let "
					var "scope tokens"
					- " be an empty list."
				}
			}
			li {
