			a href="#concept-fs-enctype" id=introduction-5:concept-fs-enctype enctype
			- ", and then sent to the destination specified by the "
			a href="#concept-fs-action" id=introduction-5:concept-fs-action action
			- " using the given "
			a href="#concept-fs-method" id=introduction-5:concept-fs-method method
			- .
		}
		p "For example, take the following form:"
		pre {
			code class=html {
				c- p="" <
				c- f="" form
				c- e="" action
				c- o="" "="
				c- s="" "\"/find.cgi\""
				c- e="" method
				c- o="" "="
				c- s="" get
				c- p="" >
				c- p="" <
				c- f="" input
				c- e="" type
				c- o="" "="
				c- s="" text
				c- e="" name
				c- o="" "="
				c- s="" t
				c- p="" >
				c- p="" <
				c- f="" input
				c- e="" type
				c- o="" "="
				c- s="" search
				c- e="" name
				c- o="" "="
				c- s="" q
				c- p="" >
				c- p="" <
				c- f="" input
				c- e="" type
				c- o="" "="
				c- s="" submit
				c- p="" >
				c- p="" "</"
				c- f="" form
				c- p="" >
			}
		}
		p {
			- "If the user types in \"cats\" in the first field and \"fur\" in the second, and then hits the submit button, then the user agent will load "
			code "/find.cgi?t=cats&q=fur"
			- .
		}
		p "On the other hand, consider this form:"
		pre {
			code class=html {
				c- p="" <
				c- f="" form
				c- e="" action
				c- o="" "="
				c- s="" "\"/find.cgi\""
				c- e="" method
				c- o="" "="
				c- s="" post
				c- e="" enctype
				c- o="" "="
				c- s="" "\"multipart/form-data\""
				c- p="" >
				c- p="" <
				c- f="" input
				c- e="" type
				c- o="" "="
				c- s="" text
				c- e="" name
				c- o="" "="
				c- s="" t
				c- p="" >
				c- p="" <
				c- f="" input
				c- e="" type
				c- o="" "="
				c- s="" search
				c- e="" name
				c- o="" "="
				c- s="" q
				c- p="" >
				c- p="" <
				c- f="" input
				c- e="" type
				c- o="" "="
				c- s="" submit
				c- p="" >
				c- p="" "</"
				c- f="" form
				c- p="" >
			}
		}
		p "Given the same user input, the result on submission is quite different: the user agent instead does an HTTP POST to the given URL, with as the entity body something like the following text:"
