			a href="#concept-command" id=using-the-accesskey-attribute-to-define-a-command-on-other-elements:concept-command "defines a command"
			- .
		}
		p {
			- "If one of the earlier sections that define elements that "
			a href="#concept-command" id=using-the-accesskey-attribute-to-define-a-command-on-other-elements:concept-command-2 "define commands"
			- " define that this element "
			a href="#concept-command" id=using-the-accesskey-attribute-to-define-a-command-on-other-elements:concept-command-3 "defines a command"
			- ", then that section applies to this element, and this section does not. Otherwise, this section applies to that element."
		}
		p {
			- "The "
			a href="#command-facet-label" id=using-the-accesskey-attribute-to-define-a-command-on-other-elements:command-facet-label Label
			- " of the command depends on the element. If the element is a "
			a href="#labeled-control" id=using-the-accesskey-attribute-to-define-a-command-on-other-elements:labeled-control "labeled control"
			- ", the "
			a data-x-internal=descendant-text-content href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-descendant-text-content" id=using-the-accesskey-attribute-to-define-a-command-on-other-elements:descendant-text-content "descendant text content"
			- " of the first "
			code id=using-the-accesskey-attribute-to-define-a-command-on-other-elements:the-label-element {
				a href="#the-label-element" label
			}
			- " element in "
			a data-x-internal=tree-order href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-tree-order" id=using-the-accesskey-attribute-to-define-a-command-on-other-elements:tree-order "tree order"
			- " whose "
			a href="#labeled-control" id=using-the-accesskey-attribute-to-define-a-command-on-other-elements:labeled-control-2 "labeled control"
			- " is the element in question is the "
			a href="#command-facet-label" id=using-the-accesskey-attribute-to-define-a-command-on-other-elements:command-facet-label-2 Label
			- " (in JavaScript terms, this is given by "
			code {
				var element
				- ".labels[0].textContent"
			}
			- "). Otherwise, the "
			a href="#command-facet-label" id=using-the-accesskey-attribute-to-define-a-command-on-other-elements:command-facet-label-3 Label
			- " is the element's "
			a data-x-internal=descendant-text-content href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-descendant-text-content" id=using-the-accesskey-attribute-to-define-a-command-on-other-elements:descendant-text-content-2 "descendant text content"
			- .
		}
		p {
			- "The "
			a href="#command-facet-accesskey" id=using-the-accesskey-attribute-to-define-a-command-on-other-elements:command-facet-accesskey "Access Key"
			- " of the command is the element's "
			a href="#assigned-access-key" id=using-the-accesskey-attribute-to-define-a-command-on-other-elements:assigned-access-key-2 "assigned access key"
			- .
		}
		p {
			- "The "
			a href="#command-facet-hiddenstate" id=using-the-accesskey-attribute-to-define-a-command-on-other-elements:command-facet-hiddenstate "Hidden State"
			- " of the command is true (hidden) if the element has a "
			code id=using-the-accesskey-attribute-to-define-a-command-on-other-elements:attr-hidden {
				a href="#attr-hidden" hidden
			}
			- " attribute, and false otherwise."
		}
		p {
			- "The "
			a href="#command-facet-disabledstate" id=using-the-accesskey-attribute-to-define-a-command-on-other-elements:command-facet-disabledstate "Disabled State"
			- " of the command is true if the element or one of its ancestors is "
			a href="#inert" id=using-the-accesskey-attribute-to-define-a-command-on-other-elements:inert inert
			- ", and false otherwise."
		}
		p {
			- "The "
			a href="#command-facet-action" id=using-the-accesskey-attribute-to-define-a-command-on-other-elements:command-facet-action Action
			- " of the command is to run the following steps:"
		}
		ol {
			li {
				- "Run the "
				a href="#focusing-steps" id=using-the-accesskey-attribute-to-define-a-command-on-other-elements:focusing-steps "focusing steps"
				- " for the element."
			}
			li {
				a href="#fire-a-click-event" id=using-the-accesskey-attribute-to-define-a-command-on-other-elements:fire-a-click-event {
					- "Fire a "
					code click
					- " event"
				}
				- " at the element."
			}
		}
