		p {
			- "The "
			dfn data-dfn-for=script data-dfn-type=element-attr id=attr-script-async {
				code async
			}
			- " and "
			dfn data-dfn-for=script data-dfn-type=element-attr id=attr-script-defer {
				code defer
			}
			- " attributes are "
			a href="#boolean-attribute" id=the-script-element:boolean-attribute-2 "boolean attributes"
			- " that indicate how the script should be evaluated. "
			a href="#classic-script" id=the-script-element:classic-script-5 "Classic scripts"
			- " may specify "
			code id=the-script-element:attr-script-defer-6 {
				a href="#attr-script-defer" defer
			}
			- " or "
			code id=the-script-element:attr-script-async-6 {
				a href="#attr-script-async" async
			}
			- ", but must not specify either unless the "
			code id=the-script-element:attr-script-src-10 {
				a href="#attr-script-src" src
			}
			- " attribute is present. "
			a href="#module-script" id=the-script-element:module-script-6 "Module scripts"
			- " may specify the "
			code id=the-script-element:attr-script-async-7 {
				a href="#attr-script-async" async
			}
			- " attribute, but must not specify the "
			code id=the-script-element:attr-script-defer-7 {
				a href="#attr-script-defer" defer
			}
			- " attribute."
		}
		p "There are several possible modes that can be selected using these attributes, and depending on the script's type."
		p {
			- "For "
			a href="#classic-script" id=the-script-element:classic-script-6 "classic scripts"
			- ", if the "
			code id=the-script-element:attr-script-async-8 {
				a href="#attr-script-async" async
			}
			- " attribute is present, then the classic script will be fetched "
			a href="#in-parallel" id=the-script-element:in-parallel "in parallel"
			- " to parsing and evaluated as soon as it is available (potentially before parsing completes). If the "
			code id=the-script-element:attr-script-async-9 {
				a href="#attr-script-async" async
			}
			- " attribute is not present but the "
			code id=the-script-element:attr-script-defer-8 {
				a href="#attr-script-defer" defer
			}
			- " attribute is present, then the classic script will be fetched "
			a href="#in-parallel" id=the-script-element:in-parallel-2 "in parallel"
			- " and evaluated when the page has finished parsing. If neither attribute is present, then the script is fetched and evaluated immediately, blocking parsing until these are both complete."
		}
		p {
			- "For "
			a href="#module-script" id=the-script-element:module-script-7 "module scripts"
			- ", if the "
			code id=the-script-element:attr-script-async-10 {
				a href="#attr-script-async" async
			}
			- " attribute is present, then the module script and all its dependencies will be fetched "
			a href="#in-parallel" id=the-script-element:in-parallel-3 "in parallel"
			- " to parsing, and the module script will be evaluated as soon as it is available (potentially before parsing completes). Otherwise, the module script and its dependencies will be fetched "
			a href="#in-parallel" id=the-script-element:in-parallel-4 "in parallel"
			- " to parsing and evaluated when the page has finished parsing. (The "
			code id=the-script-element:attr-script-defer-9 {
				a href="#attr-script-defer" defer
			}
			- " attribute has no effect on module scripts.)"
		}
		p "This is all summarized in the following schematic diagram:"
		p {
			img alt="With <script>, parsing is interrupted by fetching and execution. With <script defer>, fetching is parallel to parsing and execution takes place after all parsing has finished. And with <script async>, fetching is parallel to parsing but once it finishes parsing is interrupted to execute the script. The story for <script type=\"module\"> is similar to <script defer>, but the dependencies will be fetched as well, and the story for <script type=\"module\" async> is similar to <script async> with the extra dependency fetching." class=darkmode-aware src="/images/asyncdefer.svg" style="width: 80%; min-width: 820px;"
		}
		p class=note {
			- "The exact processing details for these attributes are, for mostly historical reasons, somewhat non-trivial, involving a number of aspects of HTML. The implementation requirements are therefore by necessity scattered throughout the specification. The algorithms below (in this section) describe the core of this processing, but these algorithms reference and are referenced by the parsing rules for "
			code id=the-script-element:the-script-element-8 {
				a href="#the-script-element" script
			}
			a href="#scriptTag" start
			- " and "
			a href="#scriptEndTag" end
			- " tags in HTML, "
			a href="#scriptForeignEndTag" "in foreign content"
			- ", and "
			a href="#scriptTagXML" "in XML"
			- ", the rules for the "
			code id=the-script-element:dom-document-write {
				a href="#dom-document-write" "document.write()"
			}
			- " method, the handling of "
			a href="#scripting" scripting
			- ", etc."
		}
		p class=note {
			- "When inserted using the "
			code id=the-script-element:dom-document-write-2 {
				a href="#dom-document-write" "document.write()"
			}
			- " method, "
			code id=the-script-element:the-script-element-9 {
				a href="#the-script-element" script
			}
			- " elements "
			a href="#document-written-scripts-intervention" usually
			- " execute (typically blocking further script execution or HTML parsing). When inserted using the "
			code id=the-script-element:dom-element-innerhtml {
				a href="#dom-element-innerhtml" innerHTML
			}
			- " and "
			code id=the-script-element:dom-element-outerhtml {
				a href="#dom-element-outerhtml" outerHTML
			}
			- " attributes, they do not execute at all."
		}
		p {
			- "The "
			code id=the-script-element:attr-script-defer-10 {
				a href="#attr-script-defer" defer
			}
			- " attribute may be specified even if the "
			code id=the-script-element:attr-script-async-11 {
				a href="#attr-script-async" async
			}
			- " attribute is specified, to cause legacy web browsers that only support "
			code id=the-script-element:attr-script-defer-11 {
				a href="#attr-script-defer" defer
			}
			- " (and not "
			code id=the-script-element:attr-script-async-12 {
				a href="#attr-script-async" async
			}
			- ") to fall back to the "
			code id=the-script-element:attr-script-defer-12 {
				a href="#attr-script-defer" defer
			}
			- " behavior instead of the blocking behavior that is the default."
		}
		p {
			- "The "
			dfn data-dfn-for=script data-dfn-type=element-attr id=attr-script-crossorigin {
				code crossorigin
			}
			- " attribute is a "
			a href="#cors-settings-attribute" id=the-script-element:cors-settings-attribute "CORS settings attribute"
			- ". For "
			a href="#classic-script" id=the-script-element:classic-script-7 "classic scripts"
			- ", it controls whether error information will be exposed, when the script is obtained from other "
			a href="#concept-origin" id=the-script-element:concept-origin origins
			- ". For "
			a href="#module-script" id=the-script-element:module-script-8 "module scripts"
			- ", it controls the "
			a data-x-internal=concept-request-credentials-mode href="https://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-request-credentials-mode" id=the-script-element:concept-request-credentials-mode "credentials mode"
			- " used for cross-origin requests."
		}
		p class=note {
			- "Unlike "
			a href="#classic-script" id=the-script-element:classic-script-8 "classic scripts"
			- ", "
			a href="#module-script" id=the-script-element:module-script-9 "module scripts"
			- " require the use of the "
			a data-x-internal=cors-protocol href="https://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/#http-cors-protocol" id=the-script-element:cors-protocol "CORS protocol"
			- " for cross-origin fetching."
		}
		p {
			- "The "
			dfn data-dfn-for=script data-dfn-type=element-attr id=attr-script-integrity {
				code integrity
			}
			- " attribute represents the "
			a data-x-internal=concept-request-integrity-metadata href="https://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-request-integrity-metadata" id=the-script-element:concept-request-integrity-metadata "integrity metadata"
			- " for requests which this element is responsible for. The value is text. The "
			code id=the-script-element:attr-script-integrity-4 {
				a href="#attr-script-integrity" integrity
			}
			- " attribute must not be specified when the "
			code id=the-script-element:attr-script-src-11 {
				a href="#attr-script-src" src
			}
			- " attribute is not specified. "
			a href="#refsSRI" "[SRI]"
		}
		p {
			- "The "
			dfn data-dfn-for=script data-dfn-type=element-attr id=attr-script-referrerpolicy {
				code referrerpolicy
			}
			- " attribute is a "
			a href="#referrer-policy-attribute" id=the-script-element:referrer-policy-attribute "referrer policy attribute"
			- ". Its purpose is to set the "
			a data-x-internal=referrer-policy href="https://w3c.github.io/webappsec-referrer-policy/#referrer-policy" id=the-script-element:referrer-policy-2 "referrer policy"
			- " used when "
			a data-x-internal=concept-fetch href="https://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-fetch" id=the-script-element:concept-fetch-3 fetching
			- " the script, as well as any scripts imported from it. "
			a href="#refsREFERRERPOLICY" "[REFERRERPOLICY]"
		}
		div class=example {
			p {
				- "An example of a "
				code id=the-script-element:the-script-element-10 {
					a href="#the-script-element" script
				}
				- " element's referrer policy being used when fetching imported scripts but not other subresources:"
			}
			pre {
