		p {
			- "The "
			code id=the-canvas-element:the-canvas-element {
				a href="#the-canvas-element" canvas
			}
			- " element provides scripts with a resolution-dependent bitmap canvas, which can be used for rendering graphs, game graphics, art, or other visual images on the fly."
		}
		p {
			- "Authors should not use the "
			code id=the-canvas-element:the-canvas-element-2 {
				a href="#the-canvas-element" canvas
			}
			- " element in a document when a more suitable element is available. For example, it is inappropriate to use a "
			code id=the-canvas-element:the-canvas-element-3 {
				a href="#the-canvas-element" canvas
			}
			- " element to render a page heading: if the desired presentation of the heading is graphically intense, it should be marked up using appropriate elements (typically "
			code id=the-canvas-element:the-h1,-h2,-h3,-h4,-h5,-and-h6-elements {
				a href="#the-h1,-h2,-h3,-h4,-h5,-and-h6-elements" h1
			}
			- ") and then styled using CSS and supporting technologies such as "
			a data-x-internal=shadow-tree href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-shadow-tree" id=the-canvas-element:shadow-tree "shadow trees"
			- .
		}
		p {
			- "When authors use the "
			code id=the-canvas-element:the-canvas-element-4 {
				a href="#the-canvas-element" canvas
			}
			- " element, they must also provide content that, when presented to the user, conveys essentially the same function or purpose as the "
			code id=the-canvas-element:the-canvas-element-5 {
				a href="#the-canvas-element" canvas
			}
			- "'s bitmap. This content may be placed as content of the "
			code id=the-canvas-element:the-canvas-element-6 {
				a href="#the-canvas-element" canvas
			}
			- " element. The contents of the "
			code id=the-canvas-element:the-canvas-element-7 {
				a href="#the-canvas-element" canvas
			}
			- " element, if any, are the element's "
			a href="#fallback-content" id=the-canvas-element:fallback-content "fallback content"
			- .
		}
		hr
		p {
			- "In interactive visual media, if "
			a href="#concept-n-script" id=the-canvas-element:concept-n-script "scripting is enabled"
			- " for the "
			code id=the-canvas-element:the-canvas-element-8 {
				a href="#the-canvas-element" canvas
			}
			- " element, and if support for "
			code id=the-canvas-element:the-canvas-element-9 {
				a href="#the-canvas-element" canvas
			}
			- " elements has been enabled, then the "
			code id=the-canvas-element:the-canvas-element-10 {
				a href="#the-canvas-element" canvas
			}
			- " element "
			a href="#represents" id=the-canvas-element:represents represents
			a href="#embedded-content-category" id=the-canvas-element:embedded-content-category-3 "embedded content"
			- " consisting of a dynamically created image, the element's bitmap."
		}
		p {
			- "In non-interactive, static, visual media, if the "
			code id=the-canvas-element:the-canvas-element-11 {
				a href="#the-canvas-element" canvas
			}
			- " element has been previously associated with a rendering context (e.g. if the page was viewed in an interactive visual medium and is now being printed, or if some script that ran during the page layout process painted on the element), then the "
			code id=the-canvas-element:the-canvas-element-12 {
				a href="#the-canvas-element" canvas
			}
			- " element "
			a href="#represents" id=the-canvas-element:represents-2 represents
			a href="#embedded-content-category" id=the-canvas-element:embedded-content-category-4 "embedded content"
			- " with the element's current bitmap and size. Otherwise, the element represents its "
			a href="#fallback-content" id=the-canvas-element:fallback-content-2 "fallback content"
			- " instead."
		}
		p {
			- "In non-visual media, and in visual media if "
			a href="#concept-n-noscript" id=the-canvas-element:concept-n-noscript "scripting is disabled"
			- " for the "
			code id=the-canvas-element:the-canvas-element-13 {
				a href="#the-canvas-element" canvas
			}
			- " element or if support for "
			code id=the-canvas-element:the-canvas-element-14 {
				a href="#the-canvas-element" canvas
			}
			- " elements has been disabled, the "
			code id=the-canvas-element:the-canvas-element-15 {
				a href="#the-canvas-element" canvas
			}
			- " element "
			a href="#represents" id=the-canvas-element:represents-3 represents
			- " its "
			a href="#fallback-content" id=the-canvas-element:fallback-content-3 "fallback content"
			- " instead."
		}
		p {
			- "When a "
			code id=the-canvas-element:the-canvas-element-16 {
				a href="#the-canvas-element" canvas
			}
			- " element "
			a href="#represents" id=the-canvas-element:represents-4 represents
			a href="#embedded-content-category" id=the-canvas-element:embedded-content-category-5 "embedded content"
			- ", the user can still focus descendants of the "
			code id=the-canvas-element:the-canvas-element-17 {
				a href="#the-canvas-element" canvas
			}
			- " element (in the "
			a href="#fallback-content" id=the-canvas-element:fallback-content-4 "fallback content"
			- "). When an element is "
			a href="#focused" id=the-canvas-element:focused focused
			- ", it is the target of keyboard interaction events (even though the element itself is not visible). This allows authors to make an interactive canvas keyboard-accessible: authors should have a one-to-one mapping of interactive regions to "
			i id=the-canvas-element:focusable-area {
				a href="#focusable-area" "focusable areas"
			}
			- " in the "
			a href="#fallback-content" id=the-canvas-element:fallback-content-5 "fallback content"
			- ". (Focus has no effect on mouse interaction events.) "
			a href="#refsUIEVENTS" "[UIEVENTS]"
		}
		p {
			- "An element whose nearest "
			code id=the-canvas-element:the-canvas-element-18 {
				a href="#the-canvas-element" canvas
			}
			- " element ancestor is "
			a href="#being-rendered" id=the-canvas-element:being-rendered "being rendered"
			- " and "
			a href="#represents" id=the-canvas-element:represents-5 represents
			a href="#embedded-content-category" id=the-canvas-element:embedded-content-category-6 "embedded content"
			- " is an element that is "
			dfn id=being-used-as-relevant-canvas-fallback-content "being used as relevant canvas fallback content"
			- .
		}
		hr
		p {
			- "The "
			code id=the-canvas-element:the-canvas-element-19 {
				a href="#the-canvas-element" canvas
			}
			- " element has two attributes to control the size of the element's bitmap: "
			dfn data-dfn-for=canvas data-dfn-type=element-attr id=attr-canvas-width {
				code width
			}
			- " and "
			dfn data-dfn-for=canvas data-dfn-type=element-attr id=attr-canvas-height {
				code height
			}
			- ". These attributes, when specified, must have values that are "
			a href="#valid-non-negative-integer" id=the-canvas-element:valid-non-negative-integer "valid non-negative integers"
			- ". The "
			a href="#rules-for-parsing-non-negative-integers" id=the-canvas-element:rules-for-parsing-non-negative-integers "rules for parsing non-negative integers"
			- " must be used to "
			dfn id=obtain-numeric-values "obtain their numeric values"
			- ". If an attribute is missing, or if parsing its value returns an error, then the default value must be used instead. The "
			code id=the-canvas-element:attr-canvas-width-2 {
				a href="#attr-canvas-width" width
			}
			- " attribute defaults to 300, and the "
			code id=the-canvas-element:attr-canvas-height-2 {
				a href="#attr-canvas-height" height
			}
			- " attribute defaults to 150."
		}
		p {
			- "When setting the value of the "
			code id=the-canvas-element:attr-canvas-width-3 {
				a href="#attr-canvas-width" width
			}
			- " or "
			code id=the-canvas-element:attr-canvas-height-3 {
				a href="#attr-canvas-height" height
			}
			- " attribute, if the "
			a href="#concept-canvas-context-mode" id=the-canvas-element:concept-canvas-context-mode "context mode"
			- " of the "
			code id=the-canvas-element:the-canvas-element-20 {
				a href="#the-canvas-element" canvas
			}
			- " element is set to "
			a href="#concept-canvas-placeholder" id=the-canvas-element:concept-canvas-placeholder placeholder
			- ", the user agent must throw an "
			a data-x-internal=invalidstateerror href="https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#invalidstateerror" id=the-canvas-element:invalidstateerror {
				- "\""
				code InvalidStateError
				- "\""
			}
			code id=the-canvas-element:domexception {
				a data-x-internal=domexception href="https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#dfn-DOMException" DOMException
			}
			- " and leave the attribute's value unchanged."
		}
		p {
			- "The "
			a data-x-internal=natural-dimensions href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-images/#natural-dimensions" id=the-canvas-element:natural-dimensions "natural dimensions"
			- " of the "
			code id=the-canvas-element:the-canvas-element-21 {
				a href="#the-canvas-element" canvas
			}
			- " element when it "
			a href="#represents" id=the-canvas-element:represents-6 represents
			a href="#embedded-content-category" id=the-canvas-element:embedded-content-category-7 "embedded content"
			- " are equal to the dimensions of the element's bitmap."
		}
		p {
			- "The user agent must use a square pixel density consisting of one pixel of image data per coordinate space unit for the bitmaps of a "
			code id=the-canvas-element:the-canvas-element-22 {
				a href="#the-canvas-element" canvas
			}
			- " and its rendering contexts."
		}
		p class=note {
			- "A "
			code id=the-canvas-element:the-canvas-element-23 {
				a href="#the-canvas-element" canvas
			}
			- " element can be sized arbitrarily by a style sheet, its bitmap is then subject to the "
			a data-x-internal='object-fit' href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-images/#the-object-fit" id=the-canvas-element:'object-fit' 'object-fit'
			- " CSS property."
		}
		hr
		p {
			- "The bitmaps of "
			code id=the-canvas-element:the-canvas-element-24 {
				a href="#the-canvas-element" canvas
			}
			- " elements, the bitmaps of "
			code id=the-canvas-element:imagebitmap {
				a href="#imagebitmap" ImageBitmap
			}
			- " objects, as well as some of the bitmaps of rendering contexts, such as those described in the sections on the "
			code id=the-canvas-element:canvasrenderingcontext2d-2 {
				a href="#canvasrenderingcontext2d" CanvasRenderingContext2D
			}
			- " and "
			code id=the-canvas-element:imagebitmaprenderingcontext-2 {
				a href="#imagebitmaprenderingcontext" ImageBitmapRenderingContext
			}
			- " objects below, have an "
			dfn id=concept-canvas-origin-clean origin-clean
			- " flag, which can be set to true or false. Initially, when the "
			code id=the-canvas-element:the-canvas-element-25 {
				a href="#the-canvas-element" canvas
			}
			- " element or "
			code id=the-canvas-element:imagebitmap-2 {
				a href="#imagebitmap" ImageBitmap
			}
			- " object is created, its bitmap's "
			a href="#concept-canvas-origin-clean" id=the-canvas-element:concept-canvas-origin-clean origin-clean
			- " flag must be set to true."
		}
		p {
			- "A "
			code id=the-canvas-element:the-canvas-element-26 {
				a href="#the-canvas-element" canvas
			}
			- " element can have a rendering context bound to it. Initially, it does not have a bound rendering context. To keep track of whether it has a rendering context or not, and what kind of rendering context it is, a "
			code id=the-canvas-element:the-canvas-element-27 {
				a href="#the-canvas-element" canvas
			}
			- " also has a "
			dfn id=concept-canvas-context-mode "canvas context mode"
			- ", which is initially "
			dfn id=concept-canvas-none none
			- " but can be changed to either "
			dfn id=concept-canvas-placeholder placeholder
			- ", "
			dfn id=concept-canvas-2d "2d"
			- ", "
			dfn id=concept-canvas-bitmaprenderer bitmaprenderer
			- ", "
			dfn id=concept-canvas-webgl webgl
			- ", "
			dfn id=concept-canvas-webgl2 webgl2
			- ", or "
			dfn id=concept-canvas-webgpu webgpu
			- " by algorithms defined in this specification."
		}
		p {
			- "When its "
			a href="#concept-canvas-context-mode" id=the-canvas-element:concept-canvas-context-mode-2 "canvas context mode"
			- " is "
			a href="#concept-canvas-none" id=the-canvas-element:concept-canvas-none none
			- ", a "
			code id=the-canvas-element:the-canvas-element-28 {
				a href="#the-canvas-element" canvas
			}
			- " element has no rendering context, and its bitmap must be "
			a data-x-internal=transparent-black href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-color/#transparent-black" id=the-canvas-element:transparent-black "transparent black"
			- " with a "
			a data-x-internal=natural-width href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-images/#natural-width" id=the-canvas-element:natural-width "natural width"
			- " equal to "
			a href="#obtain-numeric-values" id=the-canvas-element:obtain-numeric-values "the numeric value"
			- " of the element's "
			code id=the-canvas-element:attr-canvas-width-4 {
				a href="#attr-canvas-width" width
			}
			- " attribute and a "
			a data-x-internal=natural-height href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-images/#natural-height" id=the-canvas-element:natural-height "natural height"
			- " equal to "
			a href="#obtain-numeric-values" id=the-canvas-element:obtain-numeric-values-2 "the numeric value"
			- " of the element's "
			code id=the-canvas-element:attr-canvas-height-4 {
				a href="#attr-canvas-height" height
			}
			- " attribute, those values being interpreted in "
			a data-x-internal='px' href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-values/#px" id=the-canvas-element:'px' "CSS pixels"
			- ", and being updated as the attributes are set, changed, or removed."
		}
		p {
			- "When its "
			a href="#concept-canvas-context-mode" id=the-canvas-element:concept-canvas-context-mode-3 "canvas context mode"
			- " is "
			a href="#concept-canvas-placeholder" id=the-canvas-element:concept-canvas-placeholder-2 placeholder
			- ", a "
			code id=the-canvas-element:the-canvas-element-29 {
				a href="#the-canvas-element" canvas
			}
			- " element has no rendering context. It serves as a placeholder for an "
			code id=the-canvas-element:offscreencanvas-2 {
				a href="#offscreencanvas" OffscreenCanvas
			}
			- " object, and the content of the "
			code id=the-canvas-element:the-canvas-element-30 {
				a href="#the-canvas-element" canvas
			}
			- " element is updated by the "
			code id=the-canvas-element:offscreencanvas-3 {
				a href="#offscreencanvas" OffscreenCanvas
			}
			- " object's rendering context."
		}
		p {
			- "When a "
			code id=the-canvas-element:the-canvas-element-31 {
				a href="#the-canvas-element" canvas
			}
			- " element represents "
			a href="#embedded-content-category" id=the-canvas-element:embedded-content-category-8 "embedded content"
			- ", it provides a "
