			- "'s "
			a href="#concept-canvas-will-read-frequently" id="2dcontext:concept-canvas-will-read-frequently-5" "will read frequently"
			- " ]»."
		}
		hr
		p {
			- "The "
			code id="2dcontext:canvasrenderingcontext2d-29" {
				a href="#canvasrenderingcontext2d" CanvasRenderingContext2D
			}
			- " 2D rendering context represents a flat linear Cartesian surface whose origin (0,0) is at the top left corner, with the coordinate space having "
			var x
			- " values increasing when going right, and "
			var y
			- " values increasing when going down. The "
			var x
			- "-coordinate of the right-most edge is equal to the width of the rendering context's "
			a href="#output-bitmap" id="2dcontext:output-bitmap-6" "output bitmap"
			- " in "
			a data-x-internal='px' href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-values/#px" id="2dcontext:'px'" "CSS pixels"
			- "; similarly, the "
			var y
			- "-coordinate of the bottom-most edge is equal to the height of the rendering context's "
			a href="#output-bitmap" id="2dcontext:output-bitmap-7" "output bitmap"
			- " in "
			a data-x-internal='px' href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-values/#px" id="2dcontext:'px'-2" "CSS pixels"
			- .
		}
		p "The size of the coordinate space does not necessarily represent the size of the actual bitmaps that the user agent will use internally or during rendering. On high-definition displays, for instance, the user agent may internally use bitmaps with four device pixels per unit in the coordinate space, so that the rendering remains at high quality throughout. Anti-aliasing can similarly be implemented using oversampling with bitmaps of a higher resolution than the final image on the display."
		div class=example {
			p {
				- "Using "
				a data-x-internal='px' href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-values/#px" id="2dcontext:'px'-3" "CSS pixels"
				- " to describe the size of a rendering context's "
				a href="#output-bitmap" id="2dcontext:output-bitmap-8" "output bitmap"
				- " does not mean that when rendered the canvas will cover an equivalent area in "
				a data-x-internal='px' href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-values/#px" id="2dcontext:'px'-4" "CSS pixels"
				- ". "
				a data-x-internal='px' href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-values/#px" id="2dcontext:'px'-5" "CSS pixels"
				- " are reused for ease of integration with CSS features, such as text layout."
			}
			p {
				- "In other words, the "
				code id="2dcontext:the-canvas-element-3" {
					a href="#the-canvas-element" canvas
				}
				- " element below's rendering context has a 200x200 "
				a href="#output-bitmap" id="2dcontext:output-bitmap-9" "output bitmap"
				- " (which internally uses "
				a data-x-internal='px' href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-values/#px" id="2dcontext:'px'-6" "CSS pixels"
				- " as a unit for ease of integration with CSS) and is rendered as 100x100 "
				a data-x-internal='px' href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-values/#px" id="2dcontext:'px'-7" "CSS pixels"
				- ": "
			}
			pre {
