		p {
			- "The "
			dfn data-dfn-for=CanvasTextDrawingStyles data-dfn-type=attribute id=dom-context-2d-font {
				code font
			}
			- " IDL attribute, on setting, must be "
			a data-x-internal=parse-something-according-to-a-css-grammar href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-syntax/#parse-grammar" id=text-styles:parse-something-according-to-a-css-grammar "parsed as a CSS <'font'> value"
			- " (but without supporting property-independent style sheet syntax like 'inherit'), and the resulting font must be assigned to the context, with the "
			a data-x-internal='line-height' href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css2/#propdef-line-height" id=text-styles:'line-height' 'line-height'
			- " component forced to 'normal', with the "
			a data-x-internal='font-size' href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-fonts/#font-size-prop" id=text-styles:'font-size' 'font-size'
			- " component converted to "
			a data-x-internal='px' href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-values/#px" id=text-styles:'px' "CSS pixels"
			- ", and with system fonts being computed to explicit values. If the new value is syntactically incorrect (including using property-independent style sheet syntax like 'inherit' or 'initial'), then it must be ignored, without assigning a new font value. "
			a href="#refsCSS" "[CSS]"
		}
		p {
			- "Font family names must be interpreted in the context of the "
			a href="#font-style-source-object" id=text-styles:font-style-source-object-4 "font style source object"
			- " when the font is to be used; any fonts embedded using "
			code @font-face
			- " or loaded using "
			code id=text-styles:fontface {
				a href="#fontface" FontFace
			}
			- " objects that are visible to the "
			a href="#font-style-source-object" id=text-styles:font-style-source-object-5 "font style source object"
			- " must therefore be available once they are loaded. (Each "
			a href="#font-style-source-object" id=text-styles:font-style-source-object-6 "font style source object"
			- " has a "
			a data-x-internal=font-source href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-font-loading/#font-source" id=text-styles:font-source-2 "font source"
			- ", which determines what fonts are available.) If a font is used before it is fully loaded, or if the "
			a href="#font-style-source-object" id=text-styles:font-style-source-object-7 "font style source object"
			- " does not have that font in scope at the time the font is to be used, then it must be treated as if it was an unknown font, falling back to another as described by the relevant CSS specifications. "
			a href="#refsCSSFONTS" "[CSSFONTS]"
			a href="#refsCSSFONTLOAD" "[CSSFONTLOAD]"
		}
		p {
			- "On getting, the "
			code id=text-styles:dom-context-2d-font-2 {
				a href="#dom-context-2d-font" font
			}
			- " attribute must return the "
			a data-x-internal=serializing-a-css-value href="https://drafts.csswg.org/cssom/#serialize-a-css-value" id=text-styles:serializing-a-css-value "serialized form"
			- " of the current font of the context (with no "
			a data-x-internal='line-height' href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css2/#propdef-line-height" id=text-styles:'line-height'-2 'line-height'
			- " component). "
			a href="#refsCSSOM" "[CSSOM]"
		}
		div class=example {
			p "For example, after the following statement:"
			pre {
				code class=js {
					- context
					c- p="" .
					- "font "
					c- o="" "="
					c- t="" "'italic 400 12px/2 Unknown Font, sans-serif'"
