		p {
			- "The "
			code id=text-styles:dom-context-2d-textbaseline-3 {
				a href="#dom-context-2d-textbaseline" textBaseline
			}
			- " attribute's allowed keywords correspond to alignment points in the font:"
		}
		p {
			img alt="The em-over baseline is roughly at the top of the glyphs in a font, the hanging baseline is where some glyphs like आ are anchored, the middle is half-way between the em-over and em-under baselines, the alphabetic baseline is where characters like Á, ÿ, f, and Ω are anchored, the ideographic-under baseline is where glyphs like 私 and 達 are anchored, and the em-under baseline is roughly at the bottom of the glyphs in a font. The top and bottom of the bounding box can be far from these baselines, due to glyphs extending far outside em-over and em-under baselines." height="300" src="/images/baselines.png" width="738"
		}
		p "The keywords map to these alignment points as follows:"
		dl {
			dt {
				dfn data-dfn-for=CanvasTextBaseline data-dfn-type=enum-value id=dom-context-2d-textbaseline-top {
					code top
				}
			}
			dd {
				- "The "
				a data-x-internal=em-over-baseline href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-inline/#em-over-baseline" id=text-styles:em-over-baseline "em-over baseline"
			}
			dt {
				dfn data-dfn-for=CanvasTextBaseline data-dfn-type=enum-value id=dom-context-2d-textbaseline-hanging {
					code hanging
				}
			}
			dd {
				- "The "
