		p {
			- "Objects that implement the "
			code id=drawing-text-to-the-bitmap:canvastext {
				a href="#canvastext" CanvasText
			}
			- " interface provide the following methods for rendering text."
		}
		p {
			- "The "
			dfn data-dfn-for=CanvasText data-dfn-type=method id=dom-context-2d-filltext {
				code {
					- "fillText("
					var text
					- ", "
					var x
					- ", "
					var y
					- ", "
					var maxWidth
					- ")"
				}
			}
			- " and "
			dfn data-dfn-for=CanvasText data-dfn-type=method id=dom-context-2d-stroketext {
				code {
					- "strokeText("
					var text
					- ", "
					var x
					- ", "
					var y
					- ", "
					var maxWidth
					- ")"
				}
			}
			- " methods render the given "
			var text
			- " at the given ("
			var x
			- ", "
			var y
			- ") coordinates ensuring that the text isn't wider than "
			var maxWidth
			- " if specified, using the current "
			code id=drawing-text-to-the-bitmap:dom-context-2d-font {
				a href="#dom-context-2d-font" font
			}
			- ", "
			code id=drawing-text-to-the-bitmap:dom-context-2d-textalign {
				a href="#dom-context-2d-textalign" textAlign
			}
			- ", and "
			code id=drawing-text-to-the-bitmap:dom-context-2d-textbaseline {
				a href="#dom-context-2d-textbaseline" textBaseline
			}
			- " values. Specifically, when the methods are invoked, the user agent must run these steps:"
		}
		ol {
			li {
				p "If any of the arguments are infinite or NaN, then return."
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "Run the "
					a href="#text-preparation-algorithm" id=drawing-text-to-the-bitmap:text-preparation-algorithm "text preparation algorithm"
					- ", passing it "
					var text
					- ", the object implementing the "
					code id=drawing-text-to-the-bitmap:canvastext-2 {
						a href="#canvastext" CanvasText
					}
					- " interface, and, if the "
					var maxWidth
					- " argument was provided, that argument. Let "
					var glyphs
					- " be the result."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "Move all the shapes in "
					var glyphs
					- " to the right by "
					var x
					a data-x-internal='px' href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-values/#px" id=drawing-text-to-the-bitmap:'px' "CSS pixels"
					- " and down by "
					var y
					a data-x-internal='px' href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-values/#px" id=drawing-text-to-the-bitmap:'px'-2 "CSS pixels"
					- .
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "Paint the shapes given in "
					var glyphs
					- ", as transformed by the "
					a href="#transformations" id=drawing-text-to-the-bitmap:transformations "current transformation matrix"
					- ", with each "
					a data-x-internal='px' href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-values/#px" id=drawing-text-to-the-bitmap:'px'-3 "CSS pixel"
					- " in the coordinate space of "
					var glyphs
					- " mapped to one coordinate space unit."
				}
				p {
					- "For "
					code id=drawing-text-to-the-bitmap:dom-context-2d-filltext {
						a href="#dom-context-2d-filltext" "fillText()"
					}
					- ", "
					a data-x-internal=this href="https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#this" id=drawing-text-to-the-bitmap:this this
					- "'s "
					a href="#concept-canvasfillstrokestyles-fill-style" id=drawing-text-to-the-bitmap:concept-canvasfillstrokestyles-fill-style "fill style"
					- " must be applied to the shapes and "
					a data-x-internal=this href="https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#this" id=drawing-text-to-the-bitmap:this-2 this
					- "'s "
					a href="#concept-canvasfillstrokestyles-stroke-style" id=drawing-text-to-the-bitmap:concept-canvasfillstrokestyles-stroke-style "stroke style"
					- " must be ignored. For "
					code id=drawing-text-to-the-bitmap:dom-context-2d-stroketext {
						a href="#dom-context-2d-stroketext" "strokeText()"
					}
					- ", the reverse holds: "
					a data-x-internal=this href="https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#this" id=drawing-text-to-the-bitmap:this-3 this
					- "'s "
					a href="#concept-canvasfillstrokestyles-stroke-style" id=drawing-text-to-the-bitmap:concept-canvasfillstrokestyles-stroke-style-2 "stroke style"
					- " must be applied to the result of "
					a href="#trace-a-path" id=drawing-text-to-the-bitmap:trace-a-path tracing
					- " the shapes using the object implementing the "
					code id=drawing-text-to-the-bitmap:canvastext-3 {
						a href="#canvastext" CanvasText
					}
					- " interface for the line styles, and "
					a data-x-internal=this href="https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#this" id=drawing-text-to-the-bitmap:this-4 this
					- "'s "
					a href="#concept-canvasfillstrokestyles-fill-style" id=drawing-text-to-the-bitmap:concept-canvasfillstrokestyles-fill-style-2 "fill style"
					- " must be ignored."
				}
				p {
					- "These shapes are painted without affecting the current path, and are subject to "
					a href="#shadows" id=drawing-text-to-the-bitmap:shadows "shadow effects"
					- ", "
					a href="#concept-canvas-global-alpha" id=drawing-text-to-the-bitmap:concept-canvas-global-alpha "global alpha"
					- ", the "
					a href="#clipping-region" id=drawing-text-to-the-bitmap:clipping-region "clipping region"
					- ", and the "
					a href="#current-compositing-and-blending-operator" id=drawing-text-to-the-bitmap:current-compositing-and-blending-operator "current compositing and blending operator"
					- .
				}
			}
		}
		p {
			a class=tracking-vector data-x-internal=tracking-vector href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#tracking-vector" id=drawing-text-to-the-bitmap:tracking-vector title="There is a tracking vector here." {
				img alt="(This is a tracking vector.)" crossorigin="" height="64" src="https://resources.whatwg.org/tracking-vector.svg" width="46"
			}
			- " The "
			dfn data-dfn-for=CanvasText data-dfn-type=method id=dom-context-2d-measuretext {
				code {
					- "measureText("
					var text
					- ")"
				}
			}
			- " method steps are to run the "
			a href="#text-preparation-algorithm" id=drawing-text-to-the-bitmap:text-preparation-algorithm-2 "text preparation algorithm"
			- ", passing it "
			var text
			- " and the object implementing the "
			code id=drawing-text-to-the-bitmap:canvastext-4 {
				a href="#canvastext" CanvasText
			}
			- " interface, and then using the returned "
			a data-x-internal=inline-box href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css2/#inline-box" id=drawing-text-to-the-bitmap:inline-box "inline box"
			- " must return a new "
			code id=drawing-text-to-the-bitmap:textmetrics-2 {
				a href="#textmetrics" TextMetrics
			}
			- " object with members behaving as described in the following list: "
			a href="#refsCSS" "[CSS]"
		}
		dl {
			dt {
				dfn data-dfn-for=TextMetrics data-dfn-type=attribute id=dom-textmetrics-width {
					code width
				}
				- " attribute"
			}
			dd {
				p {
					- "The width of that "
					a data-x-internal=inline-box href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css2/#inline-box" id=drawing-text-to-the-bitmap:inline-box-2 "inline box"
					- ", in "
					a data-x-internal='px' href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-values/#px" id=drawing-text-to-the-bitmap:'px'-4 "CSS pixels"
					- ". (The text's advance width.)"
				}
			}
			dt {
				dfn data-dfn-for=TextMetrics data-dfn-type=attribute id=dom-textmetrics-actualboundingboxleft {
					code actualBoundingBoxLeft
				}
				- " attribute"
			}
			dd {
				p {
					- "The distance parallel to the baseline from the alignment point given by the "
					code id=drawing-text-to-the-bitmap:dom-context-2d-textalign-2 {
						a href="#dom-context-2d-textalign" textAlign
					}
					- " attribute to the left side of the bounding rectangle of the given text, in "
					a data-x-internal='px' href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-values/#px" id=drawing-text-to-the-bitmap:'px'-5 "CSS pixels"
					- "; positive numbers indicating a distance going left from the given alignment point. "
				}
				p class=note {
					- "The sum of this value and the next ("
					code id=drawing-text-to-the-bitmap:dom-textmetrics-actualboundingboxright {
						a href="#dom-textmetrics-actualboundingboxright" actualBoundingBoxRight
					}
					- ") can be wider than the width of the "
					a data-x-internal=inline-box href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css2/#inline-box" id=drawing-text-to-the-bitmap:inline-box-3 "inline box"
					- " ("
					code id=drawing-text-to-the-bitmap:dom-textmetrics-width {
						a href="#dom-textmetrics-width" width
					}
					- "), in particular with slanted fonts where characters overhang their advance width."
				}
			}
			dt {
				dfn data-dfn-for=TextMetrics data-dfn-type=attribute id=dom-textmetrics-actualboundingboxright {
					code actualBoundingBoxRight
				}
				- " attribute"
			}
			dd {
				p {
					- "The distance parallel to the baseline from the alignment point given by the "
					code id=drawing-text-to-the-bitmap:dom-context-2d-textalign-3 {
						a href="#dom-context-2d-textalign" textAlign
					}
					- " attribute to the right side of the bounding rectangle of the given text, in "
					a data-x-internal='px' href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-values/#px" id=drawing-text-to-the-bitmap:'px'-6 "CSS pixels"
					- "; positive numbers indicating a distance going right from the given alignment point."
				}
			}
			dt {
				dfn data-dfn-for=TextMetrics data-dfn-type=attribute id=dom-textmetrics-fontboundingboxascent {
					code fontBoundingBoxAscent
				}
				- " attribute"
			}
			dd {
				p {
					- "The distance from the horizontal line indicated by the "
					code id=drawing-text-to-the-bitmap:dom-context-2d-textbaseline-2 {
						a href="#dom-context-2d-textbaseline" textBaseline
					}
					- " attribute to the "
					a data-x-internal=ascent-metric href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-inline/#ascent-metric" id=drawing-text-to-the-bitmap:ascent-metric "ascent metric"
					- " of the "
					a data-x-internal=first-available-font href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-fonts/#first-available-font" id=drawing-text-to-the-bitmap:first-available-font "first available font"
					- ", in "
					a data-x-internal='px' href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-values/#px" id=drawing-text-to-the-bitmap:'px'-7 "CSS pixels"
					- "; positive numbers indicating a distance going up from the given baseline."
				}
				p class=note {
					- "This value and the next are useful when rendering a background that have to have a consistent height even if the exact text being rendered changes. The "
					code id=drawing-text-to-the-bitmap:dom-textmetrics-actualboundingboxascent {
						a href="#dom-textmetrics-actualboundingboxascent" actualBoundingBoxAscent
					}
					- " attribute (and its corresponding attribute for the descent) are useful when drawing a bounding box around specific text."
				}
			}
			dt {
				dfn data-dfn-for=TextMetrics data-dfn-type=attribute id=dom-textmetrics-fontboundingboxdescent {
					code fontBoundingBoxDescent
				}
				- " attribute"
			}
			dd {
				p {
					- "The distance from the horizontal line indicated by the "
					code id=drawing-text-to-the-bitmap:dom-context-2d-textbaseline-3 {
						a href="#dom-context-2d-textbaseline" textBaseline
					}
					- " attribute to the "
