			- " is a string parseable as a "
			a data-x-internal=filter-value-list href="https://drafts.fxtf.org/filter-effects/#typedef-filter-value-list" id=filters:filter-value-list-4 <filter-value-list>
			- " with a reference to an SVG filter in the same document, and this SVG filter changes, then the changed filter is used for the next draw operation."
		}
		p {
			- "If the value of the "
			a href="#concept-canvas-current-filter" id=filters:concept-canvas-current-filter-10 "current filter"
			- " is a string parseable as a "
			a data-x-internal=filter-value-list href="https://drafts.fxtf.org/filter-effects/#typedef-filter-value-list" id=filters:filter-value-list-5 <filter-value-list>
			- " with a reference to an SVG filter in an external resource document and that document is not loaded when a drawing operation is invoked, then the drawing operation must proceed with no filtering."
		}
		h6 id=working-with-externally-defined-svg-filters {
			span class=secno "4.12.5.1.20"
			- " Working with externally-defined SVG filters"
			a class=self-link href="#working-with-externally-defined-svg-filters"
		}
		p {
			i "This section is non-normative."
		}
		p {
			- "Since drawing is performed using filter value \""
			code none
			- "\" until an externally-defined filter has finished loading, authors might wish to determine whether such a filter has finished loading before proceeding with a drawing operation. One way to accomplish this is to load the externally-defined filter elsewhere within the same page in some element that sends a "
			code load
			- " event (for example, an "
			a data-x-internal=svg-use href="https://svgwg.org/svg2-draft/struct.html#UseElement" id=working-with-externally-defined-svg-filters:svg-use {
				- "SVG "
				code use
			}
			- " element), and wait for the "
			code load
			- " event to be dispatched."
		}
		h6 id=drawing-model {
			span class=secno "4.12.5.1.21"
			dfn "Drawing model"
			a class=self-link href="#drawing-model"
		}
		p "When a shape or image is painted, user agents must follow these steps, in the order given (or act as if they do):"
		ol {
			li {
				p {
					- "Render the shape or image onto an infinite "
					a data-x-internal=transparent-black href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-color/#transparent-black" id=drawing-model:transparent-black "transparent black"
					- " bitmap, creating image "
					var A
					- ", as described in the previous sections. For shapes, the current fill, stroke, and line styles must be honored, and the stroke must itself also be subjected to the current transformation matrix."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "Multiply the alpha component of every pixel in "
					var A
					- " by "
					code id=drawing-model:concept-canvas-global-alpha {
						a href="#concept-canvas-global-alpha" "global alpha"
					}
					- .
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "When the "
					a href="#concept-canvas-current-filter" id=drawing-model:concept-canvas-current-filter "current filter"
					- " is set to a value other than \""
					code none
					- "\" and all the externally-defined filters it references, if any, are in documents that are currently loaded, then use image "
					var A
					- " as the input to the "
					a href="#concept-canvas-current-filter" id=drawing-model:concept-canvas-current-filter-2 "current filter"
					- ", creating image "
					var B
					- ". If the "
					a href="#concept-canvas-current-filter" id=drawing-model:concept-canvas-current-filter-3 "current filter"
					- " is a string parseable as a "
					a data-x-internal=filter-value-list href="https://drafts.fxtf.org/filter-effects/#typedef-filter-value-list" id=drawing-model:filter-value-list <filter-value-list>
					- ", then draw using the "
					a href="#concept-canvas-current-filter" id=drawing-model:concept-canvas-current-filter-4 "current filter"
					- " in the same manner as SVG."
				}
				p {
					- "Otherwise, let "
					var B
					- " be an alias for "
					var A
					- .
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					a href="#when-shadows-are-drawn" id=drawing-model:when-shadows-are-drawn "When shadows are drawn"
					- ", render the shadow from image "
					var B
					- ", using the current shadow styles, creating image "
					var C
					- .
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					a href="#when-shadows-are-drawn" id=drawing-model:when-shadows-are-drawn-2 "When shadows are drawn"
					- ", composite "
					var C
					- " within the "
					a href="#clipping-region" id=drawing-model:clipping-region "clipping region"
					- " over the current "
					a href="#output-bitmap" id=drawing-model:output-bitmap "output bitmap"
					- " using the "
					a href="#current-compositing-and-blending-operator" id=drawing-model:current-compositing-and-blending-operator "current compositing and blending operator"
					- .
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "Composite "
					var B
					- " within the "
					a href="#clipping-region" id=drawing-model:clipping-region-2 "clipping region"
					- " over the current "
					a href="#output-bitmap" id=drawing-model:output-bitmap-2 "output bitmap"
					- " using the "
					a href="#current-compositing-and-blending-operator" id=drawing-model:current-compositing-and-blending-operator-2 "current compositing and blending operator"
					- .
				}
			}
		}
		p {
			- "When compositing onto the "
			a href="#output-bitmap" id=drawing-model:output-bitmap-3 "output bitmap"
			- ", pixels that would fall outside of the "
			a href="#output-bitmap" id=drawing-model:output-bitmap-4 "output bitmap"
			- " must be discarded."
		}
		h6 id=best-practices {
			span class=secno "4.12.5.1.22"
			- " Best practices"
			a class=self-link href="#best-practices"
		}
		p {
			- "When a canvas is interactive, authors should include "
			a href="#focusable" id=best-practices:focusable focusable
			- " elements in the element's fallback content corresponding to each "
			a href="#focusable" id=best-practices:focusable-2 focusable
			- " part of the canvas, as in the "
			a href="#drawCustomFocusRingExample" "example above"
			- .
		}
		p {
			- "When rendering focus rings, to ensure that focus rings have the appearance of native focus rings, authors should use the "
			code id=best-practices:dom-context-2d-drawfocusifneeded {
				a href="#dom-context-2d-drawfocusifneeded" "drawFocusIfNeeded()"
			}
			- " method, passing it the element for which a ring is being drawn. This method only draws the focus ring if the element is "
			a href="#focused" id=best-practices:focused focused
			- ", so that it can simply be called whenever drawing the element, without checking whether the element is focused or not first."
		}
		p id=no-text-editing-in-canvas-please {
			- "Authors should avoid implementing text editing controls using the "
			code id=best-practices:the-canvas-element {
				a href="#the-canvas-element" canvas
			}
			- " element. Doing so has a large number of disadvantages:"
		}
		ul {
			li "Mouse placement of the caret has to be reimplemented."
			li "Keyboard movement of the caret has to be reimplemented (possibly across lines, for multiline text input)."
			li "Scrolling of the text control has to be implemented (horizontally for long lines, vertically for multiline input)."
			li "Native features such as copy-and-paste have to be reimplemented."
			li "Native features such as spell-checking have to be reimplemented."
			li "Native features such as drag-and-drop have to be reimplemented."
			li "Native features such as page-wide text search have to be reimplemented."
			li "Native features specific to the user, for example custom text services, have to be reimplemented. This is close to impossible since each user might have different services installed, and there is an unbounded set of possible such services."
			li "Bidirectional text editing has to be reimplemented."
			li "For multiline text editing, line wrapping has to be implemented for all relevant languages."
			li "Text selection has to be reimplemented."
			li "Dragging of bidirectional text selections has to be reimplemented."
			li "Platform-native keyboard shortcuts have to be reimplemented."
			li "Platform-native input method editors (IMEs) have to be reimplemented."
			li "Undo and redo functionality has to be reimplemented."
			li "Accessibility features such as magnification following the caret or selection have to be reimplemented."
		}
		p {
			- "This is a huge amount of work, and authors are most strongly encouraged to avoid doing any of it by instead using the "
			code id=best-practices:the-input-element {
				a href="#the-input-element" input
			}
			- " element, the "
			code id=best-practices:the-textarea-element {
				a href="#the-textarea-element" textarea
			}
			- " element, or the "
			code id=best-practices:attr-contenteditable {
				a href="#attr-contenteditable" contenteditable
			}
			- " attribute."
		}
		h6 id=examples {
			span class=secno "4.12.5.1.23"
			- " Examples"
			a class=self-link href="#examples"
		}
		p {
			i "This section is non-normative."
		}
