		p {
			- "Even with this rather-complicated element definition, the element is not a pleasure to use for consumers: it will be continually \"sprouting\" "
			code id=custom-elements-autonomous-drawbacks:attr-tabindex-3 {
				a href="#attr-tabindex" tabindex
			}
			- " attributes of its own volition, and its choice of "
			code "tabindex=\"0\""
			- " focusability behavior may not match the "
			code id=custom-elements-autonomous-drawbacks:the-button-element {
				a href="#the-button-element" button
			}
			- " behavior on the current platform. This is because as of now there is no way to specify default focus behavior for custom elements, forcing the use of the "
			code id=custom-elements-autonomous-drawbacks:attr-tabindex-4 {
				a href="#attr-tabindex" tabindex
			}
			- " attribute to do so (even though it is usually reserved for allowing the consumer to override default behavior)."
		}
		p {
			- "In contrast, a simple "
			a href="#customized-built-in-element" id=custom-elements-autonomous-drawbacks:customized-built-in-element "customized built-in element"
			- ", as shown in the previous section, would automatically inherit the semantics and behavior of the "
			code id=custom-elements-autonomous-drawbacks:the-button-element-2 {
				a href="#the-button-element" button
			}
			- " element, with no need to implement these behaviors manually. In general, for any elements with nontrivial behavior and semantics that build on top of existing elements of HTML, "
			a href="#customized-built-in-element" id=custom-elements-autonomous-drawbacks:customized-built-in-element-2 "customized built-in elements"
			- " will be easier to develop, maintain, and consume."
		}
		h5 id=custom-elements-upgrades-examples {
			span class=secno "4.13.1.6"
			- " Upgrading elements after their creation"
			a class=self-link href="#custom-elements-upgrades-examples"
		}
		p {
			i "This section is non-normative."
		}
		p {
			- "Because "
			a href="#element-definition" id=custom-elements-upgrades-examples:element-definition "element definition"
			- " can occur at any time, a non-custom element could be "
			a data-x-internal=create-an-element href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-create-element" id=custom-elements-upgrades-examples:create-an-element created
			- ", and then later become a "
			a href="#custom-element" id=custom-elements-upgrades-examples:custom-element "custom element"
			- " after an appropriate "
			a href="#custom-element-definition" id=custom-elements-upgrades-examples:custom-element-definition definition
			- " is registered. We call this process \"upgrading\" the element, from a normal element into a custom element."
		}
		p {
			a href="#upgrades" id=custom-elements-upgrades-examples:upgrades Upgrades
			- " enable scenarios where it may be preferable for "
			a href="#custom-element-definition" id=custom-elements-upgrades-examples:custom-element-definition-2 "custom element definitions"
			- " to be registered after relevant elements have been initially created, such as by the parser. They allow progressive enhancement of the content in the custom element. For example, in the following HTML document the element definition for "
			code img-viewer
			- " is loaded asynchronously:"
		}
		pre {
			code class=html {
				c- cp="" "<!DOCTYPE html>"
				c- p="" <
				c- f="" html
				c- e="" lang
				c- o="" "="
				c- s="" "\"en\""
				c- p="" >
				c- p="" <
				c- f="" title
				c- p="" >
				- "Image viewer example"
				c- p="" "</"
				c- f="" title
				c- p="" >
				c- p="" <
				c- f="" img-viewer
				c- e="" filter
				c- o="" "="
				c- s="" "\"Kelvin\""
				c- p="" >
				c- p="" <
				c- f="" img
				c- e="" src
				c- o="" "="
				c- s="" "\"images/tree.jpg\""
				c- e="" alt
				c- o="" "="
				c- s="" "\"A beautiful tree towering over an empty savannah\""
				c- p="" >
				c- p="" "</"
				c- f="" img-viewer
				c- p="" >
				c- p="" <
				c- f="" script
				c- e="" src
				c- o="" "="
				c- s="" "\"js/elements/img-viewer.js\""
				c- e="" async
				c- p="" "></"
				c- f="" script
				c- p="" >
			}
		}
		p {
			- "The definition for the "
			code img-viewer
			- " element here is loaded using a "
			code id=custom-elements-upgrades-examples:the-script-element {
				a href="#the-script-element" script
			}
			- " element marked with the "
			code id=custom-elements-upgrades-examples:attr-script-async {
				a href="#attr-script-async" async
			}
			- " attribute, placed after the "
			code <img-viewer>
			- " tag in the markup. While the script is loading, the "
			code img-viewer
			- " element will be treated as an undefined element, similar to a "
			code id=custom-elements-upgrades-examples:the-span-element {
				a href="#the-span-element" span
			}
			- ". Once the script loads, it will define the "
			code img-viewer
			- " element, and the existing "
			code img-viewer
			- " element on the page will be upgraded, applying the custom element's definition (which presumably includes applying an image filter identified by the string \"Kelvin\", enhancing the image's visual appearance)."
		}
		hr
		p {
			- "Note that "
			a href="#upgrades" id=custom-elements-upgrades-examples:upgrades-2 upgrades
			- " only apply to elements in the document tree. (Formally, elements that are "
			a data-x-internal=connected href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#connected" id=custom-elements-upgrades-examples:connected connected
			- ".) An element that is not inserted into a document will stay un-upgraded. An example illustrates this point:"
		}
		pre {
			code class=html {
				c- cp="" "<!DOCTYPE html>"
				c- p="" <
				c- f="" html
				c- e="" lang
				c- o="" "="
				c- s="" "\"en\""
				c- p="" >
				c- p="" <
				c- f="" title
				c- p="" >
				- "Upgrade edge-cases example"
				c- p="" "</"
				c- f="" title
				c- p="" >
				c- p="" <
				c- f="" example-element
				c- p="" "></"
				c- f="" example-element
				c- p="" >
				c- p="" <
				c- f="" script
				c- p="" >
				c- u="" "\"use strict\""
				c- p="" ";"
				c- a="" const
				- " inDocument "
				c- o="" "="
				- " document"
				c- p="" .
				- querySelector
				c- p="" "("
				c- u="" "\"example-element\""
				c- p="" ");"
				c- a="" const
				- " outOfDocument "
				c- o="" "="
				- " document"
				c- p="" .
				- createElement
				c- p="" "("
				c- u="" "\"example-element\""
				c- p="" ");"
				c- c1="" "// Before the element definition, both are HTMLElement:"
				- " console"
				c- p="" .
				- assert
				c- p="" "("
				- "inDocument "
				c- k="" instanceof
				- " HTMLElement"
				c- p="" ");"
				- " console"
				c- p="" .
				- assert
				c- p="" "("
				- "outOfDocument "
				c- k="" instanceof
				- " HTMLElement"
				c- p="" ");"
				c- a="" class
				- " ExampleElement "
				c- k="" extends
				- " HTMLElement "
				c- p="" "{}"
				- " customElements"
				c- p="" .
				- define
				c- p="" "("
				c- u="" "\"example-element\""
				c- p="" ,
