		p {
			- "Elements with an "
			code id=items:attr-itemscope-8 {
				a href="#attr-itemscope" itemscope
			}
			- " attribute may have an "
			dfn data-dfn-for=html-global data-dfn-type=element-attr id=attr-itemref {
				code itemref
			}
			- " attribute specified, to give a list of additional elements to crawl to find the name-value pairs of the "
			a href="#concept-item" id=items:concept-item-11 item
			- .
		}
		p {
			- "The "
			code id=items:attr-itemref {
				a href="#attr-itemref" itemref
			}
			- " attribute, if specified, must have a value that is an "
			a href="#unordered-set-of-unique-space-separated-tokens" id=items:unordered-set-of-unique-space-separated-tokens-2 "unordered set of unique space-separated tokens"
			- " none of which are "
			a data-x-internal=identical-to href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#string-is" id=items:identical-to-2 "identical to"
			- " another token and consisting of "
			a data-x-internal=concept-id href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-id" id=items:concept-id IDs
			- " of elements in the same "
			a data-x-internal=tree href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-tree" id=items:tree tree
			- .
		}
		p {
			- "The "
			code id=items:attr-itemref-2 {
				a href="#attr-itemref" itemref
			}
			- " attribute must not be specified on elements that do not have an "
			code id=items:attr-itemscope-9 {
				a href="#attr-itemscope" itemscope
			}
			- " attribute specified."
		}
		p class=note {
			- "The "
			code id=items:attr-itemref-3 {
				a href="#attr-itemref" itemref
			}
			- " attribute is not part of the microdata data model. It is merely a syntactic construct to aid authors in adding annotations to pages where the data to be annotated does not follow a convenient tree structure. For example, it allows authors to mark up data in a table so that each column defines a separate "
			a href="#concept-item" id=items:concept-item-12 item
			- ", while keeping the properties in the cells."
		}
		div class=example {
			p "This example shows a simple vocabulary used to describe the products of a model railway manufacturer. The vocabulary has just five property names:"
			dl {
				dt product-code
				dd "An integer that names the product in the manufacturer's catalog."
				dt name
				dd "A brief description of the product."
				dt scale
				dd "One of \"HO\", \"1\", or \"Z\" (potentially with leading or trailing whitespace), indicating the scale of the product."
				dt digital
				dd "If present, one of \"Digital\", \"Delta\", or \"Systems\" (potentially with leading or trailing whitespace) indicating that the product has a digital decoder of the given type."
				dt track-type
				dd "For track-specific products, one of \"K\", \"M\", \"C\" (potentially with leading or trailing whitespace) indicating the type of track for which the product is intended."
			}
			p {
				- "This vocabulary has four defined "
				a href="#item-types" id=items:item-types-10 "item types"
				- :
			}
			dl {
				dt "https://md.example.com/loco"
				dd "Rolling stock with an engine"
				dt "https://md.example.com/passengers"
				dd "Passenger rolling stock"
				dt "https://md.example.com/track"
				dd "Track pieces"
				dt "https://md.example.com/lighting"
				dd "Equipment with lighting"
			}
			p {
				- "Each "
				a href="#concept-item" id=items:concept-item-13 item
				- " that uses this vocabulary can be given one or more of these types, depending on what the product is."
			}
			p "Thus, a locomotive might be marked up as:"
			pre {
				code class=html {
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" dl
					c- e="" itemscope
					c- e="" itemtype
					c- o="" "="
					c- s="" "\"https://md.example.com/loco"
					c- s="" " https://md.example.com/lighting\""
					c- p="" >
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" dt
					c- p="" >
					- "Name: "
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" dd
					c- e="" itemprop
					c- o="" "="
					c- s="" "\"name\""
					c- p="" >
					- "Tank Locomotive (DB 80) "
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" dt
					c- p="" >
					- "Product code: "
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" dd
					c- e="" itemprop
					c- o="" "="
					c- s="" "\"product-code\""
					c- p="" >
					- "33041 "
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" dt
					c- p="" >
					- "Scale: "
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" dd
					c- e="" itemprop
					c- o="" "="
					c- s="" "\"scale\""
					c- p="" >
					- "HO "
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" dt
					c- p="" >
					- "Digital: "
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" dd
					c- e="" itemprop
					c- o="" "="
					c- s="" "\"digital\""
					c- p="" >
					- "Delta "
					c- p="" "</"
					c- f="" dl
					c- p="" >
				}
			}
			p "A turnout lantern retrofit kit might be marked up as:"
			pre {
				code class=html {
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" dl
					c- e="" itemscope
					c- e="" itemtype
					c- o="" "="
					c- s="" "\"https://md.example.com/track"
					c- s="" " https://md.example.com/lighting\""
					c- p="" >
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" dt
					c- p="" >
					- "Name: "
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" dd
					c- e="" itemprop
					c- o="" "="
					c- s="" "\"name\""
					c- p="" >
					- "Turnout Lantern Kit "
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" dt
					c- p="" >
					- "Product code: "
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" dd
					c- e="" itemprop
					c- o="" "="
					c- s="" "\"product-code\""
					c- p="" >
					- "74470 "
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" dt
					c- p="" >
					- "Purpose: "
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" dd
					c- p="" >
					- "For retrofitting 2 "
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" span
					c- e="" itemprop
					c- o="" "="
					c- s="" "\"track-type\""
					c- p="" >
					- C
					c- p="" "</"
					c- f="" span
					c- p="" >
					- " Track turnouts. "
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" meta
					c- e="" itemprop
					c- o="" "="
					c- s="" "\"scale\""
					c- e="" content
					c- o="" "="
					c- s="" "\"HO\""
					c- p="" >
					c- p="" "</"
					c- f="" dl
					c- p="" >
				}
			}
			p "A passenger car with no lighting might be marked up as:"
			pre {
				code class=html {
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" dl
					c- e="" itemscope
					c- e="" itemtype
					c- o="" "="
					c- s="" "\"https://md.example.com/passengers\""
					c- p="" >
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" dt
					c- p="" >
					- "Name: "
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" dd
					c- e="" itemprop
					c- o="" "="
					c- s="" "\"name\""
					c- p="" >
					- "Express Train Passenger Car (DB Am 203) "
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" dt
					c- p="" >
					- "Product code: "
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" dd
					c- e="" itemprop
					c- o="" "="
					c- s="" "\"product-code\""
					c- p="" >
					- "8710 "
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" dt
					c- p="" >
					- "Scale: "
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" dd
					c- e="" itemprop
					c- o="" "="
					c- s="" "\"scale\""
					c- p="" >
					- "Z "
					c- p="" "</"
					c- f="" dl
					c- p="" >
				}
			}
			p "Great care is necessary when creating new vocabularies. Often, a hierarchical approach to types can be taken that results in a vocabulary where each item only ever has a single type, which is generally much simpler to manage."
		}
		h4 id=names:-the-itemprop-attribute {
			span class=secno "5.2.3"
			- " Names: the "
			dfn data-dfn-for=html-global data-dfn-type=element-attr {
				code itemprop
			}
			- " attribute"
			a class=self-link href="#names:-the-itemprop-attribute"
		}
		div class="mdn-anno wrapped" {
			button class=mdn-anno-btn onclick="toggleStatus(this)" {
				b class=all-engines-flag title="Support in all current engines." ✔
				span MDN
			}
			div class=feature {
				p {
					a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTML/Global_attributes/itemprop" title="The itemprop global attribute is used to add properties to an item. Every HTML element can have an itemprop attribute specified, and an itemprop consists of a name-value pair. Each name-value pair is called a property, and a group of one or more properties forms an item. Property values are either a string or a URL and can be associated with a very wide range of elements including <audio>, <embed>, <iframe>, <img>, <link>, <object>, <source>, <track>, and <video>." "Global_attributes/itemprop"
				}
				p class=all-engines-text "Support in all current engines."
				div class=support {
					span class="firefox yes" {
						span Firefox
						span Yes
					}
					span class="safari yes" {
						span Safari
						span Yes
					}
					span class="chrome yes" {
						span Chrome
						span Yes
					}
					hr
					span class="opera unknown" {
						span Opera
						span ?
					}
					span class="edge_blink yes" {
						span Edge
						span Yes
					}
					hr
					span class="edge yes" {
						span "Edge (Legacy)"
						span "12+"
					}
					span class="ie yes" {
						span "Internet Explorer"
						span Yes
					}
					hr
					span class="firefox_android unknown" {
						span "Firefox Android"
						span ?
					}
					span class="safari_ios unknown" {
						span "Safari iOS"
						span ?
					}
					span class="chrome_android unknown" {
						span "Chrome Android"
						span ?
					}
					span class="webview_android unknown" {
						span "WebView Android"
						span ?
					}
					span class="samsunginternet_android unknown" {
						span "Samsung Internet"
						span ?
					}
					span class="opera_android unknown" {
						span "Opera Android"
						span ?
					}
				}
			}
		}
		p {
			- "Every "
			a href="#html-elements" id=names:-the-itemprop-attribute:html-elements "HTML element"
			- " may have an "
			code id=names:-the-itemprop-attribute:names:-the-itemprop-attribute {
				a href="#names:-the-itemprop-attribute" itemprop
			}
			- " attribute specified, if doing so "
			a href="#the-properties-of-an-item" id=names:-the-itemprop-attribute:the-properties-of-an-item "adds one or more properties"
			- " to one or more "
			a href="#concept-item" id=names:-the-itemprop-attribute:concept-item items
			- " (as defined below)."
		}
		p {
			- "The "
			code id=names:-the-itemprop-attribute:names:-the-itemprop-attribute-2 {
				a href="#names:-the-itemprop-attribute" itemprop
			}
			- " attribute, if specified, must have a value that is an "
			a href="#unordered-set-of-unique-space-separated-tokens" id=names:-the-itemprop-attribute:unordered-set-of-unique-space-separated-tokens "unordered set of unique space-separated tokens"
			- " none of which are "
			a data-x-internal=identical-to href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#string-is" id=names:-the-itemprop-attribute:identical-to "identical to"
			- " another token, representing the names of the name-value pairs that it adds. The attribute's value must have at least one token."
		}
		p "Each token must be either:"
		ul {
			li {
				- "If the item is a "
				a href="#typed-item" id=names:-the-itemprop-attribute:typed-item "typed item"
				- ": a "
				dfn id=defined-property-name "defined property name"
				- " allowed in this situation according to the specification that defines the "
				a href="#relevant-types" id=names:-the-itemprop-attribute:relevant-types "relevant types"
				- " for the item, or"
			}
			li {
				- "A "
				a data-x-internal=valid-url-string href="https://url.spec.whatwg.org/#valid-url-string" id=names:-the-itemprop-attribute:valid-url-string "valid URL string"
				- " that is an "
				a data-x-internal=absolute-url href="https://url.spec.whatwg.org/#syntax-url-absolute" id=names:-the-itemprop-attribute:absolute-url "absolute URL"
				- " defined as an item property name allowed in this situation by a vocabulary specification, or"
			}
			li {
				- "A "
				a data-x-internal=valid-url-string href="https://url.spec.whatwg.org/#valid-url-string" id=names:-the-itemprop-attribute:valid-url-string-2 "valid URL string"
				- " that is an "
				a data-x-internal=absolute-url href="https://url.spec.whatwg.org/#syntax-url-absolute" id=names:-the-itemprop-attribute:absolute-url-2 "absolute URL"
				- ", used as a proprietary item property name (i.e. one used by the author for private purposes, not defined in a public specification), or"
			}
			li {
				- "If the item is not a "
				a href="#typed-item" id=names:-the-itemprop-attribute:typed-item-2 "typed item"
				- ": a string that contains no U+002E FULL STOP characters (.) and no U+003A COLON characters (:), used as a proprietary item property name (i.e. one used by the author for private purposes, not defined in a public specification)."
			}
		}
		p {
			- "Specifications that introduce "
			a href="#defined-property-name" id=names:-the-itemprop-attribute:defined-property-name "defined property names"
			- " must ensure all such property names contain no U+002E FULL STOP characters (.), no U+003A COLON characters (:), and no "
			a data-x-internal=space-characters href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ascii-whitespace" id=names:-the-itemprop-attribute:space-characters "ASCII whitespace"
			- .
		}
		p class=note {
			- "The rules above disallow U+003A COLON characters (:) in non-URL values because otherwise they could not be distinguished from URLs. Values with U+002E FULL STOP characters (.) are reserved for future extensions. "
			a data-x-internal=space-characters href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ascii-whitespace" id=names:-the-itemprop-attribute:space-characters-2 "ASCII whitespace"
			- " are disallowed because otherwise the values would be parsed as multiple tokens."
		}
		p {
			- "When an element with an "
			code id=names:-the-itemprop-attribute:names:-the-itemprop-attribute-3 {
				a href="#names:-the-itemprop-attribute" itemprop
			}
			- " attribute "
			a href="#the-properties-of-an-item" id=names:-the-itemprop-attribute:the-properties-of-an-item-2 "adds a property"
			- " to multiple "
			a href="#concept-item" id=names:-the-itemprop-attribute:concept-item-2 items
			- ", the requirement above regarding the tokens applies for each "
			a href="#concept-item" id=names:-the-itemprop-attribute:concept-item-3 item
			- " individually."
