					span class="firefox yes" {
						span Firefox
						span title="Requires setting a user preference or runtime flag." "🔰 114+"
					}
					span class="safari yes" {
						span Safari
						span "17+"
					}
					span class="chrome yes" {
						span Chrome
						span "114+"
					}
					hr
					span class="opera unknown" {
						span Opera
						span ?
					}
					span class="edge_blink yes" {
						span Edge
						span "114+"
					}
					hr
					span class="edge unknown" {
						span "Edge (Legacy)"
						span ?
					}
					span class="ie no" {
						span "Internet Explorer"
						span No
					}
					hr
					span class="firefox_android unknown" {
						span "Firefox Android"
						span ?
					}
					span class="safari_ios unknown" {
						span "Safari iOS"
						span ?
					}
					span class="chrome_android unknown" {
						span "Chrome Android"
						span ?
					}
					span class="webview_android unknown" {
						span "WebView Android"
						span ?
					}
					span class="samsunginternet_android unknown" {
						span "Samsung Internet"
						span ?
					}
					span class="opera_android unknown" {
						span "Opera Android"
						span ?
					}
				}
			}
		}
		p {
			- "The "
			dfn data-dfn-for=ToggleEvent data-dfn-type=attribute id=dom-toggleevent-oldstate {
				code oldState
			}
			- " and "
			dfn data-dfn-for=ToggleEvent data-dfn-type=attribute id=dom-toggleevent-newstate {
				code newState
			}
			- " attributes must return the values they are initialized to."
		}
		p {
			- "A "
			dfn id=toggle-task-tracker "toggle task tracker"
			- " is a "
			a data-x-internal=struct href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#struct" id=the-toggleevent-interface:struct struct
			- " which has:"
		}
		dl {
			dt {
				dfn id=toggle-task-task task
			}
			dd {
				- "A "
				a href="#concept-task" id=the-toggleevent-interface:concept-task task
				- " which fires a "
				code id=the-toggleevent-interface:toggleevent-2 {
					a href="#toggleevent" ToggleEvent
				}
				- .
			}
			dt {
				dfn id=toggle-task-old-state "old state"
			}
			dd {
				- "A string which represents the "
				a href="#toggle-task-task" id=the-toggleevent-interface:toggle-task-task task
				- "'s event's value for the "
				code id=the-toggleevent-interface:dom-toggleevent-oldstate-2 {
					a href="#dom-toggleevent-oldstate" oldState
				}
				- " attribute."
			}
		}
		h3 id=focus {
			span class=secno "6.6"
			- " Focus"
			a class=self-link href="#focus"
		}
		h4 id=introduction-8 {
			span class=secno "6.6.1"
			- " Introduction"
			a class=self-link href="#introduction-8"
		}
		p {
			i "This section is non-normative."
		}
		p "An HTML user interface typically consists of multiple interactive widgets, such as form controls, scrollable regions, links, dialog boxes, browser tabs, and so forth. These widgets form a hierarchy, with some (e.g. browser tabs, dialog boxes) containing others (e.g. links, form controls)."
		p {
			- "When interacting with an interface using a keyboard, key input is channeled from the system, through the hierarchy of interactive widgets, to an active widget, which is said to be "
			a href="#focused" id=introduction-8:focused focused
			- .
		}
		div class=example {
			p "Consider an HTML application running in a browser tab running in a graphical environment. Suppose this application had a page with some text controls and links, and was currently showing a modal dialog, which itself had a text control and a button."
			p "The hierarchy of focusable widgets, in this scenario, would include the browser window, which would have, amongst its children, the browser tab containing the HTML application. The tab itself would have as its children the various links and text controls, as well as the dialog. The dialog itself would have as its children the text control and the button."
			p {
				img alt="" height="450" src="/images/focus-tree.png" width="800"
			}
			p {
				- "If the widget with "
				a href="#focused" id=introduction-8:focused-2 focus
				- " in this example was the text control in the dialog box, then key input would be channeled from the graphical system to ① the web browser, then to ② the tab, then to ③ the dialog, and finally to ④ the text control."
			}
		}
		p {
			- "Keyboard "
			em events
			- " are always targeted at this "
			a href="#focused" id=introduction-8:focused-3 focused
			- " element."
		}
		h4 id=data-model {
			span class=secno "6.6.2"
			- " Data model"
			a class=self-link href="#data-model"
		}
		p id=tlbc-system-focus {
			- "A "
			a href="#top-level-traversable" id=data-model:top-level-traversable "top-level traversable"
			- " has "
			dfn data-dfn-for="top-level\n  traversable" data-export="" id=system-focus "system focus"
			- " when it can receive keyboard input channeled from the operating system, possibly targeted at one of its "
			a href="#nav-document" id=data-model:nav-document "active document"
			- "'s "
			a href="#descendant-navigables" id=data-model:descendant-navigables "descendant navigables"
			- .
		}
		p {
			- "A "
			a href="#top-level-traversable" id=data-model:top-level-traversable-2 "top-level traversable"
			- " has "
			dfn data-dfn-for="top-level traversable" id=user-attention "user attention"
			- " when its "
			a href="#system-visibility-state" id=data-model:system-visibility-state "system visibility state"
			- " is \""
			code visible
			- "\", and it either has "
			a href="#system-focus" id=data-model:system-focus "system focus"
			- " or user agent widgets directly related to it can receive keyboard input channeled from the operating system."
		}
		p class=note "User attention is lost when a browser window loses focus, whereas system focus might also be lost to other system widgets in the browser window such as a location bar."
		p {
			- "A "
			code id=data-model:document {
				a href="#document" Document
			}
			var d
			- " is a "
			dfn data-dfn-for=Document data-export="" id=fully-active-descendant-of-a-top-level-traversable-with-user-attention "fully active descendant of a top-level traversable with user attention"
			- " when "
			var d
			- " is "
			a href="#fully-active" id=data-model:fully-active "fully active"
			- " and "
			var d
			- "'s "
			a href="#node-navigable" id=data-model:node-navigable "node navigable"
			- "'s "
			a href="#nav-top" id=data-model:nav-top "top-level traversable"
			- " has "
			a href="#user-attention" id=data-model:user-attention "user attention"
			- .
		}
		p {
			- "The term "
			dfn id=focusable-area "focusable area"
			- " is used to refer to regions of the interface that can further become the target of such keyboard input. Focusable areas can be elements, parts of elements, or other regions managed by the user agent."
		}
		p {
			- "Each "
			a href="#focusable-area" id=data-model:focusable-area "focusable area"
			- " has a "
			dfn id=dom-anchor "DOM anchor"
			- ", which is a "
			code id=data-model:node {
				a data-x-internal=node href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#interface-node" Node
			}
			- " object that represents the position of the "
			a href="#focusable-area" id=data-model:focusable-area-2 "focusable area"
			- " in the DOM. (When the "
			a href="#focusable-area" id=data-model:focusable-area-3 "focusable area"
			- " is itself a "
			code id=data-model:node-2 {
				a data-x-internal=node href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#interface-node" Node
			}
			- ", it is its own "
			a href="#dom-anchor" id=data-model:dom-anchor "DOM anchor"
			- ".) The "
			a href="#dom-anchor" id=data-model:dom-anchor-2 "DOM anchor"
			- " is used in some APIs as a substitute for the "
			a href="#focusable-area" id=data-model:focusable-area-4 "focusable area"
			- " when there is no other DOM object to represent the "
			a href="#focusable-area" id=data-model:focusable-area-5 "focusable area"
			- .
		}
		p {
			- "The following table describes what objects can be "
			a href="#focusable-area" id=data-model:focusable-area-6 "focusable areas"
			- ". The cells in the left column describe objects that can be "
			a href="#focusable-area" id=data-model:focusable-area-7 "focusable areas"
			- "; the cells in the right column describe the "
			a href="#dom-anchor" id=data-model:dom-anchor-3 "DOM anchors"
			- " for those elements. (The cells that span both columns are non-normative examples.)"
		}
		table id=table-fa {
			thead {
				tr {
					th id=th-fa-area {
						a href="#focusable-area" id=data-model:focusable-area-8 "Focusable area"
					}
					th id=th-fa-dom-rep {
						a href="#dom-anchor" id=data-model:dom-anchor-4 "DOM anchor"
					}
				}
				tr {
					th colspan="2" id=th-fa-examples "Examples "
				}
			}
			tbody {
				tr {
					th class=data-header headers=th-fa-area id=td-fa-1 {
						- " Elements that meet all the following criteria: "
						ul class=brief {
							li {
								- "the element's "
								a href="#tabindex-value" id=data-model:tabindex-value "tabindex value"
								- " is non-null, or the element is determined by the user agent to be focusable;"
							}
							li {
								- "the element is either not a "
								a data-x-internal=shadow-host href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#element-shadow-host" id=data-model:shadow-host "shadow host"
								- ", or has a "
								a data-x-internal=concept-element-shadow-root href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-element-shadow-root" id=data-model:concept-element-shadow-root "shadow root"
								- " whose "
								a data-x-internal=delegates-focus href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#shadowroot-delegates-focus" id=data-model:delegates-focus "delegates focus"
								- " is false;"
							}
							li {
								- "the element is not "
								a href="#concept-element-disabled" id=data-model:concept-element-disabled "actually disabled"
								- ";"
							}
							li {
								- "the element is not "
								a href="#inert" id=data-model:inert inert
								- ";"
							}
							li {
								- "the element is either "
								a href="#being-rendered" id=data-model:being-rendered "being rendered"
								- ", "
								a href="#delegating-its-rendering-to-its-children" id=data-model:delegating-its-rendering-to-its-children "delegating its rendering to its children"
								- ", or "
								a href="#being-used-as-relevant-canvas-fallback-content" id=data-model:being-used-as-relevant-canvas-fallback-content "being used as relevant canvas fallback content"
								- .
							}
						}
					}
					td headers="td-fa-1 th-fa-dom-rep" " The element itself. "
				}
				tr {
					td colspan="2" headers="td-fa-1 th-fa-examples" {
						p class=example {
							code id=data-model:the-iframe-element {
								a href="#the-iframe-element" iframe
							}
							- ", "
							code id=data-model:the-dialog-element {
								a href="#the-dialog-element" dialog
							}
							- ", "
							code id="data-model:text-(type=text)-state-and-search-state-(type=search)" {
								a href="#text-(type=text)-state-and-search-state-(type=search)" "<input type=text>"
							}
							- ", sometimes "
							code id=data-model:the-a-element {
								a href="#the-a-element" "<a href=\"\">"
							}
							- " (depending on platform conventions). "
						}
					}
				}
			}
			tbody {
				tr {
					th class=data-header headers=th-fa-area id=td-fa-2 {
						- " The shapes of "
						code id=data-model:the-area-element {
							a href="#the-area-element" area
						}
						- " elements in an "
