		}
		p class=note id=bc-focus-ergo-bcc-focus {
			- "A "
			a href="#navigable-container" id=data-model:navigable-container "navigable container"
			- " (e.g. an "
			code id=data-model:the-iframe-element-3 {
				a href="#the-iframe-element" iframe
			}
			- ") is a "
			a href="#focusable-area" id=data-model:focusable-area-10 "focusable area"
			- ", but key events routed to a "
			a href="#navigable-container" id=data-model:navigable-container-2 "navigable container"
			- " get immediately routed to its "
			a href="#content-navigable" id=data-model:content-navigable "content navigable"
			- "'s "
			a href="#nav-document" id=data-model:nav-document-2 "active document"
			- ". Similarly, in sequential focus navigation a "
			a href="#navigable-container" id=data-model:navigable-container-3 "navigable container"
			- " essentially acts merely as a placeholder for its "
			a href="#content-navigable" id=data-model:content-navigable-2 "content navigable"
			- "'s "
			a href="#nav-document" id=data-model:nav-document-3 "active document"
			- .
		}
		hr
		p {
			- "One "
			a href="#focusable-area" id=data-model:focusable-area-11 "focusable area"
			- " in each "
			code id=data-model:document-4 {
				a href="#document" Document
			}
			- " is designated the "
			dfn id=focused-area-of-the-document "focused area of the document"
			- ". Which control is so designated changes over time, based on algorithms in this specification."
		}
		p class=note {
			- "Even if a document is not "
			a href="#fully-active" id=data-model:fully-active-2 "fully active"
			- " and not shown to the user, it can still have a "
			a href="#focused-area-of-the-document" id=data-model:focused-area-of-the-document "focused area of the document"
			- ". If a document's "
			a href="#fully-active" id=data-model:fully-active-3 "fully active"
			- " state changes, its "
			a href="#focused-area-of-the-document" id=data-model:focused-area-of-the-document-2 "focused area of the document"
			- " will stay the same."
		}
