		h4 id=keyboard-shortcuts-processing-model {
			span class=secno "6.7.3"
			span id=processing-model-6
			- "Processing model"
			a class=self-link href="#keyboard-shortcuts-processing-model"
		}
		p {
			- "An element's "
			dfn id=assigned-access-key "assigned access key"
			- " is a key combination derived from the element's "
			code id=keyboard-shortcuts-processing-model:the-accesskey-attribute {
				a href="#the-accesskey-attribute" accesskey
			}
			- " content attribute. Initially, an element must not have an "
			a href="#assigned-access-key" id=keyboard-shortcuts-processing-model:assigned-access-key "assigned access key"
			- .
		}
		p {
			- "Whenever an element's "
			code id=keyboard-shortcuts-processing-model:the-accesskey-attribute-2 {
				a href="#the-accesskey-attribute" accesskey
			}
			- " attribute is set, changed, or removed, the user agent must update the element's "
			a href="#assigned-access-key" id=keyboard-shortcuts-processing-model:assigned-access-key-2 "assigned access key"
			- " by running the following steps:"
		}
		ol {
			li {
				p {
					- "If the element has no "
					code id=keyboard-shortcuts-processing-model:the-accesskey-attribute-3 {
						a href="#the-accesskey-attribute" accesskey
					}
					- " attribute, then skip to the "
					i fallback
					- " step below."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "Otherwise, "
					a data-x-internal=split-a-string-on-spaces href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#split-on-ascii-whitespace" id=keyboard-shortcuts-processing-model:split-a-string-on-spaces "split the attribute's value on ASCII whitespace"
					- ", and let "
					var keys
					- " be the resulting tokens."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "For each value in "
					var keys
					- " in turn, in the order the tokens appeared in the attribute's value, run the following substeps:"
				}
				ol {
					li {
						p "If the value is not a string exactly one code point in length, then skip the remainder of these steps for this value."
					}
					li {
						p "If the value does not correspond to a key on the system's keyboard, then skip the remainder of these steps for this value."
					}
					li {
						p {
							a class=tracking-vector data-x-internal=tracking-vector href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#tracking-vector" id=keyboard-shortcuts-processing-model:tracking-vector title="There is a tracking vector here." {
								img alt="(This is a tracking vector.)" crossorigin="" height="64" src="https://resources.whatwg.org/tracking-vector.svg" width="46"
							}
							- " If the user agent can find a mix of zero or more modifier keys that, combined with the key that corresponds to the value given in the attribute, can be used as the access key, then the user agent may assign that combination of keys as the element's "
							a href="#assigned-access-key" id=keyboard-shortcuts-processing-model:assigned-access-key-3 "assigned access key"
							- " and return."
						}
					}
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					i Fallback
					- ": Optionally, the user agent may assign a key combination of its choosing as the element's "
					a href="#assigned-access-key" id=keyboard-shortcuts-processing-model:assigned-access-key-4 "assigned access key"
					- " and then return."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "If this step is reached, the element has no "
					a href="#assigned-access-key" id=keyboard-shortcuts-processing-model:assigned-access-key-5 "assigned access key"
					- .
				}
			}
		}
		p {
			- "Once a user agent has selected and assigned an access key for an element, the user agent should not change the element's "
			a href="#assigned-access-key" id=keyboard-shortcuts-processing-model:assigned-access-key-6 "assigned access key"
			- " unless the "
			code id=keyboard-shortcuts-processing-model:the-accesskey-attribute-4 {
				a href="#the-accesskey-attribute" accesskey
			}
			- " content attribute is changed or the element is moved to another "
			code id=keyboard-shortcuts-processing-model:document {
				a href="#document" Document
			}
			- .
		}
		p {
			- "When the user presses the key combination corresponding to the "
			a href="#assigned-access-key" id=keyboard-shortcuts-processing-model:assigned-access-key-7 "assigned access key"
			- " for an element, if the element "
			a href="#concept-command" id=keyboard-shortcuts-processing-model:concept-command "defines a command"
			- ", the command's "
			a href="#command-facet-hiddenstate" id=keyboard-shortcuts-processing-model:command-facet-hiddenstate "Hidden State"
			- " facet is false (visible), the command's "
			a href="#command-facet-disabledstate" id=keyboard-shortcuts-processing-model:command-facet-disabledstate "Disabled State"
			- " facet is also false (enabled), the element is "
			a data-x-internal=in-a-document href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#in-a-document" id=keyboard-shortcuts-processing-model:in-a-document "in a document"
			- " that has a non-null "
			a href="#concept-document-bc" id=keyboard-shortcuts-processing-model:concept-document-bc "browsing context"
			- ", and neither the element nor any of its ancestors has a "
			code id=keyboard-shortcuts-processing-model:attr-hidden {
				a href="#attr-hidden" hidden
			}
			- " attribute specified, then the user agent must trigger the "
			a href="#command-facet-action" id=keyboard-shortcuts-processing-model:command-facet-action Action
			- " of the command."
		}
		p class=note {
			- "User agents "
			a href="#expose-commands-in-ui" "might expose"
			- " elements that have an "
			code id=keyboard-shortcuts-processing-model:the-accesskey-attribute-5 {
