		p {
			- "The "
			dfn data-dfn-for=ElementContentEditable data-dfn-type=attribute id=dom-contenteditable {
				code contentEditable
			}
			- " IDL attribute, on getting, must return the string \""
			code "true"
			- "\" if the content attribute is set to the "
			a href="#attr-contenteditable-true-state" id=contenteditable:attr-contenteditable-true-state "true"
			- " state, \""
			code plaintext-only
			- "\" if the content attribute is set to the "
			a href="#attr-contenteditable-plaintextonly-state" id=contenteditable:attr-contenteditable-plaintextonly-state plaintext-only
			- " state, \""
			code "false"
			- "\" if the content attribute is set to the "
			a href="#attr-contenteditable-false-state" id=contenteditable:attr-contenteditable-false-state "false"
			- " state, and \""
			code id=contenteditable:attr-contenteditable-inherit-state-2 {
				a href="#attr-contenteditable-inherit-state" inherit
			}
			- "\" otherwise. On setting, if the new value is an "
			a data-x-internal=ascii-case-insensitive href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ascii-case-insensitive" id=contenteditable:ascii-case-insensitive "ASCII case-insensitive"
			- " match for the string \""
			code inherit
			- "\" then the content attribute must be removed, if the new value is an "
			a data-x-internal=ascii-case-insensitive href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ascii-case-insensitive" id=contenteditable:ascii-case-insensitive-2 "ASCII case-insensitive"
			- " match for the string \""
			code "true"
			- "\" then the content attribute must be set to the string \""
			code "true"
			- "\", if the new value is an "
			a data-x-internal=ascii-case-insensitive href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ascii-case-insensitive" id=contenteditable:ascii-case-insensitive-3 "ASCII case-insensitive"
			- " match for the string \""
			code plaintext-only
			- "\" then the content attribute must be set to the string \""
			code plaintext-only
			- "\", if the new value is an "
			a data-x-internal=ascii-case-insensitive href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ascii-case-insensitive" id=contenteditable:ascii-case-insensitive-4 "ASCII case-insensitive"
			- " match for the string \""
			code "false"
			- "\" then the content attribute must be set to the string \""
			code "false"
			- "\", and otherwise the attribute setter must throw a "
			a data-x-internal=syntaxerror href="https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#syntaxerror" id=contenteditable:syntaxerror-2 {
				- "\""
				code SyntaxError
				- "\""
			}
			code id=contenteditable:domexception-2 {
				a data-x-internal=domexception href="https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#dfn-DOMException" DOMException
			}
			- .
		}
		p {
			- "The "
			dfn data-dfn-for=ElementContentEditable data-dfn-type=attribute id=dom-iscontenteditable {
				code isContentEditable
			}
			- " IDL attribute, on getting, must return true if the element is either an "
			a href="#editing-host" id=contenteditable:editing-host "editing host"
			- " or "
			a data-x-internal=editable href="https://w3c.github.io/editing/docs/execCommand/#editable" id=contenteditable:editable editable
			- ", and false otherwise."
		}
		h4 id=making-entire-documents-editable:-the-designmode-idl-attribute {
			span class=secno "6.8.2"
			- " Making entire documents editable: the "
			code id=making-entire-documents-editable:-the-designmode-idl-attribute:designMode {
				a href="#designMode" designMode
			}
			- " getter and setter"
			a class=self-link href="#making-entire-documents-editable:-the-designmode-idl-attribute"
		}
		dl class=domintro {
			dt {
				code {
					var document
					- .
					a href="#designMode" id=dom-document-designmode-dev designMode
					- " [ = "
					var value
					- " ]"
				}
				div class="mdn-anno wrapped before" {
					button class=mdn-anno-btn onclick="toggleStatus(this)" {
						b class=all-engines-flag title="Support in all current engines." ✔
						span MDN
					}
					div class=feature {
						p {
							a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Document/designMode" title="document.designMode controls whether the entire document is editable. Valid values are \"on\" and \"off\". According to the specification, this property is meant to default to \"off\". Firefox follows this standard. The earlier versions of Chrome and IE default to \"inherit\". Starting in Chrome 43, the default is \"off\" and \"inherit\" is no longer supported. In IE6-10, the value is capitalized." "Document/designMode"
						}
						p class=all-engines-text "Support in all current engines."
						div class=support {
							span class="firefox yes" {
								span Firefox
								span "1+"
							}
							span class="safari yes" {
								span Safari
								span "1.2+"
							}
							span class="chrome yes" {
								span Chrome
								span "1+"
							}
							hr
							span class="opera yes" {
								span Opera
								span "9+"
							}
							span class="edge_blink yes" {
								span Edge
								span "79+"
							}
							hr
							span class="edge yes" {
								span "Edge (Legacy)"
								span "12+"
							}
							span class="ie yes" {
								span "Internet Explorer"
								span "4+"
							}
							hr
							span class="firefox_android unknown" {
								span "Firefox Android"
								span ?
							}
							span class="safari_ios unknown" {
								span "Safari iOS"
								span ?
							}
							span class="chrome_android unknown" {
								span "Chrome Android"
								span ?
							}
							span class="webview_android unknown" {
								span "WebView Android"
								span ?
							}
							span class="samsunginternet_android unknown" {
								span "Samsung Internet"
								span ?
							}
							span class="opera_android yes" {
								span "Opera Android"
								span "10.1+"
							}
						}
					}
				}
			}
			dd {
				p {
					- "Returns \""
					code on
					- "\" if the document is editable, and \""
					code off
					- "\" if it isn't."
				}
				p "Can be set, to change the document's current state. This focuses the document and resets the selection in that document."
			}
		}
		p {
			code id=making-entire-documents-editable:-the-designmode-idl-attribute:document {
				a href="#document" Document
			}
			- " objects have an associated "
			dfn id=design-mode-enabled "design mode enabled"
			- ", which is a boolean. It is initially false."
		}
		p {
			- "The "
			dfn data-dfn-for=Document data-dfn-type=attribute id=designMode {
				code designMode
			}
			- " getter steps are to return \""
			code on
			- "\" if "
			a data-x-internal=this href="https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#this" id=making-entire-documents-editable:-the-designmode-idl-attribute:this this
			- "'s "
			a href="#design-mode-enabled" id=making-entire-documents-editable:-the-designmode-idl-attribute:design-mode-enabled "design mode enabled"
			- " is true; otherwise \""
			code off
			- "\"."
		}
		p {
			- "The "
			code id=making-entire-documents-editable:-the-designmode-idl-attribute:designMode-2 {
				a href="#designMode" designMode
			}
			- " setter steps are:"
		}
		ol {
			li {
				p {
					- "Let "
					var value
					- " be the given value, "
					a data-x-internal=converted-to-ascii-lowercase href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ascii-lowercase" id=making-entire-documents-editable:-the-designmode-idl-attribute:converted-to-ascii-lowercase "converted to ASCII lowercase"
					- .
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "If "
					var value
					- " is \""
					code on
					- "\" and "
					a data-x-internal=this href="https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#this" id=making-entire-documents-editable:-the-designmode-idl-attribute:this-2 this
					- "'s "
					a href="#design-mode-enabled" id=making-entire-documents-editable:-the-designmode-idl-attribute:design-mode-enabled-2 "design mode enabled"
					- " is false, then:"
				}
				ol {
					li {
						p {
							- "Set "
							a data-x-internal=this href="https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#this" id=making-entire-documents-editable:-the-designmode-idl-attribute:this-3 this
							- "'s "
							a href="#design-mode-enabled" id=making-entire-documents-editable:-the-designmode-idl-attribute:design-mode-enabled-3 "design mode enabled"
							- " to true."
						}
					}
					li {
						p {
							- "Reset "
							a data-x-internal=this href="https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#this" id=making-entire-documents-editable:-the-designmode-idl-attribute:this-4 this
							- "'s "
							a data-x-internal=active-range href="https://w3c.github.io/editing/docs/execCommand/#active-range" id=making-entire-documents-editable:-the-designmode-idl-attribute:active-range "active range"
							- "'s start and end boundary points to be at the start of "
							a data-x-internal=this href="https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#this" id=making-entire-documents-editable:-the-designmode-idl-attribute:this-5 this
							- .
						}
					}
					li {
						p {
							- "Run the "
							a href="#focusing-steps" id=making-entire-documents-editable:-the-designmode-idl-attribute:focusing-steps "focusing steps"
							- " for "
							a data-x-internal=this href="https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#this" id=making-entire-documents-editable:-the-designmode-idl-attribute:this-6 this
							- "'s "
							a data-x-internal=document-element href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#document-element" id=making-entire-documents-editable:-the-designmode-idl-attribute:document-element "document element"
							- ", if non-null."
						}
					}
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "If "
					var value
					- " is \""
					code off
					- "\", then set "
					a data-x-internal=this href="https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#this" id=making-entire-documents-editable:-the-designmode-idl-attribute:this-7 this
					- "'s "
					a href="#design-mode-enabled" id=making-entire-documents-editable:-the-designmode-idl-attribute:design-mode-enabled-4 "design mode enabled"
					- " to false."
				}
			}
		}
		h4 id=best-practices-for-in-page-editors {
			span class=secno "6.8.3"
			- " Best practices for in-page editors"
			a class=self-link href="#best-practices-for-in-page-editors"
		}
		p {
			- "Authors are encouraged to set the "
			a data-x-internal='white-space' href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-text/#white-space-property" id=best-practices-for-in-page-editors:'white-space' 'white-space'
			- " property on "
			a href="#editing-host" id=best-practices-for-in-page-editors:editing-host "editing hosts"
			- " and on markup that was originally created through these editing mechanisms to the value 'pre-wrap'. Default HTML whitespace handling is not well suited to WYSIWYG editing, and line wrapping will not work correctly in some corner cases if "
			a data-x-internal='white-space' href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-text/#white-space-property" id=best-practices-for-in-page-editors:'white-space'-2 'white-space'
			- " is left at its default value."
		}
		div class=example {
			p {
				- "As an example of problems that occur if the default 'normal' value is used instead, consider the case of the user typing \""
				kbd yellow␣␣ball
				- "\", with two spaces (here represented by \"␣\") between the words. With the editing rules in place for the default value of "
				a data-x-internal='white-space' href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-text/#white-space-property" id=best-practices-for-in-page-editors:'white-space'-3 'white-space'
				- " ('normal'), the resulting markup will either consist of \""
				samp "yellow&nbsp; ball"
				- "\" or \""
				samp "yellow &nbsp;ball"
				- "\"; i.e., there will be a non-breaking space between the two words in addition to the regular space. This is necessary because the 'normal' value for "
				a data-x-internal='white-space' href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-text/#white-space-property" id=best-practices-for-in-page-editors:'white-space'-4 'white-space'
				- " requires adjacent regular spaces to be collapsed together."
			}
			p {
				- "In the former case, \""
				samp yellow⍽
				- "\" might wrap to the next line (\"⍽\" being used here to represent a non-breaking space) even though \""
				samp yellow
				- "\" alone might fit at the end of the line; in the latter case, \""
				samp ⍽ball
				- "\", if wrapped to the start of the line, would have visible indentation from the non-breaking space."
			}
			p {
				- "When "
				a data-x-internal='white-space' href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-text/#white-space-property" id=best-practices-for-in-page-editors:'white-space'-5 'white-space'
				- " is set to 'pre-wrap', however, the editing rules will instead simply put two regular spaces between the words, and should the two words be split at the end of a line, the spaces would be neatly removed from the rendering."
			}
		}
		h4 id=editing-apis {
			span class=secno "6.8.4"
			- " Editing APIs"
			a class=self-link href="#editing-apis"
		}
		p {
			- "An "
			dfn data-export="" id=editing-host "editing host"
			- " is either an "
			a href="#html-elements" id=editing-apis:html-elements "HTML element"
			- " with its "
			code id=editing-apis:attr-contenteditable {
				a href="#attr-contenteditable" contenteditable
			}
			- " attribute in the "
			i "true"
			- " state or "
			i plaintext-only
			- " state, or a "
			a data-x-internal=concept-tree-child href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-tree-child" id=editing-apis:concept-tree-child child
			a href="#html-elements" id=editing-apis:html-elements-2 "HTML element"
			- " of a "
			code id=editing-apis:document {
				a href="#document" Document
			}
			- " whose "
			a href="#design-mode-enabled" id=editing-apis:design-mode-enabled "design mode enabled"
			- " is true."
		}
		p {
			- "The definition of the terms "
			dfn id=active-range {
				a href="https://w3c.github.io/editing/docs/execCommand/#active-range" "active range"
			}
			- ", "
			dfn id=editing-host-of {
				a href="https://w3c.github.io/editing/docs/execCommand/#editing-host-of" "editing host of"
			}
			- ", and "
			dfn id=editable {
				a href="https://w3c.github.io/editing/docs/execCommand/#editable" editable
			}
			- ", the user interface requirements of elements that are "
			a href="#editing-host" id=editing-apis:editing-host "editing hosts"
			- " or "
			a data-x-internal=editable href="https://w3c.github.io/editing/docs/execCommand/#editable" id=editing-apis:editable editable
			- ", the "
			dfn id=execCommand {
				a href="https://w3c.github.io/editing/docs/execCommand/#execcommand%28%29" {
					code "execCommand()"
				}
			}
			- ", "
			dfn id=dom-document-querycommandenabled {
				a href="https://w3c.github.io/editing/docs/execCommand/#querycommandenabled%28%29" {
					code "queryCommandEnabled()"
				}
			}
			- ", "
			dfn id=dom-document-querycommandindeterm {
				a href="https://w3c.github.io/editing/docs/execCommand/#querycommandindeterm%28%29" {
					code "queryCommandIndeterm()"
				}
			}
			- ", "
			dfn id=dom-document-querycommandstate {
				a href="https://w3c.github.io/editing/docs/execCommand/#querycommandstate%28%29" {
					code "queryCommandState()"
				}
			}
			- ", "
			dfn id=dom-document-querycommandsupported {
				a href="https://w3c.github.io/editing/docs/execCommand/#querycommandsupported%28%29" {
					code "queryCommandSupported()"
				}
			}
			- ", and "
			dfn id=dom-document-querycommandvalue {
				a href="https://w3c.github.io/editing/docs/execCommand/#querycommandvalue%28%29" {
					code "queryCommandValue()"
				}
			}
			- " methods, text selections, and the "
			dfn id=delete-the-selection {
				a href="https://w3c.github.io/editing/docs/execCommand/#delete-the-selection" "delete the selection"
			}
			- " algorithm are defined in "
			cite execCommand
			- ". "
			a href="#refsEXECCOMMAND" "[EXECCOMMAND]"
		}
		h4 id=spelling-and-grammar-checking {
			span class=secno "6.8.5"
			- " Spelling and grammar checking"
			a class=self-link href="#spelling-and-grammar-checking"
		}
		p {
			- "User agents can support the checking of spelling and grammar of editable text, either in form controls (such as the value of "
			code id=spelling-and-grammar-checking:the-textarea-element {
				a href="#the-textarea-element" textarea
			}
			- " elements), or in elements in an "
			a href="#editing-host" id=spelling-and-grammar-checking:editing-host "editing host"
			- " (e.g. using "
			code id=spelling-and-grammar-checking:attr-contenteditable {
				a href="#attr-contenteditable" contenteditable
			}
			- ")."
		}
		p {
			- "For each element, user agents must establish a "
			dfn id=concept-spellcheck-default "default behavior"
			- ", either through defaults or through preferences expressed by the user. There are three possible default behaviors for each element:"
		}
		dl {
			dt {
				dfn id=concept-spellcheck-default-true true-by-default
			}
			dd {
				- "The element will be checked for spelling and grammar if its contents are editable and spellchecking is not explicitly disabled through the "
				code id=spelling-and-grammar-checking:attr-spellcheck {
					a href="#attr-spellcheck" spellcheck
				}
				- " attribute. "
			}
			dt {
				dfn id=concept-spellcheck-default-false false-by-default
			}
			dd {
				- "The element will never be checked for spelling and grammar unless spellchecking is explicitly enabled through the "
