		h4 id=the-drag-data-store {
			span class=secno "6.11.2"
			- " The drag data store"
			a class=self-link href="#the-drag-data-store"
		}
		p {
			- "The data that underlies a drag-and-drop operation, known as the "
			dfn id=drag-data-store "drag data store"
			- ", consists of the following information:"
		}
		ul {
			li {
				p {
					- "A "
					dfn id=drag-data-store-item-list "drag data store item list"
					- ", which is a list of items representing the dragged data, each consisting of the following information:"
				}
				dl {
					dt {
						dfn id=the-drag-data-item-kind "The drag data item kind"
					}
					dd {
						p "The kind of data:"
						dl {
							dt {
								i Text
							}
							dd {
								p Text.
							}
							dt {
								i File
							}
							dd {
								p "Binary data with a filename."
							}
						}
					}
					dt {
						dfn id=the-drag-data-item-type-string "The drag data item type string"
					}
					dd {
						p {
							- "A Unicode string giving the type or format of the data, generally given by a "
							a data-x-internal=mime-type href="https://mimesniff.spec.whatwg.org/#mime-type" id=the-drag-data-store:mime-type "MIME type"
							- ". Some values that are not "
							a data-x-internal=mime-type href="https://mimesniff.spec.whatwg.org/#mime-type" id=the-drag-data-store:mime-type-2 "MIME types"
							- " are special-cased for legacy reasons. The API does not enforce the use of "
							a data-x-internal=mime-type href="https://mimesniff.spec.whatwg.org/#mime-type" id=the-drag-data-store:mime-type-3 "MIME types"
							- "; other values can be used as well. In all cases, however, the values are all "
							a data-x-internal=converted-to-ascii-lowercase href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ascii-lowercase" id=the-drag-data-store:converted-to-ascii-lowercase "converted to ASCII lowercase"
							- " by the API."
						}
						p {
							- "There is a limit of one "
							i text
							- " item per "
							a href="#the-drag-data-item-type-string" id=the-drag-data-store:the-drag-data-item-type-string "item type string"
							- .
						}
					}
					dt "The actual data"
					dd {
						p {
							- "A Unicode or binary string, in some cases with a filename (itself a Unicode string), as per "
							a href="#the-drag-data-item-kind" id=the-drag-data-store:the-drag-data-item-kind "the drag data item kind"
							- .
						}
					}
				}
				p {
					- "The "
					a href="#drag-data-store-item-list" id=the-drag-data-store:drag-data-store-item-list "drag data store item list"
					- " is ordered in the order that the items were added to the list; most recently added last."
				}
			}
			li {
				p "The following information, used to generate the UI feedback during the drag:"
				ul {
					li {
						- "User-agent-defined default feedback information, known as the "
						dfn id=drag-data-store-default-feedback "drag data store default feedback"
						- .
					}
					li {
						- "Optionally, a bitmap image and the coordinate of a point within that image, known as the "
						dfn id=drag-data-store-bitmap "drag data store bitmap"
						- " and "
						dfn id=drag-data-store-hot-spot-coordinate "drag data store hot spot coordinate"
						- .
					}
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "A "
					dfn id=drag-data-store-mode "drag data store mode"
					- ", which is one of the following:"
				}
				dl {
					dt {
						dfn id=concept-dnd-rw "Read/write mode"
					}
					dd {
						p {
							- "For the "
							code id=the-drag-data-store:event-dnd-dragstart {
								a href="#event-dnd-dragstart" dragstart
							}
							- " event. New data can be added to the "
							a href="#drag-data-store" id=the-drag-data-store:drag-data-store "drag data store"
							- .
						}
					}
					dt {
						dfn id=concept-dnd-ro "Read-only mode"
					}
					dd {
						p {
							- "For the "
							code id=the-drag-data-store:event-dnd-drop {
								a href="#event-dnd-drop" drop
							}
							- " event. The list of items representing dragged data can be read, including the data. No new data can be added."
						}
					}
					dt {
						dfn id=concept-dnd-p "Protected mode"
					}
					dd {
						p {
							- "For all other events. The formats and kinds in the "
							a href="#drag-data-store" id=the-drag-data-store:drag-data-store-2 "drag data store"
							- " list of items representing dragged data can be enumerated, but the data itself is unavailable and no new data can be added."
						}
					}
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "A "
					dfn id=drag-data-store-allowed-effects-state "drag data store allowed effects state"
					- ", which is a string."
				}
			}
		}
		p {
			- "When a "
			a href="#drag-data-store" id=the-drag-data-store:drag-data-store-3 "drag data store"
			- " is "
			dfn id=create-a-drag-data-store created
			- ", it must be initialized such that its "
			a href="#drag-data-store-item-list" id=the-drag-data-store:drag-data-store-item-list-2 "drag data store item list"
			- " is empty, it has no "
			a href="#drag-data-store-default-feedback" id=the-drag-data-store:drag-data-store-default-feedback "drag data store default feedback"
			- ", it has no "
			a href="#drag-data-store-bitmap" id=the-drag-data-store:drag-data-store-bitmap "drag data store bitmap"
			- " and "
			a href="#drag-data-store-hot-spot-coordinate" id=the-drag-data-store:drag-data-store-hot-spot-coordinate "drag data store hot spot coordinate"
			- ", its "
			a href="#drag-data-store-mode" id=the-drag-data-store:drag-data-store-mode "drag data store mode"
			- " is "
			a href="#concept-dnd-p" id=the-drag-data-store:concept-dnd-p "protected mode"
			- ", and its "
			a href="#drag-data-store-allowed-effects-state" id=the-drag-data-store:drag-data-store-allowed-effects-state "drag data store allowed effects state"
			- " is the string \""
			code id=the-drag-data-store:dom-datatransfer-effectallowed-uninitialized {
				a href="#dom-datatransfer-effectallowed-uninitialized" uninitialized
			}
			- "\"."
		}
		h4 id=the-datatransfer-interface {
			span class=secno "6.11.3"
			- " The "
			code id=the-datatransfer-interface:datatransfer {
