		h4 id=origin-keyed-agent-clusters {
			span class=secno "7.1.2"
			span id=origin-isolation
			- "Origin-keyed agent clusters"
			a class=self-link href="#origin-keyed-agent-clusters"
		}
		dl class=domintro {
			dt {
				code {
					- window.
					a href="#dom-originagentcluster" id=dom-originagentcluster-dev originAgentCluster
				}
			}
			dd {
				p {
					- "Returns true if this "
					code id=origin-keyed-agent-clusters:window {
						a href="#window" Window
					}
					- " belongs to an "
					a data-x-internal=agent-cluster href="https://tc39.es/ecma262/#sec-agent-clusters" id=origin-keyed-agent-clusters:agent-cluster "agent cluster"
					- " which is "
					a href="#concept-origin" id=origin-keyed-agent-clusters:concept-origin origin
					- -
					a href="#agent-cluster-key" id=origin-keyed-agent-clusters:agent-cluster-key keyed
					- ", in the manner described in this section."
				}
			}
		}
		p {
			- "A "
			code id=origin-keyed-agent-clusters:document {
				a href="#document" Document
			}
			- " delivered over a "
			a href="#secure-context" id=origin-keyed-agent-clusters:secure-context "secure context"
			- " can request that it be placed in an "
			a href="#concept-origin" id=origin-keyed-agent-clusters:concept-origin-2 origin
			- -
			a href="#agent-cluster-key" id=origin-keyed-agent-clusters:agent-cluster-key-2 keyed
			a data-x-internal=agent-cluster href="https://tc39.es/ecma262/#sec-agent-clusters" id=origin-keyed-agent-clusters:agent-cluster-2 "agent cluster"
			- ", by using the `"
			dfn data-dfn-type=http-header id=origin-agent-cluster {
				code Origin-Agent-Cluster
			}
			- "` HTTP response header. This header is a "
			a data-x-internal=http-structured-header href="https://httpwg.org/specs/rfc8941.html" id=origin-keyed-agent-clusters:http-structured-header "structured header"
			- " whose value must be a "
			a data-x-internal=http-structured-header-boolean href="https://httpwg.org/specs/rfc8941.html#boolean" id=origin-keyed-agent-clusters:http-structured-header-boolean boolean
			- ". "
			a href="#refsSTRUCTURED-FIELDS" "[STRUCTURED-FIELDS]"
		}
		p {
			- "Per the processing model in the "
			a href="#initialise-the-document-object" id=origin-keyed-agent-clusters:initialise-the-document-object {
				- "create and initialize a new "
				code Document
				- " object"
			}
			- ", values that are not the "
			a data-x-internal=http-structured-header-boolean href="https://httpwg.org/specs/rfc8941.html#boolean" id=origin-keyed-agent-clusters:http-structured-header-boolean-2 "structured header boolean"
			- " true value (i.e., `"
			code ?1
			- "`) will be ignored."
		}
		p {
			- "The consequences of using this header are that the resulting "
			code id=origin-keyed-agent-clusters:document-2 {
				a href="#document" Document
			}
			- "'s "
			a href="#agent-cluster-key" id=origin-keyed-agent-clusters:agent-cluster-key-3 "agent cluster key"
			- " is its "
			a data-x-internal=concept-document-origin href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-document-origin" id=origin-keyed-agent-clusters:concept-document-origin origin
			- ", instead of the "
			a href="#obtain-a-site" id=origin-keyed-agent-clusters:obtain-a-site "corresponding site"
			- ". In terms of observable effects, this means that attempting to "
			a href="#relaxing-the-same-origin-restriction" "relax the same-origin restriction"
			- " using "
			code id=origin-keyed-agent-clusters:dom-document-domain {
				a href="#dom-document-domain" document.domain
			}
			- " will instead do nothing, and it will not be possible to send "
			code id=origin-keyed-agent-clusters:webassembly.module {
				a data-x-internal=webassembly.module href="https://webassembly.github.io/spec/js-api/#module" WebAssembly.Module
			}
			- " objects to cross-origin "
			code id=origin-keyed-agent-clusters:document-3 {
				a href="#document" Document
			}
			- "s (even if they are "
			a href="#same-site" id=origin-keyed-agent-clusters:same-site "same site"
			- "). Behind the scenes, this isolation can allow user agents to allocate implementation-specific resources corresponding to "
			a data-x-internal=agent-cluster href="https://tc39.es/ecma262/#sec-agent-clusters" id=origin-keyed-agent-clusters:agent-cluster-3 "agent clusters"
			- ", such as processes or threads, more efficiently."
		}
		p {
			- "Note that within a "
			a href="#browsing-context-group" id=origin-keyed-agent-clusters:browsing-context-group "browsing context group"
			- ", the `"
			code id=origin-keyed-agent-clusters:origin-agent-cluster {
				a href="#origin-agent-cluster" Origin-Agent-Cluster
			}
			- "` header can never cause same-origin "
			code id=origin-keyed-agent-clusters:document-4 {
				a href="#document" Document
			}
			- " objects to end up in different "
			a data-x-internal=agent-cluster href="https://tc39.es/ecma262/#sec-agent-clusters" id=origin-keyed-agent-clusters:agent-cluster-4 "agent clusters"
			- ", even if one sends the header and the other doesn't. This is prevented by means of the "
			a href="#historical-agent-cluster-key-map" id=origin-keyed-agent-clusters:historical-agent-cluster-key-map "historical agent cluster key map"
			- .
		}
		p class=note {
			- "This means that the "
			code id=origin-keyed-agent-clusters:dom-originagentcluster {
				a href="#dom-originagentcluster" originAgentCluster
			}
			- " getter can return false, even if the header is set, if the header was omitted on a previously-loaded same-origin page in the same "
			a href="#browsing-context-group" id=origin-keyed-agent-clusters:browsing-context-group-2 "browsing context group"
			- ". Similarly, it can return true even when the header is not set."
		}
		p {
			- "The "
			dfn data-dfn-for=Window data-dfn-type=attribute id=dom-originagentcluster {
				code originAgentCluster
			}
			- " getter steps are to return the "
			a data-x-internal=surrounding-agent href="https://tc39.es/ecma262/#surrounding-agent" id=origin-keyed-agent-clusters:surrounding-agent "surrounding agent"
			- "'s "
			a data-x-internal=agent-cluster href="https://tc39.es/ecma262/#sec-agent-clusters" id=origin-keyed-agent-clusters:agent-cluster-5 "agent cluster"
			- "'s "
			a href="#is-origin-keyed" id=origin-keyed-agent-clusters:is-origin-keyed "is origin-keyed"
			- .
		}
		p class=note {
			code id=origin-keyed-agent-clusters:document-5 {
				a href="#document" Document
			}
			- "s with an "
			a href="#concept-origin-opaque" id=origin-keyed-agent-clusters:concept-origin-opaque "opaque origin"
			- " can be considered unconditionally origin-keyed; for them the header has no effect, and the "
			code id=origin-keyed-agent-clusters:dom-originagentcluster-2 {
				a href="#dom-originagentcluster" originAgentCluster
			}
			- " getter will always return true."
		}
		p class=note {
			- "Similarly, "
			code id=origin-keyed-agent-clusters:document-6 {
				a href="#document" Document
			}
			- "s whose "
			a data-x-internal=agent-cluster href="https://tc39.es/ecma262/#sec-agent-clusters" id=origin-keyed-agent-clusters:agent-cluster-6 "agent cluster"
			- "'s "
			a href="#agent-cluster-cross-origin-isolation" id=origin-keyed-agent-clusters:agent-cluster-cross-origin-isolation "cross-origin isolation mode"
			- " is not \""
			code id=origin-keyed-agent-clusters:cross-origin-isolation-none {
				a href="#cross-origin-isolation-none" none
			}
			- "\" are automatically origin-keyed. The `"
			code id=origin-keyed-agent-clusters:origin-agent-cluster-2 {
				a href="#origin-agent-cluster" Origin-Agent-Cluster
			}
			- "` header might be useful as an additional hint to implementations about resource allocation, since the `"
			code id=origin-keyed-agent-clusters:cross-origin-opener-policy-2 {
				a href="#cross-origin-opener-policy-2" Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy
			}
			- "` and `"
			code id=origin-keyed-agent-clusters:cross-origin-embedder-policy {
				a href="#cross-origin-embedder-policy" Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy
			}
			- "` headers used to achieve cross-origin isolation are more about ensuring that everything in the same address space opts in to being there. But adding it would have no additional observable effects on author code."
		}
		h4 id=cross-origin-opener-policies {
			span class=secno "7.1.3"
			- " Cross-origin opener policies"
			a class=self-link href="#cross-origin-opener-policies"
		}
		p {
			- "An "
			dfn id=cross-origin-opener-policy-value "opener policy value"
			- " allows a document which is navigated to in a "
			a href="#top-level-browsing-context" id=cross-origin-opener-policies:top-level-browsing-context "top-level browsing context"
			- " to force the creation of a new "
			a href="#top-level-browsing-context" id=cross-origin-opener-policies:top-level-browsing-context-2 "top-level browsing context"
			- ", and a corresponding "
			a href="#tlbc-group" id=cross-origin-opener-policies:tlbc-group group
			- ". The possible values are:"
		}
		dl {
			dt {
				- "\""
				dfn id=coop-unsafe-none {
					code unsafe-none
				}
				- "\""
			}
			dd {
				p {
					- "This is the (current) default and means that the document will occupy the same "
					a href="#top-level-browsing-context" id=cross-origin-opener-policies:top-level-browsing-context-3 "top-level browsing context"
					- " as its predecessor, unless that document specified a different "
					a href="#cross-origin-opener-policy" id=cross-origin-opener-policies:cross-origin-opener-policy "opener policy"
					- .
				}
			}
			dt {
				- "\""
				dfn id=coop-same-origin-allow-popups {
					code same-origin-allow-popups
				}
				- "\""
			}
			dd {
				p {
					- "This forces the creation of a new "
					a href="#top-level-browsing-context" id=cross-origin-opener-policies:top-level-browsing-context-4 "top-level browsing context"
					- " for the document, unless its predecessor specified the same "
					a href="#cross-origin-opener-policy" id=cross-origin-opener-policies:cross-origin-opener-policy-2 "opener policy"
					- " and they are "
					a href="#same-origin" id=cross-origin-opener-policies:same-origin "same origin"
					- .
				}
			}
			dt {
				- "\""
				dfn id=coop-same-origin {
					code same-origin
				}
				- "\""
			}
			dd {
				p {
					- "This behaves the same as \""
					code id=cross-origin-opener-policies:coop-same-origin-allow-popups {
						a href="#coop-same-origin-allow-popups" same-origin-allow-popups
					}
					- "\", with the addition that any "
					a href="#auxiliary-browsing-context" id=cross-origin-opener-policies:auxiliary-browsing-context "auxiliary browsing context"
					- " created needs to contain "
					a href="#same-origin" id=cross-origin-opener-policies:same-origin-2 "same origin"
					- " documents that also have the same "
					a href="#cross-origin-opener-policy" id=cross-origin-opener-policies:cross-origin-opener-policy-3 "opener policy"
					- " or it will appear closed to the opener."
				}
			}
			dt {
				- "\""
				dfn id=coop-same-origin-plus-coep {
					code same-origin-plus-COEP
				}
				- "\""
			}
			dd {
				p {
					- "This behaves the same as \""
					code id=cross-origin-opener-policies:coop-same-origin {
						a href="#coop-same-origin" same-origin
					}
					- "\", with the addition that it sets the (new) "
					a href="#top-level-browsing-context" id=cross-origin-opener-policies:top-level-browsing-context-5 "top-level browsing context"
					- "'s "
					a href="#tlbc-group" id=cross-origin-opener-policies:tlbc-group-2 group
					- "'s "
					a href="#bcg-cross-origin-isolation" id=cross-origin-opener-policies:bcg-cross-origin-isolation "cross-origin isolation mode"
					- " to one of \""
					code id=cross-origin-opener-policies:cross-origin-isolation-logical {
						a href="#cross-origin-isolation-logical" logical
					}
					- "\" or \""
					code id=cross-origin-opener-policies:cross-origin-isolation-concrete {
						a href="#cross-origin-isolation-concrete" concrete
					}
					- "\"."
				}
				p class=note {
					- "\""
					code id=cross-origin-opener-policies:coop-same-origin-plus-coep {
						a href="#coop-same-origin-plus-coep" same-origin-plus-COEP
					}
					- "\" cannot be directly set via the `"
					code id=cross-origin-opener-policies:cross-origin-opener-policy-2-2 {
						a href="#cross-origin-opener-policy-2" Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy
					}
					- "` header, but results from a combination of setting both `"
					code {
						a href="#cross-origin-opener-policy-2" id=cross-origin-opener-policies:cross-origin-opener-policy-2-3 Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy
						- ": "
						a href="#coop-same-origin" id=cross-origin-opener-policies:coop-same-origin-2 same-origin
					}
					- "` and a `"
					code id=cross-origin-opener-policies:cross-origin-embedder-policy {
						a href="#cross-origin-embedder-policy" Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy
					}
					- "` header whose value is "
					a href="#compatible-with-cross-origin-isolation" id=cross-origin-opener-policies:compatible-with-cross-origin-isolation "compatible with cross-origin isolation"
					- " together."
				}
			}
			dt {
				- "\""
				dfn id=coop-noopener-allow-popups {
					code noopener-allow-popups
				}
				- "\""
			}
			dd {
				p {
					- "This forces the creation of a new "
					a href="#top-level-browsing-context" id=cross-origin-opener-policies:top-level-browsing-context-6 "top-level browsing context"
					- " for the document, regardless of its predecessor."
				}
				div class=note {
					p {
						- "While including a "
						code id=cross-origin-opener-policies:coop-noopener-allow-popups {
							a href="#coop-noopener-allow-popups" noopener-allow-popups
						}
						- " value severs the opener relationship between the document on which it is applied and its opener, it does not create a robust security boundary between those same-origin documents."
					}
					p "Other risks from same-origin applications include:"
					ul {
						li {
							p {
								- "Same-origin requests fetching the document's content — could be mitigated through Fetch Metadata filtering. "
								a href="#refsFETCHMETADATA" "[FETCHMETADATA]"
							}
						}
						li {
							p {
								- "Same-origin framing - could be mitigated through "
								code id=cross-origin-opener-policies:x-frame-options {
									a href="#x-frame-options" X-Frame-Options
								}
								- " or CSP "
								code id=cross-origin-opener-policies:frame-ancestors-directive {
									a data-x-internal=frame-ancestors-directive href="https://w3c.github.io/webappsec-csp/#frame-ancestors" frame-ancestors
								}
								- .
							}
						}
						li {
							p {
								- "JavaScript accessible cookies - can be mitigated by ensuring all cookies are "
								code httponly
								- .
							}
						}
						li {
							p {
								code id=cross-origin-opener-policies:dom-localstorage {
									a href="#dom-localstorage" localStorage
								}
								- " access to sensitive data."
							}
						}
						li {
							p "Service worker installation."
						}
						li {
							p {
								a href="https://w3c.github.io/ServiceWorker/#cache" "Cache API"
								- " manipulation or access to sensitive data. "
								a href="#refsSW" "[SW]"
							}
						}
						li {
							p {
								code postMessage
								- " or "
								code id=cross-origin-opener-policies:broadcastchannel {
									a href="#broadcastchannel" BroadcastChannel
								}
								- " messaging that exposes sensitive information."
							}
						}
						li {
							p "Autofill which may not require user interaction for same-origin documents."
						}
					}
					p {
						- "Developers using "
						code id=cross-origin-opener-policies:coop-noopener-allow-popups-2 {
							a href="#coop-noopener-allow-popups" noopener-allow-popups
						}
						- " need to make sure that their sensitive applications don't rely on client-side features accessible to other same-origin documents, e.g., "
						code id=cross-origin-opener-policies:dom-localstorage-2 {
							a href="#dom-localstorage" localStorage
						}
						- " and other client-side storage APIs, "
						code id=cross-origin-opener-policies:broadcastchannel-2 {
							a href="#broadcastchannel" BroadcastChannel
						}
						- " and related same-origin communication mechanisms. They also need to make sure that their server-side endpoints don't return sensitive data to non-navigation requests, whose response content is accessible to same-origin documents."
					}
				}
			}
		}
		p {
			- "An "
			dfn id=cross-origin-opener-policy "opener policy"
			- " consists of:"
		}
		ul {
			li {
				p {
					- "A "
					dfn id=coop-struct-value value
					- ", which is an "
