		p {
			- "Note that traversals are again limited to same-"
			a href="#concept-origin" id=navigation-api-intro:concept-origin-2 origin
			- " destinations, meaning that, for example, "
			code id=navigation-api-intro:dom-navigation-cangoback {
				a href="#dom-navigation-cangoback" navigation.canGoBack
			}
			- " will be false if the previous "
			a href="#session-history-entry" id=navigation-api-intro:session-history-entry-3 "session history entry"
			- " is for a page from another origin."
		}
		hr
		p {
			- "The most powerful part of the navigation API is the "
			code id=navigation-api-intro:event-navigate {
				a href="#event-navigate" navigate
			}
			- " event, which fires whenever almost any navigation or traversal occurs in the current "
			a href="#navigable" id=navigation-api-intro:navigable-2 navigable
			- :
