		}
		p {
			- "A major feature of the navigation API is the "
			code id=the-navigate-event:event-navigate-2 {
				a href="#event-navigate" navigate
			}
			- " event. This event is fired on any navigation (in the "
			a href="#navigationtype" id=the-navigate-event:navigationtype "broad sense of the word"
			- "), allowing web developers to monitor such outgoing navigations. In many cases, the event is "
			code id=the-navigate-event:dom-event-cancelable {
				a data-x-internal=dom-event-cancelable href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#dom-event-cancelable" cancelable
			}
			- ", which allows preventing the navigation from happening. And in others, the navigation can be intercepted and replaced with a same-document navigation by using the "
			code id=the-navigate-event:dom-navigateevent-intercept {
				a href="#dom-navigateevent-intercept" "intercept()"
			}
			- " method of the "
