		h3 id=infrastructure-for-sequences-of-documents {
			span class=secno "7.3"
			- " Infrastructure for sequences of documents"
			a class=self-link href="#infrastructure-for-sequences-of-documents"
		}
		p "This standard contains several related concepts for grouping sequences of documents. As a brief, non-normative summary:"
		ul {
			li {
				p {
					a href="#navigable" id=infrastructure-for-sequences-of-documents:navigable Navigables
					- " are a user-facing representation of a sequence of documents, i.e., they represent something that can be navigated between documents. Typical examples are tabs or windows in a web browser, or "
					code id=infrastructure-for-sequences-of-documents:the-iframe-element {
						a href="#the-iframe-element" iframe
					}
					- "s, or "
					code id=infrastructure-for-sequences-of-documents:frame {
						a href="#frame" frame
					}
					- "s in a "
					code id=infrastructure-for-sequences-of-documents:frameset {
						a href="#frameset" frameset
					}
					- .
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					a href="#traversable-navigable" id=infrastructure-for-sequences-of-documents:traversable-navigable "Traversable navigables"
					- " are a special type of navigable which control the session history of themselves and of their descendant navigables. That is, in addition to their own series of documents, they represent a tree of further series of documents, plus the ability to linearly traverse back and forward through a flattened view of this tree."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					a href="#browsing-context" id=infrastructure-for-sequences-of-documents:browsing-context "Browsing contexts"
					- " are a developer-facing representation of a series of documents. They correspond 1:1 with "
					code id=infrastructure-for-sequences-of-documents:windowproxy {
						a href="#windowproxy" WindowProxy
					}
					- " objects. Each navigable can present a series of browsing contexts, with "
					a href="#browsing-context-group-switches-due-to-cross-origin-opener-policy" switches
					- " between those browsing contexts occuring under certain well-defined circumstances."
				}
			}
		}
		p "Most of this standard works in the language of navigables, but certain APIs expose the existence of browsing context switches, and so some parts of the standard need to work in terms of browsing contexts."
		h4 id=navigables {
			span class=secno "7.3.1"
			- " Navigables"
			a class=self-link href="#navigables"
		}
		p {
			- "A "
			dfn data-export="" id=navigable navigable
			- " presents a "
			code id=navigables:document {
				a href="#document" Document
			}
			- " to the user via its "
			a href="#nav-active-history-entry" id=navigables:nav-active-history-entry "active session history entry"
			- ". Each navigable has:"
		}
		ul {
			li {
				p {
					- "An "
					dfn id=nav-id id
					- ", a "
					a href="#new-unique-internal-value" id=navigables:new-unique-internal-value "new unique internal value"
					- .
				}
			}
			li {
				p id=parent-browsing-context {
					- "A "
					dfn data-dfn-for=navigable data-export="" id=nav-parent parent
					- ", a "
					a href="#navigable" id=navigables:navigable navigable
					- " or null."
				}
			}
			li {
				p id=current-entry {
					- "A "
