		h5 id=jake-diagrams {
			span class=secno "7.3.1.4"
			- " Jake diagrams"
			a class=self-link href="#jake-diagrams"
		}
		p {
			- "A useful method for visualizing sequences of documents, and in particular "
			a href="#navigable" id=jake-diagrams:navigable navigables
			- " and their "
			a href="#session-history-entry" id=jake-diagrams:session-history-entry "session history entries"
			- ", is the "
			dfn id=jake-diagram "Jake diagram"
			- ". A typical Jake diagram is the following:"
		}
		table class=jake-diagram {
			thead {
				tr {
					td
					th class=step "0"
					th class="step current" "1"
					th class=step "2"
					th class=step "3"
					th class=step "4"
				}
			}
			tbody {
				tr {
					th {
						code top
					}
					td class="doc-0 current next-is-same-doc" colspan="3" "/t-a"
					td class="doc-0 prev-is-same-doc" colspan="1" "/t-a#foo"
					td class=doc-1 colspan="1" "/t-b"
				}
				tr {
					th {
						code "frames[0]"
					}
					td class=doc-2 colspan="1" "/i-0-a"
					td class="doc-3 current" colspan="3" "/i-0-b"
				}
				tr {
					th {
						code "frames[1]"
					}
					td class="doc-4 current" colspan="2" "/i-1-a"
					td class=doc-5 colspan="2" "/i-1-b"
				}
			}
		}
		p {
			- "Here, each numbered column denotes a possible value for the traversable's "
			a href="#tn-current-session-history-step" id=jake-diagrams:tn-current-session-history-step "session history step"
			- ". Each labeled row depicts a "
			a href="#navigable" id=jake-diagrams:navigable-2 navigable
			- ", as it transitions between different URLs and documents. The first, labeled "
			code top
			- ", being the "
			a href="#top-level-traversable" id=jake-diagrams:top-level-traversable "top-level traversable"
			- ", and the others being "
			a href="#child-navigable" id=jake-diagrams:child-navigable "child navigables"
			- ". The documents are given by the background color of each cell, with a new background color indicating a new document in that "
			a href="#navigable" id=jake-diagrams:navigable-3 navigable
			- ". The URLs are given by the text content of the cells; usually they are given as "
			a data-x-internal=relative-url href="https://url.spec.whatwg.org/#syntax-url-relative" id=jake-diagrams:relative-url "relative URLs"
			- " for brevity, unless a cross-origin case is specifically under investigation. A given navigable might not exist at a given step, in which case the corresponding cells are empty. The bold-italic step number depicts the "
			a href="#tn-current-session-history-step" id=jake-diagrams:tn-current-session-history-step-2 "current session history step"
			- " of the traversable, and all cells with bold-italic URLs represent the "
			a href="#nav-current-history-entry" id=jake-diagrams:nav-current-history-entry "current session history entry"
			- " for that row's navigable."
		}
		p "Thus, the above Jake diagram depicts the following sequence of events:"
		ol start="0" {
			li {
				p {
					- "A "
					a href="#top-level-traversable" id=jake-diagrams:top-level-traversable-2 "top-level traversable"
					- " is created, starting a the URL "
					code "/t-a"
					- ", with two "
					a href="#child-navigable" id=jake-diagrams:child-navigable-2 "child navigables"
					- " starting at "
					code "/i-0-a"
					- " and "
					code "/i-1-a"
					- " respectively."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "The first child navigable is "
					a href="#navigate" id=jake-diagrams:navigate navigated
					- " to another document, with URL "
					code "/i-0-b"
					- .
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "The second child navigable is "
					a href="#navigate" id=jake-diagrams:navigate-2 navigated
