		p class=warning id=warning-avoid-using-bcs {
			- "Modern specifications should avoid using the "
			a href="#browsing-context" id=windows:browsing-context-7 "browsing context"
			- " concept in most cases, unless they are dealing with the subtleties of "
			a href="#browsing-context-group-switches-due-to-cross-origin-opener-policy" "browsing context group switches"
			- " and "
			a href="#agent-cluster-map" id=windows:agent-cluster-map "agent cluster allocation"
			- ". Instead, the "
			code id=windows:document {
				a href="#document" Document
			}
			- " and "
			a href="#navigable" id=windows:navigable-2 navigable
			- " concepts are usually more appropriate."
		}
		hr
		p {
			- "A "
			dfn data-dfn-for=Document data-export="" data-lt="browsing context" id=concept-document-bc {
				code Document
				- "'s browsing context"
			}
			- " is a "
			a href="#browsing-context" id=windows:browsing-context-8 "browsing context"
			- " or null, initially null."
		}
		p class=note {
			- "A "
			code id=windows:document-2 {
				a href="#document" Document
			}
			- " does not necessarily have a non-null "
			a href="#concept-document-bc" id=windows:concept-document-bc "browsing context"
			- ". In particular, data mining tools are likely to never instantiate browsing contexts. A "
			code id=windows:document-3 {
				a href="#document" Document
			}
			- " created using an API such as "
			code id=windows:dom-domimplementation-createdocument {
				a data-x-internal=dom-domimplementation-createdocument href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#dom-domimplementation-createdocument" "createDocument()"
			}
			- " never has a non-null "
			a href="#concept-document-bc" id=windows:concept-document-bc-2 "browsing context"
			- ". And the "
			code id=windows:document-4 {
				a href="#document" Document
			}
			- " originally created for an "
			code id=windows:the-iframe-element {
				a href="#the-iframe-element" iframe
			}
			- " element, which has since been "
			a href="#remove-an-element-from-a-document" id=windows:remove-an-element-from-a-document "removed from the document"
			- ", has no associated browsing context, since that browsing context was "
			a href="#destroy-a-document" id=windows:destroy-a-document "nulled out"
			- .
		}
		p class=note {
			- "In general, there is a 1-to-1 mapping from the "
			code id=windows:window {
				a href="#window" Window
			}
			- " object to the "
			code id=windows:document-5 {
				a href="#document" Document
			}
			- " object, as long as the "
			code id=windows:document-6 {
				a href="#document" Document
			}
			- " object has a non-null "
			a href="#concept-document-bc" id=windows:concept-document-bc-3 "browsing context"
			- ". There is one exception. A "
			code id=windows:window-2 {
				a href="#window" Window
			}
			- " can be reused for the presentation of a second "
			code id=windows:document-7 {
				a href="#document" Document
			}
			- " in the same "
			a href="#browsing-context" id=windows:browsing-context-9 "browsing context"
			- ", such that the mapping is then 1-to-2. This occurs when a "
			a href="#browsing-context" id=windows:browsing-context-10 "browsing context"
			- " is "
			a href="#navigate" id=windows:navigate navigated
			- " from the "
			a href="#is-initial-about:blank" id=windows:is-initial-about:blank {
				- "initial "
				code about:blank
			}
			code id=windows:document-8 {
				a href="#document" Document
			}
			- " to another, which will be done with "
			a href="#navigationhistorybehavior-replace" id=windows:navigationhistorybehavior-replace replacement
			- .
		}
