			p "And the following code runs at the top level:"
			pre {
				code class=js {
					- history
					c- p="" .
					- back
					c- p="" "();"
					- " location"
					c- p="" .
					- "href "
					c- o="" "="
					c- t="" "'#foo'"
					c- p="" ";"
				}
			}
			p "The desired result is:"
			table class=jake-diagram {
				thead {
					tr {
						td
						th class="step current" "0"
						th class=step "1"
						th class=step "2"
					}
				}
				tbody {
					tr {
						th {
							code top
						}
						td class="doc-0 current" colspan="1" "/a"
						td class="doc-1 next-is-same-doc" colspan="1" "/b"
						td class="doc-1 prev-is-same-doc" colspan="1" "/b#foo"
					}
				}
			}
			p {
				- "This isn't straightforward, as the sync navigation wins the race in terms of being observable, whereas the traversal wins the race in terms of queuing steps on the "
				a href="#session-history-traversal-parallel-queue" id=centralized-modifications-of-session-history:session-history-traversal-parallel-queue-4 "session history traversal parallel queue"
				- ". To achieve this result, the following happens:"
			}
			ol {
				li {
					p {
						code id=centralized-modifications-of-session-history:dom-history-back {
							a href="#dom-history-back" "history.back()"
						}
						a href="#tn-append-session-history-traversal-steps" id=centralized-modifications-of-session-history:tn-append-session-history-traversal-steps "appends steps"
						- " intended to traverse by a delta of −1."
					}
				}
				li {
					p {
						code id=centralized-modifications-of-session-history:dom-location-href {
							a href="#dom-location-href" "location.href = '#foo'"
						}
						- " synchronously changes the "
						a href="#nav-active-history-entry" id=centralized-modifications-of-session-history:nav-active-history-entry "active session history entry"
						- " entry to a newly-created one, with the URL "
						code "/b#foo"
						- ", and "
						a href="#tn-append-session-history-sync-nav-steps" id=centralized-modifications-of-session-history:tn-append-session-history-sync-nav-steps "appends synchronous steps"
						- " to notify the central source of truth about that new entry. Note that this does "
						em not
						- " yet update the "
						a href="#nav-current-history-entry" id=centralized-modifications-of-session-history:nav-current-history-entry "current session history entry"
						- ", "
						a href="#tn-current-session-history-step" id=centralized-modifications-of-session-history:tn-current-session-history-step "current session history step"
						- ", or the "
						a href="#tn-session-history-entries" id=centralized-modifications-of-session-history:tn-session-history-entries-2 "session history entries"
						- " list; those updates cannot be done synchronously, and instead must be done as part of the queued steps."
					}
				}
				li {
					p {
						- "On the "
						a href="#session-history-traversal-parallel-queue" id=centralized-modifications-of-session-history:session-history-traversal-parallel-queue-5 "session history traversal parallel queue"
						- ", the steps queued by "
						code id=centralized-modifications-of-session-history:dom-history-back-2 {
							a href="#dom-history-back" "history.back()"
						}
						- " run:"
					}
					ol {
						li {
							p {
								- "The target history step is determined to be 0: the "
								a href="#tn-current-session-history-step" id=centralized-modifications-of-session-history:tn-current-session-history-step-2 "current session history step"
								- " (i.e., 1) plus the intended delta of −1."
							}
						}
						li {
							p {
								- "We enter the main "
								a href="#apply-the-history-step" id=centralized-modifications-of-session-history:apply-the-history-step "apply the history step"
								- " algorithm."
							}
							p {
								- "The entry at step 0, for the "
								code "/a"
								- " URL, has its "
								a href="#she-document" id=centralized-modifications-of-session-history:she-document document
								a href="#attempt-to-populate-the-history-entry's-document" id=centralized-modifications-of-session-history:attempt-to-populate-the-history-entry's-document populated
								- .
							}
							p {
								- "Meanwhile, the queue is checked for "
								a href="#session-history-traversal-parallel-queue-sync-nav-steps" id=centralized-modifications-of-session-history:session-history-traversal-parallel-queue-sync-nav-steps-3 "synchronous navigation steps"
								- ". The steps queued by the "
								code id=centralized-modifications-of-session-history:dom-location-href-2 {
									a href="#dom-location-href" location.href
								}
								- " setter now run, and block the traversal from performing effects beyond document population (such as, unloading documents and switching active history entries) until they are finished. Those steps cause the following to happen:"
							}
							ol {
								li {
									p {
										- "The entry with URL "
										code "/b#foo"
										- " is added, with its "
										a href="#she-step" id=centralized-modifications-of-session-history:she-step step
										- " determined to be 2: the "
										a href="#tn-current-session-history-step" id=centralized-modifications-of-session-history:tn-current-session-history-step-3 "current session history step"
										- " (i.e., 1) plus 1."
									}
								}
								li {
									p {
										- "We fully switch to that newly added entry, including a nested call to "
										a href="#apply-the-history-step" id=centralized-modifications-of-session-history:apply-the-history-step-2 "apply the history step"
										- ". This ultimately results in "
										a href="#update-document-for-history-step-application" id=centralized-modifications-of-session-history:update-document-for-history-step-application "updating the document"
										- " by dispatching events like "
										code id=centralized-modifications-of-session-history:event-hashchange {
											a href="#event-hashchange" hashchange
										}
										- .
									}
								}
							}
							p {
								- "Only once that is all complete, and the "
								code "/a"
								- " history entry has been fully populated with a "
								a href="#she-document" id=centralized-modifications-of-session-history:she-document-2 document
								- ", do we move on with applying the history step given the target step of 0."
							}
							p {
								- "At this point, the "
								code id=centralized-modifications-of-session-history:document {
									a href="#document" Document
								}
								- " with URL "
								code "/b#foo"
								a href="#unload-a-document" id=centralized-modifications-of-session-history:unload-a-document unloads
								- ", and we finish moving to our target history step 0, which makes the entry with URL "
								code "/a"
								- " become the "
								a href="#nav-active-history-entry" id=centralized-modifications-of-session-history:nav-active-history-entry-2 "active session history entry"
								- " and 0 become the "
								a href="#tn-current-session-history-step" id=centralized-modifications-of-session-history:tn-current-session-history-step-4 "current session history step"
								- .
							}
						}
					}
				}
			}
		}
		div class=example id=example-sync-navigation-steps-queue-jumping-complex {
			p {
				- "Here is another more complex example, involving races between populating two different "
				code id=centralized-modifications-of-session-history:the-iframe-element {
					a href="#the-iframe-element" iframe
				}
				- "s, and a synchronous navigation once one of those iframes loads. We start with this setup:"
			}
			table class=jake-diagram {
				thead {
					tr {
						td
						th class=step "0"
						th class=step "1"
						th class="step current" "2"
					}
				}
				tbody {
					tr {
						th {
							code top
						}
						td class="doc-0 current" colspan="3" "/t"
					}
					tr {
						th {
							code "frames[0]"
						}
						td class=doc-1 colspan="1" "/i-0-a"
						td class="doc-2 current" colspan="2" "/i-0-b"
					}
					tr {
						th {
							code "frames[1]"
						}
						td class=doc-3 colspan="2" "/i-1-a"
						td class="doc-4 current" colspan="1" "/i-1-b"
					}
				}
			}
			p {
				- "and then call "
				code id=centralized-modifications-of-session-history:dom-history-go {
					a href="#dom-history-go" "history.go(-2)"
				}
				- ". The following then occurs:"
			}
			ol {
				li {
					p {
						code id=centralized-modifications-of-session-history:dom-history-go-2 {
							a href="#dom-history-go" "history.go(-2)"
						}
						a href="#tn-append-session-history-traversal-steps" id=centralized-modifications-of-session-history:tn-append-session-history-traversal-steps-2 "appends steps"
						- " intended to traverse by a delta of −2. Once those steps run:"
					}
					ol {
						li {
							p "The target step is determined to be 2 + (−2) = 0."
						}
						li {
							p {
								- "In parallel, the fetches are made to "
								a href="#attempt-to-populate-the-history-entry's-document" id=centralized-modifications-of-session-history:attempt-to-populate-the-history-entry's-document-2 populate
								- " the two iframes, fetching "
								code "/i-0-a"
								- " and "
								code "/i-1-a"
								- " respectively."
							}
							p {
								- "Meanwhile, the queue is checked for "
								a href="#session-history-traversal-parallel-queue-sync-nav-steps" id=centralized-modifications-of-session-history:session-history-traversal-parallel-queue-sync-nav-steps-4 "synchronous navigation steps"
								- ". There aren't any right now."
							}
						}
						li {
							p {
								- "In the fetch race, the fetch for "
								code "/i-0-a"
								- " wins. We proceed onward to finish all of "
								a href="#apply-the-history-step" id=centralized-modifications-of-session-history:apply-the-history-step-3 "apply the history step"
								- "'s work for how the traversal impacts the "
								code "frames[0]"
								a href="#navigable" id=centralized-modifications-of-session-history:navigable-4 navigable
								- ", including updating its "
								a href="#nav-active-history-entry" id=centralized-modifications-of-session-history:nav-active-history-entry-3 "active session history entry"
								- " to the entry with URL "
								code "/i-0-a"
								- .
							}
						}
						li {
							p {
								- "Before the fetch for "
								code "/i-1-a"
								- " finishes, we reach the point where "
								a href="#scripts-may-run-for-the-newly-created-document" id=centralized-modifications-of-session-history:scripts-may-run-for-the-newly-created-document "scripts may run for the newly-created document"
								- " in the "
								code "frames[0]"
								a href="#navigable" id=centralized-modifications-of-session-history:navigable-5 navigable
								- "'s "
								a href="#nav-document" id=centralized-modifications-of-session-history:nav-document "active document"
								- ". Some such script does run:"
							}
							pre {
								code class=js {
									- location
									c- p="" .
									- "href "
									c- o="" "="
									c- t="" "'#foo'"
								}
							}
							p {
								- "This synchronously changes the "
								code "frames[0]"
								- " navigable's "
								a href="#nav-active-history-entry" id=centralized-modifications-of-session-history:nav-active-history-entry-4 "active session history entry"
								- " entry to a newly-created one, with the URL "
								code "/i-0-a#foo"
								- ", and "
								a href="#tn-append-session-history-sync-nav-steps" id=centralized-modifications-of-session-history:tn-append-session-history-sync-nav-steps-2 "appends synchronous steps"
								- " to notify the central source of truth about that new entry."
							}
							p {
								- "Unlike in the "
								a href="#example-sync-navigation-steps-queue-jumping-basic" "previous example"
								- ", these synchronous steps do "
								em not
								- " \"jump the queue\" and update the "
								a href="#traversable-navigable" id=centralized-modifications-of-session-history:traversable-navigable-4 traversable
								- " before we finish the fetch for "
								code "/i-1-a"
								- ". This is because the navigable in question, "
								code "frames[0]"
								- ", has already been altered as part of the traversal, so we know that with the "
								a href="#tn-current-session-history-step" id=centralized-modifications-of-session-history:tn-current-session-history-step-5 "current session history step"
								- " being 2, adding the new entry as a step 3 doesn't make sense."
							}
						}
						li {
							p {
								- "Once the fetch for "
								code "/i-1-a"
								- " finally finishes, we proceed to finish updating the "
								code "frames[1]"
								a href="#navigable" id=centralized-modifications-of-session-history:navigable-6 navigable
								- " for the traversal, including updating its "
								a href="#nav-active-history-entry" id=centralized-modifications-of-session-history:nav-active-history-entry-5 "active session history entry"
								- " to the entry with URL "
								code "/i-1-a"
								- .
							}
						}
						li {
							p {
								- "Now that both navigables have finished processing the traversal, we update the "
								a href="#tn-current-session-history-step" id=centralized-modifications-of-session-history:tn-current-session-history-step-6 "current session history step"
								- " to the target step of 0."
							}
						}
					}
				}
				li {
					p "Now we can process the steps that were queued for the synchronous navigation:"
					ol {
						li {
							p {
								- "The "
								code "/i-0-a#foo"
								- " entry is added, with its "
								a href="#she-step" id=centralized-modifications-of-session-history:she-step-2 step
								- " determined to be 1: the "
								a href="#tn-current-session-history-step" id=centralized-modifications-of-session-history:tn-current-session-history-step-7 "current session history step"
								- " (i.e., 0) plus 1. This also "
								a href="#clear-the-forward-session-history" id=centralized-modifications-of-session-history:clear-the-forward-session-history "clears existing forward history"
								- .
							}
						}
						li {
							p {
								- "We fully switch to that newly added entry, including calling "
								a href="#apply-the-history-step" id=centralized-modifications-of-session-history:apply-the-history-step-4 "apply the history step"
								- ". This ultimately results in "
								a href="#update-document-for-history-step-application" id=centralized-modifications-of-session-history:update-document-for-history-step-application-2 "updating the document"
								- " by dispatching events like "
								code id=centralized-modifications-of-session-history:event-hashchange-2 {
									a href="#event-hashchange" hashchange
								}
								- ", as well as updating the "
								a href="#tn-current-session-history-step" id=centralized-modifications-of-session-history:tn-current-session-history-step-8 "current session history step"
								- " to the target step of 1."
							}
						}
					}
				}
			}
			p "The end result is:"
			table class=jake-diagram {
				thead {
					tr {
						td
						th class=step "0"
						th class="step current" "1"
					}
				}
				tbody {
					tr {
						th {
							code top
						}
						td class="doc-0 current" colspan="2" "/t"
					}
					tr {
						th {
							code "frames[0]"
						}
						td class="doc-1 next-is-same-doc" colspan="1" "/i-0-a"
						td class="doc-1 current prev-is-same-doc" colspan="1" "/i-0-a#foo"
					}
					tr {
						th {
							code "frames[1]"
						}
						td class="doc-3 current" colspan="2" "/i-1-a"
					}
				}
			}
		}
