		h4 id=navigating-across-documents {
			span class=secno "7.4.2"
			span id=browsing-the-web
			- Navigation
			a class=self-link href="#navigating-across-documents"
		}
		p {
			- "Certain actions cause a "
			a href="#navigable" id=navigating-across-documents:navigable navigable
			- " to "
			i id=navigating-across-documents:navigate {
				a href="#navigate" navigate
			}
			- " to a new resource."
		}
		p class=example {
			- "For example, "
			a href="#following-hyperlinks-2" id=navigating-across-documents:following-hyperlinks-2 "following a hyperlink"
			- ", "
			a href="#concept-form-submit" id=navigating-across-documents:concept-form-submit "form submission"
			- ", and the "
			code id=navigating-across-documents:dom-open {
				a href="#dom-open" "window.open()"
			}
			- " and "
			code id=navigating-across-documents:dom-location-assign {
				a href="#dom-location-assign" "location.assign()"
			}
			- " methods can all cause navigation."
		}
		div class=note id=note-meaning-of-navigate {
			p {
				- "Although in this standard the word \"navigation\" refers specifically to the "
				a href="#navigate" id=navigating-across-documents:navigate-2 navigate
				- " algorithm, this doesn't always line up with web developer or user perceptions. For example:"
			}
			ul {
				li {
					p {
						- "The "
						a href="#url-and-history-update-steps" id=navigating-across-documents:url-and-history-update-steps "URL and history update steps"
						- " are often used during so-called \"single-page app navigations\" or \"same-document navigations\", but they do not trigger the "
						a href="#navigate" id=navigating-across-documents:navigate-3 navigate
						- " algorithm."
					}
				}
				li {
					p {
						a href="#reload" id=navigating-across-documents:reload Reloads
						- " and "
						a href="#traverse-the-history-by-a-delta" id=navigating-across-documents:traverse-the-history-by-a-delta traversals
						- " are sometimes talked about as a type of navigation, since all three will often "
						a href="#attempt-to-populate-the-history-entry's-document" id=navigating-across-documents:attempt-to-populate-the-history-entry's-document "attempt to populate the history entry's document"
						- " and thus could perform navigational fetches. See, e.g., the APIs exposed "
						cite "Navigation Timing"
						- ". But they have their own entry point algorithms, separate from the "
						a href="#navigate" id=navigating-across-documents:navigate-4 navigate
						- " algorithm. "
						a href="#refsNAVIGATIONTIMING" "[NAVIGATIONTIMING]"
					}
				}
				li {
					p {
						- "Although "
						a href="#navigate-fragid" id=navigating-across-documents:navigate-fragid "fragment navigations"
						- " are always done through the "
						a href="#navigate" id=navigating-across-documents:navigate-5 navigate
						- " algorithm, a user might perceive them as more like jumping around a single page, than as a true navigation."
					}
				}
			}
		}
		h5 id=navigation-supporting-concepts {
			span class=secno "7.4.2.1"
			- " Supporting concepts"
			a class=self-link href="#navigation-supporting-concepts"
		}
		p {
			- "Before we can jump into the "
			a href="#navigate" id=navigation-supporting-concepts:navigate "navigation algorithm"
			- " itself, we need to establish several important structures that it uses."
		}
		p {
			- "The "
			dfn id=source-snapshot-params "source snapshot params"
			a data-x-internal=struct href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#struct" id=navigation-supporting-concepts:struct struct
			- " is used to capture data from a "
			code id=navigation-supporting-concepts:document {
				a href="#document" Document
			}
			- " initiating a navigation. It is snapshotted at the beginning of a navigation and used throughout the navigation's lifetime. It has the following "
			a data-x-internal=struct-item href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#struct-item" id=navigation-supporting-concepts:struct-item items
			- :
		}
		dl {
			dt {
				dfn id=source-snapshot-params-activation "has transient activation"
			}
			dd "a boolean"
			dt {
				dfn id=source-snapshot-params-sandbox "sandboxing flags"
			}
			dd {
				- "a "
				a href="#sandboxing-flag-set" id=navigation-supporting-concepts:sandboxing-flag-set "sandboxing flag set"
			}
			dt {
				dfn id=source-snapshot-params-download "allows downloading"
			}
			dd "a boolean"
			dt {
				dfn id=source-snapshot-params-client "fetch client"
			}
			dd {
				- "an "
				a href="#environment-settings-object" id=navigation-supporting-concepts:environment-settings-object "environment settings object"
				- ", only to be used as a "
				a data-x-internal=concept-request-client href="https://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-request-client" id=navigation-supporting-concepts:concept-request-client "request client"
			}
			dt {
				dfn id=source-snapshot-params-policy-container "source policy container"
			}
			dd {
				- "a "
				a href="#policy-container" id=navigation-supporting-concepts:policy-container "policy container"
			}
		}
		p {
			- "To "
			dfn id=snapshotting-source-snapshot-params "snapshot source snapshot params"
			- " given a "
			code id=navigation-supporting-concepts:document-2 {
				a href="#document" Document
			}
			var sourceDocument
			- ", return a new "
			a href="#source-snapshot-params" id=navigation-supporting-concepts:source-snapshot-params "source snapshot params"
			- " with"
		}
		dl class=props {
			dt {
				a href="#source-snapshot-params-activation" id=navigation-supporting-concepts:source-snapshot-params-activation "has transient activation"
			}
			dd {
				- "true if "
				var sourceDocument
				- "'s "
				a href="#concept-relevant-global" id=navigation-supporting-concepts:concept-relevant-global "relevant global object"
				- " has "
				a href="#transient-activation" id=navigation-supporting-concepts:transient-activation "transient activation"
				- "; otherwise false"
			}
			dt {
				a href="#source-snapshot-params-sandbox" id=navigation-supporting-concepts:source-snapshot-params-sandbox "sandboxing flags"
			}
			dd {
				var sourceDocument
				- "'s "
				a href="#active-sandboxing-flag-set" id=navigation-supporting-concepts:active-sandboxing-flag-set "active sandboxing flag set"
			}
			dt {
				a href="#source-snapshot-params-download" id=navigation-supporting-concepts:source-snapshot-params-download "allows downloading"
			}
			dd {
				- "false if "
				var sourceDocument
				- "'s "
				a href="#active-sandboxing-flag-set" id=navigation-supporting-concepts:active-sandboxing-flag-set-2 "active sandboxing flag set"
				- " has the "
