		h4 id=realms-and-their-counterparts {
			span class=secno "8.1.3"
			- " Realms and their counterparts"
			a class=self-link href="#realms-and-their-counterparts"
		}
		p {
			- "The JavaScript specification introduces the "
			a data-x-internal=realm href="https://tc39.es/ecma262/#sec-code-realms" id=realms-and-their-counterparts:realm realm
			- " concept, representing a global environment in which script is run. Each realm comes with an "
			a data-x-internal=implementation-defined href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#implementation-defined" id=realms-and-their-counterparts:implementation-defined implementation-defined
			a href="#global-object" id=realms-and-their-counterparts:global-object "global object"
			- "; much of this specification is devoted to defining that global object and its properties."
		}
		p {
			- "For web specifications, it is often useful to associate values or algorithms with a realm/global object pair. When the values are specific to a particular type of realm, they are associated directly with the global object in question, e.g., in the definition of the "
			code id=realms-and-their-counterparts:window {
				a href="#window" Window
			}
			- " or "
			code id=realms-and-their-counterparts:workerglobalscope {
				a href="#workerglobalscope" WorkerGlobalScope
			}
			- " interfaces. When the values have utility across multiple realms, we use the "
			a href="#environment-settings-object" id=realms-and-their-counterparts:environment-settings-object "environment settings object"
			- " concept."
		}
		p {
			- "Finally, in some cases it is necessary to track associated values before a realm/global object/environment settings object even comes into existence (for example, during "
			a href="#navigate" id=realms-and-their-counterparts:navigate navigation
			- "). These values are tracked in the "
			a href="#environment" id=realms-and-their-counterparts:environment environment
			- " concept."
		}
		h5 id=environments {
			span class=secno "8.1.3.1"
			- " Environments"
			a class=self-link href="#environments"
		}
		p {
			- "An "
			dfn data-export="" id=environment environment
			- " is an object that identifies the settings of a current or potential execution environment (i.e., a "
			a href="#navigation-params" id=environments:navigation-params "navigation params"
			- "'s "
			a href="#navigation-params-reserved-environment" id=environments:navigation-params-reserved-environment "reserved environment"
			- " or a "
			a data-x-internal=concept-request href="https://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-request" id=environments:concept-request request
			- "'s "
			a data-x-internal=concept-request-reserved-client href="https://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-request-reserved-client" id=environments:concept-request-reserved-client "reserved client"
			- "). An "
			a href="#environment" id=environments:environment environment
			- " has the following fields:"
		}
		dl {
			dt {
				- "An "
				dfn data-dfn-for=environment data-export="" id=concept-environment-id id
			}
			dd {
				p {
					- "An opaque string that uniquely identifies this "
					a href="#environment" id=environments:environment-2 environment
					- .
				}
			}
			dt {
				- "A "
				dfn data-dfn-for=environment data-export="" id=concept-environment-creation-url "creation URL"
			}
			dd {
				p {
					- "A "
					a data-x-internal=url href="https://url.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-url" id=environments:url URL
					- " that represents the location of the resource with which this "
					a href="#environment" id=environments:environment-3 environment
					- " is associated."
				}
				p class=note {
					- "In the case of a "
					code id=environments:window {
						a href="#window" Window
					}
					a href="#environment-settings-object" id=environments:environment-settings-object "environment settings object"
					- ", this URL might be distinct from its "
					a href="#concept-settings-object-global" id=environments:concept-settings-object-global "global object"
					- "'s "
					a href="#concept-document-window" id=environments:concept-document-window {
						- "associated "
						code Document
					}
					- "'s "
					a data-x-internal=the-document's-address href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-document-url" id=environments:the-document's-address URL
					- ", due to mechanisms such as "
					code id=environments:dom-history-pushstate {
						a href="#dom-history-pushstate" "history.pushState()"
					}
					- " which modify the latter."
				}
			}
			dt {
				- "A "
				dfn data-dfn-for=environment data-export="" id=concept-environment-top-level-creation-url "top-level creation URL"
			}
			dd {
				p {
					- "Null or a "
					a data-x-internal=url href="https://url.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-url" id=environments:url-2 URL
					- " that represents the "
					a href="#concept-environment-creation-url" id=environments:concept-environment-creation-url "creation URL"
					- " of the \"top-level\" "
					a href="#environment" id=environments:environment-4 environment
					- ". It is null for workers and worklets."
				}
			}
			dt {
				- "A "
				dfn data-dfn-for=environment data-export="" id=concept-environment-top-level-origin "top-level origin"
			}
			dd {
				p {
					- "A "
					span class=XXX "for now"
					a data-x-internal=implementation-defined href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#implementation-defined" id=environments:implementation-defined implementation-defined
					- " value, null, or an "
					a href="#concept-origin" id=environments:concept-origin origin
					- ". For a \"top-level\" potential execution environment it is null (i.e., when there is no response yet); otherwise it is the \"top-level\" "
					a href="#environment" id=environments:environment-5 environment
					- "'s "
					a href="#concept-settings-object-origin" id=environments:concept-settings-object-origin origin
					- ". For a dedicated worker or worklet it is the "
					a href="#concept-environment-top-level-origin" id=environments:concept-environment-top-level-origin "top-level origin"
					- " of its creator. For a shared or service worker it is an "
					a data-x-internal=implementation-defined href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#implementation-defined" id=environments:implementation-defined-2 implementation-defined
					- " value."
				}
				p class=note {
					- "This is distinct from the "
					a href="#concept-environment-top-level-creation-url" id=environments:concept-environment-top-level-creation-url "top-level creation URL"
					- "'s "
					a data-x-internal=concept-url-origin href="https://url.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-url-origin" id=environments:concept-url-origin origin
					- " when sandboxing, workers, and worklets are involved."
				}
			}
			dt {
				- "A "
				dfn data-dfn-for=environment data-export="" id=concept-environment-target-browsing-context "target browsing context"
			}
			dd {
				p {
					- "Null or a target "
					a href="#browsing-context" id=environments:browsing-context "browsing context"
					- " for a "
					a data-x-internal=navigation-request href="https://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/#navigation-request" id=environments:navigation-request "navigation request"
					- .
				}
			}
			dt {
				- "An "
				dfn data-dfn-for=environment data-export="" id=concept-environment-active-service-worker "active service worker"
			}
			dd {
				p {
					- "Null or a "
					a data-x-internal=dfn-service-worker href="https://w3c.github.io/ServiceWorker/#dfn-service-worker" id=environments:dfn-service-worker "service worker"
					- " that "
					a data-x-internal=dfn-control href="https://w3c.github.io/ServiceWorker/#dfn-control" id=environments:dfn-control controls
					- " the "
					a href="#environment" id=environments:environment-6 environment
					- .
				}
			}
			dt {
				- "An "
				dfn data-dfn-for=environment data-export="" id=concept-environment-execution-ready-flag "execution ready flag"
			}
			dd {
				p "A flag that indicates whether the environment setup is done. It is initially unset."
			}
		}
		p {
			- "Specifications may define "
			dfn data-export="" id=environment-discarding-steps "environment discarding steps"
			- " for environments. The steps take an "
			a href="#environment" id=environments:environment-7 environment
			- " as input."
		}
		p class=note {
			- "The "
			a href="#environment-discarding-steps" id=environments:environment-discarding-steps "environment discarding steps"
			- " are run for only a select few environments: the ones that will never become execution ready because, for example, they failed to load."
		}
		h5 id=environment-settings-objects {
			span class=secno "8.1.3.2"
			- " Environment settings objects"
			a class=self-link href="#environment-settings-objects"
		}
		p {
			- "An "
			dfn data-export="" id=environment-settings-object "environment settings object"
			- " is an "
			a href="#environment" id=environment-settings-objects:environment environment
			- " that additionally specifies algorithms for:"
		}
		dl {
			dt {
				- "A "
				dfn data-dfn-for="environment settings object" data-export="" id=realm-execution-context "realm execution context"
			}
			dd {
				p {
					- "A "
					a data-x-internal=javascript-execution-context href="https://tc39.es/ecma262/#sec-execution-contexts" id=environment-settings-objects:javascript-execution-context "JavaScript execution context"
					- " shared by all "
					a href="#the-script-element" id=environment-settings-objects:the-script-element scripts
					- " that use this settings object, i.e., all scripts in a given "
					a data-x-internal=realm href="https://tc39.es/ecma262/#sec-code-realms" id=environment-settings-objects:realm realm
					- ". When we "
					a href="#run-a-classic-script" id=environment-settings-objects:run-a-classic-script "run a classic script"
					- " or "
					a href="#run-a-module-script" id=environment-settings-objects:run-a-module-script "run a module script"
					- ", this execution context becomes the top of the "
					a data-x-internal=javascript-execution-context-stack href="https://tc39.es/ecma262/#execution-context-stack" id=environment-settings-objects:javascript-execution-context-stack "JavaScript execution context stack"
					- ", on top of which another execution context specific to the script in question is pushed. (This setup ensures "
					a data-x-internal=source-text-module-record href="https://tc39.es/ecma262/#sec-source-text-module-records" id=environment-settings-objects:source-text-module-record "Source Text Module Record"
					- "'s "
					a data-x-internal=js-evaluate href="https://tc39.es/ecma262/#sec-moduleevaluation" id=environment-settings-objects:js-evaluate Evaluate
					- " knows which realm to use.)"
				}
			}
			dt {
				- "A "
				dfn data-dfn-for="environment\n   settings object" data-export="" id=concept-settings-object-module-map "module map"
			}
			dd {
