		h5 id=import-maps {
			span class=secno "8.1.5.2"
			- " Import maps"
			a class=self-link href="#import-maps"
		}
		p {
			- "An "
			a href="#import-map" id=import-map-dev "import map"
			- " allows control over module specifier resolution. Import maps are delivered via inline "
			code id=import-maps:the-script-element {
				a href="#the-script-element" script
			}
			- " elements with their "
			code id=import-maps:attr-script-type {
				a href="#attr-script-type" type
			}
			- " attribute set to \""
			code importmap
			- "\", and with their "
			a data-x-internal=child-text-content href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-child-text-content" id=import-maps:child-text-content "child text content"
			- " containing a JSON representation of the import map."
		}
		p {
			- "A "
			code id=import-maps:document {
				a href="#document" Document
			}
			- " can have multiple import maps processed, which can happen either before or after any modules have been imported, e.g., via "
			code id="import-maps:import()" {
				a data-x-internal="import()" href="https://tc39.es/ecma262/#sec-import-calls" "import()"
			}
			- " expressions or "
			code id=import-maps:the-script-element-2 {
				a href="#the-script-element" script
			}
			- " elements with their "
			code id=import-maps:attr-script-type-2 {
				a href="#attr-script-type" type
			}
			- " attribute set to \""
			code module
			- "\". The "
			a href="#merge-existing-and-new-import-maps" id=import-maps:merge-existing-and-new-import-maps "merge existing and new import maps"
			- " algorithm ensures that new import maps cannot define the module resolution for modules that were already defined by past import maps, or for ones that were already resolved."
		}
		div class=example id=example-import-map-bare-specifier {
			p "The simplest use of import maps is to globally remap a bare module specifier:"
			pre {
				code class=json {
					c- p="" "{"
					c- u="" "\"imports\""
					c- o="" :
					c- p="" "{"
					c- u="" "\"moment\""
					c- o="" :
					c- u="" "\"/node_modules/moment/src/moment.js\""
					c- p="" "}"
					c- p="" "}"
				}
			}
			p {
				- "This enables statements like "
				code class=js "import moment from \"moment\";"
				- " to work, fetching and evaluating the JavaScript module at the "
				code "/node_modules/moment/src/moment.js"
				- " URL."
			}
		}
		div class=example id=example-import-map-trailing-slashes {
			p "An import map can remap a class of module specifiers into a class of URLs by using trailing slashes, like so:"
			pre {
				code class=json {
					c- p="" "{"
					c- u="" "\"imports\""
					c- o="" :
					c- p="" "{"
					c- u="" "\"moment/\""
					c- o="" :
					c- u="" "\"/node_modules/moment/src/\""
					c- p="" "}"
					c- p="" "}"
				}
			}
			p {
				- "This enables statements like "
				code class=js "import localeData from \"moment/locale/zh-cn.js\";"
				- " to work, fetching and evaluating the JavaScript module at the "
				code "/node_modules/moment/src/locale/zh-cn.js"
				- " URL. Such trailing-slash mappings are often combined with bare-specifier mappings, e.g."
			}
			pre {
				code class=json {
					c- p="" "{"
					c- u="" "\"imports\""
					c- o="" :
					c- p="" "{"
					c- u="" "\"moment\""
					c- o="" :
					c- u="" "\"/node_modules/moment/src/moment.js\""
					c- p="" ,
					c- u="" "\"moment/\""
					c- o="" :
					c- u="" "\"/node_modules/moment/src/\""
					c- p="" "}"
					c- p="" "}"
				}
			}
			p {
				- "so that both the \"main module\" specified by \""
				code moment
				- "\" and the \"submodules\" specified by paths such as \""
				code "moment/locale/zh-cn.js"
				- "\" are available."
			}
		}
		div class=example id=example-import-map-url-like-specifier {
			p {
				- "Bare specifiers are not the only type of module specifiers which import maps can remap. \"URL-like\" specifiers, i.e., those that are either parseable as absolute URLs or start with \""
				code "/"
				- "\", \""
				code "./"
				- "\", or \""
				code "../"
				- "\", can be remapped as well:"
			}
			pre {
				code class=json {
					c- p="" "{"
					c- u="" "\"imports\""
					c- o="" :
					c- p="" "{"
					c- u="" "\"https://cdn.example.com/vue/dist/vue.runtime.esm.js\""
					c- o="" :
					c- u="" "\"/node_modules/vue/dist/vue.runtime.esm.js\""
					c- p="" ,
					c- u="" "\"/js/app.mjs\""
					c- o="" :
					c- u="" "\"/js/app-8e0d62a03.mjs\""
					c- p="" ,
					c- u="" "\"../helpers/\""
					c- o="" :
					c- u="" "\"https://cdn.example/helpers/\""
					c- p="" "}"
					c- p="" "}"
				}
			}
			p {
				- "Note how the URL to be remapped, as well as the URL being mapped to, can be specified either as absolute URLs, or as relative URLs starting with \""
				code "/"
				- "\", \""
				code "./"
				- "\", or \""
				code "../"
				- "\". (They cannot be specified as relative URLs without those starting sigils, as those help distinguish from bare module specifiers.) Also note how the "
				a href="#example-import-map-trailing-slashes" "trailing slash mapping"
				- " works in this context as well."
			}
			p {
				- "Such remappings operate on the post-canonicalization URL, and do not require a match between the literal strings supplied in the import map key and the imported module specifier. So for example, if this import map was included on "
				code "https://example.com/app.html"
				- ", then not only would "
				code class=js "import \"/js/app.mjs\""
				- " be remapped, but so would "
				code class=js "import \"./js/app.mjs\""
				- " and "
				code class=js "import \"./foo/../js/app.mjs\""
				- .
			}
		}
		div class=example id=example-import-map-scopes {
			p {
				- "All previous examples have globally remapped module specifiers, by using the top-level \""
				code imports
				- "\" key in the import map. The top-level \""
				code scopes
				- "\" key can be used to provide localized remappings, which only apply when the referring module matches a specific URL prefix. For example:"
			}
			pre {
				code class=json {
					c- p="" "{"
					c- u="" "\"scopes\""
					c- o="" :
					c- p="" "{"
					c- u="" "\"/a/\""
					c- o="" :
					c- p="" "{"
					c- u="" "\"moment\""
					c- o="" :
					c- u="" "\"/node_modules/moment/src/moment.js\""
					c- p="" "},"
					c- u="" "\"/b/\""
					c- o="" :
					c- p="" "{"
					c- u="" "\"moment\""
					c- o="" :
					c- u="" "\"https://cdn.example.com/moment/src/moment.js\""
					c- p="" "}"
					c- p="" "}"
					c- p="" "}"
				}
			}
			p {
				- "With this import map, the statement "
				code "import \"moment\""
				- " will have different meanings depending on which referrer script contains the statement:"
			}
			ul {
				li {
					p {
						- "Inside scripts located under "
						code "/a/"
						- ", this will import "
						code "/node_modules/moment/src/moment.js"
						- .
					}
				}
				li {
					p {
						- "Inside scripts located under "
						code "/b/"
						- ", this will import "
						code "https://cdn.example.com/moment/src/moment.js"
						- .
					}
				}
				li {
					p {
						- "Inside scripts located under "
						code "/c/"
						- ", this will fail to resolve and thus throw an exception."
					}
				}
			}
			p "A typical usage of scopes is to allow multiple versions of the \"same\" module to exist in a web application, with some parts of the module graph importing one version, and other parts importing another version. "
		}
		div class=example id=example-import-map-scopes-overlapping {
			p {
				- "Scopes can overlap each other, and overlap the global \""
				code imports
				- "\" specifier map. At resolution time, scopes are consulted in order of most- to least-specific, where specificity is measured by sorting the scopes using the "
				a data-x-internal=code-unit-less-than href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#code-unit-less-than" id=import-maps:code-unit-less-than "code unit less than"
				- " operation. So, for example, \""
				code "/scope2/scope3/"
				- "\" is treated as more specific than \""
				code "/scope2/"
				- "\", which is treated as more specific than the top-level (unscoped) mappings."
			}
			p "The following import map illustrates this:"
			pre {
				code class=json {
					c- p="" "{"
					c- u="" "\"imports\""
					c- o="" :
					c- p="" "{"
					c- u="" "\"a\""
					c- o="" :
					c- u="" "\"/a-1.mjs\""
					c- p="" ,
					c- u="" "\"b\""
					c- o="" :
					c- u="" "\"/b-1.mjs\""
					c- p="" ,
					c- u="" "\"c\""
					c- o="" :
					c- u="" "\"/c-1.mjs\""
					c- p="" "},"
					c- u="" "\"scopes\""
					c- o="" :
					c- p="" "{"
					c- u="" "\"/scope2/\""
					c- o="" :
					c- p="" "{"
					c- u="" "\"a\""
					c- o="" :
					c- u="" "\"/a-2.mjs\""
					c- p="" "},"
					c- u="" "\"/scope2/scope3/\""
					c- o="" :
					c- p="" "{"
					c- u="" "\"b\""
					c- o="" :
					c- u="" "\"/b-3.mjs\""
					c- p="" "}"
					c- p="" "}"
					c- p="" "}"
				}
			}
			p "This results in the following resolutions (using relative URLs for brevity):"
			table id=table-import-map-scopes-example {
				thead {
					tr {
						td colspan="2" rowspan="2" {						}
						th colspan="3" "Specifier "
					}
					tr {
						th {
							- "\""
							code a
							- "\" "
						}
						th {
							- "\""
							code b
							- "\" "
						}
						th {
							- "\""
							code c
							- "\" "
						}
					}
				}
				tbody {
					tr {
						th rowspan="3" "Referrer "
						th {
							code "/scope1/r.mjs"
						}
						td {
							code "/a-1.mjs"
						}
						td {
							code "/b-1.mjs"
						}
						td {
							code "/c-1.mjs"
						}
					}
					tr {
						th {
							code "/scope2/r.mjs"
						}
						td {
							code "/a-2.mjs"
						}
						td {
							code "/b-1.mjs"
						}
						td {
							code "/c-1.mjs"
						}
					}
					tr {
						th {
							code "/scope2/scope3/r.mjs"
						}
						td {
							code "/a-2.mjs"
						}
						td {
							code "/b-3.mjs"
						}
						td {
							code "/c-1.mjs"
						}
					}
				}
			}
		}
		div class=example id=example-import-map-integrity {
			p {
				- "Import maps can also be used to provide modules with integrity metadata to be used in "
				cite "Subresource Integrity"
				- " checks. "
				a href="#refsSRI" "[SRI]"
			}
			p "The following import map illustrates this:"
			pre {
				code class=json {
					c- p="" "{"
					c- u="" "\"imports\""
					c- o="" :
					c- p="" "{"
					c- u="" "\"a\""
					c- o="" :
					c- u="" "\"/a-1.mjs\""
					c- p="" ,
					c- u="" "\"b\""
					c- o="" :
					c- u="" "\"/b-1.mjs\""
					c- p="" ,
					c- u="" "\"c\""
					c- o="" :
					c- u="" "\"/c-1.mjs\""
					c- p="" "},"
					c- u="" "\"integrity\""
					c- o="" :
					c- p="" "{"
					c- u="" "\"/a-1.mjs\""
					c- o="" :
					c- u="" "\"sha384-Li9vy3DqF8tnTXuiaAJuML3ky+er10rcgNR/VqsVpcw+ThHmYcwiB1pbOxEbzJr7\""
					c- p="" ,
					c- u="" "\"/d-1.mjs\""
					c- o="" :
					c- u="" "\"sha384-MBO5IDfYaE6c6Aao94oZrIOiC6CGiSN2n4QUbHNPhzk5Xhm0djZLQqTpL0HzTUxk\""
					c- p="" "}"
					c- p="" "}"
				}
			}
			p {
				- "The above example provides integrity metadata to be enforced on the modules "
				code "/a-1.mjs"
				- " and "
				code "/d-1.mjs"
				- ", even if the latter is not defined as an import in the map."
			}
		}
		hr
		p {
			- "The "
			a data-x-internal=child-text-content href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-child-text-content" id=import-maps:child-text-content-2 "child text content"
			- " of a "
