					- .
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "Let "
					var "active script"
					- " be the "
					a href="#active-script" id=hostmakejobcallback:active-script "active script"
					- .
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "Let "
					var "script execution context"
					- " be null."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "If "
					var "active script"
					- " is not null, set "
					var "script execution context"
					- " to a new "
					a data-x-internal=javascript-execution-context href="https://tc39.es/ecma262/#sec-execution-contexts" id=hostmakejobcallback:javascript-execution-context "JavaScript execution context"
					- ", with its Function field set to null, its Realm field set to "
					var "active script"
					- "'s "
					a href="#settings-object" id=hostmakejobcallback:settings-object "settings object"
					- "'s "
					a href="#environment-settings-object's-realm" id=hostmakejobcallback:environment-settings-object's-realm realm
					- ", and its ScriptOrModule set to "
					var "active script"
					- "'s "
					a href="#concept-script-record" id=hostmakejobcallback:concept-script-record record
					- .
				}
				p class=note {
					- "As seen below, this is used in order to propagate the current "
					a href="#active-script" id=hostmakejobcallback:active-script-2 "active script"
					- " forward to the time when the job callback is invoked."
				}
				div class=example {
					p {
						- "A case where "
						var "active script"
						- " is non-null, and saving it in this way is useful, is the following:"
					}
					pre {
						code class=js {
							- Promise
							c- p="" .
							- resolve
							c- p="" "("
							c- t="" "'import(`./example.mjs`)'"
							c- p="" ")."
							- then
							c- p="" "("
							- eval
							c- p="" ");"
						}
					}
					p {
						- "Without this step (and the steps that use it in "
						a href="#hostcalljobcallback" id=hostmakejobcallback:hostcalljobcallback HostCallJobCallback
						- "), there would be no "
						a href="#active-script" id=hostmakejobcallback:active-script-3 "active script"
						- " when the "
						code id="hostmakejobcallback:import()" {
							a data-x-internal="import()" href="https://tc39.es/ecma262/#sec-import-calls" "import()"
						}
						- " expression is evaluated, since "
						code id="hostmakejobcallback:eval()" {
							a data-x-internal="eval()" href="https://tc39.es/ecma262/#sec-eval-x" "eval()"
						}
						- " is a built-in function that does not originate from any particular "
						a href="#concept-script" id=hostmakejobcallback:concept-script script
						- .
					}
					p {
						- "With this step in place, the active script is propagated from the above code into the job, allowing "
						code id="hostmakejobcallback:import()-2" {
							a data-x-internal="import()" href="https://tc39.es/ecma262/#sec-import-calls" "import()"
						}
						- " to use the original script's "
						a href="#concept-script-base-url" id=hostmakejobcallback:concept-script-base-url "base URL"
						- " appropriately."
					}
				}
				div class=example {
					p {
						var "active script"
						- " can be null if the user clicks on the following button:"
					}
					pre {
						code class=html {
							c- p="" <
							c- f="" button
							c- e="" onclick
							c- o="" "="
							c- s="" "\"Promise.resolve('import(`./example.mjs`)').then(eval)\""
							c- p="" >
							- "Click me"
							c- p="" "</"
							c- f="" button
							c- p="" >
						}
					}
					p {
						- "In this case, the JavaScript function for the "
						a href="#event-handlers" id=hostmakejobcallback:event-handlers "event handler"
						- " will be created by the "
						a href="#getting-the-current-value-of-the-event-handler" id=hostmakejobcallback:getting-the-current-value-of-the-event-handler "get the current value of the event handler"
						- " algorithm, which creates a function with null [[ScriptOrModule]] value. Thus, when the promise machinery calls "
						a href="#hostmakejobcallback" id=hostmakejobcallback:hostmakejobcallback HostMakeJobCallback
						- ", there will be no "
						a href="#active-script" id=hostmakejobcallback:active-script-4 "active script"
						- " to pass along."
					}
					p {
						- "As a consequence, this means that when the "
						code id="hostmakejobcallback:import()-3" {
							a data-x-internal="import()" href="https://tc39.es/ecma262/#sec-import-calls" "import()"
						}
						- " expression is evaluated, there will still be no "
						a href="#active-script" id=hostmakejobcallback:active-script-5 "active script"
						- ". Fortunately that is handled by our implementation of "
						a href="#hostloadimportedmodule" id=hostmakejobcallback:hostloadimportedmodule HostLoadImportedModule
						- " by falling back to using the "
						a href="#current-settings-object" id=hostmakejobcallback:current-settings-object "current settings object"
						- "'s "
						a href="#api-base-url" id=hostmakejobcallback:api-base-url "API base URL"
						- .
					}
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "Return the "
					a data-x-internal=jobcallback-record href="https://tc39.es/ecma262/#sec-jobcallback-records" id=hostmakejobcallback:jobcallback-record "JobCallback Record"
					- " { [[Callback]]: "
					var callable
					- ", [[HostDefined]]: { [[IncumbentSettings]]: "
					var "incumbent settings"
					- ", [[ActiveScriptContext]]: "
					var "script execution context"
					- " } }."
				}
			}
		}
		h5 id=integration-with-the-javascript-module-system {
			span class=secno "8.1.6.7"
			- " Module-related host hooks"
			a class=self-link href="#integration-with-the-javascript-module-system"
		}
		p {
			- "The JavaScript specification defines a syntax for modules, as well as some host-agnostic parts of their processing model. This specification defines the rest of their processing model: how the module system is bootstrapped, via the "
			code id=integration-with-the-javascript-module-system:the-script-element {
				a href="#the-script-element" script
			}
			- " element with "
			code id=integration-with-the-javascript-module-system:attr-script-type {
				a href="#attr-script-type" type
			}
			- " attribute set to \""
			code module
			- "\", and how modules are fetched, resolved, and executed. "
			a href="#refsJAVASCRIPT" "[JAVASCRIPT]"
		}
		p class=note {
			- "Although the JavaScript specification speaks in terms of \"scripts\" versus \"modules\", in general this specification speaks in terms of "
			a href="#classic-script" id=integration-with-the-javascript-module-system:classic-script "classic scripts"
			- " versus "
			a href="#module-script" id=integration-with-the-javascript-module-system:module-script "module scripts"
			- ", since both of them use the "
			code id=integration-with-the-javascript-module-system:the-script-element-2 {
				a href="#the-script-element" script
			}
			- " element."
		}
		dl class=domintro {
			dt {
				code {
					var modulePromise
					- " = "
					a data-x-internal="import()" href="https://tc39.es/ecma262/#sec-import-calls" id="integration-with-the-javascript-module-system:import()" {
						- "import("
						var specifier
						- ")"
					}
				}
			}
			dd {
				p {
					- "Returns a promise for the module namespace object for the "
					a href="#module-script" id=integration-with-the-javascript-module-system:module-script-2 "module script"
					- " identified by "
					var specifier
					- ". This allows dynamic importing of module scripts at runtime, instead of statically using the "
					code import
					- " statement form. The specifier will be "
					a href="#resolve-a-module-specifier" id=integration-with-the-javascript-module-system:resolve-a-module-specifier resolved
					- " relative to the "
					a href="#active-script" id=integration-with-the-javascript-module-system:active-script "active script"
					- .
				}
				p {
					- "The returned promise will be rejected if an invalid specifier is given, or if a failure is encountered while "
					a href="#hostloadimportedmodule" id=integration-with-the-javascript-module-system:hostloadimportedmodule fetching
					- " or evaluating the resulting module graph."
				}
				p {
					- "This syntax can be used inside both "
					a href="#classic-script" id=integration-with-the-javascript-module-system:classic-script-2 classic
					- " and "
					a href="#module-script" id=integration-with-the-javascript-module-system:module-script-3 "module scripts"
					- ". It thus provides a bridge into the module-script world, from the classic-script world."
				}
			}
			dt {
				code {
					var url
					- " = "
					a data-x-internal=import.meta href="https://tc39.es/ecma262/#sec-meta-properties" id=integration-with-the-javascript-module-system:import.meta import.meta
					- .
					a href="#import-meta-url" id=integration-with-the-javascript-module-system:import-meta-url url
				}
			}
			dd {
				p {
					- "Returns the "
					a href="#active-script" id=integration-with-the-javascript-module-system:active-script-2 "active module script"
					- "'s "
					a href="#concept-script-base-url" id=integration-with-the-javascript-module-system:concept-script-base-url "base URL"
					- .
				}
				p {
					- "This syntax can only be used inside "
					a href="#module-script" id=integration-with-the-javascript-module-system:module-script-4 "module scripts"
					- .
				}
			}
			dt {
				code {
					var url
					- " = "
					a data-x-internal=import.meta href="https://tc39.es/ecma262/#sec-meta-properties" id=integration-with-the-javascript-module-system:import.meta-2 import.meta
					- .
					a href="#import-meta-resolve" id=integration-with-the-javascript-module-system:import-meta-resolve resolve
					- "("
					var specifier
					- ")"
				}
			}
			dd {
				p {
					- "Returns "
					var specifier
					- ", "
					a href="#resolve-a-module-specifier" id=integration-with-the-javascript-module-system:resolve-a-module-specifier-2 resolved
					- " relative to the "
					a href="#active-script" id=integration-with-the-javascript-module-system:active-script-3 "active script"
					- ". That is, this returns the URL that would be imported by using "
					code id="integration-with-the-javascript-module-system:import()-2" {
						a data-x-internal="import()" href="https://tc39.es/ecma262/#sec-import-calls" {
							- "import("
							var specifier
							- ")"
						}
					}
					- .
				}
				p {
					- "Throws a "
					code id=integration-with-the-javascript-module-system:typeerror {
						a data-x-internal=typeerror href="https://tc39.es/ecma262/#sec-native-error-types-used-in-this-standard-typeerror" TypeError
					}
					- " exception if an invalid specifier is given."
				}
				p {
					- "This syntax can only be used inside "
					a href="#module-script" id=integration-with-the-javascript-module-system:module-script-5 "module scripts"
					- .
				}
			}
		}
		p {
			- "A "
			dfn id=module-map "module map"
			- " is a "
			a data-x-internal=ordered-map href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ordered-map" id=integration-with-the-javascript-module-system:ordered-map map
			- " keyed by "
			a data-x-internal=tuple href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#tuple" id=integration-with-the-javascript-module-system:tuple tuples
			- " consisting of a "
			a data-x-internal=url-record href="https://url.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-url" id=integration-with-the-javascript-module-system:url-record "URL record"
			- " and a "
			a data-x-internal=string href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#string" id=integration-with-the-javascript-module-system:string string
			- ". The "
			a data-x-internal=url-record href="https://url.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-url" id=integration-with-the-javascript-module-system:url-record-2 "URL record"
			- " is the "
			a data-x-internal=concept-request-url href="https://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-request-url" id=integration-with-the-javascript-module-system:concept-request-url "request URL"
			- " at which the module was fetched, and the "
			a data-x-internal=string href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#string" id=integration-with-the-javascript-module-system:string-2 string
			- " indicates the type of the module (e.g. \""
			code javascript-or-wasm
			- "\"). The "
			a href="#module-map" id=integration-with-the-javascript-module-system:module-map "module map"
			- "'s values are either a "
			a href="#module-script" id=integration-with-the-javascript-module-system:module-script-6 "module script"
			- ", null (used to represent failed fetches), or a placeholder value \""
			code fetching
			- "\". "
			a href="#module-map" id=integration-with-the-javascript-module-system:module-map-2 "Module maps"
			- " are used to ensure that imported module scripts are only fetched, parsed, and evaluated once per "
			code id=integration-with-the-javascript-module-system:document {
				a href="#document" Document
			}
			- " or "
			a href="#workers" worker
			- .
		}
		div class=example {
			p {
				- "Since "
				a href="#module-map" id=integration-with-the-javascript-module-system:module-map-3 "module maps"
				- " are keyed by (URL, module type), the following code will create three separate entries in the "
				a href="#module-map" id=integration-with-the-javascript-module-system:module-map-4 "module map"
				- ", since it results in three different (URL, module type) "
				a data-x-internal=tuple href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#tuple" id=integration-with-the-javascript-module-system:tuple-2 tuples
				- " (all with \""
				code javascript-or-wasm
				- "\" type):"
			}
			pre {
				code class=js {
					c- k="" import
					c- u="" "\"https://example.com/module.mjs\""
					c- p="" ";"
					c- k="" import
					c- u="" "\"https://example.com/module.mjs#map-buster\""
					c- p="" ";"
					c- k="" import
					c- u="" "\"https://example.com/module.mjs?debug=true\""
					c- p="" ";"
				}
			}
			p {
				- "That is, URL "
				a data-x-internal=concept-url-query href="https://url.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-url-query" id=integration-with-the-javascript-module-system:concept-url-query queries
				- " and "
				a data-x-internal=concept-url-fragment href="https://url.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-url-fragment" id=integration-with-the-javascript-module-system:concept-url-fragment fragments
				- " can be varied to create distinct entries in the "
				a href="#module-map" id=integration-with-the-javascript-module-system:module-map-5 "module map"
				- "; they are not ignored. Thus, three separate fetches and three separate module evaluations will be performed."
			}
			p {
				- "In contrast, the following code would only create a single entry in the "
				a href="#module-map" id=integration-with-the-javascript-module-system:module-map-6 "module map"
				- ", since after applying the "
				a data-x-internal=url-parser href="https://url.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-url-parser" id=integration-with-the-javascript-module-system:url-parser "URL parser"
				- " to these inputs, the resulting "
				a data-x-internal=url-record href="https://url.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-url" id=integration-with-the-javascript-module-system:url-record-3 "URL records"
				- " are equal:"
			}
			pre {
				code class=js {
					c- k="" import
					c- u="" "\"https://example.com/module2.mjs\""
					c- p="" ";"
					c- k="" import
					c- u="" "\"https:example.com/module2.mjs\""
					c- p="" ";"
					c- k="" import
					c- u="" "\"https://///example.com\\\\module2.mjs\""
					c- p="" ";"
					c- k="" import
					c- u="" "\"https://example.com/foo/../module2.mjs\""
					c- p="" ";"
				}
			}
			p "So in this second example, only one fetch and one module evaluation will occur."
			p {
				- "Note that this behavior is the same as how "
				a href="#sharedworker" id=integration-with-the-javascript-module-system:sharedworker "shared workers"
				- " are keyed by their parsed "
				a href="#concept-sharedworkerglobalscope-constructor-url" id=integration-with-the-javascript-module-system:concept-sharedworkerglobalscope-constructor-url "constructor url"
				- .
			}
		}
		div class=example {
			p {
				- "Since module type is also part of the "
				a href="#module-map" id=integration-with-the-javascript-module-system:module-map-7 "module map"
				- " key, the following code will create two separate entries in the "
				a href="#module-map" id=integration-with-the-javascript-module-system:module-map-8 "module map"
				- " (the type is \""
				code javascript-or-wasm
				- "\" for the first, and \""
				code css
				- "\" for the second):"
			}
			pre {
				code class=html {
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" script
					c- e="" type
					c- o="" "="
					c- s="" module
					c- p="" >
					c- k="" import
					c- u="" "\"https://example.com/module\""
					c- p="" ";"
					c- p="" "</"
					c- f="" script
					c- p="" >
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" script
					c- e="" type
					c- o="" "="
					c- s="" module
					c- p="" >
					c- k="" import
					c- u="" "\"https://example.com/module\""
					c- a="" with
					c- p="" "{"
					- " type"
					c- o="" :
					c- u="" "\"css\""
					c- p="" "};"
					c- p="" "</"
					c- f="" script
					c- p="" >
				}
			}
			p "This can result in two separate fetches and two separate module evaluations being performed."
			p class=XXX {
				- "In practice, due to the as-yet-unspecified memory cache (see issue "
				a href="https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/6110" "#6110"
				- ") the resource may only be fetched once in WebKit and Blink-based browsers. Additionally, as long as all module types are mutually exclusive, the module type check in "
				a href="#fetch-a-single-module-script" id=integration-with-the-javascript-module-system:fetch-a-single-module-script "fetch a single module script"
				- " will fail for at least one of the imports, so at most one module evaluation will occur."
			}
			p {
				- "The purpose of including the type in the "
				a href="#module-map" id=integration-with-the-javascript-module-system:module-map-9 "module map"
				- " key is so that an import with the wrong type attribute does not prevent a different import of the same specifier but with the correct type from succeeding."
			}
		}
		div class=example {
			p {
				- "JavaScript module scripts are the default import type when importing from another JavaScript module; that is, when an "
				code import
				- " statement lacks a "
				code type
				- " import attribute the imported module script's type will be JavaScript. Attempting to import a JavaScript resource using an "
				code import
				- " statement with a "
				code type
