			- " (e.g. printed copy), or the representation of a physical form (e.g. PDF copy), of a document."
		}
		p {
			- "The "
			dfn id=printing-steps "printing steps"
			- " for a "
			code id=printing:document {
				a href="#document" Document
			}
			var document
			- " are:"
		}
		ol {
			li {
				p "The user agent may display a message to the user or return (or both)."
				p class=example {
					- "For instance, a kiosk browser could silently ignore any invocations of the "
					code id=printing:dom-print {
						a href="#dom-print" "print()"
					}
					- " method."
				}
				p class=example "For instance, a browser on a mobile device could detect that there are no printers in the vicinity and display a message saying so before continuing to offer a \"save to PDF\" option."
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "If the "
					a href="#active-sandboxing-flag-set" id=printing:active-sandboxing-flag-set "active sandboxing flag set"
					- " of "
					var document
					- " has the "
					a href="#sandboxed-modals-flag" id=printing:sandboxed-modals-flag "sandboxed modals flag"
					- " set, then return."
				}
				p class=note {
					- "If the printing dialog is blocked by a "
					code id=printing:document-2 {
						a href="#document" Document
					}
					- "'s sandbox, then neither the "
					code id=printing:event-beforeprint {
						a href="#event-beforeprint" beforeprint
					}
					- " nor "
					code id=printing:event-afterprint {
						a href="#event-afterprint" afterprint
					}
					- " events will be fired."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "The user agent must "
					a data-x-internal=concept-event-fire href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-event-fire" id=printing:concept-event-fire "fire an event"
					- " named "
					code id=printing:event-beforeprint-2 {
						a href="#event-beforeprint" beforeprint
					}
					- " at the "
					a href="#concept-relevant-global" id=printing:concept-relevant-global "relevant global object"
					- " of "
					var document
					- ", as well as any "
					a href="#child-navigable" id=printing:child-navigable "child navigable"
					- " in it."
				}
				p class=XXX {
					- "Firing in children only doesn't seem right here, and some tasks likely need to be queued. See "
					a href="https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/5096" "issue #5096"
					- .
				}
				p class=example {
					- "The "
					code id=printing:event-beforeprint-3 {
						a href="#event-beforeprint" beforeprint
					}
					- " event can be used to annotate the printed copy, for instance adding the time at which the document was printed."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "The user agent should offer the user the opportunity to "
					a href="#obtain-a-physical-form" id=printing:obtain-a-physical-form-2 "obtain a physical form"
					- " (or the representation of a physical form) of "
					var document
					- ". The user agent may wait for the user to either accept or decline before returning; if so, the user agent must "
					a href="#pause" id=printing:pause pause
					- " while the method is waiting. Even if the user agent doesn't wait at this point, the user agent must use the state of the relevant documents as they are at this point in the algorithm if and when it eventually creates the alternate form."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "The user agent must "
					a data-x-internal=concept-event-fire href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-event-fire" id=printing:concept-event-fire-2 "fire an event"
					- " named "
					code id=printing:event-afterprint-2 {
						a href="#event-afterprint" afterprint
					}
					- " at the "
					a href="#concept-relevant-global" id=printing:concept-relevant-global-2 "relevant global object"
					- " of "
					var document
					- ", as well as any "
					a href="#child-navigable" id=printing:child-navigable-2 "child navigables"
					- " in it."
				}
				p class=XXX {
					- "Firing in children only doesn't seem right here, and some tasks likely need to be queued. See "
					a href="https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/5096" "issue #5096"
					- .
				}
				p class=example {
					- "The "
					code id=printing:event-afterprint-3 {
						a href="#event-afterprint" afterprint
					}
					- " event can be used to revert annotations added in the earlier event, as well as showing post-printing UI. For instance, if a page is walking the user through the steps of applying for a home loan, the script could automatically advance to the next step after having printed a form or other."
				}
			}
		}
