				p "User agents should keep track of which sites have registered handlers (even if the user has declined such registrations) so that the user is not repeatedly prompted with the same request."
				p {
					- "If the "
					a href="#registerprotocolhandler()-automation-mode" id="custom-handlers:registerprotocolhandler()-automation-mode" {
						code "registerProtocolHandler()"
						- " automation mode"
					}
					- " of "
					a data-x-internal=this href="https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#this" id=custom-handlers:this-2 this
					- "'s "
					a href="#concept-relevant-global" id=custom-handlers:concept-relevant-global "relevant global object"
					- "'s "
					a href="#concept-document-window" id=custom-handlers:concept-document-window {
						- "associated "
						code Document
					}
					- " is not \""
					dfn id=rph-automation-mode-none {
						code none
					}
					- "\", the user agent should first verify that it is in an automation context (see "
					a data-x-internal=webdriver's-security-considerations href="https://w3c.github.io/webdriver/#security" id=custom-handlers:webdriver's-security-considerations "WebDriver's security considerations"
					- "). The user agent should then bypass the above communication of information and gathering of user consent, and instead do the following based on the value of the "
					a href="#registerprotocolhandler()-automation-mode" id="custom-handlers:registerprotocolhandler()-automation-mode-2" {
						code "registerProtocolHandler()"
						- " automation mode"
					}
					- :
				}
				dl {
					dt {
						- "\""
						dfn id=rph-automation-mode-auto-accept {
							code autoAccept
						}
						- "\""
					}
					dd {
						p "Act as if the user has seen the registration details and accepted the request."
					}
					dt {
						- "\""
						dfn id=rph-automation-mode-auto-reject {
							code autoReject
						}
						- "\""
					}
					dd {
