					a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Server-sent_events" title="Traditionally, a web page has to send a request to the server to receive new data; that is, the page requests data from the server. With server-sent events, it's possible for a server to send new data to a web page at any time, by pushing messages to the web page. These incoming messages can be treated as Events + data inside the web page." Server-sent_events
				}
