		hr
		h4 id=sse-processing-model {
			span class=secno "9.2.3"
			span id=processing-model-9
			- "Processing model"
			a class=self-link href="#sse-processing-model"
		}
		p {
			- "When a user agent is to "
			dfn id=announce-the-connection "announce the connection"
			- ", the user agent must "
			a href="#queue-a-task" id=sse-processing-model:queue-a-task "queue a task"
			- " which, if the "
			code id=sse-processing-model:dom-eventsource-readystate {
				a href="#dom-eventsource-readystate" readyState
			}
			- " attribute is set to a value other than "
			code id=sse-processing-model:dom-eventsource-closed {
				a href="#dom-eventsource-closed" CLOSED
			}
			- ", sets the "
			code id=sse-processing-model:dom-eventsource-readystate-2 {
				a href="#dom-eventsource-readystate" readyState
			}
			- " attribute to "
			code id=sse-processing-model:dom-eventsource-open {
				a href="#dom-eventsource-open" OPEN
			}
			- " and "
			a data-x-internal=concept-event-fire href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-event-fire" id=sse-processing-model:concept-event-fire "fires an event"
			- " named "
			code id=sse-processing-model:event-open {
				a href="#event-open" open
			}
			- " at the "
			code id=sse-processing-model:eventsource {
				a href="#eventsource" EventSource
			}
			- " object."
		}
		p {
			- "When a user agent is to "
			dfn id=reestablish-the-connection "reestablish the connection"
			- ", the user agent must run the following steps. These steps are run "
			a href="#in-parallel" id=sse-processing-model:in-parallel "in parallel"
			- ", not as part of a "
			a href="#concept-task" id=sse-processing-model:concept-task task
			- ". (The tasks that it queues, of course, are run like normal tasks and not themselves "
			a href="#in-parallel" id=sse-processing-model:in-parallel-2 "in parallel"
			- ".)"
		}
		ol {
			li {
				p {
					a href="#queue-a-task" id=sse-processing-model:queue-a-task-2 "Queue a task"
					- " to run the following steps:"
				}
				ol {
					li {
						p {
							- "If the "
							code id=sse-processing-model:dom-eventsource-readystate-3 {
								a href="#dom-eventsource-readystate" readyState
							}
							- " attribute is set to "
							code id=sse-processing-model:dom-eventsource-closed-2 {
								a href="#dom-eventsource-closed" CLOSED
							}
							- ", abort the task."
						}
					}
					li {
						p {
							- "Set the "
							code id=sse-processing-model:dom-eventsource-readystate-4 {
								a href="#dom-eventsource-readystate" readyState
							}
							- " attribute to "
							code id=sse-processing-model:dom-eventsource-connecting {
								a href="#dom-eventsource-connecting" CONNECTING
							}
							- .
						}
					}
					li {
						p {
							a data-x-internal=concept-event-fire href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-event-fire" id=sse-processing-model:concept-event-fire-2 "Fire an event"
							- " named "
							code id=sse-processing-model:event-error {
								a href="#event-error" error
							}
							- " at the "
							code id=sse-processing-model:eventsource-2 {
								a href="#eventsource" EventSource
							}
							- " object."
						}
					}
				}
			}
			li {
				p "Wait a delay equal to the reconnection time of the event source."
			}
			li {
				p "Optionally, wait some more. In particular, if the previous attempt failed, then user agents might introduce an exponential backoff delay to avoid overloading a potentially already overloaded server. Alternatively, if the operating system has reported that there is no network connectivity, user agents might wait for the operating system to announce that the network connection has returned before retrying."
			}
			li {
				p "Wait until the aforementioned task has run, if it has not yet run."
			}
			li {
				p {
					a href="#queue-a-task" id=sse-processing-model:queue-a-task-3 "Queue a task"
					- " to run the following steps:"
				}
				ol {
					li {
						p {
							- "If the "
							code id=sse-processing-model:eventsource-3 {
								a href="#eventsource" EventSource
							}
							- " object's "
							code id=sse-processing-model:dom-eventsource-readystate-5 {
								a href="#dom-eventsource-readystate" readyState
							}
							- " attribute is not set to "
							code id=sse-processing-model:dom-eventsource-connecting-2 {
								a href="#dom-eventsource-connecting" CONNECTING
							}
							- ", then return."
						}
					}
					li {
						p {
							- "Let "
							var request
							- " be the "
							code id=sse-processing-model:eventsource-4 {
								a href="#eventsource" EventSource
							}
							- " object's "
							a href="#concept-event-stream-request" id=sse-processing-model:concept-event-stream-request request
							- ". "
						}
					}
					li {
						p {
							- "If the "
							code id=sse-processing-model:eventsource-5 {
								a href="#eventsource" EventSource
							}
							- " object's "
							a href="#concept-event-stream-last-event-id" id=sse-processing-model:concept-event-stream-last-event-id "last event ID string"
							- " is not the empty string, then:"
						}
						ol {
							li {
								p {
									- "Let "
									var lastEventIDValue
									- " be the "
									code id=sse-processing-model:eventsource-6 {
										a href="#eventsource" EventSource
									}
									- " object's "
									a href="#concept-event-stream-last-event-id" id=sse-processing-model:concept-event-stream-last-event-id-2 "last event ID string"
									- ", "
									a data-x-internal=utf-8-encode href="https://encoding.spec.whatwg.org/#utf-8-encode" id=sse-processing-model:utf-8-encode "encoded as UTF-8"
									- .
								}
							}
							li {
								p {
									a data-x-internal=concept-header-list-set href="https://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-header-list-set" id=sse-processing-model:concept-header-list-set Set
									- " (`"
									code id=sse-processing-model:last-event-id {
										a href="#last-event-id" Last-Event-ID
									}
									- "`, "
									var lastEventIDValue
									- ") in "
									var request
									- "'s "
									a data-x-internal=concept-request-header-list href="https://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-request-header-list" id=sse-processing-model:concept-request-header-list "header list"
									- .
								}
							}
						}
					}
					li {
						p {
							a data-x-internal=concept-fetch href="https://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-fetch" id=sse-processing-model:concept-fetch Fetch
							var request
							- " and process the response obtained in this fashion, if any, as described earlier in this section."
						}
					}
				}
			}
		}
		p {
			- "When a user agent is to "
			dfn id=fail-the-connection "fail the connection"
			- ", the user agent must "
			a href="#queue-a-task" id=sse-processing-model:queue-a-task-4 "queue a task"
			- " which, if the "
			code id=sse-processing-model:dom-eventsource-readystate-6 {
				a href="#dom-eventsource-readystate" readyState
			}
			- " attribute is set to a value other than "
			code id=sse-processing-model:dom-eventsource-closed-3 {
				a href="#dom-eventsource-closed" CLOSED
			}
			- ", sets the "
			code id=sse-processing-model:dom-eventsource-readystate-7 {
				a href="#dom-eventsource-readystate" readyState
			}
			- " attribute to "
			code id=sse-processing-model:dom-eventsource-closed-4 {
				a href="#dom-eventsource-closed" CLOSED
			}
			- " and "
			a data-x-internal=concept-event-fire href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-event-fire" id=sse-processing-model:concept-event-fire-3 "fires an event"
			- " named "
			code id=sse-processing-model:event-error-2 {
				a href="#event-error" error
			}
			- " at the "
			code id=sse-processing-model:eventsource-7 {
				a href="#eventsource" EventSource
			}
			- " object. "
			strong {
				- "Once the user agent has "
				a href="#fail-the-connection" id=sse-processing-model:fail-the-connection "failed the connection"
				- ", it does "
				em not
				- " attempt to reconnect."
			}
		}
		hr
		p {
			- "The "
			a href="#task-source" id=sse-processing-model:task-source "task source"
			- " for any "
			a href="#concept-task" id=sse-processing-model:concept-task-2 tasks
			- " that are "
			a href="#queue-a-task" id=sse-processing-model:queue-a-task-5 queued
			- " by "
			code id=sse-processing-model:eventsource-8 {
				a href="#eventsource" EventSource
			}
			- " objects is the "
			dfn id=remote-event-task-source "remote event task source"
			- .
		}
		h4 id=the-last-event-id-header {
			span class=secno "9.2.4"
			- " The `"
			code id=the-last-event-id-header:last-event-id {
				a href="#last-event-id" Last-Event-ID
			}
			- "` header"
			a class=self-link href="#the-last-event-id-header"
		}
		p {
			- "The "
			dfn data-dfn-type=http-header id=last-event-id {
				code Last-Event-ID
			}
			- "` HTTP request header reports an "
			code id=the-last-event-id-header:eventsource {
				a href="#eventsource" EventSource
			}
			- " object's "
			a href="#concept-event-stream-last-event-id" id=the-last-event-id-header:concept-event-stream-last-event-id "last event ID string"
			- " to the server when the user agent is to "
			a href="#reestablish-the-connection" id=the-last-event-id-header:reestablish-the-connection "reestablish the connection"
			- ". "
		}
		p class=XXX {
			- "See "
			a href="https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/7363" "whatwg/html issue #7363"
			- " to define the value space better. It is essentially any UTF-8 encoded string, that does not contain U+0000 NULL, U+000A LF, or U+000D CR."
		}
		h4 id=parsing-an-event-stream {
			span class=secno "9.2.5"
			- " Parsing an event stream"
			a class=self-link href="#parsing-an-event-stream"
		}
		p {
			- "This event stream format's "
			a data-x-internal=mime-type href="https://mimesniff.spec.whatwg.org/#mime-type" id=parsing-an-event-stream:mime-type "MIME type"
			- " is "
			code id="parsing-an-event-stream:text/event-stream" {
				a href="#text/event-stream" "text/event-stream"
			}
			- .
		}
		p {
			- "The event stream format is as described by the "
			code stream
			- " production of the following ABNF, the character set for which is Unicode. "
			a href="#refsABNF" "[ABNF]"
		}
		pre {
			code class=abnf {
				c- nc="" stream
				c- o="" "="
				c- p="" "["
				c- nc="" bom
				c- p="" "]"
				c- o="" *
				c- nc="" event
				c- nc="" event
				c- o="" "="
				c- o="" *
				c- p="" "("
				c- nc="" comment
				c- o="" "/"
				c- nc="" field
				c- p="" ")"
				c- nc="" end-of-line
				c- nc="" comment
				c- o="" "="
				c- nc="" colon
				c- o="" *
				c- nc="" any-char
				c- nc="" end-of-line
				c- nc="" field
				c- o="" "="
				c- o="" "1*"
				c- nc="" name-char
				c- p="" "["
				c- nc="" colon
				c- p="" "["
				c- nc="" space
				c- p="" "]"
				c- o="" *
				c- nc="" any-char
				c- p="" "]"
				c- nc="" end-of-line
				c- nc="" end-of-line
				c- o="" "="
				c- p="" "("
				c- nc="" cr
				c- nc="" lf
				c- o="" "/"
				c- nc="" cr
				c- o="" "/"
				c- nc="" lf
				c- p="" ")"
				c- c1="" "; characters"
				c- nc="" lf
				c- o="" "="
				c- l="" %x000A
				c- c1="" "; U+000A LINE FEED (LF)"
				c- nc="" cr
				c- o="" "="
				c- l="" %x000D
				c- c1="" "; U+000D CARRIAGE RETURN (CR)"
				c- nc="" space
				c- o="" "="
				c- l="" %x0020
				c- c1="" "; U+0020 SPACE"
				c- nc="" colon
				c- o="" "="
				c- l="" %x003A
				c- c1="" "; U+003A COLON (:)"
				c- nc="" bom
				c- o="" "="
				c- l="" %xFEFF
				c- c1="" "; U+FEFF BYTE ORDER MARK"
				c- nc="" name-char
				c- o="" "="
				c- l="" %x0000-0009
				c- o="" "/"
				c- l="" %x000B-000C
				c- o="" "/"
				c- l="" %x000E-0039
				c- o="" "/"
				c- l="" %x003B-10FFFF
				c- c1="" "; a "
				a data-x-internal=scalar-value href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#scalar-value" id=parsing-an-event-stream:scalar-value {
					c- c1="" "scalar value"
				}
				c- c1="" " other than U+000A LINE FEED (LF), U+000D CARRIAGE RETURN (CR), or U+003A COLON (:)"
				c- nc="" any-char
				c- o="" "="
				c- l="" %x0000-0009
				c- o="" "/"
				c- l="" %x000B-000C
				c- o="" "/"
				c- l="" %x000E-10FFFF
				c- c1="" "; a "
				a data-x-internal=scalar-value href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#scalar-value" id=parsing-an-event-stream:scalar-value-2 {
					c- c1="" "scalar value"
				}
				c- c1="" " other than U+000A LINE FEED (LF) or U+000D CARRIAGE RETURN (CR)"
			}
		}
		p {
			- "Event streams in this format must always be encoded as UTF-8. "
			a href="#refsENCODING" "[ENCODING]"
		}
		p "Lines must be separated by either a U+000D CARRIAGE RETURN U+000A LINE FEED (CRLF) character pair, a single U+000A LINE FEED (LF) character, or a single U+000D CARRIAGE RETURN (CR) character."
		p "Since connections established to remote servers for such resources are expected to be long-lived, UAs should ensure that appropriate buffering is used. In particular, while line buffering with lines are defined to end with a single U+000A LINE FEED (LF) character is safe, block buffering or line buffering with different expected line endings can cause delays in event dispatch."
		h4 id=event-stream-interpretation {
			span class=secno "9.2.6"
			- " Interpreting an event stream"
			a class=self-link href="#event-stream-interpretation"
		}
		p {
			- "Streams must be decoded using the "
			a data-x-internal=utf-8-decode href="https://encoding.spec.whatwg.org/#utf-8-decode" id=event-stream-interpretation:utf-8-decode "UTF-8 decode"
			- " algorithm."
		}
		p class=note {
			- "The "
			a data-x-internal=utf-8-decode href="https://encoding.spec.whatwg.org/#utf-8-decode" id=event-stream-interpretation:utf-8-decode-2 "UTF-8 decode"
			- " algorithm strips one leading UTF-8 Byte Order Mark (BOM), if any."
		}
		p "The stream must then be parsed by reading everything line by line, with a U+000D CARRIAGE RETURN U+000A LINE FEED (CRLF) character pair, a single U+000A LINE FEED (LF) character not preceded by a U+000D CARRIAGE RETURN (CR) character, and a single U+000D CARRIAGE RETURN (CR) character not followed by a U+000A LINE FEED (LF) character being the ways in which a line can end."
		p {
			- "When a stream is parsed, a "
			var data
			- " buffer, an "
			var "event type"
			- " buffer, and a "
			var "last event ID"
			- " buffer must be associated with it. They must be initialized to the empty string."
		}
		p "Lines must be processed, in the order they are received, as follows:"
		dl class=switch {
			dt "If the line is empty (a blank line)"
			dd {
				p {
					a href="#dispatchMessage" id=event-stream-interpretation:dispatchMessage "Dispatch the event"
					- ", as defined below."
				}
			}
			dt "If the line starts with a U+003A COLON character (:)"
			dd {
				p "Ignore the line."
			}
			dt "If the line contains a U+003A COLON character (:)"
			dd {
				p {
					- "Collect the characters on the line before the first U+003A COLON character (:), and let "
					var field
					- " be that string."
				}
				p {
					- "Collect the characters on the line after the first U+003A COLON character (:), and let "
					var value
					- " be that string. If "
					var value
					- " starts with a U+0020 SPACE character, remove it from "
					var value
					- .
				}
				p {
					a href="#processField" "Process the field"
					- " using the steps described below, using "
					var field
					- " as the field name and "
					var value
					- " as the field value."
				}
			}
			dt "Otherwise, the string is not empty but does not contain a U+003A COLON character (:)"
			dd {
				p {
					a href="#processField" "Process the field"
					- " using the steps described below, using the whole line as the field name, and the empty string as the field value."
				}
			}
		}
		p "Once the end of the file is reached, any pending data must be discarded. (If the file ends in the middle of an event, before the final empty line, the incomplete event is not dispatched.)"
		hr
		p id=processField {
			- "The steps to "
			dfn "process the field"
			- " given a field name and a field value depend on the field name, as given in the following list. Field names must be compared literally, with no case folding performed."
		}
		dl class=switch {
			dt "If the field name is \"event\""
			dd {
				p {
					- "Set the "
					var "event type"
					- " buffer to field value."
				}
			}
			dt "If the field name is \"data\""
			dd {
				p {
					- "Append the field value to the "
					var data
					- " buffer, then append a single U+000A LINE FEED (LF) character to the "
					var data
					- " buffer."
				}
			}
			dt "If the field name is \"id\""
			dd {
				p {
					- "If the field value does not contain U+0000 NULL, then set the "
					var "last event ID"
					- " buffer to the field value. Otherwise, ignore the field."
				}
			}
			dt "If the field name is \"retry\""
			dd {
				p {
					- "If the field value consists of only "
					a data-x-internal=ascii-digits href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ascii-digit" id=event-stream-interpretation:ascii-digits "ASCII digits"
					- ", then interpret the field value as an integer in base ten, and set the event stream's "
					a href="#concept-event-stream-reconnection-time" id=event-stream-interpretation:concept-event-stream-reconnection-time "reconnection time"
					- " to that integer. Otherwise, ignore the field."
				}
			}
			dt Otherwise
			dd {
				p "The field is ignored."
			}
		}
		p {
			- "When the user agent is required to "
			dfn id=dispatchMessage "dispatch the event"
			- ", the user agent must process the "
			var data
			- " buffer, the "
			var "event type"
			- " buffer, and the "
			var "last event ID"
			- " buffer using steps appropriate for the user agent."
		}
		p {
			- "For web browsers, the appropriate steps to "
			a href="#dispatchMessage" id=event-stream-interpretation:dispatchMessage-2 "dispatch the event"
			- " are as follows:"
		}
		ol {
			li {
				p {
					- "Set the "
					a href="#concept-event-stream-last-event-id" id=event-stream-interpretation:concept-event-stream-last-event-id "last event ID string"
					- " of the event source to the value of the "
					var "last event ID"
					- " buffer. The buffer does not get reset, so the "
					a href="#concept-event-stream-last-event-id" id=event-stream-interpretation:concept-event-stream-last-event-id-2 "last event ID string"
					- " of the event source remains set to this value until the next time it is set by the server."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "If the "
					var data
					- " buffer is an empty string, set the "
					var data
					- " buffer and the "
					var "event type"
					- " buffer to the empty string and return."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "If the "
					var data
					- " buffer's last character is a U+000A LINE FEED (LF) character, then remove the last character from the "
					var data
					- " buffer."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "Let "
					var event
					- " be the result of "
					a data-x-internal=creating-an-event href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-event-create" id=event-stream-interpretation:creating-an-event "creating an event"
					- " using "
					code id=event-stream-interpretation:messageevent {
						a href="#messageevent" MessageEvent
					}
					- ", in the "
					a href="#concept-relevant-realm" id=event-stream-interpretation:concept-relevant-realm "relevant realm"
					- " of the "
					code id=event-stream-interpretation:eventsource {
						a href="#eventsource" EventSource
					}
					- " object."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "Initialize "
					var event
					- "'s "
					code id=event-stream-interpretation:dom-event-type {
						a data-x-internal=dom-event-type href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#dom-event-type" type
					}
					- " attribute to \""
					code id=event-stream-interpretation:event-message {
						a href="#event-message" message
					}
					- "\", its "
					code id=event-stream-interpretation:dom-messageevent-data {
						a href="#dom-messageevent-data" data
					}
					- " attribute to "
					var data
					- ", its "
					code id=event-stream-interpretation:dom-messageevent-origin {
						a href="#dom-messageevent-origin" origin
					}
					- " attribute to the "
					a href="#ascii-serialisation-of-an-origin" id=event-stream-interpretation:ascii-serialisation-of-an-origin serialization
					- " of the "
					a data-x-internal=concept-url-origin href="https://url.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-url-origin" id=event-stream-interpretation:concept-url-origin origin
					- " of the event stream's final URL (i.e., the URL after redirects), and its "
					code id=event-stream-interpretation:dom-messageevent-lasteventid {
						a href="#dom-messageevent-lasteventid" lastEventId
					}
					- " attribute to the "
					a href="#concept-event-stream-last-event-id" id=event-stream-interpretation:concept-event-stream-last-event-id-3 "last event ID string"
					- " of the event source."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "If the "
					var "event type"
					- " buffer has a value other than the empty string, change the "
					a data-x-internal=concept-event-type href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#dom-event-type" id=event-stream-interpretation:concept-event-type type
					- " of the newly created event to equal the value of the "
					var "event type"
					- " buffer."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "Set the "
					var data
					- " buffer and the "
					var "event type"
					- " buffer to the empty string."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					a href="#queue-a-task" id=event-stream-interpretation:queue-a-task "Queue a task"
					- " which, if the "
					code id=event-stream-interpretation:dom-eventsource-readystate {
						a href="#dom-eventsource-readystate" readyState
					}
					- " attribute is set to a value other than "
					code id=event-stream-interpretation:dom-eventsource-closed {
						a href="#dom-eventsource-closed" CLOSED
					}
					- ", "
					a data-x-internal=concept-event-dispatch href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-event-dispatch" id=event-stream-interpretation:concept-event-dispatch dispatches
					- " the newly created event at the "
					code id=event-stream-interpretation:eventsource-2 {
						a href="#eventsource" EventSource
					}
					- " object."
				}
			}
		}
		p class=note {
			- "If an event doesn't have an \"id\" field, but an earlier event did set the event source's "
			a href="#concept-event-stream-last-event-id" id=event-stream-interpretation:concept-event-stream-last-event-id-4 "last event ID string"
			- ", then the event's "
			code id=event-stream-interpretation:dom-messageevent-lasteventid-2 {
				a href="#dom-messageevent-lasteventid" lastEventId
			}
			- " field will be set to the value of whatever the last seen \"id\" field was."
		}
		p {
			- "For other user agents, the appropriate steps to "
			a href="#dispatchMessage" id=event-stream-interpretation:dispatchMessage-3 "dispatch the event"
			- " are implementation dependent, but at a minimum they must set the "
			var data
			- " and "
			var "event type"
			- " buffers to the empty string before returning."
		}
		div class=example {
			p "The following event stream, once followed by a blank line:"
			pre "data: YHOO data: +2 data: 10"
			p {
				- "...would cause an event "
				code id=event-stream-interpretation:event-message-2 {
					a href="#event-message" message
				}
				- " with the interface "
				code id=event-stream-interpretation:messageevent-2 {
					a href="#messageevent" MessageEvent
				}
				- " to be dispatched on the "
				code id=event-stream-interpretation:eventsource-3 {
					a href="#eventsource" EventSource
				}
				- " object. The event's "
				code id=event-stream-interpretation:dom-messageevent-data-2 {
					a href="#dom-messageevent-data" data
				}
				- " attribute would contain the string \""
				code "YHOO\\n+2\\n10"
				- "\" (where \""
				code "\\n"
				- "\" represents a newline)."
			}
			p "This could be used as follows: "
			pre {
				code class=js {
					c- a="" var
					- " stocks "
					c- o="" "="
					c- k="" new
					- " EventSource"
					c- p="" "("
					c- u="" "\"https://stocks.example.com/ticker.php\""
					c- p="" ");"
					- " stocks"
					c- p="" .
					- "onmessage "
					c- o="" "="
					c- a="" function
					c- p="" "("
					- event
					c- p="" ")"
					c- p="" "{"
					c- a="" var
					- " data "
					c- o="" "="
					- " event"
					c- p="" .
					- data
					c- p="" .
					- split
					c- p="" "("
					c- t="" "'\\n'"
					c- p="" ");"
					- " updateStocks"
					c- p="" "("
					- data
					c- p="" "["
					c- mf="" "0"
					c- p="" "],"
					- " data"
					c- p="" "["
					c- mf="" "1"
					c- p="" "],"
					- " data"
					c- p="" "["
					c- mf="" "2"
					c- p="" "]);"
					c- p="" "};"
				}
			}
			p {
				- "...where "
				code "updateStocks()"
				- " is a function defined as:"
			}
			pre {
				code class=js {
					c- a="" function
					- " updateStocks"
					c- p="" "("
					- symbol
					c- p="" ,
					- " delta"
					c- p="" ,
					- " value"
					c- p="" ")"
					c- p="" "{"
					c- p="" ...
					c- p="" "}"
				}
			}
			p "...or some such."
		}
		div class=example {
			p {
				- "The following stream contains four blocks. The first block has just a comment, and will fire nothing. The second block has two fields with names \"data\" and \"id\" respectively; an event will be fired for this block, with the data \"first event\", and will then set the last event ID to \"1\" so that if the connection died between this block and the next, the server would be sent a `"
				code id=event-stream-interpretation:last-event-id {
					a href="#last-event-id" Last-Event-ID
				}
				- "` header with the value `"
				code "1"
				- "`. The third block fires an event with data \"second event\", and also has an \"id\" field, this time with no value, which resets the last event ID to the empty string (meaning no `"
				code id=event-stream-interpretation:last-event-id-2 {
					a href="#last-event-id" Last-Event-ID
				}
				- "` header will now be sent in the event of a reconnection being attempted). Finally, the last block just fires an event with the data \" third event\" (with a single leading space character). Note that the last still has to end with a blank line, the end of the stream is not enough to trigger the dispatch of the last event."
			}
			pre ": test stream data: first event id: 1 data:second event id data: third event "
		}
		div class=example {
			p "The following stream fires two events:"
			pre "data data data data:"
			p "The first block fires events with the data set to the empty string, as would the last block if it was followed by a blank line. The middle block fires an event with the data set to a single newline character. The last block is discarded because it is not followed by a blank line."
		}
		div class=example {
			p "The following stream fires two identical events:"
			pre "data:test data: test "
			p "This is because the space after the colon is ignored if present."
		}
		h4 id=authoring-notes {
			span class=secno "9.2.7"
			- " Authoring notes"
			a class=self-link href="#authoring-notes"
		}
		p "Legacy proxy servers are known to, in certain cases, drop HTTP connections after a short timeout. To protect against such proxy servers, authors can include a comment line (one starting with a ':' character) every 15 seconds or so."
		p "Authors wishing to relate event source connections to each other or to specific documents previously served might find that relying on IP addresses doesn't work, as individual clients can have multiple IP addresses (due to having multiple proxy servers) and individual IP addresses can have multiple clients (due to sharing a proxy server). It is better to include a unique identifier in the document when it is served and then pass that identifier as part of the URL when the connection is established."
		p "Authors are also cautioned that HTTP chunking can have unexpected negative effects on the reliability of this protocol, in particular if the chunking is done by a different layer unaware of the timing requirements. If this is a problem, chunking can be disabled for serving event streams."
		p {
			- "Clients that support HTTP's per-server connection limitation might run into trouble when opening multiple pages from a site if each page has an "
			code id=authoring-notes:eventsource {
				a href="#eventsource" EventSource
			}
			- " to the same domain. Authors can avoid this using the relatively complex mechanism of using unique domain names per connection, or by allowing the user to enable or disable the "
			code id=authoring-notes:eventsource-2 {
				a href="#eventsource" EventSource
			}
			- " functionality on a per-page basis, or by sharing a single "
			code id=authoring-notes:eventsource-3 {
				a href="#eventsource" EventSource
			}
			- " object using a "
			a href="#sharedworkerglobalscope" id=authoring-notes:sharedworkerglobalscope "shared worker"
			- .
		}
		h4 id=eventsource-push {
			span class=secno "9.2.8"
			- " Connectionless push and other features"
			a class=self-link href="#eventsource-push"
		}
		p "User agents running in controlled environments, e.g. browsers on mobile handsets tied to specific carriers, may offload the management of the connection to a proxy on the network. In such a situation, the user agent for the purposes of conformance is considered to include both the handset software and the network proxy."
		div class=example {
			p "For example, a browser on a mobile device, after having established a connection, might detect that it is on a supporting network and request that a proxy server on the network take over the management of the connection. The timeline for such a situation might be as follows:"
			ol {
				li {
					- "Browser connects to a remote HTTP server and requests the resource specified by the author in the "
					code id=eventsource-push:dom-eventsource {
						a href="#dom-eventsource" EventSource
					}
					- " constructor."
				}
				li "The server sends occasional messages."
				li "In between two messages, the browser detects that it is idle except for the network activity involved in keeping the TCP connection alive, and decides to switch to sleep mode to save power."
				li "The browser disconnects from the server."
				li "The browser contacts a service on the network, and requests that the service, a \"push proxy\", maintain the connection instead."
				li {
					- "The \"push proxy\" service contacts the remote HTTP server and requests the resource specified by the author in the "
					code id=eventsource-push:dom-eventsource-2 {
						a href="#dom-eventsource" EventSource
					}
					- " constructor (possibly including a `"
					code id=eventsource-push:last-event-id {
						a href="#last-event-id" Last-Event-ID
					}
					- "` HTTP header, etc.)."
				}
				li "The browser allows the mobile device to go to sleep."
				li "The server sends another message."
				li "The \"push proxy\" service uses a technology such as OMA push to convey the event to the mobile device, which wakes only enough to process the event and then returns to sleep."
			}
		}
		p "This can reduce the total data usage, and can therefore result in considerable power savings."
		p {
			- "As well as implementing the existing API and "
			code id="eventsource-push:text/event-stream" {
				a href="#text/event-stream" "text/event-stream"
			}
			- " wire format as defined by this specification and in more distributed ways as described above, formats of event framing defined by "
			a href="#other-applicable-specifications" id=eventsource-push:other-applicable-specifications "other applicable specifications"
			- " may be supported. This specification does not define how they are to be parsed or processed."
		}
		h4 id=garbage-collection {
			span class=secno "9.2.9"
			- " Garbage collection"
			a class=self-link href="#garbage-collection"
		}
		p {
			- "While an "
			code id=garbage-collection:eventsource {
				a href="#eventsource" EventSource
			}
			- " object's "
			code id=garbage-collection:dom-eventsource-readystate {
				a href="#dom-eventsource-readystate" readyState
			}
			- " is "
			code id=garbage-collection:dom-eventsource-connecting {
				a href="#dom-eventsource-connecting" CONNECTING
			}
			- ", and the object has one or more event listeners registered for "
			code id=garbage-collection:event-open {
				a href="#event-open" open
			}
			- ", "
			code id=garbage-collection:event-message {
				a href="#event-message" message
			}
			- ", or "
			code id=garbage-collection:event-error {
				a href="#event-error" error
			}
			- " events, there must be a strong reference from the "
			code id=garbage-collection:window {
				a href="#window" Window
			}
			- " or "
			code id=garbage-collection:workerglobalscope {
				a href="#workerglobalscope" WorkerGlobalScope
			}
			- " object that the "
			code id=garbage-collection:eventsource-2 {
				a href="#eventsource" EventSource
			}
			- " object's constructor was invoked from to the "
			code id=garbage-collection:eventsource-3 {
				a href="#eventsource" EventSource
			}
			- " object itself."
		}
		p {
			- "While an "
			code id=garbage-collection:eventsource-4 {
				a href="#eventsource" EventSource
			}
			- " object's "
			code id=garbage-collection:dom-eventsource-readystate-2 {
				a href="#dom-eventsource-readystate" readyState
			}
			- " is "
			code id=garbage-collection:dom-eventsource-open {
				a href="#dom-eventsource-open" OPEN
			}
			- ", and the object has one or more event listeners registered for "
			code id=garbage-collection:event-message-2 {
				a href="#event-message" message
			}
			- " or "
			code id=garbage-collection:event-error-2 {
				a href="#event-error" error
			}
			- " events, there must be a strong reference from the "
			code id=garbage-collection:window-2 {
				a href="#window" Window
			}
			- " or "
			code id=garbage-collection:workerglobalscope-2 {
				a href="#workerglobalscope" WorkerGlobalScope
			}
			- " object that the "
			code id=garbage-collection:eventsource-5 {
				a href="#eventsource" EventSource
			}
			- " object's constructor was invoked from to the "
			code id=garbage-collection:eventsource-6 {
				a href="#eventsource" EventSource
			}
			- " object itself."
		}
		p {
			- "While there is a task queued by an "
			code id=garbage-collection:eventsource-7 {
				a href="#eventsource" EventSource
			}
			- " object on the "
			a href="#remote-event-task-source" id=garbage-collection:remote-event-task-source "remote event task source"
			- ", there must be a strong reference from the "
			code id=garbage-collection:window-3 {
				a href="#window" Window
			}
			- " or "
			code id=garbage-collection:workerglobalscope-3 {
				a href="#workerglobalscope" WorkerGlobalScope
			}
			- " object that the "
			code id=garbage-collection:eventsource-8 {
				a href="#eventsource" EventSource
			}
			- " object's constructor was invoked from to that "
			code id=garbage-collection:eventsource-9 {
				a href="#eventsource" EventSource
			}
			- " object."
		}
		p {
			- "If a user agent is to "
			dfn id=concept-eventsource-forcibly-close "forcibly close"
			- " an "
			code id=garbage-collection:eventsource-10 {
				a href="#eventsource" EventSource
			}
			- " object (this happens when a "
			code id=garbage-collection:document {
				a href="#document" Document
			}
			- " object goes away permanently), the user agent must abort any instances of the "
			a data-x-internal=concept-fetch href="https://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-fetch" id=garbage-collection:concept-fetch fetch
			- " algorithm started for this "
			code id=garbage-collection:eventsource-11 {
				a href="#eventsource" EventSource
			}
			- " object, and must set the "
			code id=garbage-collection:dom-eventsource-readystate-3 {
				a href="#dom-eventsource-readystate" readyState
			}
			- " attribute to "
			code id=garbage-collection:dom-eventsource-closed {
				a href="#dom-eventsource-closed" CLOSED
			}
			- .
		}
		p {
			- "If an "
			code id=garbage-collection:eventsource-12 {
				a href="#eventsource" EventSource
			}
			- " object is garbage collected while its connection is still open, the user agent must abort any instance of the "
			a data-x-internal=concept-fetch href="https://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-fetch" id=garbage-collection:concept-fetch-2 fetch
			- " algorithm opened by this "
			code id=garbage-collection:eventsource-13 {
				a href="#eventsource" EventSource
			}
			- .
		}
		h4 id=implementation-advice {
			span class=secno "9.2.10"
			- " Implementation advice"
			a class=self-link href="#implementation-advice"
		}
		p {
			i "This section is non-normative."
		}
		p {
			- "User agents are strongly urged to provide detailed diagnostic information about "
			code id=implementation-advice:eventsource {
				a href="#eventsource" EventSource
			}
			- " objects and their related network connections in their development consoles, to aid authors in debugging code using this API."
		}
		p {
			- "For example, a user agent could have a panel displaying all the "
			code id=implementation-advice:eventsource-2 {
				a href="#eventsource" EventSource
			}
			- " objects a page has created, each listing the constructor's arguments, whether there was a network error, what the CORS status of the connection is and what headers were sent by the client and received from the server to lead to that status, the messages that were received and how they were parsed, and so forth."
		}
		p {
			- "Implementations are especially encouraged to report detailed information to their development consoles whenever an "
			code id=implementation-advice:event-error {
				a href="#event-error" error
			}
			- " event is fired, since little to no information can be made available in the events themselves."
		}
		h3 id=web-messaging {
			span class=secno "9.3"
			dfn id=crossDocumentMessages "Cross-document messaging"
			a class=self-link href="#web-messaging"
