		p "Web browsers, for security and privacy reasons, prevent documents in different domains from affecting each other; that is, cross-site scripting is disallowed."
		p "While this is an important security feature, it prevents pages from different domains from communicating even when those pages are not hostile. This section introduces a messaging system that allows documents to communicate with each other regardless of their source domain, in a way designed to not enable cross-site scripting attacks."
		p class=note id=fingerprint-postMessage {
			- " The "
			code id=web-messaging:dom-window-postmessage {
				a href="#dom-window-postmessage" "postMessage()"
			}
			- " API can be used as a "
			a data-x-internal=tracking-vector href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#tracking-vector" id=web-messaging:tracking-vector "tracking vector"
			- .
		}
		h4 id=introduction-12 {
			span class=secno "9.3.1"
			- " Introduction"
			a class=self-link href="#introduction-12"
		}
		p {
			i "This section is non-normative."
		}
		div class=example {
			p {
				- "For example, if document A contains an "
				code id=introduction-12:the-iframe-element {
					a href="#the-iframe-element" iframe
				}
				- " element that contains document B, and script in document A calls "
				code id=introduction-12:dom-window-postmessage {
					a href="#dom-window-postmessage" "postMessage()"
				}
				- " on the "
				code id=introduction-12:window {
					a href="#window" Window
				}
				- " object of document B, then a message event will be fired on that object, marked as originating from the "
				code id=introduction-12:window-2 {
					a href="#window" Window
				}
				- " of document A. The script in document A might look like:"
			}
			pre {
				code class=js {
					c- a="" var
					- " o "
					c- o="" "="
					- " document"
					c- p="" .
					- getElementsByTagName
					c- p="" "("
					c- t="" 'iframe'
