		h4 id=introduction-13 {
			span class=secno "9.4.1"
			- " Introduction"
			a class=self-link href="#introduction-13"
		}
		p {
			i "This section is non-normative."
		}
		p {
			- "To enable independent pieces of code (e.g. running in different "
			a href="#browsing-context" id=introduction-13:browsing-context "browsing contexts"
			- ") to communicate directly, authors can use "
			a href="#channel-messaging" id=introduction-13:channel-messaging "channel messaging"
			- .
		}
		p {
			- "Communication channels in this mechanism are implemented as two-ways pipes, with a port at each end. Messages sent in one port are delivered at the other port, and vice-versa. Messages are delivered as DOM events, without interrupting or blocking running "
			a href="#concept-task" id=introduction-13:concept-task tasks
			- .
		}
		p {
			- "To create a connection (two \"entangled\" ports), the "
			code "MessageChannel()"
			- " constructor is called:"
		}
		pre {
			code class=js {
				c- a="" var
				- " channel "
				c- o="" "="
				c- k="" new
				- " MessageChannel"
				c- p="" "();"
			}
		}
		p {
			- "One of the ports is kept as the local port, and the other port is sent to the remote code, e.g. using "
			code id=introduction-13:dom-window-postmessage {
				a href="#dom-window-postmessage" "postMessage()"
			}
			- :
		}
		pre {
			code class=js {
				- otherWindow
				c- p="" .
				- postMessage
				c- p="" "("
				c- t="" 'hello'
				c- p="" ,
				c- t="" "'https://example.com'"
				c- p="" ,
				c- p="" "["
				- channel
				c- p="" .
				- port2
				c- p="" "]);"
			}
		}
		p {
			- "To send messages, the "
			code id=introduction-13:dom-messageport-postmessage {
				a href="#dom-messageport-postmessage" "postMessage()"
			}
			- " method on the port is used:"
		}
		pre {
			code class=js {
				- channel
				c- p="" .
				- port1
				c- p="" .
				- postMessage
				c- p="" "("
				c- t="" 'hello'
				c- p="" ");"
			}
		}
		p {
			- "To receive messages, one listens to "
			code id=introduction-13:event-message {
				a href="#event-message" message
			}
			- " events:"
		}
		pre {
			code class=js {
				- channel
				c- p="" .
				- port1
				c- p="" .
				- "onmessage "
				c- o="" "="
				- " handleMessage"
				c- p="" ";"
				c- a="" function
				- " handleMessage"
				c- p="" "("
				- event
				c- p="" ")"
				c- p="" "{"
				c- c1="" "// message is in event.data"
				c- c1="" "// ..."
				c- p="" "}"
			}
		}
		p {
			- "Data sent on a port can be structured data; for example here an array of strings is passed on a "
			code id=introduction-13:messageport {
				a href="#messageport" MessagePort
			}
			- :
		}
		pre {
			code class=js {
				- port1
				c- p="" .
				- postMessage
				c- p="" "(["
				c- t="" 'hello'
				c- p="" ,
				c- t="" 'world'
				c- p="" "]);"
			}
		}
		h5 id=examples-5 {
