			- " must be enabled, as if the "
			code id=message-ports:dom-messageport-start-2 {
				a href="#dom-messageport-start" "start()"
			}
			- " method had been called."
		}
		h4 id=ports-and-garbage-collection {
			span class=secno "9.4.5"
			- " Ports and garbage collection"
			a class=self-link href="#ports-and-garbage-collection"
		}
		p {
			- "When a "
			code id=ports-and-garbage-collection:messageport {
				a href="#messageport" MessagePort
			}
			- " object "
			var o
			- " is garbage collected, if "
			var o
			- " is entangled, then the user agent must "
			a href="#disentangle" id=ports-and-garbage-collection:disentangle disentangle
			var o
			- .
		}
		p {
			- "When a "
			code id=ports-and-garbage-collection:messageport-2 {
				a href="#messageport" MessagePort
			}
			- " object "
			var o
			- " is entangled and "
			code id=ports-and-garbage-collection:event-message {
				a href="#event-message" message
			}
			- " or "
			code id=ports-and-garbage-collection:event-messageerror {
				a href="#event-messageerror" messageerror
			}
			- " event listener is registered, user agents must act as if "
			var o
			- "'s entangled "
			code id=ports-and-garbage-collection:messageport-3 {
				a href="#messageport" MessagePort
			}
			- " object has a strong reference to "
			var o
			- .
		}
		p {
			- "Furthermore, a "
			code id=ports-and-garbage-collection:messageport-4 {
				a href="#messageport" MessagePort
			}
			- " object must not be garbage collected while there exists an event referenced by a "
			a href="#concept-task" id=ports-and-garbage-collection:concept-task task
			- " in a "
			a href="#task-queue" id=ports-and-garbage-collection:task-queue "task queue"
			- " that is to be dispatched on that "
			code id=ports-and-garbage-collection:messageport-5 {
				a href="#messageport" MessagePort
			}
			- " object, or while the "
			code id=ports-and-garbage-collection:messageport-6 {
				a href="#messageport" MessagePort
			}
			- " object's "
			a href="#port-message-queue" id=ports-and-garbage-collection:port-message-queue "port message queue"
			- " is enabled and not empty."
		}
		div class=note {
			p "Thus, a message port can be received, given an event listener, and then forgotten, and so long as that event listener could receive a message, the channel will be maintained."
			p "Of course, if this was to occur on both sides of the channel, then both ports could be garbage collected, since they would not be reachable from live code, despite having a strong reference to each other. However, if a message port has a pending message, it is not garbage collected."
		}
		p class=note {
			- "Authors are strongly encouraged to explicitly close "
			code id=ports-and-garbage-collection:messageport-7 {
				a href="#messageport" MessagePort
			}
			- " objects to disentangle them, so that their resources can be recollected. Creating many "
			code id=ports-and-garbage-collection:messageport-8 {
				a href="#messageport" MessagePort
			}
			- " objects and discarding them without closing them can lead to high transient memory usage since garbage collection is not necessarily performed promptly, especially for "
			code id=ports-and-garbage-collection:messageport-9 {
				a href="#messageport" MessagePort
			}
			- "s where garbage collection can involve cross-process coordination."
		}
