		p "There are several key things worth noting about the way the viewer is written."
		p {
			strong "Multiple listeners"
			- ". Instead of a single message processing function, the code here attaches multiple event listeners, each one performing a quick check to see if it is relevant for the message. In this example it doesn't make much difference, but if multiple authors wanted to collaborate using a single port to communicate with a worker, it would allow for independent code instead of changes having to all be made to a single event handling function."
		}
		p {
			- "Registering event listeners in this way also allows you to unregister specific listeners when you are done with them, as is done with the "
			code "configure()"
			- " method in this example."
		}
		p "Finally, the worker:"
