			li {
				- "the user agent has a "
				a href="#navigable" id=the-worker's-lifetime:navigable navigable
				- " whose "
				a href="#nav-document" id=the-worker's-lifetime:nav-document "active document"
				- " is not "
				a href="#completely-loaded" id=the-worker's-lifetime:completely-loaded "completely loaded"
				- .
			}
		}
		p class=note "The second part of this definition allows a shared worker to survive for a short time while a page is loading, in case that page is going to contact the shared worker again. This can be used by user agents as a way to avoid the cost of restarting a shared worker used by a site when the user is navigating from page to page within that site."
		p {
			- "A worker is said to be an "
			dfn id=active-needed-worker "active needed worker"
			- " if any of its "
			a href="#concept-WorkerGlobalScope-owner-set" id=the-worker's-lifetime:concept-WorkerGlobalScope-owner-set-3 owners
			- " are either "
			code id=the-worker's-lifetime:document {
				a href="#document" Document
			}
			- " objects that are "
			a href="#fully-active" id=the-worker's-lifetime:fully-active "fully active"
			- " or "
			a href="#active-needed-worker" id=the-worker's-lifetime:active-needed-worker "active needed workers"
			- .
		}
		p {
			- "A worker is said to be a "
			dfn id=protected-worker "protected worker"
			- " if it is an "
			a href="#active-needed-worker" id=the-worker's-lifetime:active-needed-worker-2 "active needed worker"
			- " and either it has outstanding timers, database transactions, or network connections, or its list of "
			a href="#the-worker's-ports" id=the-worker's-lifetime:the-worker's-ports "the worker's ports"
			- " is not empty, or its "
			code id=the-worker's-lifetime:workerglobalscope-5 {
				a href="#workerglobalscope" WorkerGlobalScope
			}
			- " is actually a "
			code id=the-worker's-lifetime:sharedworkerglobalscope-2 {
				a href="#sharedworkerglobalscope" SharedWorkerGlobalScope
			}
			- " object (i.e., the worker is a shared worker)."
		}
		p {
			- "A worker is said to be a "
			dfn id=suspendable-worker "suspendable worker"
			- " if it is not an "
			a href="#active-needed-worker" id=the-worker's-lifetime:active-needed-worker-3 "active needed worker"
			- " but it is a "
			a href="#permissible-worker" id=the-worker's-lifetime:permissible-worker "permissible worker"
			- .
		}
