		}
		div class=example {
			p {
				- "For example, in the following case it's ok to remove the \""
				code <html>
				- "\" tag:"
			}
			pre {
				code class=html {
					c- cp="" "<!DOCTYPE HTML>"
					strong {
						c- p="" <
						c- f="" html
						c- p="" >
					}
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" head
					c- p="" >
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" title
					c- p="" >
					- Hello
					c- p="" "</"
					c- f="" title
					c- p="" >
					c- p="" "</"
					c- f="" head
					c- p="" >
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" body
					c- p="" >
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" p
					c- p="" >
					- "Welcome to this example."
					c- p="" "</"
					c- f="" p
					c- p="" >
					c- p="" "</"
					c- f="" body
					c- p="" >
					c- p="" "</"
					c- f="" html
					c- p="" >
				}
			}
			p "Doing so would make the document look like this:"
			pre {
				code class=html {
					c- cp="" "<!DOCTYPE HTML>"
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" head
					c- p="" >
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" title
					c- p="" >
					- Hello
					c- p="" "</"
					c- f="" title
					c- p="" >
					c- p="" "</"
					c- f="" head
					c- p="" >
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" body
					c- p="" >
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" p
					c- p="" >
					- "Welcome to this example."
					c- p="" "</"
					c- f="" p
					c- p="" >
					c- p="" "</"
					c- f="" body
					c- p="" >
					c- p="" "</"
					c- f="" html
					c- p="" >
				}
			}
			p {
				- "This has the exact same DOM. In particular, note that whitespace around the "
				a data-x-internal=document-element href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#document-element" id=optional-tags:document-element "document element"
				- " is ignored by the parser. The following example would also have the exact same DOM:"
			}
			pre {
				code class=html {
					c- cp="" "<!DOCTYPE HTML>"
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" head
					c- p="" >
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" title
					c- p="" >
					- Hello
					c- p="" "</"
					c- f="" title
					c- p="" >
					c- p="" "</"
					c- f="" head
					c- p="" >
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" body
					c- p="" >
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" p
					c- p="" >
					- "Welcome to this example."
					c- p="" "</"
					c- f="" p
					c- p="" >
					c- p="" "</"
					c- f="" body
					c- p="" >
					c- p="" "</"
					c- f="" html
					c- p="" >
				}
			}
			p {
				- "However, in the following example, removing the start tag moves the comment to before the "
				code id=optional-tags:the-html-element-4 {
					a href="#the-html-element" html
				}
				- " element:"
			}
			pre {
				code class=html {
					c- cp="" "<!DOCTYPE HTML>"
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" html
					c- p="" >
					strong {
						c- c="" "<!-- where is this comment in the DOM? -->"
					}
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" head
					c- p="" >
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" title
					c- p="" >
					- Hello
					c- p="" "</"
					c- f="" title
					c- p="" >
					c- p="" "</"
					c- f="" head
					c- p="" >
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" body
					c- p="" >
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" p
					c- p="" >
					- "Welcome to this example."
					c- p="" "</"
					c- f="" p
					c- p="" >
					c- p="" "</"
					c- f="" body
					c- p="" >
					c- p="" "</"
					c- f="" html
					c- p="" >
				}
			}
			p "With the tag removed, the document actually turns into the same as this:"
			pre {
				code class=html {
					c- cp="" "<!DOCTYPE HTML>"
					c- c="" "<!-- where is this comment in the DOM? -->"
					small {
						c- p="" <
						c- f="" html
						c- p="" >
					}
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" head
					c- p="" >
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" title
					c- p="" >
					- Hello
					c- p="" "</"
					c- f="" title
					c- p="" >
					c- p="" "</"
					c- f="" head
					c- p="" >
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" body
					c- p="" >
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" p
					c- p="" >
					- "Welcome to this example."
					c- p="" "</"
					c- f="" p
					c- p="" >
					c- p="" "</"
					c- f="" body
					c- p="" >
					c- p="" "</"
					c- f="" html
					c- p="" >
				}
			}
			p "This is why the tag can only be removed if it is not followed by a comment: removing the tag when there is a comment there changes the document's resulting parse tree. Of course, if the position of the comment does not matter, then the tag can be omitted, as if the comment had been moved to before the start tag in the first place."
		}
