					- "Control Unit "
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" th
					c- p="" >
					- "Central Station "
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" tbody
					c- p="" >
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" tr
					c- p="" >
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" td
					c- p="" >
					- "Headlights "
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" td
					c- p="" >
					- "✔ "
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" td
					c- p="" >
					- "✔ "
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" tr
					c- p="" >
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" td
					c- p="" >
					- "Interior Lights "
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" td
					c- p="" >
					- "✔ "
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" td
					c- p="" >
					- "✔ "
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" tr
					c- p="" >
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" td
					c- p="" >
					- "Electric locomotive operating sounds "
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" td
					c- p="" >
					- "✔ "
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" td
					c- p="" >
					- "✔ "
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" tr
					c- p="" >
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" td
					c- p="" >
					- "Engineer's cab lighting "
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" td
					c- p="" >
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" td
					c- p="" >
					- "✔ "
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" tr
					c- p="" >
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" td
					c- p="" >
					- "Station Announcements - Swiss "
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" td
					c- p="" >
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" td
					c- p="" >
					- "✔ "
					c- p="" "</"
					c- f="" table
					c- p="" >
				}
			}
			p "The only differences between these tables, at the DOM level, is with the precise position of the (in any case semantically-neutral) whitespace."
		}
		p {
			strong However
			- ", a "
			a href="#syntax-start-tag" id=optional-tags:syntax-start-tag-7 "start tag"
			- " must never be omitted if it has any attributes."
		}
		div class=example {
			p "Returning to the earlier example with all the whitespace removed and then all the optional tags removed:"
			pre {
				code class=html {
					c- cp="" "<!DOCTYPE HTML>"
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" title
					c- p="" >
					- Hello
					c- p="" "</"
					c- f="" title
					c- p="" ><
					c- f="" p
					c- p="" >
					- "Welcome to this example."
				}
			}
			p {
				- "If the "
				code id=optional-tags:the-body-element-9 {
					a href="#the-body-element" body
				}
				- " element in this example had to have a "
				code id=optional-tags:classes {
					a href="#classes" class
				}
				- " attribute and the "
				code id=optional-tags:the-html-element-8 {
					a href="#the-html-element" html
				}
				- " element had to have a "
				code id=optional-tags:attr-lang {
					a href="#attr-lang" lang
				}
				- " attribute, the markup would have to become:"
			}
			pre {
				code class=html {
					c- cp="" "<!DOCTYPE HTML>"
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" html
					c- e="" lang
					c- o="" "="
					c- s="" "\"en\""
					c- p="" ><
					c- f="" title
					c- p="" >
					- Hello
					c- p="" "</"
					c- f="" title
					c- p="" ><
					c- f="" body
					c- e="" class
					c- o="" "="
					c- s="" "\"demo\""
					c- p="" ><
					c- f="" p
					c- p="" >
					- "Welcome to this example."
				}
			}
		}
		p class=note {
			- "This section assumes that the document is conforming, in particular, that there are no "
			a href="#content-models" id=optional-tags:content-models "content model"
			- " violations. Omitting tags in the fashion described in this section in a document that does not conform to the "
			a href="#content-models" id=optional-tags:content-models-2 "content models"
			- " described in this specification is likely to result in unexpected DOM differences (this is, in part, what the content models are designed to avoid)."
		}
		h5 id=element-restrictions {
			span class=secno "13.1.2.5"
			- " Restrictions on content models"
			a class=self-link href="#element-restrictions"
		}
		p "For historical reasons, certain elements have extra restrictions beyond even the restrictions given by their content model."
		p {
			- "A "
			code id=element-restrictions:the-table-element {
				a href="#the-table-element" table
			}
			- " element must not contain "
			code id=element-restrictions:the-tr-element {
				a href="#the-tr-element" tr
			}
			- " elements, even though these elements are technically allowed inside "
			code id=element-restrictions:the-table-element-2 {
				a href="#the-table-element" table
			}
			- " elements according to the content models described in this specification. (If a "
			code id=element-restrictions:the-tr-element-2 {
				a href="#the-tr-element" tr
			}
			- " element is put inside a "
			code id=element-restrictions:the-table-element-3 {
				a href="#the-table-element" table
			}
			- " in the markup, it will in fact imply a "
			code id=element-restrictions:the-tbody-element {
				a href="#the-tbody-element" tbody
			}
			- " start tag before it.)"
		}
		p {
			- "A single "
			a href="#syntax-newlines" id=element-restrictions:syntax-newlines newline
			- " may be placed immediately after the "
			a href="#syntax-start-tag" id=element-restrictions:syntax-start-tag "start tag"
			- " of "
			code id=element-restrictions:the-pre-element {
				a href="#the-pre-element" pre
			}
			- " and "
			code id=element-restrictions:the-textarea-element {
				a href="#the-textarea-element" textarea
			}
			- " elements. This does not affect the processing of the element. The otherwise optional "
			a href="#syntax-newlines" id=element-restrictions:syntax-newlines-2 newline
			em must
			- " be included if the element's contents themselves start with a "
			a href="#syntax-newlines" id=element-restrictions:syntax-newlines-3 newline
			- " (because otherwise the leading newline in the contents would be treated like the optional newline, and ignored)."
		}
		div class=example {
			p {
				- "The following two "
				code id=element-restrictions:the-pre-element-2 {
					a href="#the-pre-element" pre
				}
				- " blocks are equivalent:"
			}
			pre {
				code class=html {
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" pre
					c- p="" >
					- Hello
					c- p="" "</"
					c- f="" pre
					c- p="" >
				}
			}
			pre {
				code class=html {
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" pre
					c- p="" >
					br
					- Hello
					c- p="" "</"
					c- f="" pre
					c- p="" >
				}
			}
		}
		h5 id=cdata-rcdata-restrictions {
			span class=secno "13.1.2.6"
			- " Restrictions on the contents of raw text and escapable raw text elements"
			a class=self-link href="#cdata-rcdata-restrictions"
		}
		p {
			- "The text in "
			a href="#raw-text-elements" id=cdata-rcdata-restrictions:raw-text-elements "raw text"
			- " and "
			a href="#escapable-raw-text-elements" id=cdata-rcdata-restrictions:escapable-raw-text-elements "escapable raw text elements"
			- " must not contain any occurrences of the string \""
			code "</"
			- "\" (U+003C LESS-THAN SIGN, U+002F SOLIDUS) followed by characters that case-insensitively match the tag name of the element followed by one of U+0009 CHARACTER TABULATION (tab), U+000A LINE FEED (LF), U+000C FORM FEED (FF), U+000D CARRIAGE RETURN (CR), U+0020 SPACE, U+003E GREATER-THAN SIGN (>), or U+002F SOLIDUS (/)."
		}
		h4 id=text-2 {
			span class=secno "13.1.3"
			- " Text"
			a class=self-link href="#text-2"
		}
		p {
			dfn id=syntax-text Text
			- " is allowed inside elements, attribute values, and comments. Extra constraints are placed on what is and what is not allowed in text based on where the text is to be put, as described in the other sections."
		}
		h5 id=newlines {
			span class=secno "13.1.3.1"
			- " Newlines"
			a class=self-link href="#newlines"
		}
		p {
			dfn id=syntax-newlines Newlines
			- " in HTML may be represented either as U+000D CARRIAGE RETURN (CR) characters, U+000A LINE FEED (LF) characters, or pairs of U+000D CARRIAGE RETURN (CR), U+000A LINE FEED (LF) characters in that order."
		}
		p {
			- "Where "
			a href="#syntax-charref" id=newlines:syntax-charref "character references"
			- " are allowed, a character reference of a U+000A LINE FEED (LF) character (but not a U+000D CARRIAGE RETURN (CR) character) also represents a "
			a href="#syntax-newlines" id=newlines:syntax-newlines newline
			- .
		}
		h4 id=character-references {
			span class=secno "13.1.4"
			- " Character references"
			a class=self-link href="#character-references"
		}
		p {
			- "In certain cases described in other sections, "
			a href="#syntax-text" id=character-references:syntax-text text
			- " may be mixed with "
			dfn id=syntax-charref "character references"
			- ". These can be used to escape characters that couldn't otherwise legally be included in "
			a href="#syntax-text" id=character-references:syntax-text-2 text
			- .
		}
		p "Character references must start with a U+0026 AMPERSAND character (&). Following this, there are three possible kinds of character references:"
		dl {
			dt "Named character references"
			dd {
				- "The ampersand must be followed by one of the names given in the "
				a href="#named-character-references" id=character-references:named-character-references "named character references"
				- " section, using the same case. The name must be one that is terminated by a U+003B SEMICOLON character (;)."
			}
			dt "Decimal numeric character reference"
			dd {
				- "The ampersand must be followed by a U+0023 NUMBER SIGN character (#), followed by one or more "
				a data-x-internal=ascii-digits href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ascii-digit" id=character-references:ascii-digits "ASCII digits"
				- ", representing a base-ten integer that corresponds to a code point that is allowed according to the definition below. The digits must then be followed by a U+003B SEMICOLON character (;)."
			}
			dt "Hexadecimal numeric character reference"
			dd {
				- "The ampersand must be followed by a U+0023 NUMBER SIGN character (#), which must be followed by either a U+0078 LATIN SMALL LETTER X character (x) or a U+0058 LATIN CAPITAL LETTER X character (X), which must then be followed by one or more "
				a data-x-internal=ascii-hex-digits href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ascii-hex-digit" id=character-references:ascii-hex-digits "ASCII hex digits"
				- ", representing a hexadecimal integer that corresponds to a code point that is allowed according to the definition below. The digits must then be followed by a U+003B SEMICOLON character (;)."
			}
		}
		p {
			- "The numeric character reference forms described above are allowed to reference any code point excluding U+000D CR, "
			a data-x-internal=noncharacter href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#noncharacter" id=character-references:noncharacter noncharacters
			- ", and "
			a data-x-internal=control href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#control" id=character-references:control controls
			- " other than "
			a data-x-internal=space-characters href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ascii-whitespace" id=character-references:space-characters "ASCII whitespace"
			- .
		}
		p {
			- "An "
			dfn id=syntax-ambiguous-ampersand "ambiguous ampersand"
			- " is a U+0026 AMPERSAND character (&) that is followed by one or more "
			a data-x-internal=alphanumeric-ascii-characters href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ascii-alphanumeric" id=character-references:alphanumeric-ascii-characters "ASCII alphanumerics"
			- ", followed by a U+003B SEMICOLON character (;), where these characters do not match any of the names given in the "
			a href="#named-character-references" id=character-references:named-character-references-2 "named character references"
			- " section."
		}
		h4 id=cdata-sections {
			span class=secno "13.1.5"
			- " CDATA sections"
			a class=self-link href="#cdata-sections"
		}
		p {
			dfn id=syntax-cdata "CDATA sections"
			- " must consist of the following components, in this order:"
		}
		ol {
			li {
				- "The string \""
				code "<![CDATA["
				- "\"."
			}
			li {
				- "Optionally, "
				a href="#syntax-text" id=cdata-sections:syntax-text text
				- ", with the additional restriction that the text must not contain the string \""
				code "]]>"
				- "\"."
			}
			li {
				- "The string \""
				code "]]>"
				- "\"."
			}
		}
		div class=example {
			p {
				- "CDATA sections can only be used in foreign content (MathML or SVG). In this example, a CDATA section is used to escape the contents of a "
				a data-x-internal=mathml-ms href="https://w3c.github.io/mathml-core/#string-literal-ms" id=cdata-sections:mathml-ms {
					- "MathML "
					code ms
				}
				- " element:"
			}
			pre {
				code class=html {
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" p
					c- p="" >
					- "You can add a string to a number, but this stringifies the number:"
					c- p="" "</"
					c- f="" p
					c- p="" >
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" math
					c- p="" >
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" ms
					c- p="" >
					c- cp="" "<![CDATA[x<y]]>"
					c- p="" "</"
					c- f="" ms
					c- p="" >
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" mo
					c- p="" >
					- +
					c- p="" "</"
					c- f="" mo
					c- p="" >
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" mn
					c- p="" >
					- "3"
					c- p="" "</"
					c- f="" mn
					c- p="" >
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" mo
					c- p="" >
					- "="
					c- p="" "</"
					c- f="" mo
					c- p="" >
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" ms
					c- p="" >
					c- cp="" "<![CDATA[x<y3]]>"
					c- p="" "</"
					c- f="" ms
					c- p="" >
					c- p="" "</"
					c- f="" math
					c- p="" >
				}
			}
		}
		h4 id=comments {
			span class=secno "13.1.6"
			- " Comments"
			a class=self-link href="#comments"
		}
		p {
			dfn id=syntax-comments Comments
			- " must have the following format:"
		}
		ol {
			li {
				- "The string \""
				code <!--
				- "\"."
			}
			li {
				- "Optionally, "
				a href="#syntax-text" id=comments:syntax-text text
				- ", with the additional restriction that the text must not start with the string \""
				code >
				- "\", nor start with the string \""
				code ->
				- "\", nor contain the strings \""
				code <!--
				- "\", \""
				code -->
				- "\", or \""
				code --!>
				- "\", nor end with the string \""
				code <!-
				- "\"."
			}
			li {
				- "The string \""
				code -->
				- "\"."
			}
		}
		p class=note {
			- "The "
			a href="#syntax-text" id=comments:syntax-text-2 text
			- " is allowed to end with the string \""
			code <!
			- "\", as in "
			code "<!--My favorite operators are > and <!-->"
			- .
		}
		h3 id=parsing {
			span class=secno "13.2"
			- " Parsing HTML documents"
			a class=self-link href="#parsing"
		}
		p {
			i "This section only applies to user agents, data mining tools, and conformance checkers."
		}
		p class=note {
			- "The rules for parsing XML documents into DOM trees are covered by the next section, entitled \""
			a href="#the-xhtml-syntax" id=parsing:the-xhtml-syntax "The XML syntax"
			- "\"."
		}
		p {
			- "User agents must use the parsing rules described in this section to generate the DOM trees from "
			code id="parsing:text/html" {
				a href="#text/html" "text/html"
			}
			- " resources. Together, these rules define what is referred to as the "
			dfn data-export="" id=html-parser "HTML parser"
			- .
		}
		div class=note {
			p "While the HTML syntax described in this specification bears a close resemblance to SGML and XML, it is a separate language with its own parsing rules."
			p "Some earlier versions of HTML (in particular from HTML2 to HTML4) were based on SGML and used SGML parsing rules. However, few (if any) web browsers ever implemented true SGML parsing for HTML documents; the only user agents to strictly handle HTML as an SGML application have historically been validators. The resulting confusion — with validators claiming documents to have one representation while widely deployed web browsers interoperably implemented a different representation — has wasted decades of productivity. This version of HTML thus returns to a non-SGML basis."
			p "Authors interested in using SGML tools in their authoring pipeline are encouraged to use XML tools and the XML serialization of HTML."
		}
		p {
			- "For the purposes of conformance checkers, if a resource is determined to be in "
			a href="#syntax" id=parsing:syntax "the HTML syntax"
			- ", then it is an "
			a data-x-internal=html-documents href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#html-document" id=parsing:html-documents "HTML document"
			- .
		}
		p class=note {
			- "As stated "
			a href="#html-elements" id=parsing:html-elements "in the terminology section"
			- ", references to "
			a href="#element-type" id=parsing:element-type "element types"
			- " that do not explicitly specify a namespace always refer to elements in the "
			a data-x-internal=html-namespace-2 href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#html-namespace" id=parsing:html-namespace-2 "HTML namespace"
			- ". For example, if the spec talks about \"a "
			code id=parsing:the-menu-element {
				a href="#the-menu-element" menu
			}
			- " element\", then that is an element with the local name \""
			code menu
			- "\", the namespace \""
			code "http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"
			- "\", and the interface "
			code id=parsing:htmlmenuelement {
				a href="#htmlmenuelement" HTMLMenuElement
			}
			- ". Where possible, references to such elements are hyperlinked to their definition."
		}
		h4 id=overview-of-the-parsing-model {
			span class=secno "13.2.1"
			- " Overview of the parsing model"
			a class=self-link href="#overview-of-the-parsing-model"
		}
		p class=overview {
			img alt="" class=darkmode-aware height="535" src="/images/parsing-model-overview.svg" width="345"
		}
		p {
			- "The input to the HTML parsing process consists of a stream of "
			a data-x-internal=code-point href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#code-point" id=overview-of-the-parsing-model:code-point "code points"
			- ", which is passed through a "
			a href="#tokenization" id=overview-of-the-parsing-model:tokenization tokenization
			- " stage followed by a "
			a href="#tree-construction" id=overview-of-the-parsing-model:tree-construction "tree construction"
			- " stage. The output is a "
			code id=overview-of-the-parsing-model:document {
				a href="#document" Document
			}
			- " object."
		}
		p class=note {
			- "Implementations that "
			a href="#non-scripted" "do not support scripting"
			- " do not have to actually create a DOM "
			code id=overview-of-the-parsing-model:document-2 {
				a href="#document" Document
			}
			- " object, but the DOM tree in such cases is still used as the model for the rest of the specification."
		}
		p {
			- "In the common case, the data handled by the tokenization stage comes from the network, but "
			a href="#dynamic-markup-insertion" id=overview-of-the-parsing-model:dynamic-markup-insertion "it can also come from script"
			- " running in the user agent, e.g. using the "
			code id=overview-of-the-parsing-model:dom-document-write {
				a href="#dom-document-write" "document.write()"
			}
			- " API."
		}
		p id=nestedParsing "There is only one set of states for the tokenizer stage and the tree construction stage, but the tree construction stage is reentrant, meaning that while the tree construction stage is handling one token, the tokenizer might be resumed, causing further tokens to be emitted and processed before the first token's processing is complete."
		div class=example {
			p "In the following example, the tree construction stage will be called upon to handle a \"p\" start tag token while handling the \"script\" end tag token:"
			pre {
				code class=html {
					- "... "
					c- p="" <
					c- f="" script
					c- p="" >
					- " document"
					c- p="" .
					- write
					c- p="" "("
					c- t="" '<p>'
					c- p="" ");"
					c- p="" "</"
					c- f="" script
					c- p="" >
					- " ..."
				}
			}
		}
		p {
			- "To handle these cases, parsers have a "
			dfn id=script-nesting-level "script nesting level"
			- ", which must be initially set to zero, and a "
			dfn id=parser-pause-flag "parser pause flag"
			- ", which must be initially set to false."
		}
		h4 id=parse-errors {
			span class=secno "13.2.2"
			dfn "Parse errors"
			a class=self-link href="#parse-errors"
		}
		p {
			- "This specification defines the parsing rules for HTML documents, whether they are syntactically correct or not. Certain points in the parsing algorithm are said to be "
			a href="#parse-errors" id=parse-errors:parse-errors "parse errors"
			- ". The error handling for parse errors is well-defined (that's the processing rules described throughout this specification), but user agents, while parsing an HTML document, may "
			a href="#abort-a-parser" id=parse-errors:abort-a-parser "abort the parser"
			- " at the first "
			a href="#parse-errors" id=parse-errors:parse-errors-2 "parse error"
			- " that they encounter for which they do not wish to apply the rules described in this specification."
		}
		p "Conformance checkers must report at least one parse error condition to the user if one or more parse error conditions exist in the document and must not report parse error conditions if none exist in the document. Conformance checkers may report more than one parse error condition if more than one parse error condition exists in the document."
		p class=note {
			- "Parse errors are only errors with the "
			em syntax
			- " of HTML. In addition to checking for parse errors, conformance checkers will also verify that the document obeys all the other conformance requirements described in this specification."
		}
		p "Some parse errors have dedicated codes outlined in the table below that should be used by conformance checkers in reports."
		p {
			i "Error descriptions in the table below are non-normative."
		}
		table class=parse-error-table {
			thead {
				tr {
					th "Code "
					th "Description "
				}
			}
			tbody {
				tr {
					td {
						dfn id=parse-error-abrupt-closing-of-empty-comment abrupt-closing-of-empty-comment
					}
					td {
						p {
							- "This error occurs if the parser encounters an empty "
							a href="#syntax-comments" id=parse-errors:syntax-comments comment
							- " that is abruptly closed by a U+003E (>) "
							a data-x-internal=code-point href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#code-point" id=parse-errors:code-point "code point"
							- " (i.e., "
							code <!-->
							- " or "
							code <!--->
							- "). The parser behaves as if the comment is closed correctly."
						}
					}
				}
				tr {
					td {
						dfn id=parse-error-abrupt-doctype-public-identifier abrupt-doctype-public-identifier
					}
					td {
						p {
							- "This error occurs if the parser encounters a U+003E (>) "
							a data-x-internal=code-point href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#code-point" id=parse-errors:code-point-2 "code point"
							- " in the "
							a href="#syntax-doctype" id=parse-errors:syntax-doctype DOCTYPE
							- " public identifier (e.g., "
							code "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"foo>"
							- "). In such a case, if the DOCTYPE is correctly placed as a document preamble, the parser sets the "
							code id=parse-errors:document {
								a href="#document" Document
							}
							- " to "
							a data-x-internal=quirks-mode href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-document-quirks" id=parse-errors:quirks-mode "quirks mode"
							- .
						}
					}
				}
				tr {
					td {
						dfn id=parse-error-abrupt-doctype-system-identifier abrupt-doctype-system-identifier
					}
					td {
						p {
							- "This error occurs if the parser encounters a U+003E (>) "
							a data-x-internal=code-point href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#code-point" id=parse-errors:code-point-3 "code point"
							- " in the "
							a href="#syntax-doctype" id=parse-errors:syntax-doctype-2 DOCTYPE
							- " system identifier (e.g., "
							code "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01//EN\" \"foo>"
							- "). In such a case, if the DOCTYPE is correctly placed as a document preamble, the parser sets the "
							code id=parse-errors:document-2 {
								a href="#document" Document
							}
							- " to "
							a data-x-internal=quirks-mode href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-document-quirks" id=parse-errors:quirks-mode-2 "quirks mode"
							- .
						}
					}
				}
				tr {
					td {
						dfn id=parse-error-absence-of-digits-in-numeric-character-reference absence-of-digits-in-numeric-character-reference
					}
					td {
						p {
							- "This error occurs if the parser encounters a numeric "
							a href="#syntax-charref" id=parse-errors:syntax-charref "character reference"
							- " that doesn't contain any digits (e.g., "
							code "&#qux;"
							- "). In this case the parser doesn't resolve the character reference."
						}
					}
				}
				tr {
					td {
						dfn id=parse-error-cdata-in-html-content cdata-in-html-content
					}
					td {
						p {
							- "This error occurs if the parser encounters a "
							a href="#syntax-cdata" id=parse-errors:syntax-cdata "CDATA section"
							- " outside of foreign content (SVG or MathML). The parser treats such CDATA sections (including leading \""
							code "[CDATA["
							- "\" and trailing \""
							code "]]"
							- "\" strings) as comments."
						}
					}
				}
				tr {
					td {
						dfn id=parse-error-character-reference-outside-unicode-range character-reference-outside-unicode-range
					}
					td {
						p {
							- "This error occurs if the parser encounters a numeric "
							a href="#syntax-charref" id=parse-errors:syntax-charref-2 "character reference"
							- " that references a "
							a data-x-internal=code-point href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#code-point" id=parse-errors:code-point-4 "code point"
							- " that is greater than the valid Unicode range. The parser resolves such a character reference to a U+FFFD REPLACEMENT CHARACTER."
						}
					}
				}
				tr {
					td {
						dfn id=parse-error-control-character-in-input-stream control-character-in-input-stream
					}
					td {
						p {
							- "This error occurs if the "
							a href="#input-stream" id=parse-errors:input-stream "input stream"
							- " contains a "
							a data-x-internal=control href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#control" id=parse-errors:control control
							a data-x-internal=code-point href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#code-point" id=parse-errors:code-point-5 "code point"
							- " that is not "
							a data-x-internal=space-characters href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ascii-whitespace" id=parse-errors:space-characters "ASCII whitespace"
							- " or U+0000 NULL. Such code points are parsed as-is and usually, where parsing rules don't apply any additional restrictions, make their way into the DOM."
						}
					}
				}
				tr {
					td {
						dfn id=parse-error-control-character-reference control-character-reference
					}
					td {
						p {
							- "This error occurs if the parser encounters a numeric "
							a href="#syntax-charref" id=parse-errors:syntax-charref-3 "character reference"
							- " that references a "
							a data-x-internal=control href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#control" id=parse-errors:control-2 control
							a data-x-internal=code-point href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#code-point" id=parse-errors:code-point-6 "code point"
							- " that is not "
							a data-x-internal=space-characters href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ascii-whitespace" id=parse-errors:space-characters-2 "ASCII whitespace"
							- " or is a U+000D CARRIAGE RETURN. The parser resolves such character references as-is except C1 control references that are replaced according to the "
							a href="#numeric-character-reference-end-state" id=parse-errors:numeric-character-reference-end-state "numeric character reference end state"
							- .
						}
					}
				}
				tr {
					td {
						dfn id=parse-error-duplicate-attribute duplicate-attribute
					}
					td {
						p {
							- "This error occurs if the parser encounters an "
							a href="#syntax-attributes" id=parse-errors:syntax-attributes attribute
							- " in a tag that already has an attribute with the same name. The parser ignores all such duplicate occurrences of the attribute. "
						}
					}
				}
				tr {
					td {
						dfn id=parse-error-end-tag-with-attributes end-tag-with-attributes
					}
					td {
						p {
							- "This error occurs if the parser encounters an "
							a href="#syntax-end-tag" id=parse-errors:syntax-end-tag "end tag"
							- " with "
							a href="#syntax-attributes" id=parse-errors:syntax-attributes-2 attributes
							- ". Attributes in end tags are ignored and do not make their way into the DOM."
						}
					}
				}
				tr {
					td {
						dfn id=parse-error-end-tag-with-trailing-solidus end-tag-with-trailing-solidus
					}
					td {
						p {
							- "This error occurs if the parser encounters an "
							a href="#syntax-end-tag" id=parse-errors:syntax-end-tag-2 "end tag"
							- " that has a U+002F (/) "
							a data-x-internal=code-point href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#code-point" id=parse-errors:code-point-7 "code point"
							- " right before the closing U+003E (>) code point (e.g., "
							code "</div/>"
							- "). Such a tag is treated as a regular end tag."
						}
					}
				}
				tr {
					td {
						dfn id=parse-error-eof-before-tag-name eof-before-tag-name
					}
					td {
						p {
							- "This error occurs if the parser encounters the end of the "
							a href="#input-stream" id=parse-errors:input-stream-2 "input stream"
							- " where a tag name is expected. In this case the parser treats the beginning of a "
							a href="#syntax-start-tag" id=parse-errors:syntax-start-tag "start tag"
							- " (i.e., "
							code <
							- ") or an "
							a href="#syntax-end-tag" id=parse-errors:syntax-end-tag-3 "end tag"
							- " (i.e., "
							code "</"
							- ") as text content."
						}
					}
				}
				tr {
					td {
						dfn id=parse-error-eof-in-cdata eof-in-cdata
					}
					td {
						p {
							- "This error occurs if the parser encounters the end of the "
							a href="#input-stream" id=parse-errors:input-stream-3 "input stream"
							- " in a "
							a href="#syntax-cdata" id=parse-errors:syntax-cdata-2 "CDATA section"
							- ". The parser treats such CDATA sections as if they are closed immediately before the end of the input stream."
						}
					}
				}
				tr {
					td {
						dfn id=parse-error-eof-in-comment eof-in-comment
					}
					td {
						p {
							- "This error occurs if the parser encounters the end of the "
							a href="#input-stream" id=parse-errors:input-stream-4 "input stream"
							- " in a "
							a href="#syntax-comments" id=parse-errors:syntax-comments-2 comment
							- ". The parser treats such comments as if they are closed immediately before the end of the input stream."
						}
					}
				}
				tr {
					td {
						dfn id=parse-error-eof-in-doctype eof-in-doctype
					}
					td {
						p {
							- "This error occurs if the parser encounters the end of the input stream in a "
							a href="#syntax-doctype" id=parse-errors:syntax-doctype-3 DOCTYPE
							- ". In such a case, if the DOCTYPE is correctly placed as a document preamble, the parser sets the "
							code id=parse-errors:document-3 {
								a href="#document" Document
							}
							- " to "
							a data-x-internal=quirks-mode href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-document-quirks" id=parse-errors:quirks-mode-3 "quirks mode"
							- .
						}
					}
				}
				tr {
					td {
						dfn id=parse-error-eof-in-script-html-comment-like-text eof-in-script-html-comment-like-text
					}
					td {
						p {
							- "This error occurs if the parser encounters the end of the "
							a href="#input-stream" id=parse-errors:input-stream-5 "input stream"
							- " in text that resembles an "
							a href="#syntax-comments" id=parse-errors:syntax-comments-3 "HTML comment"
							- " inside "
							code id=parse-errors:the-script-element {
								a href="#the-script-element" script
							}
							- " element content (e.g., "
							code "<script><!-- foo"
							- ")."
						}
						p class=note {
							- "Syntactic structures that resemble HTML comments in "
							code id=parse-errors:the-script-element-2 {
								a href="#the-script-element" script
							}
							- " elements are parsed as text content. They can be a part of a scripting language-specific syntactic structure or be treated as an HTML-like comment, if the scripting language supports them (e.g., parsing rules for HTML-like comments can be found in Annex B of the JavaScript specification). The common reason for this error is a violation of the "
							a href="#restrictions-for-contents-of-script-elements" id=parse-errors:restrictions-for-contents-of-script-elements {
								- "restrictions for contents of "
								code script
								- " elements"
							}
							- ". "
							a href="#refsJAVASCRIPT" "[JAVASCRIPT]"
						}
					}
				}
				tr {
					td {
						dfn id=parse-error-eof-in-tag eof-in-tag
					}
					td {
						p {
							- "This error occurs if the parser encounters the end of the "
							a href="#input-stream" id=parse-errors:input-stream-6 "input stream"
							- " in a "
							a href="#syntax-start-tag" id=parse-errors:syntax-start-tag-2 "start tag"
							- " or an "
							a href="#syntax-end-tag" id=parse-errors:syntax-end-tag-4 "end tag"
							- " (e.g., "
							code "<div id="
							- "). Such a tag is ignored."
						}
					}
				}
				tr {
					td {
						dfn id=parse-error-incorrectly-closed-comment incorrectly-closed-comment
					}
					td {
						p {
							- "This error occurs if the parser encounters a "
							a href="#syntax-comments" id=parse-errors:syntax-comments-4 comment
							- " that is closed by the \""
							code --!>
							- "\" "
							a data-x-internal=code-point href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#code-point" id=parse-errors:code-point-8 "code point"
							- " sequence. The parser treats such comments as if they are correctly closed by the \""
							code -->
							- "\" code point sequence."
						}
					}
				}
				tr {
					td {
						dfn id=parse-error-incorrectly-opened-comment incorrectly-opened-comment
					}
					td {
						p {
							- "This error occurs if the parser encounters the \""
							code <!
							- "\" "
							a data-x-internal=code-point href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#code-point" id=parse-errors:code-point-9 "code point"
							- " sequence that is not immediately followed by two U+002D (-) code points and that is not the start of a "
							a href="#syntax-doctype" id=parse-errors:syntax-doctype-4 DOCTYPE
							- " or a "
							a href="#syntax-cdata" id=parse-errors:syntax-cdata-3 "CDATA section"
							- ". All content that follows the \""
							code <!
							- "\" code point sequence up to a U+003E (>) code point (if present) or to the end of the "
							a href="#input-stream" id=parse-errors:input-stream-7 "input stream"
							- " is treated as a comment."
						}
						p class=note {
							- "One possible cause of this error is using an XML markup declaration (e.g., "
							code "<!ELEMENT br EMPTY>"
							- ") in HTML."
						}
					}
				}
				tr {
					td {
						dfn id=parse-error-invalid-character-sequence-after-doctype-name invalid-character-sequence-after-doctype-name
					}
					td {
						p {
							- "This error occurs if the parser encounters any "
							a data-x-internal=code-point href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#code-point" id=parse-errors:code-point-10 "code point"
							- " sequence other than \""
							code PUBLIC
							- "\" and \""
							code SYSTEM
							- "\" keywords after a "
							a href="#syntax-doctype" id=parse-errors:syntax-doctype-5 DOCTYPE
							- " name. In such a case, the parser ignores any following public or system identifiers, and if the DOCTYPE is correctly placed as a document preamble, and if the "
							a href="#parser-cannot-change-the-mode-flag" id=parse-errors:parser-cannot-change-the-mode-flag "parser cannot change the mode flag"
							- " is false, sets the "
							code id=parse-errors:document-4 {
								a href="#document" Document
							}
							- " to "
							a data-x-internal=quirks-mode href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-document-quirks" id=parse-errors:quirks-mode-4 "quirks mode"
							- .
						}
					}
				}
				tr {
					td {
						dfn id=parse-error-invalid-first-character-of-tag-name invalid-first-character-of-tag-name
					}
					td {
						p {
							- "This error occurs if the parser encounters a "
							a data-x-internal=code-point href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#code-point" id=parse-errors:code-point-11 "code point"
							- " that is not an "
							a data-x-internal=ascii-letters href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ascii-alpha" id=parse-errors:ascii-letters "ASCII alpha"
							- " where first code point of a "
							a href="#syntax-start-tag" id=parse-errors:syntax-start-tag-3 "start tag"
							- " name or an "
							a href="#syntax-end-tag" id=parse-errors:syntax-end-tag-5 "end tag"
							- " name is expected. If a start tag was expected such code point and a preceding U+003C (<) is treated as text content, and all content that follows is treated as markup. Whereas, if an end tag was expected, such code point and all content that follows up to a U+003E (>) code point (if present) or to the end of the "
							a href="#input-stream" id=parse-errors:input-stream-8 "input stream"
							- " is treated as a comment."
						}
						div class=example {
							p "For example, consider the following markup:"
							pre {
								code class=html {
									c- p="" <
									c- f="" "42"
									c- p="" "></"
									c- f="" "42"
									c- p="" >
								}
							}
							p "This will be parsed into:"
							ul class=domTree {
								li class=t1 {
									code id=parse-errors:the-html-element {
										a href="#the-html-element" html
									}
									ul {
										li class=t1 {
											code id=parse-errors:the-head-element {
												a href="#the-head-element" head
											}
										}
										li class=t1 {
											code id=parse-errors:the-body-element {
												a href="#the-body-element" body
											}
											ul {
												li class=t3 {
													code id=parse-errors:text {
														a data-x-internal=text href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#interface-text" "#text"
													}
													- ": "
													span <42>
												}
												li class=t8 {
													code id=parse-errors:comment-2 {
														a data-x-internal=comment-2 href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#interface-comment" "#comment"
													}
													- ": "
													span "42"
												}
											}
										}
									}
								}
							}
						}
						p class=note {
							- "While the first code point of a tag name is limited to an "
							a data-x-internal=ascii-letters href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ascii-alpha" id=parse-errors:ascii-letters-2 "ASCII alpha"
							- ", a wide range of code points (including "
							a data-x-internal=ascii-digits href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ascii-digit" id=parse-errors:ascii-digits "ASCII digits"
							- ") is allowed in subsequent positions."
						}
					}
				}
				tr {
					td {
						dfn id=parse-error-missing-attribute-value missing-attribute-value
					}
					td {
						p {
							- "This error occurs if the parser encounters a U+003E (>) "
							a data-x-internal=code-point href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#code-point" id=parse-errors:code-point-12 "code point"
							- " where an "
							a href="#syntax-attributes" id=parse-errors:syntax-attributes-3 attribute
							- " value is expected (e.g., "
							code "<div id=>"
							- "). The parser treats the attribute as having an empty value."
						}
					}
				}
				tr {
					td {
						dfn id=parse-error-missing-doctype-name missing-doctype-name
					}
					td {
						p {
							- "This error occurs if the parser encounters a "
							a href="#syntax-doctype" id=parse-errors:syntax-doctype-6 DOCTYPE
							- " that is missing a name (e.g., "
							code <!DOCTYPE>
							- "). In such a case, if the DOCTYPE is correctly placed as a document preamble, the parser sets the "
							code id=parse-errors:document-5 {
								a href="#document" Document
							}
							- " to "
							a data-x-internal=quirks-mode href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-document-quirks" id=parse-errors:quirks-mode-5 "quirks mode"
							- .
						}
					}
				}
				tr {
					td {
						dfn id=parse-error-missing-doctype-public-identifier missing-doctype-public-identifier
					}
					td {
						p {
							- "This error occurs if the parser encounters a U+003E (>) "
							a data-x-internal=code-point href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#code-point" id=parse-errors:code-point-13 "code point"
							- " where start of the "
							a href="#syntax-doctype" id=parse-errors:syntax-doctype-7 DOCTYPE
							- " public identifier is expected (e.g., "
							code "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC >"
							- "). In such a case, if the DOCTYPE is correctly placed as a document preamble, the parser sets the "
							code id=parse-errors:document-6 {
								a href="#document" Document
							}
							- " to "
							a data-x-internal=quirks-mode href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-document-quirks" id=parse-errors:quirks-mode-6 "quirks mode"
							- .
						}
					}
				}
				tr {
					td {
						dfn id=parse-error-missing-doctype-system-identifier missing-doctype-system-identifier
					}
					td {
						p {
							- "This error occurs if the parser encounters a U+003E (>) "
							a data-x-internal=code-point href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#code-point" id=parse-errors:code-point-14 "code point"
							- " where start of the "
							a href="#syntax-doctype" id=parse-errors:syntax-doctype-8 DOCTYPE
							- " system identifier is expected (e.g., "
							code "<!DOCTYPE html SYSTEM >"
							- "). In such a case, if the DOCTYPE is correctly placed as a document preamble, the parser sets the "
							code id=parse-errors:document-7 {
								a href="#document" Document
							}
							- " to "
							a data-x-internal=quirks-mode href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-document-quirks" id=parse-errors:quirks-mode-7 "quirks mode"
							- .
						}
					}
				}
				tr {
					td {
						dfn id=parse-error-missing-end-tag-name missing-end-tag-name
					}
					td {
						p {
							- "This error occurs if the parser encounters a U+003E (>) "
							a data-x-internal=code-point href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#code-point" id=parse-errors:code-point-15 "code point"
							- " where an "
							a href="#syntax-end-tag" id=parse-errors:syntax-end-tag-6 "end tag"
							- " name is expected, i.e., "
							code "</>"
							- ". The parser ignores the whole \""
							code "</>"
							- "\" code point sequence."
						}
					}
				}
				tr {
					td {
						dfn id=parse-error-missing-quote-before-doctype-public-identifier missing-quote-before-doctype-public-identifier
					}
					td {
						p {
							- "This error occurs if the parser encounters the "
							a href="#syntax-doctype" id=parse-errors:syntax-doctype-9 DOCTYPE
							- " public identifier that is not preceded by a quote (e.g., "
							code "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC -//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01//EN\">"
							- "). In such a case, the parser ignores the public identifier, and if the DOCTYPE is correctly placed as a document preamble, sets the "
							code id=parse-errors:document-8 {
								a href="#document" Document
							}
							- " to "
							a data-x-internal=quirks-mode href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-document-quirks" id=parse-errors:quirks-mode-8 "quirks mode"
							- .
						}
					}
				}
				tr {
					td {
						dfn id=parse-error-missing-quote-before-doctype-system-identifier missing-quote-before-doctype-system-identifier
					}
					td {
						p {
							- "This error occurs if the parser encounters the "
							a href="#syntax-doctype" id=parse-errors:syntax-doctype-10 DOCTYPE
							- " system identifier that is not preceded by a quote (e.g., "
							code "<!DOCTYPE html SYSTEM http://www.w3.org/TR/xhtml1/DTD/xhtml1-transitional.dtd\">"
							- "). In such a case, the parser ignores the system identifier, and if the DOCTYPE is correctly placed as a document preamble, sets the "
							code id=parse-errors:document-9 {
								a href="#document" Document
							}
							- " to "
							a data-x-internal=quirks-mode href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-document-quirks" id=parse-errors:quirks-mode-9 "quirks mode"
							- .
						}
					}
				}
				tr {
					td {
						dfn id=parse-error-missing-semicolon-after-character-reference missing-semicolon-after-character-reference
					}
					td {
						p {
							- "This error occurs if the parser encounters a "
							a href="#syntax-charref" id=parse-errors:syntax-charref-4 "character reference"
							- " that is not terminated by a U+003B (;) "
							a data-x-internal=code-point href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#code-point" id=parse-errors:code-point-16 "code point"
							- ". Usually the parser behaves as if character reference is terminated by the U+003B (;) code point; however, there are some ambiguous cases in which the parser includes subsequent code points in the character reference."
						}
						p class=example {
							- "For example, "
							code "&not;in"
							- " will be parsed as \""
							code ¬in
							- "\" whereas "
							code &notin
							- " will be parsed as \""
							code ∉
							- "\"."
						}
					}
				}
				tr {
					td {
						dfn id=parse-error-missing-whitespace-after-doctype-public-keyword missing-whitespace-after-doctype-public-keyword
					}
					td {
						p {
							- "This error occurs if the parser encounters a "
							a href="#syntax-doctype" id=parse-errors:syntax-doctype-11 DOCTYPE
							- " whose \""
							code PUBLIC
							- "\" keyword and public identifier are not separated by "
							a data-x-internal=space-characters href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ascii-whitespace" id=parse-errors:space-characters-3 "ASCII whitespace"
							- ". In this case the parser behaves as if ASCII whitespace is present."
						}
					}
				}
				tr {
					td {
						dfn id=parse-error-missing-whitespace-after-doctype-system-keyword missing-whitespace-after-doctype-system-keyword
					}
					td {
						p {
							- "This error occurs if the parser encounters a "
							a href="#syntax-doctype" id=parse-errors:syntax-doctype-12 DOCTYPE
							- " whose \""
							code SYSTEM
							- "\" keyword and system identifier are not separated by "
							a data-x-internal=space-characters href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ascii-whitespace" id=parse-errors:space-characters-4 "ASCII whitespace"
							- ". In this case the parser behaves as if ASCII whitespace is present."
						}
					}
				}
				tr {
					td {
						dfn id=parse-error-missing-whitespace-before-doctype-name missing-whitespace-before-doctype-name
					}
					td {
						p {
							- "This error occurs if the parser encounters a "
							a href="#syntax-doctype" id=parse-errors:syntax-doctype-13 DOCTYPE
							- " whose \""
							code DOCTYPE
							- "\" keyword and name are not separated by "
							a data-x-internal=space-characters href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ascii-whitespace" id=parse-errors:space-characters-5 "ASCII whitespace"
							- ". In this case the parser behaves as if ASCII whitespace is present."
						}
					}
				}
				tr {
					td {
						dfn id=parse-error-missing-whitespace-between-attributes missing-whitespace-between-attributes
					}
					td {
						p {
							- "This error occurs if the parser encounters "
							a href="#syntax-attributes" id=parse-errors:syntax-attributes-4 attributes
							- " that are not separated by "
							a data-x-internal=space-characters href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ascii-whitespace" id=parse-errors:space-characters-6 "ASCII whitespace"
							- " (e.g., "
							code "<div id=\"foo\"class=\"bar\">"
							- "). In this case the parser behaves as if ASCII whitespace is present."
						}
					}
				}
				tr {
					td {
						dfn id=parse-error-missing-whitespace-between-doctype-public-and-system-identifiers missing-whitespace-between-doctype-public-and-system-identifiers
					}
					td {
						p {
							- "This error occurs if the parser encounters a "
							a href="#syntax-doctype" id=parse-errors:syntax-doctype-14 DOCTYPE
							- " whose public and system identifiers are not separated by "
							a data-x-internal=space-characters href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ascii-whitespace" id=parse-errors:space-characters-7 "ASCII whitespace"
							- ". In this case the parser behaves as if ASCII whitespace is present."
						}
					}
				}
				tr {
					td {
						dfn id=parse-error-nested-comment nested-comment
					}
					td {
						p {
							- "This error occurs if the parser encounters a nested "
							a href="#syntax-comments" id=parse-errors:syntax-comments-5 comment
							- " (e.g., "
							code "<!-- <!-- nested --> -->"
							- "). Such a comment will be closed by the first occurring \""
							code -->
							- "\" "
							a data-x-internal=code-point href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#code-point" id=parse-errors:code-point-17 "code point"
							- " sequence and everything that follows will be treated as markup."
						}
					}
				}
				tr {
					td {
						dfn id=parse-error-noncharacter-character-reference noncharacter-character-reference
					}
					td {
						p {
							- "This error occurs if the parser encounters a numeric "
							a href="#syntax-charref" id=parse-errors:syntax-charref-5 "character reference"
							- " that references a "
							a data-x-internal=noncharacter href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#noncharacter" id=parse-errors:noncharacter noncharacter
							- ". The parser resolves such character references as-is."
						}
					}
				}
				tr {
					td {
						dfn id=parse-error-noncharacter-in-input-stream noncharacter-in-input-stream
					}
					td {
						p {
							- "This error occurs if the "
							a href="#input-stream" id=parse-errors:input-stream-9 "input stream"
							- " contains a "
							a data-x-internal=noncharacter href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#noncharacter" id=parse-errors:noncharacter-2 noncharacter
							- ". Such "
							a data-x-internal=code-point href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#code-point" id=parse-errors:code-point-18 "code points"
							- " are parsed as-is and usually, where parsing rules don't apply any additional restrictions, make their way into the DOM."
						}
					}
				}
				tr {
					td {
						dfn id=parse-error-non-void-html-element-start-tag-with-trailing-solidus non-void-html-element-start-tag-with-trailing-solidus
					}
					td {
						p {
							- "This error occurs if the parser encounters a "
							a href="#syntax-start-tag" id=parse-errors:syntax-start-tag-4 "start tag"
							- " for an element that is not in the list of "
							a href="#void-elements" id=parse-errors:void-elements "void elements"
							- " or is not a part of foreign content (i.e., not an SVG or MathML element) that has a U+002F (/) "
							a data-x-internal=code-point href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#code-point" id=parse-errors:code-point-19 "code point"
							- " right before the closing U+003E (>) code point. The parser behaves as if the U+002F (/) is not present."
						}
						div class=example {
							p "For example, consider the following markup:"
							pre {
								code class=html {
									c- p="" <
									c- f="" div
									c- p="" "/><"
									c- f="" span
									c- p="" "></"
									c- f="" span
									c- p="" ><
									c- f="" span
									c- p="" "></"
									c- f="" span
									c- p="" >
								}
							}
							p "This will be parsed into:"
							ul class=domTree {
								li class=t1 {
									code id=parse-errors:the-html-element-2 {
										a href="#the-html-element" html
									}
									ul {
										li class=t1 {
											code id=parse-errors:the-head-element-2 {
												a href="#the-head-element" head
											}
										}
										li class=t1 {
											code id=parse-errors:the-body-element-2 {
												a href="#the-body-element" body
											}
											ul {
												li class=t1 {
													code id=parse-errors:the-div-element {
														a href="#the-div-element" div
													}
													ul {
														li class=t1 {
															code id=parse-errors:the-span-element {
																a href="#the-span-element" span
															}
														}
														li class=t1 {
															code id=parse-errors:the-span-element-2 {
																a href="#the-span-element" span
															}
														}
													}
												}
											}
										}
									}
								}
							}
						}
						p class=note "The trailing U+002F (/) in a start tag name can be used only in foreign content to specify self-closing tags. (Self-closing tags don't exist in HTML.) It is also allowed for void elements, but doesn't have any effect in this case."
					}
				}
				tr {
					td {
						dfn id=parse-error-null-character-reference null-character-reference
					}
					td {
						p {
							- "This error occurs if the parser encounters a numeric "
							a href="#syntax-charref" id=parse-errors:syntax-charref-6 "character reference"
							- " that references a U+0000 NULL "
							a data-x-internal=code-point href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#code-point" id=parse-errors:code-point-20 "code point"
							- ". The parser resolves such character references to a U+FFFD REPLACEMENT CHARACTER."
						}
					}
				}
				tr {
					td {
						dfn id=parse-error-surrogate-character-reference surrogate-character-reference
					}
					td {
						p {
							- "This error occurs if the parser encounters a numeric "
							a href="#syntax-charref" id=parse-errors:syntax-charref-7 "character reference"
							- " that references a "
							a data-x-internal=surrogate href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#surrogate" id=parse-errors:surrogate surrogate
							- ". The parser resolves such character references to a U+FFFD REPLACEMENT CHARACTER."
						}
					}
				}
				tr {
					td {
						dfn id=parse-error-surrogate-in-input-stream surrogate-in-input-stream
					}
					td {
						p {
							- "This error occurs if the "
							a href="#input-stream" id=parse-errors:input-stream-10 "input stream"
							- " contains a "
							a data-x-internal=surrogate href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#surrogate" id=parse-errors:surrogate-2 surrogate
							- ". Such "
							a data-x-internal=code-point href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#code-point" id=parse-errors:code-point-21 "code points"
							- " are parsed as-is and usually, where parsing rules don't apply any additional restrictions, make their way into the DOM."
						}
						p class=note {
							- "Surrogates can only find their way into the input stream via script APIs such as "
							code id=parse-errors:dom-document-write {
								a href="#dom-document-write" "document.write()"
							}
							- .
						}
					}
				}
				tr {
					td {
						dfn id=parse-error-unexpected-character-after-doctype-system-identifier unexpected-character-after-doctype-system-identifier
					}
					td {
						p {
							- "This error occurs if the parser encounters any "
							a data-x-internal=code-point href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#code-point" id=parse-errors:code-point-22 "code points"
							- " other than "
							a data-x-internal=space-characters href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ascii-whitespace" id=parse-errors:space-characters-8 "ASCII whitespace"
							- " or closing U+003E (>) after the "
							a href="#syntax-doctype" id=parse-errors:syntax-doctype-15 DOCTYPE
							- " system identifier. The parser ignores these code points."
						}
					}
				}
				tr {
					td {
						dfn id=parse-error-unexpected-character-in-attribute-name unexpected-character-in-attribute-name
					}
					td {
						p {
							- "This error occurs if the parser encounters a U+0022 (\"), U+0027 ('), or U+003C (<) "
							a data-x-internal=code-point href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#code-point" id=parse-errors:code-point-23 "code point"
							- " in an "
							a href="#syntax-attribute-name" id=parse-errors:syntax-attribute-name "attribute name"
							- ". The parser includes such code points in the attribute name."
						}
						p class=note "Code points that trigger this error are usually a part of another syntactic construct and can be a sign of a typo around the attribute name."
						div class=example {
							p "For example, consider the following markup:"
							pre {
								code class=html {
									c- p="" <
									c- f="" div
									c- e="" foo
									- <
									c- e="" div
									c- p="" >
								}
							}
							p {
								- "Due to a forgotten U+003E (>) code point after "
								code foo
								- " the parser treats this markup as a single "
								code id=parse-errors:the-div-element-2 {
									a href="#the-div-element" div
								}
								- " element with a \""
								code foo<div
								- "\" attribute."
							}
							p "As another example of this error, consider the following markup:"
							pre {
								code class=html {
									c- p="" <
									c- f="" div
									c- e="" id
									- '
									c- e="" bar
									- '
									c- p="" >
								}
							}
							p {
								- "Due to a forgotten U+003D (=) code point between an attribute name and value the parser treats this markup as a "
								code id=parse-errors:the-div-element-3 {
									a href="#the-div-element" div
								}
								- " element with the attribute \""
								code id'bar'
								- "\" that has an empty value."
							}
						}
					}
				}
				tr {
					td {
						dfn id=parse-error-unexpected-character-in-unquoted-attribute-value unexpected-character-in-unquoted-attribute-value
					}
					td {
						p {
							- "This error occurs if the parser encounters a U+0022 (\"), U+0027 ('), U+003C (<), U+003D (=), or U+0060 (`) "
							a data-x-internal=code-point href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#code-point" id=parse-errors:code-point-24 "code point"
							- " in an unquoted "
							a href="#syntax-attribute-value" id=parse-errors:syntax-attribute-value "attribute value"
							- ". The parser includes such code points in the attribute value."
						}
						p class=note "Code points that trigger this error are usually a part of another syntactic construct and can be a sign of a typo around the attribute value."
						p class=note "U+0060 (`) is in the list of code points that trigger this error because certain legacy user agents treat it as a quote."
						div class=example {
							p "For example, consider the following markup:"
							pre {
								code class=html {
									c- p="" <
									c- f="" div
									c- e="" foo
									c- o="" "="
									c- s="" b'ar'
									c- p="" >
								}
							}
							p {
								- "Due to a misplaced U+0027 (') code point the parser sets the value of the \""
								code foo
								- "\" attribute to \""
								code b'ar'
								- "\"."
							}
						}
					}
				}
				tr {
					td {
						dfn id=parse-error-unexpected-equals-sign-before-attribute-name unexpected-equals-sign-before-attribute-name
					}
					td {
						p {
							- "This error occurs if the parser encounters a U+003D (=) "
							a data-x-internal=code-point href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#code-point" id=parse-errors:code-point-25 "code point"
							- " before an attribute name. In this case the parser treats U+003D (=) as the first code point of the attribute name."
						}
						p class=note "The common reason for this error is a forgotten attribute name."
						div class=example {
							p "For example, consider the following markup:"
							pre {
								code class=html {
									c- p="" <
									c- f="" div
									c- e="" foo
									c- o="" "="
									c- s="" "\"bar\""
									- " =\""
									c- e="" baz
									- "\""
									c- p="" >
								}
							}
							p {
								- "Due to a forgotten attribute name the parser treats this markup as a "
								code id=parse-errors:the-div-element-4 {
									a href="#the-div-element" div
								}
								- " element with two attributes: a \""
								code foo
								- "\" attribute with a \""
								code bar
								- "\" value and a \""
								code "=\"baz\""
								- "\" attribute with an empty value."
							}
						}
					}
				}
				tr {
					td {
						dfn id=parse-error-unexpected-null-character unexpected-null-character
					}
					td {
						p {
							- "This error occurs if the parser encounters a U+0000 NULL "
							a data-x-internal=code-point href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#code-point" id=parse-errors:code-point-26 "code point"
							- " in the "
							a href="#input-stream" id=parse-errors:input-stream-11 "input stream"
							- " in certain positions. In general, such code points are either ignored or, for security reasons, replaced with a U+FFFD REPLACEMENT CHARACTER."
						}
					}
				}
				tr {
					td {
						dfn id=parse-error-unexpected-question-mark-instead-of-tag-name unexpected-question-mark-instead-of-tag-name
					}
					td {
						p {
							- "This error occurs if the parser encounters a U+003F (?) "
							a data-x-internal=code-point href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#code-point" id=parse-errors:code-point-27 "code point"
							- " where first code point of a "
							a href="#syntax-start-tag" id=parse-errors:syntax-start-tag-5 "start tag"
							- " name is expected. The U+003F (?) and all content that follows up to a U+003E (>) code point (if present) or to the end of the "
							a href="#input-stream" id=parse-errors:input-stream-12 "input stream"
							- " is treated as a comment."
						}
						div class=example {
							p "For example, consider the following markup:"
							pre {
								code class=html {
									c- cp="" "<?xml-stylesheet type=\"text/css\" href=\"style.css\"?>"
								}
							}
							p "This will be parsed into:"
							ul class=domTree {
								li class=t8 {
									code id=parse-errors:comment-2-2 {
										a data-x-internal=comment-2 href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#interface-comment" "#comment"
									}
									- ": "
									span "?xml-stylesheet type=\"text/css\" href=\"style.css\"?"
								}
								li class=t1 {
									code id=parse-errors:the-html-element-3 {
										a href="#the-html-element" html
									}
									ul {
										li class=t1 {
											code id=parse-errors:the-head-element-3 {
												a href="#the-head-element" head
											}
										}
										li class=t1 {
											code id=parse-errors:the-body-element-3 {
												a href="#the-body-element" body
											}
										}
									}
								}
							}
						}
						p class=note {
							- "The common reason for this error is an XML processing instruction (e.g., "
							code "<?xml-stylesheet type=\"text/css\" href=\"style.css\"?>"
							- ") or an XML declaration (e.g., "
							code "<?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?>"
							- ") being used in HTML."
						}
					}
				}
				tr {
					td {
						dfn id=parse-error-unexpected-solidus-in-tag unexpected-solidus-in-tag
					}
					td {
						p {
							- "This error occurs if the parser encounters a U+002F (/) "
							a data-x-internal=code-point href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#code-point" id=parse-errors:code-point-28 "code point"
							- " that is not a part of a quoted "
							a href="#syntax-attributes" id=parse-errors:syntax-attributes-5 attribute
							- " value and not immediately followed by a U+003E (>) code point in a tag (e.g., "
							code "<div / id=\"foo\">"
							- "). In this case the parser behaves as if it encountered "
							a data-x-internal=space-characters href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ascii-whitespace" id=parse-errors:space-characters-9 "ASCII whitespace"
							- .
						}
					}
				}
				tr {
					td {
						dfn id=parse-error-unknown-named-character-reference unknown-named-character-reference
					}
					td {
						p {
							- "This error occurs if the parser encounters an "
							a href="#syntax-ambiguous-ampersand" id=parse-errors:syntax-ambiguous-ampersand "ambiguous ampersand"
							- ". In this case the parser doesn't resolve the "
							a href="#syntax-charref" id=parse-errors:syntax-charref-8 "character reference"
							- .
						}
					}
				}
			}
		}
		h4 id=the-input-byte-stream {
			span class=secno "13.2.3"
			- " The "
			dfn "input byte stream"
			a class=self-link href="#the-input-byte-stream"
		}
		p {
			- "The stream of code points that comprises the input to the tokenization stage will be initially seen by the user agent as a stream of bytes (typically coming over the network or from the local file system). The bytes encode the actual characters according to a particular "
			i "character encoding"
			- ", which the user agent uses to decode the bytes into characters."
		}
		p class=note {
			- "For XML documents, the algorithm user agents are required to use to determine the character encoding is given by "
			cite XML
			- ". This section does not apply to XML documents. "
			a href="#refsXML" "[XML]"
		}
		p {
			- "Usually, the "
			a href="#encoding-sniffing-algorithm" id=the-input-byte-stream:encoding-sniffing-algorithm "encoding sniffing algorithm"
			- " defined below is used to determine the character encoding."
		}
		p {
			- "Given a character encoding, the bytes in the "
			a href="#the-input-byte-stream" id=the-input-byte-stream:the-input-byte-stream "input byte stream"
			- " must be converted to characters for the tokenizer's "
			a href="#input-stream" id=the-input-byte-stream:input-stream "input stream"
			- ", by passing the "
			a href="#the-input-byte-stream" id=the-input-byte-stream:the-input-byte-stream-2 "input byte stream"
			- " and character encoding to "
			a data-x-internal=decode href="https://encoding.spec.whatwg.org/#decode" id=the-input-byte-stream:decode decode
			- .
		}
		p class=note "A leading Byte Order Mark (BOM) causes the character encoding argument to be ignored and will itself be skipped."
		p class=note {
			- "Bytes or sequences of bytes in the original byte stream that did not conform to the Encoding standard (e.g. invalid UTF-8 byte sequences in a UTF-8 input byte stream) are errors that conformance checkers are expected to report. "
			a href="#refsENCODING" "[ENCODING]"
		}
		p class=warning "The decoder algorithms describe how to handle invalid input; for security reasons, it is imperative that those rules be followed precisely. Differences in how invalid byte sequences are handled can result in, amongst other problems, script injection vulnerabilities (\"XSS\")."
		p {
			- "When the HTML parser is decoding an input byte stream, it uses a character encoding and a "
			dfn id=concept-encoding-confidence confidence
			- ". The confidence is either "
			i tentative
			- ", "
			i certain
			- ", or "
			i irrelevant
			- ". The encoding used, and whether the confidence in that encoding is "
			i tentative
			- " or "
			i certain
			- ", is "
			a href="#meta-charset-during-parse" "used during the parsing"
			- " to determine whether to "
			a href="#change-the-encoding" id=the-input-byte-stream:change-the-encoding "change the encoding"
			- ". If no encoding is necessary, e.g. because the parser is operating on a Unicode stream and doesn't have to use a character encoding at all, then the "
			a href="#concept-encoding-confidence" id=the-input-byte-stream:concept-encoding-confidence confidence
			- " is "
			i irrelevant
			- .
		}
		p class=note {
			- "Some algorithms feed the parser by directly adding characters to the "
			a href="#input-stream" id=the-input-byte-stream:input-stream-2 "input stream"
			- " rather than adding bytes to the "
			a href="#the-input-byte-stream" id=the-input-byte-stream:the-input-byte-stream-3 "input byte stream"
			- .
		}
		h5 id=parsing-with-a-known-character-encoding {
			span class=secno "13.2.3.1"
			- " Parsing with a known character encoding"
			a class=self-link href="#parsing-with-a-known-character-encoding"
		}
		p {
			- "When the HTML parser is to operate on an input byte stream that has "
			dfn data-export="" id=a-known-definite-encoding "a known definite encoding"
			- ", then the character encoding is that encoding and the "
			a href="#concept-encoding-confidence" id=parsing-with-a-known-character-encoding:concept-encoding-confidence confidence
			- " is "
			i certain
			- .
		}
		h5 id=determining-the-character-encoding {
			span class=secno "13.2.3.2"
			- " Determining the character encoding"
			a class=self-link href="#determining-the-character-encoding"
		}
		p "In some cases, it might be impractical to unambiguously determine the encoding before parsing the document. Because of this, this specification provides for a two-pass mechanism with an optional pre-scan. Implementations are allowed, as described below, to apply a simplified parsing algorithm to whatever bytes they have available before beginning to parse the document. Then, the real parser is started, using a tentative encoding derived from this pre-parse and other out-of-band metadata. If, while the document is being loaded, the user agent discovers a character encoding declaration that conflicts with this information, then the parser can get reinvoked to perform a parse of the document with the real encoding."
		p id=documentEncoding {
			- "User agents must use the following algorithm, called the "
			dfn id=encoding-sniffing-algorithm "encoding sniffing algorithm"
			- ", to determine the character encoding to use when decoding a document in the first pass. This algorithm takes as input any out-of-band metadata available to the user agent (e.g. the "
			a href="#content-type" id=determining-the-character-encoding:content-type "Content-Type metadata"
			- " of the document) and all the bytes available so far, and returns a character encoding and a "
			a href="#concept-encoding-confidence" id=determining-the-character-encoding:concept-encoding-confidence confidence
			- " that is either "
			i tentative
			- " or "
			i certain
			- .
		}
		ol {
			li {
				p {
					- "If the result of "
					a data-x-internal=bom-sniff href="https://encoding.spec.whatwg.org/#bom-sniff" id=determining-the-character-encoding:bom-sniff "BOM sniffing"
					- " is an encoding, return that encoding with "
					a href="#concept-encoding-confidence" id=determining-the-character-encoding:concept-encoding-confidence-2 confidence
					i certain
					- .
				}
				p class=note {
					- "Although the "
					a data-x-internal=decode href="https://encoding.spec.whatwg.org/#decode" id=determining-the-character-encoding:decode decode
					- " algorithm will itself change the encoding to use based on the presence of a byte order mark, this algorithm sniffs the BOM as well in order to set the correct "
					a data-x-internal=document's-character-encoding href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-document-encoding" id=determining-the-character-encoding:document's-character-encoding "document's character encoding"
					- " and "
					a href="#concept-encoding-confidence" id=determining-the-character-encoding:concept-encoding-confidence-3 confidence
					- .
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "If the user has explicitly instructed the user agent to override the document's character encoding with a specific encoding, optionally return that encoding with the "
					a href="#concept-encoding-confidence" id=determining-the-character-encoding:concept-encoding-confidence-4 confidence
					i certain
					- .
				}
				p class=note {
					- "Typically, user agents remember such user requests across sessions, and in some cases apply them to documents in "
					code id=determining-the-character-encoding:the-iframe-element {
						a href="#the-iframe-element" iframe
					}
					- "s as well."
				}
			}
			li {
				p "The user agent may wait for more bytes of the resource to be available, either in this step or at any later step in this algorithm. For instance, a user agent might wait 500ms or 1024 bytes, whichever came first. In general preparsing the source to find the encoding improves performance, as it reduces the need to throw away the data structures used when parsing upon finding the encoding information. However, if the user agent delays too long to obtain data to determine the encoding, then the cost of the delay could outweigh any performance improvements from the preparse."
				p class=note {
					- "The authoring conformance requirements for character encoding declarations limit them to only appearing "
					a href="#charset1024" "in the first 1024 bytes"
					- ". User agents are therefore encouraged to use the prescan algorithm below (as invoked by these steps) on the first 1024 bytes, but not to stall beyond that."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "If the transport layer specifies a character encoding, and it is supported, return that encoding with the "
					a href="#concept-encoding-confidence" id=determining-the-character-encoding:concept-encoding-confidence-5 confidence
					i certain
					- .
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "Optionally "
					a href="#prescan-a-byte-stream-to-determine-its-encoding" id=determining-the-character-encoding:prescan-a-byte-stream-to-determine-its-encoding "prescan the byte stream to determine its encoding"
					- ", with the "
					i {
						a href="#prescan-end-condition" id=determining-the-character-encoding:prescan-end-condition "end condition"
					}
					- " being when the user agent decides that scanning further bytes would not be efficient. User agents are encouraged to only prescan the first 1024 bytes. User agents may decide that scanning "
					em any
					- " bytes is not efficient, in which case these substeps are entirely skipped."
				}
				p {
					- "The aforementioned algorithm returns either a character encoding or failure. If it returns a character encoding, then return the same encoding, with "
					a href="#concept-encoding-confidence" id=determining-the-character-encoding:concept-encoding-confidence-6 confidence
					i tentative
					- .
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "If the "
					a href="#html-parser" id=determining-the-character-encoding:html-parser "HTML parser"
					- " for which this algorithm is being run is associated with a "
					code id=determining-the-character-encoding:document {
						a href="#document" Document
					}
					var d
					- " whose "
					a href="#doc-container-document" id=determining-the-character-encoding:doc-container-document "container document"
					- " is non-null, then:"
				}
				ol {
					li {
						p {
							- "Let "
							var parentDocument
							- " be "
							var d
							- "'s "
							a href="#doc-container-document" id=determining-the-character-encoding:doc-container-document-2 "container document"
							- .
						}
					}
					li {
						p {
							- "If "
							var parentDocument
							- "'s "
							a data-x-internal=concept-document-origin href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-document-origin" id=determining-the-character-encoding:concept-document-origin origin
							- " is "
							a href="#same-origin" id=determining-the-character-encoding:same-origin "same origin"
							- " with "
							var d
							- "'s "
							a data-x-internal=concept-document-origin href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-document-origin" id=determining-the-character-encoding:concept-document-origin-2 origin
							- " and "
							var parentDocument
							- "'s "
							a data-x-internal=document's-character-encoding href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-document-encoding" id=determining-the-character-encoding:document's-character-encoding-2 "character encoding"
							- " is not "
							a data-x-internal=utf-16-encoding href="https://encoding.spec.whatwg.org/#utf-16be-le" id=determining-the-character-encoding:utf-16-encoding "UTF-16BE/LE"
							- ", then return "
							var parentDocument
							- "'s "
							a data-x-internal=document's-character-encoding href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-document-encoding" id=determining-the-character-encoding:document's-character-encoding-3 "character encoding"
							- ", with the "
							a href="#concept-encoding-confidence" id=determining-the-character-encoding:concept-encoding-confidence-7 confidence
							i tentative
							- .
						}
					}
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "Otherwise, if the user agent has information on the likely encoding for this page, e.g. based on the encoding of the page when it was last visited, then return that encoding, with the "
					a href="#concept-encoding-confidence" id=determining-the-character-encoding:concept-encoding-confidence-8 confidence
					i tentative
					- .
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "The user agent may attempt to autodetect the character encoding from applying frequency analysis or other algorithms to the data stream. Such algorithms may use information about the resource other than the resource's contents, including the address of the resource. If autodetection succeeds in determining a character encoding, and that encoding is a supported encoding, then return that encoding, with the "
					a href="#concept-encoding-confidence" id=determining-the-character-encoding:concept-encoding-confidence-9 confidence
					i tentative
					- ". "
					a href="#refsUNIVCHARDET" "[UNIVCHARDET]"
				}
				p class=note "User agents are generally discouraged from attempting to autodetect encodings for resources obtained over the network, since doing so involves inherently non-interoperable heuristics. Attempting to detect encodings based on an HTML document's preamble is especially tricky since HTML markup typically uses only ASCII characters, and HTML documents tend to begin with a lot of markup rather than with text content."
				p class=note {
					- "The UTF-8 encoding has a highly detectable bit pattern. Files from the local file system that contain bytes with values greater than 0x7F which match the UTF-8 pattern are very likely to be UTF-8, while documents with byte sequences that do not match it are very likely not. When a user agent can examine the whole file, rather than just the preamble, detecting for UTF-8 specifically can be especially effective. "
					a href="#refsPPUTF8" "[PPUTF8]"
					a href="#refsUTF8DET" "[UTF8DET]"
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "Otherwise, return an "
					a data-x-internal=implementation-defined href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#implementation-defined" id=determining-the-character-encoding:implementation-defined implementation-defined
					- " or user-specified default character encoding, with the "
					a href="#concept-encoding-confidence" id=determining-the-character-encoding:concept-encoding-confidence-10 confidence
					i tentative
					- .
				}
				p {
					- "In controlled environments or in environments where the encoding of documents can be prescribed (for example, for user agents intended for dedicated use in new networks), the comprehensive "
					code UTF-8
					- " encoding is suggested."
				}
				p {
					- "In other environments, the default encoding is typically dependent on the user's locale (an approximation of the languages, and thus often encodings, of the pages that the user is likely to frequent). The following table gives suggested defaults based on the user's locale, for compatibility with legacy content. Locales are identified by BCP 47 language tags. "
					a href="#refsBCP47" "[BCP47]"
					a href="#refsENCODING" "[ENCODING]"
				}
				table {
					thead {
						tr {
							th colspan="2" "Locale language "
							th "Suggested default encoding "
						}
					}
					tbody {
						tr {
							td "ar "
							td "Arabic "
							td {
								a data-x-internal=windows-1256 href="https://encoding.spec.whatwg.org/#windows-1256" id=determining-the-character-encoding:windows-1256 windows-1256
							}
						}
						tr {
							td "az "
							td "Azeri "
							td {
								a data-x-internal=windows-1254 href="https://encoding.spec.whatwg.org/#windows-1254" id=determining-the-character-encoding:windows-1254 windows-1254
							}
						}
						tr {
							td "ba "
							td "Bashkir "
							td {
								a data-x-internal=windows-1251 href="https://encoding.spec.whatwg.org/#windows-1251" id=determining-the-character-encoding:windows-1251 windows-1251
							}
						}
						tr {
							td "be "
