		h6 id=parsing-main-inbody {
			span class=secno "13.2.6.4.7"
			- " The \""
			dfn "in body"
			- "\" insertion mode"
			a class=self-link href="#parsing-main-inbody"
		}
		p {
			- "When the user agent is to apply the rules for the \""
			a href="#parsing-main-inbody" id=parsing-main-inbody:parsing-main-inbody "in body"
			- "\" "
			a href="#insertion-mode" id=parsing-main-inbody:insertion-mode "insertion mode"
			- ", the user agent must handle the token as follows:"
		}
		dl class=switch {
			dt "A character token that is U+0000 NULL"
			dd {
				p {
					a href="#parse-errors" id=parsing-main-inbody:parse-errors "Parse error"
					- ". Ignore the token."
				}
			}
			dt "A character token that is one of U+0009 CHARACTER TABULATION, U+000A LINE FEED (LF), U+000C FORM FEED (FF), U+000D CARRIAGE RETURN (CR), or U+0020 SPACE"
			dd {
				p {
					a href="#reconstruct-the-active-formatting-elements" id=parsing-main-inbody:reconstruct-the-active-formatting-elements "Reconstruct the active formatting elements"
					- ", if any."
				}
				p {
					a href="#insert-a-character" id=parsing-main-inbody:insert-a-character "Insert the token's character"
					- .
				}
			}
			dt "Any other character token"
			dd {
				p {
					a href="#reconstruct-the-active-formatting-elements" id=parsing-main-inbody:reconstruct-the-active-formatting-elements-2 "Reconstruct the active formatting elements"
					- ", if any."
				}
				p {
					a href="#insert-a-character" id=parsing-main-inbody:insert-a-character-2 "Insert the token's character"
					- .
				}
				p {
					- "Set the "
					a href="#frameset-ok-flag" id=parsing-main-inbody:frameset-ok-flag "frameset-ok flag"
					- " to \"not ok\"."
				}
			}
			dt "A comment token"
			dd {
				p {
					a href="#insert-a-comment" id=parsing-main-inbody:insert-a-comment "Insert a comment"
					- .
				}
			}
			dt "A DOCTYPE token"
			dd {
				p {
					a href="#parse-errors" id=parsing-main-inbody:parse-errors-2 "Parse error"
					- ". Ignore the token."
				}
			}
			dt "A start tag whose tag name is \"html\""
			dd {
				p {
					a href="#parse-errors" id=parsing-main-inbody:parse-errors-3 "Parse error"
					- .
				}
				p {
					- "If there is a "
					code id=parsing-main-inbody:the-template-element {
						a href="#the-template-element" template
					}
					- " element on the "
					a href="#stack-of-open-elements" id=parsing-main-inbody:stack-of-open-elements "stack of open elements"
					- ", then ignore the token."
				}
				p {
					- "Otherwise, for each attribute on the token, check to see if the attribute is already present on the top element of the "
					a href="#stack-of-open-elements" id=parsing-main-inbody:stack-of-open-elements-2 "stack of open elements"
					- ". If it is not, add the attribute and its corresponding value to that element."
				}
			}
			dt "A start tag whose tag name is one of: \"base\", \"basefont\", \"bgsound\", \"link\", \"meta\", \"noframes\", \"script\", \"style\", \"template\", \"title\""
			dt "An end tag whose tag name is \"template\""
			dd {
				p {
					- "Process the token "
					a href="#using-the-rules-for" id=parsing-main-inbody:using-the-rules-for "using the rules for"
					- " the \""
					a href="#parsing-main-inhead" id=parsing-main-inbody:parsing-main-inhead "in head"
					- "\" "
					a href="#insertion-mode" id=parsing-main-inbody:insertion-mode-2 "insertion mode"
					- .
				}
			}
			dt "A start tag whose tag name is \"body\""
			dd {
				p {
					a href="#parse-errors" id=parsing-main-inbody:parse-errors-4 "Parse error"
					- .
				}
				p {
					- "If the "
					a href="#stack-of-open-elements" id=parsing-main-inbody:stack-of-open-elements-3 "stack of open elements"
					- " has only one node on it, if the second element on the "
					a href="#stack-of-open-elements" id=parsing-main-inbody:stack-of-open-elements-4 "stack of open elements"
					- " is not a "
					code id=parsing-main-inbody:the-body-element {
						a href="#the-body-element" body
					}
					- " element, or if there is a "
					code id=parsing-main-inbody:the-template-element-2 {
						a href="#the-template-element" template
					}
					- " element on the "
					a href="#stack-of-open-elements" id=parsing-main-inbody:stack-of-open-elements-5 "stack of open elements"
					- ", then ignore the token. ("
					a href="#fragment-case" id=parsing-main-inbody:fragment-case "fragment case"
					- " or there is a "
					code id=parsing-main-inbody:the-template-element-3 {
						a href="#the-template-element" template
					}
					- " element on the stack)"
				}
				p {
					- "Otherwise, set the "
					a href="#frameset-ok-flag" id=parsing-main-inbody:frameset-ok-flag-2 "frameset-ok flag"
					- " to \"not ok\"; then, for each attribute on the token, check to see if the attribute is already present on the "
					code id=parsing-main-inbody:the-body-element-2 {
						a href="#the-body-element" body
					}
					- " element (the second element) on the "
					a href="#stack-of-open-elements" id=parsing-main-inbody:stack-of-open-elements-6 "stack of open elements"
					- ", and if it is not, add the attribute and its corresponding value to that element."
				}
			}
			dt "A start tag whose tag name is \"frameset\""
			dd {
				p {
					a href="#parse-errors" id=parsing-main-inbody:parse-errors-5 "Parse error"
					- .
				}
				p {
					- "If the "
					a href="#stack-of-open-elements" id=parsing-main-inbody:stack-of-open-elements-7 "stack of open elements"
					- " has only one node on it, or if the second element on the "
					a href="#stack-of-open-elements" id=parsing-main-inbody:stack-of-open-elements-8 "stack of open elements"
					- " is not a "
					code id=parsing-main-inbody:the-body-element-3 {
						a href="#the-body-element" body
					}
					- " element, then ignore the token. ("
					a href="#fragment-case" id=parsing-main-inbody:fragment-case-2 "fragment case"
					- " or there is a "
					code id=parsing-main-inbody:the-template-element-4 {
						a href="#the-template-element" template
					}
					- " element on the stack)"
				}
				p {
					- "If the "
					a href="#frameset-ok-flag" id=parsing-main-inbody:frameset-ok-flag-3 "frameset-ok flag"
					- " is set to \"not ok\", ignore the token."
				}
				p "Otherwise, run the following steps:"
				ol {
					li {
