			- " Speculative HTML parsing"
			a class=self-link href="#speculative-html-parsing"
		}
		p {
			- "User agents may implement an optimization, as described in this section, to speculatively fetch resources that are declared in the HTML markup while the HTML parser is waiting for a "
			a href="#pending-parsing-blocking-script" id=speculative-html-parsing:pending-parsing-blocking-script "pending parsing-blocking script"
			- " to be fetched and executed, or during normal parsing, at the time "
			a href="#create-an-element-for-the-token" id=speculative-html-parsing:create-an-element-for-the-token "an element is created for a token"
			- ". While this optimization is not defined in precise detail, there are some rules to consider for interoperability."
		}
		p {
			- "Each "
			a href="#html-parser" id=speculative-html-parsing:html-parser "HTML parser"
			- " can have an "
			dfn data-export="" id=active-speculative-html-parser "active speculative HTML parser"
			- ". It is initially null."
		}
		p {
			- "The "
			dfn data-export="" id=speculative-html-parser "speculative HTML parser"
			- " must act like the normal HTML parser (e.g., the tree builder rules apply), with some exceptions:"
		}
		ul {
			li {
				p "The state of the normal HTML parser and the document itself must not be affected."
				p class=example {
					- "For example, the "
					a href="#next-input-character" id=speculative-html-parsing:next-input-character "next input character"
					- " or the "
					a href="#stack-of-open-elements" id=speculative-html-parsing:stack-of-open-elements "stack of open elements"
					- " for the normal HTML parser is not affected by the "
					a href="#speculative-html-parser" id=speculative-html-parsing:speculative-html-parser "speculative HTML parser"
					- .
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "Bytes pushed into the HTML parser's "
					a href="#the-input-byte-stream" id=speculative-html-parsing:the-input-byte-stream "input byte stream"
					- " must also be pushed into the speculative HTML parser's "
					a href="#the-input-byte-stream" id=speculative-html-parsing:the-input-byte-stream-2 "input byte stream"
					- ". Bytes read from the streams must be independent."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "The result of the speculative parsing is primarily a series of "
					a href="#speculative-fetch" id=speculative-html-parsing:speculative-fetch "speculative fetches"
					- ". Which kinds of resources to speculatively fetch is "
					a data-x-internal=implementation-defined href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#implementation-defined" id=speculative-html-parsing:implementation-defined implementation-defined
					- ", but user agents must not speculatively fetch resources that would not be fetched with the normal HTML parser, under the assumption that the script that is blocking the HTML parser does nothing."
				}
				p class=note {
					- "It is possible that the same markup is seen multiple times from the "
					a href="#speculative-html-parser" id=speculative-html-parsing:speculative-html-parser-2 "speculative HTML parser"
					- " and then the normal HTML parser. It is expected that duplicated fetches will be prevented by caching rules, which are not yet fully specified."
				}
			}
		}
		p {
			- "A "
			dfn id=speculative-fetch "speculative fetch"
			- " for a "
			a href="#speculative-mock-element" id=speculative-html-parsing:speculative-mock-element "speculative mock element"
			var element
			- " must follow these rules:"
		}
		p class=XXX "Should some of these things be applied to the document \"for real\", even though they are found speculatively?"
		ul {
			li {
				p {
					- "If the "
					a href="#speculative-html-parser" id=speculative-html-parsing:speculative-html-parser-3 "speculative HTML parser"
					- " encounters one of the following elements, then act as if that element is processed for the purpose of its effect of subsequent speculative fetches."
				}
				ul class=brief {
					li {
						- "A "
						code id=speculative-html-parsing:the-base-element {
							a href="#the-base-element" base
						}
						- " element."
					}
					li {
						- "A "
						code id=speculative-html-parsing:the-meta-element {
							a href="#the-meta-element" meta
						}
						- " element whose "
						code id=speculative-html-parsing:attr-meta-http-equiv {
							a href="#attr-meta-http-equiv" http-equiv
						}
						- " attribute is in the "
						a href="#attr-meta-http-equiv-content-security-policy" id=speculative-html-parsing:attr-meta-http-equiv-content-security-policy "Content security policy"
						- " state."
					}
					li {
						- "A "
						code id=speculative-html-parsing:the-meta-element-2 {
							a href="#the-meta-element" meta
						}
						- " element whose "
						code id=speculative-html-parsing:attr-meta-name {
							a href="#attr-meta-name" name
						}
						- " attribute is an "
						a data-x-internal=ascii-case-insensitive href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ascii-case-insensitive" id=speculative-html-parsing:ascii-case-insensitive "ASCII case-insensitive"
						- " match for \""
						code id=speculative-html-parsing:meta-referrer {
							a href="#meta-referrer" referrer
						}
						- "\"."
					}
					li {
						- "A "
						code id=speculative-html-parsing:the-meta-element-3 {
							a href="#the-meta-element" meta
						}
						- " element whose "
						code id=speculative-html-parsing:attr-meta-name-2 {
							a href="#attr-meta-name" name
						}
						- " attribute is an "
						a data-x-internal=ascii-case-insensitive href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ascii-case-insensitive" id=speculative-html-parsing:ascii-case-insensitive-2 "ASCII case-insensitive"
						- " match for \""
						code viewport
						- "\". (This can affect whether a media query list "
						a href="#matches-the-environment" id=speculative-html-parsing:matches-the-environment "matches the environment"
						- ".) "
						a href="#refsCSSDEVICEADAPT" "[CSSDEVICEADAPT]"
					}
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "Let "
					var url
					- " be the "
					a data-x-internal=url href="https://url.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-url" id=speculative-html-parsing:url URL
					- " that "
					var element
					- " would fetch if it was processed normally. If there is no such "
					a data-x-internal=url href="https://url.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-url" id=speculative-html-parsing:url-2 URL
					- " or if it is the empty string, then do nothing. Otherwise, if "
					a data-x-internal=url href="https://url.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-url" id=speculative-html-parsing:url-3 url
					- " is already in the "
					a href="#list-of-speculative-fetch-urls" id=speculative-html-parsing:list-of-speculative-fetch-urls "list of speculative fetch URLs"
					- ", then do nothing. Otherwise, fetch "
					a data-x-internal=url href="https://url.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-url" id=speculative-html-parsing:url-4 url
					- " as if the element was processed normally, and add "
					var url
					- " to the "
					a href="#list-of-speculative-fetch-urls" id=speculative-html-parsing:list-of-speculative-fetch-urls-2 "list of speculative fetch URLs"
					- .
				}
			}
		}
		p {
			- "Each "
			code id=speculative-html-parsing:document {
				a href="#document" Document
			}
			- " has a "
			dfn id=list-of-speculative-fetch-urls "list of speculative fetch URLs"
			- ", which is a "
			a data-x-internal=list href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list" id=speculative-html-parsing:list list
			- " of "
			a data-x-internal=url href="https://url.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-url" id=speculative-html-parsing:url-5 URLs
			- ", initially empty."
		}
		p {
			- "To "
			dfn id=start-the-speculative-html-parser "start the speculative HTML parser"
			- " for an instance of an HTML parser "
			var parser
			- :
		}
		ol {
			li {
				p "Optionally, return."
				p class=note "This step allows user agents to opt out of speculative HTML parsing."
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "If "
					var parser
					- "'s "
					a href="#active-speculative-html-parser" id=speculative-html-parsing:active-speculative-html-parser "active speculative HTML parser"
					- " is not null, then "
					a href="#stop-the-speculative-html-parser" id=speculative-html-parsing:stop-the-speculative-html-parser "stop the speculative HTML parser"
					- " for "
					var parser
					- .
				}
				p class=note {
					- "This can happen when "
					code id=speculative-html-parsing:dom-document-write {
						a href="#dom-document-write" "document.write()"
					}
					- " writes another parser-blocking script. For simplicity, this specification always restarts speculative parsing, but user agents can implement a more efficient strategy, so long as the end result is equivalent."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "Let "
					var speculativeParser
					- " be a new "
					a href="#speculative-html-parser" id=speculative-html-parsing:speculative-html-parser-4 "speculative HTML parser"
					- ", with the same state as "
					var parser
					- .
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "Let "
					var speculativeDoc
					- " be a new isomorphic representation of "
					var parser
					- "'s "
					code id=speculative-html-parsing:document-2 {
						a href="#document" Document
					}
					- ", where all elements are instead "
					a href="#speculative-mock-element" id=speculative-html-parsing:speculative-mock-element-2 "speculative mock elements"
					- ". Let "
					var speculativeParser
					- " parse into "
					var speculativeDoc
					- .
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "Set "
					var parser
					- "'s "
					a href="#active-speculative-html-parser" id=speculative-html-parsing:active-speculative-html-parser-2 "active speculative HTML parser"
					- " to "
					var speculativeParser
					- .
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					a href="#in-parallel" id=speculative-html-parsing:in-parallel "In parallel"
					- ", run "
					var speculativeParser
					- " until it is stopped or until it reaches the end of its "
					a href="#input-stream" id=speculative-html-parsing:input-stream "input stream"
					- .
				}
			}
		}
		p {
			- "To "
			dfn id=stop-the-speculative-html-parser "stop the speculative HTML parser"
			- " for an instance of an HTML parser "
			var parser
			- :
		}
		ol {
			li {
				p {
					- "Let "
					var speculativeParser
					- " be "
					var parser
					- "'s "
					a href="#active-speculative-html-parser" id=speculative-html-parsing:active-speculative-html-parser-3 "active speculative HTML parser"
					- .
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "If "
					var speculativeParser
					- " is null, then return."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "Throw away any pending content in "
					var speculativeParser
					- "'s "
					a href="#input-stream" id=speculative-html-parsing:input-stream-2 "input stream"
					- ", and discard any future content that would have been added to it."
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "Set "
					var parser
					- "'s "
					a href="#active-speculative-html-parser" id=speculative-html-parsing:active-speculative-html-parser-4 "active speculative HTML parser"
					- " to null."
				}
			}
		}
		p {
			- "The "
			a href="#speculative-html-parser" id=speculative-html-parsing:speculative-html-parser-5 "speculative HTML parser"
			- " will create "
			a href="#speculative-mock-element" id=speculative-html-parsing:speculative-mock-element-3 "speculative mock elements"
			- " instead of normal elements. DOM operations that the tree builder normally does on elements are expected to work appropriately on speculative mock elements."
		}
		p {
			- "A "
			dfn id=speculative-mock-element "speculative mock element"
			- " is a "
			a data-x-internal=struct href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#struct" id=speculative-html-parsing:struct struct
			- " with the following "
			a data-x-internal=struct-item href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#struct-item" id=speculative-html-parsing:struct-item items
			- :
		}
		ul {
			li {
				p {
					- "A "
					a data-x-internal=string href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#string" id=speculative-html-parsing:string string
					dfn id=concept-mock-namespace namespace
					- ", corresponding to an element's "
					a data-x-internal=concept-element-namespace href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-element-namespace" id=speculative-html-parsing:concept-element-namespace namespace
					- .
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "A "
					a data-x-internal=string href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#string" id=speculative-html-parsing:string-2 string
					dfn id=concept-mock-local-name "local name"
					- ", corresponding to an element's "
					a data-x-internal=concept-element-local-name href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-element-local-name" id=speculative-html-parsing:concept-element-local-name "local name"
					- .
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "A "
					a data-x-internal=list href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list" id=speculative-html-parsing:list-2 list
					dfn id=concept-mock-attribute-list "attribute list"
					- ", corresponding to an element's "
					a data-x-internal=attribute-list href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-element-attribute" id=speculative-html-parsing:attribute-list "attribute list"
					- .
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "A "
					a data-x-internal=list href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list" id=speculative-html-parsing:list-3 list
					dfn id=concept-mock-children children
					- ", corresponding to an element's "
					a data-x-internal=concept-tree-child href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-tree-child" id=speculative-html-parsing:concept-tree-child children
					- .
				}
			}
		}
		p {
			- "To "
			dfn id=create-a-speculative-mock-element "create a speculative mock element"
			- " given a "
			var namespace
			- ", "
			var tagName
			- ", and "
			var attributes
			- :
		}
		ol {
			li {
				p {
					- "Let "
					var element
					- " be a new "
					a href="#speculative-mock-element" id=speculative-html-parsing:speculative-mock-element-4 "speculative mock element"
					- .
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "Set "
					var element
					- "'s "
					a href="#concept-mock-namespace" id=speculative-html-parsing:concept-mock-namespace namespace
					- " to "
					var namespace
					- .
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "Set "
					var element
					- "'s "
					a href="#concept-mock-local-name" id=speculative-html-parsing:concept-mock-local-name "local name"
					- " to "
					var tagName
					- .
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "Set "
					var element
					- "'s "
					a href="#concept-mock-attribute-list" id=speculative-html-parsing:concept-mock-attribute-list "attribute list"
					- " to "
					var attributes
					- .
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "Set "
					var element
					- "'s "
					a href="#concept-mock-children" id=speculative-html-parsing:concept-mock-children children
					- " to a new empty "
					a data-x-internal=list href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#list" id=speculative-html-parsing:list-4 list
					- .
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "Optionally, perform a "
					a href="#speculative-fetch" id=speculative-html-parsing:speculative-fetch-2 "speculative fetch"
					- " for "
					var element
					- .
				}
			}
			li {
				p {
					- "Return "
					var element
					- .
				}
			}
		}
		p {
			- "When the tree builder says to insert an element into a "
			code id=speculative-html-parsing:the-template-element {
				a href="#the-template-element" template
			}
			- " element's "
			a href="#template-contents" id=speculative-html-parsing:template-contents "template contents"
			- ", if that is a "
			a href="#speculative-mock-element" id=speculative-html-parsing:speculative-mock-element-5 "speculative mock element"
			- ", and the "
			code id=speculative-html-parsing:the-template-element-2 {
				a href="#the-template-element" template
			}
			- " element's "
			a href="#template-contents" id=speculative-html-parsing:template-contents-2 "template contents"
			- " is not a "
			code id=speculative-html-parsing:shadowroot {
				a data-x-internal=shadowroot href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#interface-shadowroot" ShadowRoot
			}
			- " node, instead do nothing. URLs found speculatively inside non-declarative-shadow-root "
			code id=speculative-html-parsing:the-template-element-3 {
				a href="#the-template-element" template
			}
			- " elements might themselves be templates, and must not be speculatively fetched."
		}
		h4 id=coercing-an-html-dom-into-an-infoset {
			span class=secno "13.2.9"
			- " Coercing an HTML DOM into an infoset"
			a class=self-link href="#coercing-an-html-dom-into-an-infoset"
		}
		p {
			- "When an application uses an "
			a href="#html-parser" id=coercing-an-html-dom-into-an-infoset:html-parser "HTML parser"
			- " in conjunction with an XML pipeline, it is possible that the constructed DOM is not compatible with the XML tool chain in certain subtle ways. For example, an XML toolchain might not be able to represent attributes with the name "
			code xmlns
			- ", since they conflict with the Namespaces in XML syntax. There is also some data that the "
			a href="#html-parser" id=coercing-an-html-dom-into-an-infoset:html-parser-2 "HTML parser"
			- " generates that isn't included in the DOM itself. This section specifies some rules for handling these issues."
		}
		p "If the XML API being used doesn't support DOCTYPEs, the tool may drop DOCTYPEs altogether."
		p {
			- "If the XML API doesn't support attributes in no namespace that are named \""
			code xmlns
			- "\", attributes whose names start with \""
			code xmlns:
			- "\", or attributes in the "
			a data-x-internal=xmlns-namespace href="https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#xmlns-namespace" id=coercing-an-html-dom-into-an-infoset:xmlns-namespace "XMLNS namespace"
			- ", then the tool may drop such attributes."
		}
		p "The tool may annotate the output with any namespace declarations required for proper operation."
		p {
			- "If the XML API being used restricts the allowable characters in the local names of elements and attributes, then the tool may map all element and attribute local names that the API wouldn't support to a set of names that "
			em are
			- " allowed, by replacing any character that isn't supported with the uppercase letter U and the six digits of the character's code point when expressed in hexadecimal, using digits 0-9 and capital letters A-F as the symbols, in increasing numeric order."
		}
		p class=example {
			- "For example, the element name "
			code foo<bar
			- ", which can be output by the "
			a href="#html-parser" id=coercing-an-html-dom-into-an-infoset:html-parser-3 "HTML parser"
			- ", though it is neither a legal HTML element name nor a well-formed XML element name, would be converted into "
			code fooU00003Cbar
			- ", which "
			em is
			- " a well-formed XML element name (though it's still not legal in HTML by any means)."
		}
		p class=example {
			- "As another example, consider the attribute "
			code xlink:href
			- ". Used on a MathML element, it becomes, after being "
			a href="#adjust-foreign-attributes" id=coercing-an-html-dom-into-an-infoset:adjust-foreign-attributes adjusted
			- ", an attribute with a prefix \""
			code xlink
			- "\" and a local name \""
			code href
			- "\". However, used on an HTML element, it becomes an attribute with no prefix and the local name \""
			code xlink:href
			- "\", which is not a valid NCName, and thus might not be accepted by an XML API. It could thus get converted, becoming \""
			code xlinkU00003Ahref
			- "\"."
		}
		p class=note {
			- "The resulting names from this conversion conveniently can't clash with any attribute generated by the "
			a href="#html-parser" id=coercing-an-html-dom-into-an-infoset:html-parser-4 "HTML parser"
			- ", since those are all either lowercase or those listed in the "
			a href="#adjust-foreign-attributes" id=coercing-an-html-dom-into-an-infoset:adjust-foreign-attributes-2 "adjust foreign attributes"
			- " algorithm's table."
		}
		p "If the XML API restricts comments from having two consecutive U+002D HYPHEN-MINUS characters (--), the tool may insert a single U+0020 SPACE character between any such offending characters."
		p "If the XML API restricts comments from ending in a U+002D HYPHEN-MINUS character (-), the tool may insert a single U+0020 SPACE character at the end of such comments."
		p "If the XML API restricts allowed characters in character data, attribute values, or comments, the tool may replace any U+000C FORM FEED (FF) character with a U+0020 SPACE character, and any other literal non-XML character with a U+FFFD REPLACEMENT CHARACTER."
		p "If the tool has no way to convey out-of-band information, then the tool may drop the following information:"
		ul {
			li {
				- "Whether the document is set to "
				i id=coercing-an-html-dom-into-an-infoset:no-quirks-mode {
					a data-x-internal=no-quirks-mode href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-document-no-quirks" "no-quirks mode"
				}
				- ", "
				i id=coercing-an-html-dom-into-an-infoset:limited-quirks-mode {
					a data-x-internal=limited-quirks-mode href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-document-limited-quirks" "limited-quirks mode"
				}
				- ", or "
				i id=coercing-an-html-dom-into-an-infoset:quirks-mode {
					a data-x-internal=quirks-mode href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-document-quirks" "quirks mode"
				}
			}
			li {
				- "The association between form controls and forms that aren't their nearest "
				code id=coercing-an-html-dom-into-an-infoset:the-form-element {
					a href="#the-form-element" form
				}
				- " element ancestor (use of the "
				a href="#form-element-pointer" id=coercing-an-html-dom-into-an-infoset:form-element-pointer {
					code form
					- " element pointer"
				}
				- " in the parser)"
			}
			li {
				- "The "
				a href="#template-contents" id=coercing-an-html-dom-into-an-infoset:template-contents "template contents"
				- " of any "
				code id=coercing-an-html-dom-into-an-infoset:the-template-element {
					a href="#the-template-element" template
				}
				- " elements."
			}
		}
		p class=note {
			- "The mutations allowed by this section apply "
			em after
			- " the "
			a href="#html-parser" id=coercing-an-html-dom-into-an-infoset:html-parser-5 "HTML parser"
			- "'s rules have been applied. For example, a "
			code <a::>
			- " start tag will be closed by a "
			code "</a::>"
			- " end tag, and never by a "
			code "</aU00003AU00003A>"
			- " end tag, even if the user agent is using the rules above to then generate an actual element in the DOM with the name "
			code aU00003AU00003A
			- " for that start tag."
		}
		h4 id=an-introduction-to-error-handling-and-strange-cases-in-the-parser {
			span class=secno "13.2.10"
			- " An introduction to error handling and strange cases in the parser"
			a class=self-link href="#an-introduction-to-error-handling-and-strange-cases-in-the-parser"
		}
		p {
			i "This section is non-normative."
		}
		p {
			- "This section examines some erroneous markup and discusses how the "
			a href="#html-parser" id=an-introduction-to-error-handling-and-strange-cases-in-the-parser:html-parser "HTML parser"
			- " handles these cases."
		}
		h5 id="misnested-tags:-b-i-/b-/i" {
			span class=secno "13.2.10.1"
			- " Misnested tags: <b><i></b></i>"
			a class=self-link href="#misnested-tags:-b-i-/b-/i"
		}
		p {
			i "This section is non-normative."
		}
		p "The most-often discussed example of erroneous markup is as follows:"
		pre {
			code class=html {
				c- p="" <
				c- f="" p
				c- p="" >
				- "1"
				c- p="" <
				c- f="" b
				c- p="" >
				- "2"
				c- p="" <
				c- f="" i
				c- p="" >
				- "3"
				c- p="" "</"
				c- f="" b
				c- p="" >
				- "4"
				c- p="" "</"
				c- f="" i
				c- p="" >
				- "5"
				c- p="" "</"
				c- f="" p
				c- p="" >
			}
		}
		p "The parsing of this markup is straightforward up to the \"3\". At this point, the DOM looks like this:"
		ul class=domTree {
			li class=t1 {
				code id="misnested-tags:-b-i-/b-/i:the-html-element" {
					a href="#the-html-element" html
				}
				ul {
					li class=t1 {
						code id="misnested-tags:-b-i-/b-/i:the-head-element" {
							a href="#the-head-element" head
						}
					}
					li class=t1 {
						code id="misnested-tags:-b-i-/b-/i:the-body-element" {
							a href="#the-body-element" body
						}
						ul {
							li class=t1 {
								code id="misnested-tags:-b-i-/b-/i:the-p-element" {
									a href="#the-p-element" p
								}
								ul {
									li class=t3 {
										code id="misnested-tags:-b-i-/b-/i:text" {
											a data-x-internal=text href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#interface-text" "#text"
										}
										- ": "
										span "1"
									}
									li class=t1 {
										code id="misnested-tags:-b-i-/b-/i:the-b-element" {
											a href="#the-b-element" b
										}
										ul {
											li class=t3 {
												code id="misnested-tags:-b-i-/b-/i:text-2" {
													a data-x-internal=text href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#interface-text" "#text"
												}
												- ": "
												span "2"
											}
											li class=t1 {
												code id="misnested-tags:-b-i-/b-/i:the-i-element" {
													a href="#the-i-element" i
												}
												ul {
													li class=t3 {
														code id="misnested-tags:-b-i-/b-/i:text-3" {
															a data-x-internal=text href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#interface-text" "#text"
														}
														- ": "
														span "3"
													}
												}
											}
										}
									}
								}
							}
						}
					}
				}
			}
		}
		p {
			- "Here, the "
			a href="#stack-of-open-elements" id="misnested-tags:-b-i-/b-/i:stack-of-open-elements" "stack of open elements"
			- " has five elements on it: "
			code id="misnested-tags:-b-i-/b-/i:the-html-element-2" {
				a href="#the-html-element" html
			}
			- ", "
			code id="misnested-tags:-b-i-/b-/i:the-body-element-2" {
				a href="#the-body-element" body
			}
			- ", "
			code id="misnested-tags:-b-i-/b-/i:the-p-element-2" {
				a href="#the-p-element" p
			}
			- ", "
			code id="misnested-tags:-b-i-/b-/i:the-b-element-2" {
				a href="#the-b-element" b
			}
			- ", and "
			code id="misnested-tags:-b-i-/b-/i:the-i-element-2" {
				a href="#the-i-element" i
			}
			- ". The "
			a href="#list-of-active-formatting-elements" id="misnested-tags:-b-i-/b-/i:list-of-active-formatting-elements" "list of active formatting elements"
			- " just has two: "
			code id="misnested-tags:-b-i-/b-/i:the-b-element-3" {
				a href="#the-b-element" b
			}
			- " and "
			code id="misnested-tags:-b-i-/b-/i:the-i-element-3" {
				a href="#the-i-element" i
			}
			- ". The "
			a href="#insertion-mode" id="misnested-tags:-b-i-/b-/i:insertion-mode" "insertion mode"
			- " is \""
			a href="#parsing-main-inbody" id="misnested-tags:-b-i-/b-/i:parsing-main-inbody" "in body"
			- "\"."
		}
		p {
			- "Upon receiving the end tag token with the tag name \"b\", the \""
			a href="#adoptionAgency" "adoption agency algorithm"
			- "\" is invoked. This is a simple case, in that the "
			var formattingElement
			- " is the "
			code id="misnested-tags:-b-i-/b-/i:the-b-element-4" {
				a href="#the-b-element" b
			}
			- " element, and there is no "
			var "furthest block"
			- ". Thus, the "
			a href="#stack-of-open-elements" id="misnested-tags:-b-i-/b-/i:stack-of-open-elements-2" "stack of open elements"
			- " ends up with just three elements: "
			code id="misnested-tags:-b-i-/b-/i:the-html-element-3" {
				a href="#the-html-element" html
			}
			- ", "
			code id="misnested-tags:-b-i-/b-/i:the-body-element-3" {
				a href="#the-body-element" body
			}
			- ", and "
			code id="misnested-tags:-b-i-/b-/i:the-p-element-3" {
				a href="#the-p-element" p
			}
			- ", while the "
			a href="#list-of-active-formatting-elements" id="misnested-tags:-b-i-/b-/i:list-of-active-formatting-elements-2" "list of active formatting elements"
			- " has just one: "
			code id="misnested-tags:-b-i-/b-/i:the-i-element-4" {
				a href="#the-i-element" i
			}
			- ". The DOM tree is unmodified at this point."
		}
		p {
			- "The next token is a character (\"4\"), triggers the "
			a href="#reconstruct-the-active-formatting-elements" id="misnested-tags:-b-i-/b-/i:reconstruct-the-active-formatting-elements" "reconstruction of the active formatting elements"
			- ", in this case just the "
			code id="misnested-tags:-b-i-/b-/i:the-i-element-5" {
				a href="#the-i-element" i
			}
			- " element. A new "
			code id="misnested-tags:-b-i-/b-/i:the-i-element-6" {
				a href="#the-i-element" i
			}
			- " element is thus created for the \"4\" "
			code id="misnested-tags:-b-i-/b-/i:text-4" {
				a data-x-internal=text href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#interface-text" Text
			}
			- " node. After the end tag token for the \"i\" is also received, and the \"5\" "
			code id="misnested-tags:-b-i-/b-/i:text-5" {
				a data-x-internal=text href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#interface-text" Text
			}
			- " node is inserted, the DOM looks as follows:"
		}
		ul class=domTree {
			li class=t1 {
				code id="misnested-tags:-b-i-/b-/i:the-html-element-4" {
					a href="#the-html-element" html
				}
				ul {
					li class=t1 {
						code id="misnested-tags:-b-i-/b-/i:the-head-element-2" {
							a href="#the-head-element" head
						}
					}
					li class=t1 {
						code id="misnested-tags:-b-i-/b-/i:the-body-element-4" {
							a href="#the-body-element" body
						}
						ul {
							li class=t1 {
								code id="misnested-tags:-b-i-/b-/i:the-p-element-4" {
									a href="#the-p-element" p
								}
								ul {
									li class=t3 {
										code id="misnested-tags:-b-i-/b-/i:text-6" {
											a data-x-internal=text href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#interface-text" "#text"
										}
										- ": "
										span "1"
									}
									li class=t1 {
										code id="misnested-tags:-b-i-/b-/i:the-b-element-5" {
											a href="#the-b-element" b
										}
										ul {
											li class=t3 {
												code id="misnested-tags:-b-i-/b-/i:text-7" {
													a data-x-internal=text href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#interface-text" "#text"
												}
												- ": "
												span "2"
											}
											li class=t1 {
												code id="misnested-tags:-b-i-/b-/i:the-i-element-7" {
													a href="#the-i-element" i
												}
												ul {
													li class=t3 {
														code id="misnested-tags:-b-i-/b-/i:text-8" {
															a data-x-internal=text href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#interface-text" "#text"
														}
														- ": "
														span "3"
													}
												}
											}
										}
									}
									li class=t1 {
										code id="misnested-tags:-b-i-/b-/i:the-i-element-8" {
											a href="#the-i-element" i
										}
										ul {
											li class=t3 {
												code id="misnested-tags:-b-i-/b-/i:text-9" {
													a data-x-internal=text href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#interface-text" "#text"
												}
												- ": "
												span "4"
											}
										}
									}
									li class=t3 {
										code id="misnested-tags:-b-i-/b-/i:text-10" {
											a data-x-internal=text href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#interface-text" "#text"
										}
										- ": "
										span "5"
									}
								}
							}
						}
					}
				}
			}
		}
		h5 id="misnested-tags:-b-p-/b-/p" {
			span class=secno "13.2.10.2"
			- " Misnested tags: <b><p></b></p>"
			a class=self-link href="#misnested-tags:-b-p-/b-/p"
		}
		p {
			i "This section is non-normative."
		}
		p "A case similar to the previous one is the following:"
		pre {
			code class=html {
				c- p="" <
				c- f="" b
				c- p="" >
				- "1"
				c- p="" <
				c- f="" p
				c- p="" >
				- "2"
				c- p="" "</"
				c- f="" b
				c- p="" >
				- "3"
				c- p="" "</"
				c- f="" p
				c- p="" >
			}
		}
		p "Up to the \"2\" the parsing here is straightforward:"
		ul class=domTree {
			li class=t1 {
				code id="misnested-tags:-b-p-/b-/p:the-html-element" {
					a href="#the-html-element" html
				}
				ul {
					li class=t1 {
						code id="misnested-tags:-b-p-/b-/p:the-head-element" {
							a href="#the-head-element" head
						}
					}
					li class=t1 {
						code id="misnested-tags:-b-p-/b-/p:the-body-element" {
							a href="#the-body-element" body
						}
						ul {
							li class=t1 {
								code id="misnested-tags:-b-p-/b-/p:the-b-element" {
									a href="#the-b-element" b
								}
								ul {
									li class=t3 {
										code id="misnested-tags:-b-p-/b-/p:text" {
											a data-x-internal=text href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#interface-text" "#text"
										}
										- ": "
										span "1"
									}
									li class=t1 {
										code id="misnested-tags:-b-p-/b-/p:the-p-element" {
											a href="#the-p-element" p
										}
										ul {
											li class=t3 {
												code id="misnested-tags:-b-p-/b-/p:text-2" {
													a data-x-internal=text href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#interface-text" "#text"
												}
												- ": "
												span "2"
											}
										}
									}
								}
							}
						}
					}
				}
			}
		}
		p "The interesting part is when the end tag token with the tag name \"b\" is parsed."
		p {
			- "Before that token is seen, the "
			a href="#stack-of-open-elements" id="misnested-tags:-b-p-/b-/p:stack-of-open-elements" "stack of open elements"
			- " has four elements on it: "
			code id="misnested-tags:-b-p-/b-/p:the-html-element-2" {
				a href="#the-html-element" html
			}
			- ", "
			code id="misnested-tags:-b-p-/b-/p:the-body-element-2" {
				a href="#the-body-element" body
			}
			- ", "
			code id="misnested-tags:-b-p-/b-/p:the-b-element-2" {
				a href="#the-b-element" b
			}
			- ", and "
			code id="misnested-tags:-b-p-/b-/p:the-p-element-2" {
				a href="#the-p-element" p
			}
			- ". The "
			a href="#list-of-active-formatting-elements" id="misnested-tags:-b-p-/b-/p:list-of-active-formatting-elements" "list of active formatting elements"
			- " just has the one: "
			code id="misnested-tags:-b-p-/b-/p:the-b-element-3" {
				a href="#the-b-element" b
			}
			- ". The "
			a href="#insertion-mode" id="misnested-tags:-b-p-/b-/p:insertion-mode" "insertion mode"
			- " is \""
			a href="#parsing-main-inbody" id="misnested-tags:-b-p-/b-/p:parsing-main-inbody" "in body"
			- "\"."
		}
		p {
			- "Upon receiving the end tag token with the tag name \"b\", the \""
			a href="#adoptionAgency" "adoption agency algorithm"
			- "\" is invoked, as in the previous example. However, in this case, there "
			em is
			- " a "
			var "furthest block"
			- ", namely the "
			code id="misnested-tags:-b-p-/b-/p:the-p-element-3" {
				a href="#the-p-element" p
			}
			- " element. Thus, this time the adoption agency algorithm isn't skipped over."
		}
		p {
			- "The "
			var "common ancestor"
			- " is the "
			code id="misnested-tags:-b-p-/b-/p:the-body-element-3" {
				a href="#the-body-element" body
			}
			- " element. A conceptual \"bookmark\" marks the position of the "
			code id="misnested-tags:-b-p-/b-/p:the-b-element-4" {
				a href="#the-b-element" b
			}
			- " in the "
			a href="#list-of-active-formatting-elements" id="misnested-tags:-b-p-/b-/p:list-of-active-formatting-elements-2" "list of active formatting elements"
			- ", but since that list has only one element in it, the bookmark won't have much effect."
		}
		p {
			- "As the algorithm progresses, "
			var node
			- " ends up set to the formatting element ("
			code id="misnested-tags:-b-p-/b-/p:the-b-element-5" {
				a href="#the-b-element" b
			}
			- "), and "
			var "last node"
			- " ends up set to the "
			var "furthest block"
			- " ("
			code id="misnested-tags:-b-p-/b-/p:the-p-element-4" {
				a href="#the-p-element" p
			}
			- ")."
		}
		p {
			- "The "
			var "last node"
			- " gets appended (moved) to the "
			var "common ancestor"
			- ", so that the DOM looks like:"
		}
		ul class=domTree {
			li class=t1 {
				code id="misnested-tags:-b-p-/b-/p:the-html-element-3" {
					a href="#the-html-element" html
				}
				ul {
					li class=t1 {
						code id="misnested-tags:-b-p-/b-/p:the-head-element-2" {
							a href="#the-head-element" head
						}
					}
					li class=t1 {
						code id="misnested-tags:-b-p-/b-/p:the-body-element-4" {
							a href="#the-body-element" body
						}
						ul {
							li class=t1 {
								code id="misnested-tags:-b-p-/b-/p:the-b-element-6" {
									a href="#the-b-element" b
								}
								ul {
									li class=t3 {
										code id="misnested-tags:-b-p-/b-/p:text-3" {
											a data-x-internal=text href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#interface-text" "#text"
										}
										- ": "
										span "1"
									}
								}
							}
							li class=t1 {
								code id="misnested-tags:-b-p-/b-/p:the-p-element-5" {
									a href="#the-p-element" p
								}
								ul {
									li class=t3 {
										code id="misnested-tags:-b-p-/b-/p:text-4" {
											a data-x-internal=text href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#interface-text" "#text"
										}
										- ": "
										span "2"
									}
								}
							}
						}
					}
				}
			}
		}
		p {
			- "A new "
			code id="misnested-tags:-b-p-/b-/p:the-b-element-7" {
				a href="#the-b-element" b
			}
			- " element is created, and the children of the "
			code id="misnested-tags:-b-p-/b-/p:the-p-element-6" {
				a href="#the-p-element" p
			}
			- " element are moved to it:"
		}
		ul class=domTree {
			li class=t1 {
				code id="misnested-tags:-b-p-/b-/p:the-html-element-4" {
					a href="#the-html-element" html
				}
				ul {
					li class=t1 {
						code id="misnested-tags:-b-p-/b-/p:the-head-element-3" {
							a href="#the-head-element" head
						}
					}
					li class=t1 {
						code id="misnested-tags:-b-p-/b-/p:the-body-element-5" {
							a href="#the-body-element" body
						}
						ul {
							li class=t1 {
								code id="misnested-tags:-b-p-/b-/p:the-b-element-8" {
									a href="#the-b-element" b
								}
								ul {
									li class=t3 {
										code id="misnested-tags:-b-p-/b-/p:text-5" {
											a data-x-internal=text href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#interface-text" "#text"
										}
										- ": "
										span "1"
									}
								}
							}
							li class=t1 {
								code id="misnested-tags:-b-p-/b-/p:the-p-element-7" {
									a href="#the-p-element" p
								}
							}
						}
